E["item:creeper-ichor"] = {t="item",n="Creeper Ichor",z="hillsbrad",s="Creeper Ichor is a rare, virulent fluid harvested from the moss creepers lurking throughout the forests of the Hillsbrad Foothills. It is sought by the Royal Apothecary Society in Tarren Mill as a potent biological agent for formulating novel plagues against the living.",h="Creeper Ichor is a rare, virulent fluid harvested from the moss creepers lurking throughout the forests of...",sec={{t="Apothecary Research in Hillsbrad",b="In Tarren Mill, Apothecary Lydon conducts experiments to craft deadly new toxins, seeking to eradicate the surrounding human population. Despising the clean air and vibrant life of the foothills, Lydon searches for natural toxins and biological catalysts native to the local wildlife. The venomous fluids of the forest's giant arachnids, particularly the elusive ichor found within mature moss creepers, serve as an ideal base for his Elixir of Suffering. Mixed with other reagents like gray bear tongues, this fluid aids the Forsaken in perfecting their craft of lethal alchemy.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What creatures yield Creeper Ichor?",a="The fluid is harvested from moss creepers inhabiting the Hillsbrad Foothills, including Giant Moss Creepers, Forest Moss Creepers, Elder Moss Creepers, and the notable arachnid Creepthess.",al={"where to get creeper ichor","what drops creeper ichor","creeper ichor mobs"},it="origin",gp=true},{q="Why does Apothecary Lydon need this fluid?",a="Apothecary Lydon uses Creeper Ichor as a vital killing agent in his ongoing alchemical research to brew the Elixir of Suffering, designed to plague and exterminate the living humans in Hillsbrad.",al={"why lydon wants ichor","elixir of suffering purpose","what is creeper ichor used for"},it="why_wanted"},{q="Why is Creeper Ichor so difficult to find?",a="While moss creepers are common throughout the forests surrounding Tarren Mill, viable reservoirs of this particular virulent ichor are uncommon, requiring hunters to slay many arachnids before securing a usable specimen.",al={"why rare","creeper ichor drop rate"},gp=true},{q="What is Creeper Ichor?",a="Creeper Ichor is an exceptionally rare bodily fluid harvested from the moss creepers that haunt the Hillsbrad Foothills. These giant arachnids stalk the forests and fields around Tarren Mill, but only rarely does one yield ichor potent and pure enough to serve as a viable alchemical reagent. To the Royal Apothecary Society, this noxious essence represents a prime lethal agent, prized for its natural toxicity and volatile brewing potential.",al={"what is creeper ichor","creeper ichor lore","moss creeper ichor"},it="identity",add=true},{q="Where does Creeper Ichor come from?",a="Creeper Ichor is not crafted by hands, but harvested directly from the various species of moss creepers native to the Hillsbrad Foothills, including giant, forest, and elder creepers, as well as notorious beasts like Creepthess. It is a natural biological fluid that forms within these giant predatory spiders, though finding a specimen that contains a usable, concentrated amount requires tracking down and slaying dozens of the creatures throughout the wilderness.",al={"where does creeper ichor come from","creeper ichor origin","who made creeper ichor"},it="origin",add=true}},ang={["race:Undead"]="For Forsaken loyalists, securing lethal components like Creeper Ichor directly advances the Royal Apothecary Society's campaign to scour the living from Lordaeron."},kw={"apothecary lydon","creeper ichor","creepthess","elixir of suffering","hillsbrad foothills","moss creeper","tarren mill"},rel={"quest:496","subzone:tarren-mill","zone:hillsbrad","item:gray-bear-tongue","topic:human"},src={"Creeper Ichor","Elixir of Suffering (quest)"}}
E["item:elixir-of-pain"] = {t="item",n="Elixir of Pain",z="hillsbrad",s="The Elixir of Pain is an experimental alchemical concoction brewed by Forsaken apothecaries stationed in Tarren Mill. Distilled using blood harvested across the foothills, the mixture is designed to test biological agents intended to serve Lady Sylvanas's darker ambitions.",h="The Elixir of Pain is an experimental alchemical concoction brewed by Forsaken apothecaries stationed in...",sec={{t="Apothecary Experimentation",b="The Royal Apothecary Society relentlessly pursues new formulas to bolster the Forsaken's position against their mortal neighbors and the Scourge. The Elixir of Pain represents one such trial, blended from freshly harvested ingredients collected around the Hillsbrad Foothills. Concocted with little regard for the living, the potion serves as a proof of concept for volatile substances intended to aid the Dark Lady.",sp=0},{t="Field Testing on Stanley",b="Rather than risk precious military assets or immediately expose their operations to Hillsbrad's defenders, the apothecaries seek a subtle test subject. The elixir is fed to Stanley, a seemingly harmless domestic dog belonging to Farmer Ray on the northern farmstead of Hillsbrad Fields. Instead of a quiet demise, the toxic brew violently mutates the poor animal into an enraged, monstrous wolf.",sp=1}},faq={{q="What is the purpose of the Elixir of Pain?",a="The Elixir of Pain is an experimental potion crafted to test biological compounds for the Royal Apothecary Society. Its creators hope such mixtures will eventually yield devastating concoctions to serve Lady Sylvanas and secure Forsaken dominance.",al={"why make elixir of pain","elixir purpose","what does the elixir do"},it="why_wanted"},{q="Who is Stanley?",a="Stanley is a pet dog belonging to Farmer Ray at the northern farm in Hillsbrad Fields. He is chosen by the Forsaken apothecaries as an unsuspecting test subject to see the physiological effects of their newly brewed elixir.",al={"who is stanley","farmer ray dog","stanley dog"},it="target"},{q="What happens when Stanley drinks the elixir?",a="The volatile chemicals in the elixir cause Stanley to violently mutate into a feral, vicious wolf. Rather than merely poisoning the animal, the concoction warps his form and drives him into an aggressive frenzy.",al={"what happens to stanley","does stanley die","stanley wolf transformation"},sp=1,it="power"},{q="Where is the elixir tested?",a="The test takes place outside the northern farmhouse within Hillsbrad Fields, located southwest of Tarren Mill. Stanley typically rests near the front porch of Farmer Ray's house.",al={"where do i take the elixir","stanley location","farmer ray farm"},it="place",gp=true},{q="What is the Elixir of Pain?",a="The Elixir of Pain is an experimental alchemical concoction brewed for the Forsaken war effort in Hillsbrad Foothills. Brewed using freshly harvested blood combined with volatile reagents, it serves as an early prototype for the dark plagues and toxins the Royal Apothecary Society seeks to engineer for Lady Sylvanas.",al={"what is elixir of pain","elixir of pain item","pain potion"},it="identity",add=true},{q="Where does the Elixir of Pain come from, and who made it?",a="The elixir is brewed at the Forsaken outpost of Tarren Mill. An apothecary mixes fresh creature blood gathered from the surrounding foothills with other caustic ingredients, intending to craft a virulent weapon to advance the Dark Lady's conquest of the region.",al={"who made elixir of pain","elixir of pain creator","where does elixir of pain come from"},it="origin",add=true}},ang={["race:Undead"]="The Royal Apothecary Society's callous field trials demonstrate the Forsaken's willingness to use whatever means necessary to develop chemical weapons against the living.",["faction:Horde"]="Allies of the Forsaken are often called to facilitate these grim tests, witnessing firsthand the unsettling methods Tarren Mill's researchers employ."},kw={"apothecary","elixir of pain","farmer ray","hillsbrad fields","royal apothecary society","stanley","sylvanas","tarren mill"},rel={"quest:501","subzone:hillsbrad-fields","zone:hillsbrad"},src={"Elixir of Pain","Elixir of Pain (2)"}}
E["item:elixir-of-suffering"] = {t="item",n="Elixir of Suffering",z="hillsbrad",s="The Elixir of Suffering is an alchemical concoction brewed by Apothecary Lydon in Tarren Mill. Developed under the orders of the Royal Apothecary Society, the draught is an experimental step toward a virulent plague intended to eradicate both living humans and the Scourge.",h="The Elixir of Suffering is an alchemical concoction brewed by Apothecary Lydon in Tarren Mill.",sec={{t="Apothecary Experimentation",b="Within the ruined hamlet of Tarren Mill, Apothecary Lydon tirelessly combines raw reagents gathered from the surrounding wilderness into toxic draughts. The Elixir of Suffering represents an early milestone in the Royal Apothecary Society's overarching mandate: formulating a new plague designed to exterminate the living and dead alike. Lydon tests the lethal brew on his unfortunate assistant, a toad named Umpi, to ensure its potency.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is the purpose of the Elixir of Suffering?",a="The elixir is an experimental concoction brewed by Apothecary Lydon as part of the Royal Apothecary Society's research. It is intended to test lethal compounds destined for the Forsaken's new plague against humanity and the Scourge.",al={"why make elixir of suffering","what does the elixir do","elixir of suffering purpose"},it="purpose"},{q="Who is Umpi?",a="Umpi is a mundane toad kept by Apothecary Lydon in Tarren Mill. Despite being jokingly referred to as an assistant, Umpi primarily serves as an unwitting test subject for newly brewed alchemical toxins.",al={"who is the frog","who is the toad","lydon's assistant"},it="people"},{q="What happens when Umpi drinks the elixir?",a="Upon being fed the Elixir of Suffering, the unfortunate amphibian croaks and succumbs almost instantly to the poison, demonstrating the deadly efficacy of Apothecary Lydon's formulation.",al={"does umpi die","what happens to the toad"},sp=1},{q="What is the Elixir of Suffering?",a="The Elixir of Suffering is an experimental concoction brewed by the Royal Apothecary Society in Tarren Mill. Designed as part of the Forsaken's ongoing pursuit of a new plague, this lethal mixture is crafted to inflict agonizing pain and death upon both the living and the undead.",al={"what is elixir of suffering","elixir of suffering lore","what does elixir of suffering do"},it="identity",add=true},{q="Where does the Elixir of Suffering come from, and who made it?",a="The elixir is brewed by Apothecary Lydon, stationed at Tarren Mill in the Hillsbrad Foothills. Working on behalf of the Royal Apothecary Society and Lady Sylvanas Windrunner, Lydon gathers local components across the foothills to formulate and refine the deadly potion.",al={"who made elixir of suffering","creator of elixir of suffering","where did elixir of suffering come from"},it="origin",add=true},{q="Why does Apothecary Lydon want to create the Elixir of Suffering?",a="Apothecary Lydon concocts the elixir to fulfill the Dark Lady's grand design: crafting a weapon potent enough to eradicate both the Scourge and humanity. He tests its lethality on local subjects to ensure the brew inflicts maximum torment and swift demise.",al={"why make elixir of suffering","purpose of elixir of suffering","why does lydon want the elixir"},it="why_wanted",add=true}},ang={["race:Undead"]="The Royal Apothecary Society works across Lordaeron to create a weapon that will secure the Forsaken's independence from both the Scourge and living humanity, and Lydon's noxious experiments in Tarren Mill are an essential step."},kw={"apothecary lydon","elixir of suffering","forsaken plague","hillsbrad foothills","royal apothecary society","tarren mill","umpi"},rel={"subzone:tarren-mill","npc:umpi","quest:496","zone:hillsbrad","topic:scourge","topic:human"},src={"Elixir of Suffering","Elixir of Suffering (2)"}}
E["item:farren-s-report"] = {t="item",n="Farren's Report",z="hillsbrad",s="Farren's Report is an official dispatch drafted by Lieutenant Farren Orinelle in Southshore detailing his investigations into the local naga. Farren uses this document to appeal to his former mentor, Major Samuelson in Stormwind Keep, hoping to secure a reassignment back to the capital.",h="Farren's Report is an official dispatch drafted by Lieutenant Farren Orinelle in Southshore detailing his...",sec={{t="A Ticket Out of Southshore",b="Stationed on the embattled coast of Hillsbrad Foothills, Lieutenant Farren Orinelle grew weary of local leadership and the remote frontier. After tasking adventurers with hunting the Daggerspine naga to gather proof of their threat, Orinelle compiled his findings into a formal report. Rather than submitting it to his commanding officer, Magistrate Henry Maleb, or local veteran Marshal Redpath, Farren aimed to send it directly to Major Samuelson, the captain of the guard in Stormwind Keep. Having trained under Samuelson, Farren hoped the document would demonstrate his competence and justify an immediate transfer back to the comforts of Stormwind City.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is Farren's Report?",a="It is a formal military dispatch penned by Lieutenant Farren Orinelle summarizing his operations against the Daggerspine naga encroaching on Southshore's beaches.",al={"farrens report","what is this report","orinelle report"},it="identity"},{q="Why does Farren want this delivered to Stormwind?",a="Farren wants to be reassigned away from Southshore and back to Stormwind City. He addresses the report directly to Major Samuelson, his former mentor and the captain of the Stormwind guard, hoping to earn a favorable transfer.",al={"why send report to stormwind","farrens goal","why samuelson"},it="why_wanted"},{q="Why is Farren keeping the report a secret from Redpath?",a="Farren wants to avoid scrutiny from Marshal Redpath and local leadership, who might take offense to an officer leveraging a local threat strictly to engineer a personal transfer back to safety in the capital.",al={"why hide from redpath","ol redpath secret"},it="motive"},{q="How does Major Samuelson react upon receiving it?",a="Major Samuelson commends his former student for taking initiative against the Southshore naga and promises to consider the report when reviewing guard personnel assignments in the coming month.",al={"samuelson reaction","turn in reassignment"},sp=1},{q="Where does Farren's Report come from, and who made it?",a="The document was drafted in Southshore by Lieutenant Farren Orinelle himself. Stationed out in the dangerous frontier of Hillsbrad Foothills, Farren compiled the report detailing his efforts against the regional murlocs and naga to catch the eye of high command in the capital.",al={"who wrote farren's report","farrens report origin","who made farrens report"},it="origin",add=true}},ang={["faction:Alliance"]="The document highlights the bureaucratic maneuvering within the Alliance military, where distant postings in Hillsbrad clash with officers scheming for safer duty in Stormwind.",["race:Human"]="For humans of the Alliance, carrying Farren's report traces the enduring link between the besieged southern refuge of Southshore and the royal court of Stormwind Keep."},kw={"farren orinelle","farren's report","major samuelson","naga","reassignment","redpath","southshore","stormwind keep"},rel={"quest:563","npc:lieutenant-farren-orinelle","npc:major-samuelson","subzone:southshore","subzone:stormwind-keep","quest:562","quest:559","topic:naga"},src={"Farren's Report","Reassignment"}}
E["item:frostwolf-banner"] = {t="item",n="Frostwolf Banner",z="hillsbrad",s="The Frostwolf Banner is a tribal standard cached deep within Wildpaw Cavern in Alterac Valley. Horde initiates are sent to recover it as an ancestral rite of passage to awaken their battle spirit and earn their first clan insignia.",h="The Frostwolf Banner is a tribal standard cached deep within Wildpaw Cavern in Alterac Valley.",sec={{t="A Rite of Passage",b="For warriors of the Horde arriving in Alterac Valley, claiming true standing among the Frostwolf clan begins with a trial of grit. Warmaster Laggrond sends new recruits south into the damp, hostile corridors of Wildpaw Cavern, a den swarming with territorial gnolls. Reaching the banner hidden within their depths and returning it unbroken demonstrates courage, proving the warrior's battle rage has awakened and earning them the Frostwolf initiate's insignia.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Why is the Frostwolf Banner inside a gnoll cave?",a="Warmaster Laggrond and the clan purposefully treat the banner's location in Wildpaw Cavern as an initiation test. Venturing into gnoll territory forces new fighters to shake off complacency, face danger, and awaken their battle spirit.",al={"why is banner in wildpaw","gnolls have banner","frostwolf banner location"},it="place"},{q="Who do I return the Frostwolf Banner to?",a="The banner must be returned to Warmaster Laggrond in Alterac Valley. Presenting it to him formally welcomes an initiate into the Frostwolf ranks and earns an insignia of standing.",al={"who wants frostwolf banner","banner quest turn in","laggrond banner"},it="next_step",gp=true},{q="Why does the standard look unusual for a Frostwolf crest?",a="While recognized by Laggrond as a clan trial standard, its visual markings resemble older tribal insignias, including symbols associated with early orcish clans from the old Horde.",al={"twilight hammer symbol banner","banner looks wrong","frostwolf banner design"}},{q="What is the Frostwolf Banner?",a="The Frostwolf Banner is a tribal standard representing the Frostwolf clan in Alterac Valley. While its emblazoned sigil strangely resembles ancient clan iconography rather than their usual crest, it remains an honored symbol of the clan's presence and authority in the frozen valley.",al={"what is frostwolf banner","frostwolf banner lore","about frostwolf banner"},it="identity",add=true},{q="Why does Warmaster Laggrond want the Frostwolf Banner recovered?",a="Warmaster Laggrond requires all newcomers seeking to fight alongside the Frostwolves in Alterac Valley to undergo a rite of battle. Retrieving the banner from the depths of the gnoll-infested Wildpaw Cavern proves your courage, awakening your warrior spirit and earning you an initiate's insignia among the clan.",al={"why recover frostwolf banner","why does laggrond want banner","frostwolf banner purpose"},it="why_wanted",add=true}},ang={["faction:Horde"]="Recovering this banner marks a warrior's formal blooding and initiation into the legendary Frostwolf clan under Warmaster Laggrond.",["race:Orc"]="For orcs, returning a lost clan standard from savage gnolls honors the legacy of Frostfire and Thrall's ancestral heritage in the Alterac mountains."},kw={"alterac valley","frostwolf banner","gnolls","insignia","proving grounds","warmaster laggrond","wildpaw cavern"},rel={"quest:7161","npc:warmaster-laggrond","topic:horde","topic:gnoll","topic:twilight-s-hammer","zone:hillsbrad"},src={"Frostwolf Banner","Proving Grounds (Alterac Valley) (Horde)"}}
E["item:gray-bear-tongue"] = {t="item",n="Gray Bear Tongue",z="hillsbrad",s="A gray bear tongue is a raw reagent harvested from the wild bears roaming the Hillsbrad Foothills. It is sought after by the Royal Apothecary Society in Tarren Mill to serve as a biological component in their experimental toxins.",h="A gray bear tongue is a raw reagent harvested from the wild bears roaming the Hillsbrad Foothills.",sec={{t="Apothecary Research in Hillsbrad",b="The untamed wilderness surrounding Tarren Mill is rich in native fauna, including several varieties of sturdy gray bears. While natural predators pose a constant threat to travelers, the Forsaken see them as a harvestable source of raw alchemy components. Apothecary Lydon studies local wildlife to isolate potent organic agents, using the heavy muscular tissue and fluids of gray bear tongues as a base ingredient for concocting lethal solutions such as the Elixir of Suffering.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who wants gray bear tongues?",a="Apothecary Lydon, stationed at the Forsaken outpost of Tarren Mill in the Hillsbrad Foothills, seeks these tongues to brew experimental killing agents.",al={"who needs bear tongues","apothecary lydon tongues","bear tongue turn in"},it="why_wanted"},{q="What is the Apothecary using these tongues for?",a="Lydon is developing a lethal concoction known as the Elixir of Suffering, designed to help plague the living human populations of Hillsbrad. The tongues serve as one of the primary organic agents alongside creeper ichor.",al={"why does lydon want tongues","bear tongue purpose","elixir of suffering ingredients"},it="purpose"},{q="Which creatures drop these tongues?",a="They can be harvested from any of the local gray bears roaming the Hillsbrad Foothills, including standard gray bears, elder gray bears, vicious gray bears, and the notorious beast Big Samras.",al={"where do bear tongues drop","which bears have tongues","hillsbrad bears"},it="origin",gp=true},{q="What is Gray Bear Tongue?",a="It is exactly what it sounds like: a freshly carved tongue taken from one of the wild gray bears roaming the Hillsbrad Foothills. While unappealing to most travelers, alchemists and researchers among the Forsaken value animal tissues for their specific chemical properties when formulating new concoctions.",al={"what is gray bear tongue","gray bear tongue item","what are gray bear tongues"},it="identity",add=true},{q="Where does a Gray Bear Tongue come from?",a="These tongues are harvested directly from the gray bears that prowl the forests and hills surrounding Tarren Mill in the Hillsbrad Foothills. Hunters can claim them from common gray bears, elder specimens, vicious variants, or notable beasts like Big Samras.",al={"gray bear tongue source","where do gray bear tongues come from","who drops gray bear tongues"},it="origin",add=true}},ang={["race:Undead"]="Procuring organic components from local wildlife directly aids the Royal Apothecary Society's mission to craft new plagues against the living."},kw={"apothecary lydon","big samras","elixir of suffering","gray bear tongue","hillsbrad foothills","royal apothecary society","tarren mill"},rel={"quest:496","item:creeper-ichor","subzone:tarren-mill","zone:hillsbrad"},src={"Gray Bear Tongue","Elixir of Suffering (quest)"}}
E["item:hillsbrad-human-skull"] = {t="item",n="Hillsbrad Human Skull",z="hillsbrad",s="A gruesome war trophy harvested from slain human defenders and townsfolk across the Hillsbrad Foothills. These skulls are collected by Forsaken stationed at Tarren Mill as grim mementos of the relentless assault against the local human settlements.",h="A gruesome war trophy harvested from slain human defenders and townsfolk across the Hillsbrad Foothills.",sec={{t="Trophies of a Bitter War",b="As conflict rages between the Forsaken of Tarren Mill and the human inhabitants of Southshore and surrounding settlements, severed skulls serve as physical proof of the slaughter. While Deathstalkers and soldiers carry out the systematic purge ordered by Darthalia during the Battle of Hillsbrad, other guards stuck on watch duty crave a piece of the carnage. Deathguard Samsa eagerly solicits these trophies from frontline fighters, taking twisted pleasure in amassing the remains of the very people the Forsaken once lived among in life.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who wants these human skulls?",a="Deathguard Samsa, a Forsaken sentry stationed in Tarren Mill, collects them. Envious of the soldiers sent out to battle and pillage Southshore while he remains confined to guard duty, he asks passing adventurers to bring him thirty skulls to add to his private collection.",al={"who wants skulls","who takes human skulls","deathguard samsa skulls"}},{q="Where are Hillsbrad Human Skulls gathered?",a="They are recovered from human combatants and laborers throughout the Hillsbrad Foothills, notably around the human-held farms, mines, and town fortifications assaulted during the Battle of Hillsbrad campaign.",al={"where do skulls drop","farm human skulls","who drops human skulls"},it="origin",gp=true},{q="Why do the Forsaken collect human remains?",a="Beyond raw hatred and dark humor, collecting trophies of dead humans is common sport among the Forsaken. Soldiers like Samsa view the skulls as prized curiosities and satisfying proof of Southshore's impending downfall.",al={"why do forsaken want skulls","forsaken skull collection"}},{q="What is a Hillsbrad Human Skull?",a="These are the gruesome trophies severed from the fallen human defenders and townsfolk scattered across the Hillsbrad Foothills. As conflict rages between the Forsaken of Tarren Mill and the living humans of Hillsbrad, such macabre tokens serve as tangible proof of Alliance casualties in the contested territory.",al={"what are hillsbrad human skulls","hillsbrad skull item","hillsbrad human skull info"},it="identity",add=true},{q="Where does a Hillsbrad Human Skull come from, and who made it?",a="These skulls are taken directly from the mortal humans inhabiting the Hillsbrad Foothills, harvested by Horde fighters engaged in the ongoing border war. Rather than being manufactured, they are morbid battlefield remnants claimed from the slain soldiers, farmers, and citizens defending the local human settlements against the Forsaken.",al={"hillsbrad human skull origin","where do hillsbrad skulls come from","who makes hillsbrad skulls"},it="origin",add=true},{q="Why does Deathguard Samsa want Hillsbrad Human Skulls?",a="Deathguard Samsa, stationed on guard duty at Tarren Mill, is intensely envious of the warriors sent out to pillage and fight the living. Stranded behind the front lines, he collects the skulls as precious personal souvenirs of death to share vicariously in the slaughter of Hillsbrad's human defenders.",al={"why does samsa want skulls","who wants hillsbrad human skulls and why","why collect hillsbrad human skulls"},it="why_wanted",add=true}},ang={["race:Undead"]="For the Forsaken, claiming human skulls from Hillsbrad is both sweet vengeance and a macabre reminder of the living brethren who shun them.",["faction:Alliance"]="The sight of Southshore's farmers and soldiers reduced to collected trinkets represents the grim cruelty of the Forsaken campaign in Lordaeron."},kw={"darthalia","hillsbrad","samsa","skull","southshore","tarren mill","trophy"},rel={"quest:546","npc:deathguard-samsa","quest:527","subzone:tarren-mill","zone:hillsbrad","topic:human","item:courser-eye"},src={"Hillsbrad Human Skull","Souvenirs of Death"}}
E["item:hillsbrad-town-registry"] = {t="item",n="Hillsbrad Town Registry",z="hillsbrad",s="The Hillsbrad Town Registry is an official municipal ledger kept inside the town hall of the Hillsbrad Fields. It serves as an accounting of the settlement's surviving citizens, landowners, and civic records, making it a key strategic target during the Forsaken offensive against the human stronghold.",h="The Hillsbrad Town Registry is an official municipal ledger kept inside the town hall of the Hillsbrad Fields.",sec={{t="A Record of Defiance",b="Resting in the town hall near the podium of Magistrate Burnside, the Hillsbrad Town Registry documents the population, households, and administrative rights of Hillsbrad. As the Forsaken from Tarren Mill push to break human resistance in the foothills, Darthalia commands Horde champions to infiltrate the town hall, eliminate the council, and seize this ledger. Confiscating the registry strips Hillsbrad of its civic order and provides the Undercity with valuable intelligence on the surviving population and their assets.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Where is the Hillsbrad Town Registry kept?",a="The registry is housed within the town hall at the Hillsbrad Fields, sitting in a corner near the stairs leading up to Magistrate Burnside's platform.",al={"registry location","where is town registry","find hillsbrad registry"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Why do the Forsaken want to steal it?",a="High Executor Darthalia seeks to utterly dismantle human governance in the foothills. Seizing the registry robs the township of vital records regarding its citizens and property while providing the Forsaken with detailed intelligence on the surviving community.",al={"why steal registry","darthalia registry quest","purpose of registry"},it="why_wanted"},{q="Who guards the registry?",a="It is guarded by Magistrate Burnside and the Hillsbrad Councilmen, who wield defensive magic and rally inside and around the town hall.",al={"who protects registry","town hall defenders"},it="danger",gp=true},{q="What is the Hillsbrad Town Registry?",a="The Hillsbrad Town Registry is an official record book kept inside the town hall of the Hillsbrad Fields settlement. Maintained by the local human administration under Magistrate Burnside, it documents the civic affairs, population, and governance of one of the Alliance's surviving holdings in the foothills.",al={"what is hillsbrad town registry","hillsbrad registry","what is the registry book"},it="identity",add=true}},ang={["faction:Horde"]="Capturing the town registry is a decisive step in breaking human authority in the foothills and cementing the Forsaken stronghold at Tarren Mill.",["race:Human"]="The ledger represents the formal existence and rights of Hillsbrad's remaining townsfolk, making its loss a devastating blow to the regional community."},kw={"battle of hillsbrad","darthalia","hillsbrad fields","hillsbrad town hall","hillsbrad town registry","magistrate burnside"},rel={"quest:527","subzone:hillsbrad-fields","zone:hillsbrad","subzone:tarren-mill","topic:human","topic:mage"},src={"Hillsbrad Town Registry","Battle of Hillsbrad (4)"}}
E["item:humbert-s-sword"] = {t="item",n="Humbert's Sword",z="hillsbrad",s="Humbert's Sword is the personal sidearm belonging to Deathguard Humbert of Tarren Mill. The weapon was looted from his camp by dwarven soldiers while he was scouting their stronghold at Dun Garok.",h="Humbert's Sword is the personal sidearm belonging to Deathguard Humbert of Tarren Mill.",sec={{t="A Scout's Careless Moment",b="Deathguard Humbert was dispatched by High Executor Darthalia to monitor the dwarven presence at Dun Garok from a concealed position. While he left his post unattended one morning to collect firewood to boil water, dwarven patrols stumbled across his campsite and plundered all of his gear, including his personal blade. Fearing severe punishment from Darthalia if his incompetence is discovered, Humbert relies on Horde agents to infiltrate the fortress and retrieve his lost weapon.",sp=0},{t="The Dwarven Trove",b="Following the theft, Humbert's belongings were carried back behind the fortified barricades of Dun Garok. Because dwarven riflemen, mountaineers, and priests circulate supplies throughout the garrison, locating the specific thief requires searching among the defenders stationed within the stronghold's trenches and redoubts.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who owns this sword?",a="The blade belongs to Deathguard Humbert, a Forsaken sentry stationed in Tarren Mill who was assigned to scout Dun Garok.",al={"whose sword is this","humbert owner","who is humbert"},it="identity"},{q="How did the dwarves get Humbert's sword?",a="Deathguard Humbert abandoned his scout camp just outside Dun Garok to gather firewood in the morning. While he was away, a dwarven patrol ransacked the camp and carried off his gear.",al={"how did dwarves get it","why do dwarves have sword","how was sword stolen"}},{q="Why is Humbert so desperate to get his sword back?",a="Beyond needing his weapon to perform his duties, Humbert fears that his commander, High Executor Darthalia, will execute him for his blunder if she discovers he lost his equipment while on duty.",al={"why humbert want sword","what happens if humbert loses sword","why does humbert care"},it="why_wanted"},{q="Where can the sword be found?",a="The sword is held by the dwarven forces garrisoned at Dun Garok, situated in southeastern Hillsbrad Foothills. It can be recovered from the mountaineers, riflemen, or priests stationed throughout the post.",al={"where does sword drop","sword location","how to find humbert's sword"},it="place",gp=true}},ang={["race:Undead"]="High Executor Darthalia maintains merciless discipline over the Forsaken forces in Hillsbrad, leaving negligent sentries like Humbert desperate to conceal their mistakes.",["faction:Horde"]="Recovering the sword coincides with wider Horde operations targeting Dun Garok's dwarven enclave, including the collection of dwarven blood and military insignias."},kw={"darthalia","deathguard humbert","dun garok","hillsbrad","humbert's sword","tarren mill"},rel={"quest:547","npc:deathguard-humbert","subzone:dun-garok","subzone:tarren-mill","npc:high-executor-darthalia","quest:527","quest:509","zone:hillsbrad"},src={"Humbert's Sword","Humbert's Sword (quest)"}}
E["item:keg-of-shindigger-stout"] = {t="item",n="Keg of Shindigger Stout",z="hillsbrad",s="A Keg of Shindigger Stout is a barrel of potent dwarven ale brewed and guarded by the riflemen and soldiers garrisoned within Dun Garok. Desired by the Royal Apothecary Society in Tarren Mill, it serves not as an evening drink, but as a deceitful delivery vehicle for newly synthesized plagues.",h="A Keg of Shindigger Stout is a barrel of potent dwarven ale brewed and guarded by the riflemen and soldiers...",sec={{t="A Dwarven Favorite",b="Dun Garok stands as a formidable dwarven bastion in the southeastern Hillsbrad Foothills, fiercely maintained by the dwarves of Ironforge. Within its entrenched barracks and mess halls, the stout-hearted defenders share barrels of Shindigger Stout to weather the cold and the grinding siege against regional enemies. The brew is robust and plentiful, making it a staple of the garrison's day-to-day survival.",sp=0},{t="Apothecary Lydon's Poison Vessel",b="While the dwarves consider Shindigger Stout an honest reward after battle, Apothecary Lydon in Tarren Mill sees it as an ideal vector for terror. Tasked with developing the Forsaken's sinister Elixir of Agony, Lydon rejects testing his lethal formula on beasts. Instead, he seeks an intact keg of the ale to spike it with the brew, creating a tainted offering intended to sow agony and death among the living.",sp=1}},faq={{q="What is Shindigger Stout used for?",a="Apothecary Lydon in Tarren Mill wants the keg of stout to test his freshly refined Elixir of Agony. Rather than wasting the virulent poison on laboratory animals, he intends to lace the dwarven ale to conduct a lethal field test against humanoid subjects.",al={"why get shindigger stout","shindigger stout purpose","what does lydon do with the keg"},it="why_wanted"},{q="Where can a Keg of Shindigger Stout be found?",a="Kegs of the stout are stored deep within the dwarven fortress of Dun Garok, situated in southeastern Hillsbrad Foothills. They can typically be found resting in the mess halls and lower barracks rooms occupied by the dwarven infantry.",al={"keg location","where is shindigger stout","find the stout"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Who brews Shindigger Stout?",a="It is brewed and kept by the dwarves of Dun Garok, who maintain a heavily fortified garrison in Hillsbrad Foothills on behalf of Ironforge.",al={"who makes shindigger stout","is it dwarven ale"},it="origin"},{q="Why doesn't Apothecary Lydon brew his own alcohol for the test?",a="Lydon specifically targets the dwarves of Dun Garok out of malice and convenience. Using their prized ale allows the Royal Apothecary Society to turn a staple of the living Alliance soldiers into a weapon against them in the name of the Dark Lady.",al={"why steal dwarven beer","why dun garok beer"},it="motive"},{q="What is a Keg of Shindigger Stout?",a="A Keg of Shindigger Stout is a barrel of potent dwarven ale kept by the Stormpike dwarves stationed in the fortress of Dun Garok. While intended to supply the dwarven soldiers during their deployment in the Hillsbrad Foothills, its strong brew makes it a prime vehicle for Apothecary Lydon's experiments on behalf of the Royal Apothecary Society.",al={"what is keg of shindigger stout","shindigger stout keg info","what is shindigger stout"},it="identity",add=true}},ang={["race:Undead"]="For the Forsaken, stealing a barrel of prized dwarven ale is purely practical alchemy: alcohol masks the scent and taste of deadly concoctions developed for Lady Sylvanas.",["faction:Horde"]="Striking at Dun Garok disrupts a dangerous Alliance military foothold nestled directly between the Alterac Mountains and the Arathi highlands."},kw={"apothecary lydon","dun garok","dwarven ale","elixir of agony","keg of shindigger stout","shindigger stout","tarren mill"},rel={"quest:509","subzone:dun-garok","subzone:tarren-mill","npc:umpi","zone:hillsbrad","topic:horde"},src={"Keg of Shindigger Stout","Elixir of Agony (4)"}}
E["item:mountain-lion-blood"] = {t="item",n="Mountain Lion Blood",z="hillsbrad",s="Mountain Lion Blood is a reagent collected from the prowling predators of the Hillsbrad Foothills and the snowy slopes of Alterac. Apothecary Lydon of Tarren Mill seeks this fresh blood to formulate the Royal Apothecary Society's dreaded Elixir of Pain.",h="Mountain Lion Blood is a reagent collected from the prowling predators of the Hillsbrad Foothills and the...",sec={{t="Reagent of the Hills",b="The highlands and foothills flanking Hillsbrad and Alterac are prowled by feral and starving mountain lions. While ordinary hunters seek these predators for their pelts and claws, the Forsaken of the Royal Apothecary Society find value in what pumps through their veins. Fresh mountain lion blood possesses specific biological properties that Apothecary Lydon in Tarren Mill believes will serve as the base for a potent new toxic brew designed to bring misery to the living.",sp=0},{t="Fueling the New Plague",b="Apothecary Lydon's experiments in Tarren Mill contribute directly to the Royal Apothecary Society's overarching mandate: perfecting the Forsaken's New Plague. By harvesting the blood of vigorous wild beasts, Lydon seeks to refine a concoction he calls the Elixir of Pain, testing how potent local organic compounds can be weaponized against the enemies of the Dark Lady.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is Mountain Lion Blood used for?",a="Apothecary Lydon at Tarren Mill requires ten vials of Mountain Lion Blood to distill a lethal concoction known as the Elixir of Pain, part of the Royal Apothecary Society's research into new diseases.",al={"what is mountain lion blood for","who needs lion blood","elixir of pain blood"},it="why_wanted"},{q="Where can Mountain Lion Blood be collected?",a="It is gathered from mountain lions hunting across the Hillsbrad Foothills and up into the neighboring snowy crags of the Alterac Mountains.",al={"where to find mountain lion blood","mountain lion blood location","which lions drop blood"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Why does Apothecary Lydon specifically want wild cat blood?",a="Lydon believes the vital fluids of the aggressive, hardy mountain lions provide the ideal biological foundation for crafting a particularly agonizing toxic brew aimed at the living inhabitants of Hillsbrad.",al={"why lion blood","why does lydon want lion blood"},it="motive"},{q="Is Mountain Lion Blood useful for alchemy crafting recipes?",a="No. It is exclusively an experimental research reagent collected for Apothecary Lydon's personal work and is not an ingredient in standard tradeskill alchemy.",al={"can alchemists use mountain lion blood","is lion blood for alchemy"},it="item",gp=true},{q="What is Mountain Lion Blood?",a="It is fresh blood harvested from the predatory mountain lions prowling the rugged slopes of the Hillsbrad Foothills and Alterac Mountains. Though useless to common alchemists or tradesfolk, it possesses biological qualities prized by the Royal Apothecary Society for their lethal alchemical experiments.",al={"what is mountain lion blood","mountain lion blood lore","what is this blood"},it="identity",add=true},{q="Where does Mountain Lion Blood come from, and who made it?",a="It is not crafted or manufactured, but drawn directly from the feral cats indigenous to northern Lordaeron. The mountain lions that roam the highlands between Hillsbrad and Alterac are hunted and bled by agents working on behalf of the Forsaken apothecaries stationed at Tarren Mill.",al={"where does mountain lion blood come from","source of mountain lion blood","who made mountain lion blood"},it="origin",add=true}},ang={["race:Undead"]="Every vial collected aids the Royal Apothecary Society in developing devastating biological weapons to secure Lordaeron for the Forsaken.",["faction:Horde"]="Gathering beast reagents around Tarren Mill directly bolsters the Horde's fortified presence against hostile human enclaves in Hillsbrad."},kw={"alterac","apothecary lydon","elixir of pain","hillsbrad","mountain lion blood","royal apothecary society","tarren mill"},rel={"quest:501","subzone:tarren-mill","topic:royal-apothecary-society","zone:hillsbrad","zone:alterac","subzone:hillsbrad-fields","topic:horde","topic:alterac-kingdom"},src={"Mountain Lion Blood","Elixir of Pain (quest)"}}
E["item:mudsnout-blossom"] = {t="item",n="Mudsnout Blossom",z="hillsbrad",s="Mudsnout Blossoms are pungent, toxic fungal growths found sprouting in Nethander Stead in the Hillsbrad Foothills. Revered by local gnolls and harvested by the Royal Apothecary Society, these foul mushrooms are deadly to the living while surprisingly invigorating to the undead.",h="Mudsnout Blossoms are pungent, toxic fungal growths found sprouting in Nethander Stead in the Hillsbrad...",sec={{t="A Toxic Fungus",b="Despite their floral name, Mudsnout Blossoms are actually large, foul-smelling mushrooms that flourish primarily in the soiled dirt of Nethander Stead, south of Tarren Mill. They grow amidst the camps of the local Mudsnout gnolls, who defend the territory fiercely. To living organisms, the spores and flesh of the mushroom act as a virulent poison, causing agony and rapid biological deterioration. However, their necrotic nature interacts differently with unlife, granting a rejuvenating reaction to undead bodies.",sp=0},{t="Fuel for the Royal Apothecary Society",b="In Tarren Mill, Apothecary Lydon seeks out Mudsnout Blossoms as raw material for his chemical experiments. Under the mandate of Lady Sylvanas Windrunner, the Royal Apothecary Society labors relentlessly to engineer a new plague capable of eradicating both the Scourge and living humanity. The caustic, flesh-withering properties of these mushrooms make them an ideal base component for Lydon's brew, the infamous Elixir of Agony.",sp=1}},faq={{q="What is a Mudsnout Blossom?",a="Despite being called a blossom, it is a large, pungent toxic mushroom found in the damp soil of the Hillsbrad Foothills.",al={"mudsnout blossom lore","is mudsnout blossom a flower","what kind of plant is mudsnout blossom"},it="identity"},{q="Where do Mudsnout Blossoms grow?",a="They grow throughout Nethander Stead, an abandoned farmstead south of Tarren Mill and east of the river that runs past Southshore. The area is heavily infested with Mudsnout gnolls.",al={"mudsnout blossom location","where to find mudsnout blossoms","nethander stead mushrooms"},it="place"},{q="Why is the Royal Apothecary Society collecting them?",a="Apothecary Lydon in Tarren Mill requires them to brew the Elixir of Agony. The Forsaken are researching toxins to help craft a new plague capable of wiping out both the living and the Scourge.",al={"why does lydon want mudsnout blossoms","elixir of agony ingredients","apothecary lydon mushroom"},it="why_wanted"},{q="What effects does the blossom have on the living versus the undead?",a="The blossoms are acutely toxic and destructive to living flesh and organs, yet their unnatural properties provide a restorative boost to undead physiology.",al={"is mudsnout blossom poisonous","mudsnout mushroom effects","are mudsnout blossoms deadly"},it="power"},{q="Where do Mudsnout Blossoms come from?",a="Mudsnout Blossoms are large, foul-smelling mushrooms that sprout in the fields of Nethander Stead in the southern Hillsbrad Foothills. They thrive around the local Mudsnout gnolls who dwell there and fiercely guard the patch, though whether the gnolls intentionally cultivate the pungent fungi or merely nest among them is uncertain.",al={"mudsnout blossom origin","where did mudsnout blossoms come from","who made mudsnout blossom"},it="origin",add=true}},ang={["race:Undead"]="The Forsaken make extensive use of the blossom's toxic properties, harvesting it to refine biochemical weapons for the Royal Apothecary Society while benefiting from its strange restorative effect on dead tissue.",["profession:Herbalism"]="Though botanists and herbalists might mistake its name for a common flower, the Mudsnout Blossom is actually a volatile, foul-smelling fungus prized by toxicologists and dark alchemists."},kw={"apothecary lydon","elixir of agony","hillsbrad foothills","mudsnout blossom","mudsnout gnolls","nethander stead","tarren mill"},rel={"quest:509","subzone:nethander-stead","subzone:tarren-mill","topic:gnoll","zone:hillsbrad","quest:367"},src={"Mudsnout Blossom","Elixir of Agony"}}
E["item:murloc-head"] = {t="item",n="Murloc Head",z="hillsbrad",s="Murloc Heads are grim trophies severed from the amphibious creatures prowling the Western Strand in Hillsbrad Foothills. Lieutenant Farren Orinelle of Southshore requires them as physical proof of culled threats to satisfy his superior, Magistrate Redpath.",h="Murloc Heads are grim trophies severed from the amphibious creatures prowling the Western Strand in Hillsbrad...",sec={{t="A Grislier Kind of Proof",b="Southshore faces dangers from all directions, but the aggressive murlocs clustering along the Western Strand are an immediate menace to local fishermen and coastal travelers. Although Alliance adventurers frequently sweep the beaches to cull the creatures, Magistrate Henry Redpath demands undeniable verification before signing off on defensive reports. To humor the bureaucracy, Lieutenant Farren Orinelle relies on hired fighters to haul in cold, dripping murloc heads—an unpleasant task Farren himself finds entirely repulsive, especially given how thoroughly the sight has spoiled his appetite for Southshore's local seafood.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Why does Farren Orinelle want murloc heads?",a="Magistrate Henry Redpath was not satisfied with simple reports of murlocs being cleared from the beaches. To verify the threat was genuinely reduced, he demanded physical evidence, forcing Lieutenant Farren to collect severed heads as proof.",al={"farren proof","why murloc heads","who wants murloc heads in southshore"},it="why_wanted"},{q="Where are these murlocs found?",a="They are gathered from the murloc tribes infesting the Western Strand, the coastline stretching west of Southshore in Hillsbrad Foothills.",al={"murloc head location","where to get murloc heads hillsbrad","western strand murlocs"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Why is Farren so disgusted by them?",a="Farren finds walking fish inherently unnatural and stomach-turning. The sight of slimy, bleeding severed heads dripping onto the floor disgusts him so much that he refuses to eat fish, which is a major dietary staple in a port town like Southshore.",al={"farren reaction","farren eating fish"}},{q="Does collecting the heads solve Southshore's murloc problem?",a="Not immediately. Even after presenting the initial collection, Magistrate Redpath's exacting standards and continuing murloc raids lead Farren to demand further evidence before matters are resolved.",al={"do murlocs stop attacking","farren quest chain"}},{q="What is a Murloc Head?",a="It is the freshly severed skull of a murloc slain along the coast of the Hillsbrad Foothills. Cold, slimy, and oozing foul fluids, it serves as undeniable physical evidence of a beast cut down in the defense of Southshore.",al={"what is murloc head","murloc head info","murloc head item"},it="identity",add=true},{q="Where do Murloc Heads come from?",a="They are hacked directly from the bodies of the murlocs prowling the Western Strand, just west of Southshore. Rather than crafted goods, they are grisly trophies taken from the shoreline raiders troubling the Alliance garrison.",al={"where do murloc heads drop","who made murloc head","murloc head source"},it="origin",add=true}},ang={["faction:Alliance"]="Clearing the Western Strand protects Southshore's fragile fishing economy and secures the coastline for the Alliance's last stronghold in Lordaeron."},kw={"farren orinelle","farren's proof","hillsbrad foothills","magistrate redpath","murloc","murloc head","southshore","western strand"},rel={"quest:559","npc:lieutenant-farren-orinelle","subzone:southshore","zone:hillsbrad","topic:murloc","quest:536","quest:562","quest:563"},src={"Murloc Head","Farren's Proof"}}
E["item:renferrel-s-findings"] = {t="item",n="Renferrel's Findings",z="hillsbrad",s="Renferrel's Findings is a collection of research notes compiled by Apothecary Renferrel in Silverpine Forest. Entrusted to Horde couriers, these documents carry vital data southward to Apothecary Lydon in Tarren Mill to assist in brewing the Forsaken's New Plague.",h="Renferrel's Findings is a collection of research notes compiled by Apothecary Renferrel in Silverpine Forest.",sec={{t="A Plague in Development",b="The Royal Apothecary Society labours tirelessly under direct orders from the Dark Lady, Lady Sylvanas Windrunner, to engineer a New Plague. Achieving this breakthrough requires constant collaboration among researchers scattered across Lordaeron. Stationed at the Sepulcher in Silverpine Forest, Apothecary Renferrel compiles these findings to document his progress and experiments, sending the gathered intelligence south to Tarren Mill so fellow researchers can build upon his results.",sp=0},{t="To Tarren Mill",b="Carrying these papers across the border from Silverpine into the Hillsbrad Foothills represents a vital link in the Forsaken's alchemical network. In Tarren Mill, Apothecary Lydon eagerly awaits Renferrel's notes to cross-reference and advance his own concoctions against the living and the Scourge. Without reliable couriers running the contested roads of Hillsbrad, the Society's decentralized research would quickly stall.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is inside Renferrel's Findings?",a="The package contains the latest experimental data and research notes collected by Apothecary Renferrel during his work in Silverpine Forest, specifically relating to the synthesis of a New Plague for the Forsaken.",al={"what are the findings","renferrel research","what is in the notes"},it="item"},{q="Who is supposed to receive this research?",a="Apothecary Lydon receives the documents. He conducts plague research in Tarren Mill, a Forsaken settlement situated in the Hillsbrad Foothills.",al={"who gets renferrels findings","where do the findings go","delivery target"},it="target"},{q="Why are the apothecaries sharing notes?",a="Lady Sylvanas Windrunner has placed immense pressure on the Royal Apothecary Society to invent a New Plague. The apothecaries believe their breakthrough will arrive far more quickly if they coordinate and compare results rather than working in isolation.",al={"why share findings","why send to lydon","apothecary communication"},it="purpose"},{q="Where does Apothecary Renferrel conduct his experiments?",a="Apothecary Renferrel is stationed at the Sepulcher, the primary Forsaken outpost located in the heart of Silverpine Forest.",al={"where is renferrel","apothecary renferrel location","who wrote renferrels findings"},it="place"},{q="What are Renferrel's Findings?",a="Renferrel's Findings are a collection of alchemical notes and research documents compiled by Apothecary Renferrel. They detail his ongoing experiments conducted on behalf of the Royal Apothecary Society, intended to be shared directly with his fellow practitioners across Lordaeron.",al={"what is renferrels findings","renferrel findings item","what are these findings"},it="identity",add=true},{q="Where do Renferrel's Findings come from, and who made them?",a="These documents were authored by Apothecary Renferrel, an ambitious researcher stationed at the Sepulcher in Silverpine Forest. Working diligently under the mandate of the Forsaken, he penned these notes to record his progress and breakthroughs in compounding experimental concoctions.",al={"who wrote renferrels findings","where did renferrels findings come from","renferrels findings creator"},it="origin",add=true},{q="Why does anyone want Renferrel's Findings?",a="The Royal Apothecary Society faces immense pressure from Lady Sylvanas Windrunner to concoct a New Plague. Believing that collaboration will accelerate their grim work, Renferrel sent his research to Apothecary Lydon in Tarren Mill, who is eager to study his colleague's methods and integrate them into his own efforts.",al={"why deliver renferrels findings","who wants renferrels findings","why does lydon want renferrels findings"},it="why_wanted",add=true}},ang={["race:Undead"]="The research inside these documents serves Sylvanas Windrunner's ultimate ambition: perfecting a New Plague to eradicate both the Scourge and the living foes encroaching upon Forsaken lands.",["faction:Horde"]="Couriers transporting Renferrel's papers help solidify the Horde's foothold across Lordaeron, connecting isolated outposts like the Sepulcher and Tarren Mill."},kw={"findings","lydon","new plague","renferrel","royal apothecary society","sepulcher","tarren mill"},rel={"quest:493","npc:apothecary-renferrel","topic:royal-apothecary-society","subzone:tarren-mill","zone:hillsbrad","quest:367"},src={"Renferrel's Findings","Journey to Hillsbrad Foothills"}}
E["item:sack-of-murloc-heads"] = {t="item",n="Sack of Murloc Heads",z="hillsbrad",s="The Sack of Murloc Heads is a gruesome bundle collected along the beaches of the Hillsbrad Foothills. Assembled as proof of military action against local shore pests, it is pawned off by Lieutenant Farren Orinelle onto passing adventurers for delivery to Marshal Redpath in Southshore.",h="The Sack of Murloc Heads is a gruesome bundle collected along the beaches of the Hillsbrad Foothills.",sec={{t="Bureaucracy and Coastal Pests",b="Southshore stands under constant siege from Syndicate outlaws, Forsaken skirmishers, and wild murlocs crowding the coast. To secure funding and favor from town leadership, local officers must demonstrate that coastal threats are actively being culled. Lieutenant Farren Orinelle gathers proof in the form of severed heads, but the distasteful nature of the cargo—and his own squeamishness—prompts him to hand the dripping sack off to travelers rather than deliver the grisly evidence to Marshal Redpath himself.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is the Sack of Murloc Heads?",a="It is a burlap sack filled with severed murloc heads gathered from the western beaches of Hillsbrad. It serves as physical proof of coastal pacification for Southshore's garrison commander.",al={"sack of heads","murloc sack","what is this item"},it="identity"},{q="Why won't Lieutenant Farren deliver it himself?",a="Farren finds carrying a foul-smelling bag of decaying fish-beast heads revolting. Preferring to keep his uniform and hands clean, he delegates the unpleasant chore across Southshore to an obliging adventurer.",al={"why farren makes you carry it","farren's excuse","lazy farren"},it="motive"},{q="Who receives the sack?",a="The delivery is made to Marshal Redpath, the commander overseeing the defenses of Southshore, who assesses the town's security and demands hard proof of defensive efforts.",al={"who gets the heads","where do i bring it","marshal redpath turn in"},it="target"},{q="Why does Southshore require murloc heads as proof?",a="Murlocs constantly raid the coastlines and threaten the harbor. Officers are expected to verify that patrols are maintaining perimeter security, and tangible trophies ensure no soldier is simply taking credit for idle watches.",al={"why collect murloc heads","proof of kill"},it="why_wanted"},{q="Where does the Sack of Murloc Heads come from, and who made it?",a="The sack is assembled from the severed heads of the murlocs you hunted along the southern coast of the Hillsbrad Foothills. Lieutenant Farren Orinelle packed them together to present to his commanding officer, though he quickly hands the repulsive parcel back to you to deliver in his stead.",al={"who made sack of murloc heads","where did the sack of heads come from","who gave sack of murloc heads"},it="origin",add=true}},ang={["faction:Alliance"]="The delivery illustrates the frayed logistics and unglamorous day-to-day burdens carried by Southshore's defenders as they hold the northern Alliance enclave together."},kw={"bounty","farren orinelle","heads","hillsbrad","marshal redpath","murloc","southshore"},rel={"quest:559","subzone:southshore","npc:lieutenant-farren-orinelle","item:murloc-head","topic:murloc","quest:536","zone:hillsbrad"},src={"Sack of Murloc Heads","Farren's Proof (2)"}}
E["item:shipment-of-iron"] = {t="item",n="Shipment of Iron",z="hillsbrad",s="A crate of raw metal stored at the human smithy in Hillsbrad Fields. It serves as vital stock for local armament production, making it a priority target for Forsaken forces seeking to choke off Southshore's supply lines.",h="A crate of raw metal stored at the human smithy in Hillsbrad Fields.",sec={{t="Fueling the Resistance",b="In the ongoing struggle across the Hillsbrad Foothills, the human peasantry has mounted surprisingly stiff resistance against Tarren Mill. Much of this fighting capability stems directly from the smithy at the southwestern edge of the Hillsbrad Fields, where Blacksmith Verringtan and his apprentices work round the clock churning out weapons and armor from heavy shipments of iron. To break the farmers' resolve, Forsaken commanders ordered the forge extinguished, its smiths eliminated, and its stockpiled metal seized for the Horde war effort.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Where is the shipment of iron kept?",a="The shipment sits directly inside the blacksmith workshop located on the southwestern fringe of the Hillsbrad Fields, heavily guarded by Blacksmith Verringtan and his apprentices.",al={"shipment of iron location","where is the iron","hillsbrad iron location"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Why does the Forsaken want this iron?",a="Seizing the iron cuts off the weapon supply line arming local human militia. High Executor Darthalia also intends to repurpose the metal stockpiles to support the Horde war machine once the offensive turns toward razing Southshore.",al={"why steal iron","tarren mill iron","battle of hillsbrad iron purpose"},it="why_wanted"},{q="Who was using this iron originally?",a="Blacksmith Verringtan and his four apprentice smiths used the iron to outfit the townspeople and field workers, transforming simple farmers into an armed local defense force against the undead.",al={"who owns the iron","verringtan iron","hillsbrad blacksmiths"},it="origin"},{q="Who orders the retrieval of the iron shipment?",a="High Executor Darthalia, commanding the Forsaken operations out of Tarren Mill, issues the direct order to slay the smiths and claim the iron during the Battle of Hillsbrad.",al={"who gives the quest","darthalia iron quest"},it="in_charge"},{q="What is the Shipment of Iron?",a="The Shipment of Iron is a stockpile of raw metal stored at the human blacksmith shop in the Hillsbrad Fields. It serves as the primary material Blacksmith Verringtan and his apprentices use to forge weapons and armor for the local Hillsbrad townsfolk resisting the Forsaken.",al={"what is shipment of iron","shipment of iron","iron shipment hillsbrad"},it="identity",add=true}},ang={["profession:Blacksmithing"]="The stockpile represents the lifeblood of human arms production in the valley; without raw iron ingots, Verringtan's forge sits completely useless.",["faction:Horde"]="Denying supplies to Hillsbrad cripples the armed resistance of the farmers before the campaign moves against Southshore."},kw={"battle of hillsbrad","darthalia","hillsbrad fields","shipment of iron","tarren mill","verringtan"},rel={"quest:527","subzone:hillsbrad-fields","subzone:tarren-mill","subzone:southshore","zone:hillsbrad","topic:human"},src={"Shipment of Iron","Battle of Hillsbrad (3)"}}
E["item:shipment-of-rare-crystals"] = {t="item",n="Shipment of Rare Crystals",z="hillsbrad",s="The Shipment of Rare Crystals is a contested mineral haul excavated from the Azurelode Mine in Hillsbrad Foothills. Packed alongside ordinary stone shipments, these unique geological specimens were seized by Forsaken raiders before they could reach Southshore scholars.",h="The Shipment of Rare Crystals is a contested mineral haul excavated from the Azurelode Mine in Hillsbrad...",sec={{t="A Plundered Geological Prize",b="While carts rolling south from the Azurelode Mine typically carry simple building stone, one routine delivery held a crate of singular, unstudied crystals. The shipment never reached its destination in Southshore; Forsaken marauders intercepted the transport cart and hauled its contents northeast toward a ruined tower they are attempting to rebuild. According to the mine foreman, the seized crate held the only known specimens of these crystals uncovered in the mine, making their recovery a matter of urgent academic and regional interest.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Where did these crystals come from?",a="They were unearthed during excavations at the Azurelode Mine, a quarry situated in the Hillsbrad Foothills. The mine foreman noted that the crate contained the only known samples ever found there.",al={"crystal origin","where were crystals mined","azurelode crystals"},it="origin"},{q="Who stole the shipment of crystals?",a="Forsaken raiders intercepted the transport cart carrying the stone and rare minerals. They hauled the stolen cargo northeast toward a stone tower they are attempting to reconstruct.",al={"who took the crystals","forsaken raiders crystals","who intercepted the cart"},it="threat"},{q="Who wants the crystals recovered?",a="Huraan, a scholar residing in the Alliance settlement of Southshore, sought out the crystals for study and enlisted travelers to wrest them back from the Forsaken.",al={"who needs the crystals","huraan crystals","southshore scholar"},it="for_you"},{q="Why are these crystals considered rare?",a="Unlike the standard building stone commonly hauled out of Azurelode Mine, these crystalline formations are extremely uncommon. The mine foreman reported that if this batch had been lost, no replacement specimens might ever be found.",al={"why are crystals special","rare crystal importance"},it="power"},{q="What is the Shipment of Rare Crystals?",a="It is a crate containing unique mineral specimens unearthed from the Azurelode Mine in the Hillsbrad Foothills. Unlike ordinary cartloads of building stone, this particular shipment carried unprecedented crystalline samples that caught the immediate scientific curiosity of scholars in Southshore before Forsaken raiders hijacked the transport.",al={"what are the rare crystals","shipment of rare crystals","crystals shipment"},it="identity",add=true},{q="Why does anyone want the Shipment of Rare Crystals?",a="Scholars like Huraan in Southshore are eager to study the samples, as they appear to be the only known specimens of their kind ever discovered in Azurelode Mine. Meanwhile, Forsaken forces intercepted the shipment and hauled it toward a ruined tower they are rebuilding, keen to deny Southshore resources and secure valuable regional finds for themselves.",al={"why want rare crystals","who needs the crystals","why are crystals wanted"},it="why_wanted",add=true}},ang={["faction:Alliance"]="Every intercepted supply cart deepens the strain on Southshore, making the recovery of Azurelode's rare findings a matter of defiance against Forsaken expansion in Hillsbrad.",["profession:Mining"]="Miners familiar with the Azurelode quarry know it mainly produces basic stone, making a sudden vein of unique, irreplaceable crystal samples an extraordinary geological curiosity."},kw={"azurelode mine","hillsbrad foothills","huraan","shipment of rare crystals","southshore","unopened crate"},rel={"npc:huraan","subzone:azurelode-mine","subzone:southshore","zone:hillsbrad","topic:forsaken","topic:light"},src={"Shipment of Rare Crystals","Missing Crystals"}}
E["item:stormpike-banner"] = {t="item",n="Stormpike Banner",z="hillsbrad",s="The Stormpike Banner is a military standard hidden deep within the treacherous Icewing Cavern in Alterac Valley. Alliance recruits must brave wild harpies to recover it as an initiation trial, proving they are worthy to wear the Stormpike insignia.",h="The Stormpike Banner is a military standard hidden deep within the treacherous Icewing Cavern in Alterac...",sec={{t="A Rite of Induction",b="To officially join the ranks of the Stormpike expedition in Alterac Valley, prospective recruits must prove their mettle before they ever clash with the Frostwolf orcs. Lieutenant Haggerdin sends newly arrived Alliance soldiers into the Icewing Caverns, situated southwest of Dun Baldar. Planted deep inside this frozen subterranean den, the Stormpike Banner serves as a testing ground: anyone brave enough to brave the native harpies, seize the standard, and bring it back alive earns the rank and insignia of an initiate in the Stormpike Guard.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Where is the Stormpike Banner located?",a="The banner is planted deep inside the Icewing Caverns, a frost-choked cave system situated southwest of Dun Baldar within Alterac Valley.",al={"banner location","where is the stormpike banner","how to find banner"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Why do recruits have to retrieve the banner?",a="Lieutenant Haggerdin requires all Alliance recruits to demonstrate their courage before joining the battle lines. Bringing back the banner from the dangerous, harpy-infested cavern earns the recruit their initial Stormpike Insignia.",al={"proving grounds trial","why get banner","haggerdin quest"},it="why_wanted"},{q="What threats guard the banner inside the cave?",a="The Icewing Caverns are fiercely defended by savage local harpies who will viciously attack any trespassers seeking the standard.",al={"monsters near banner","icewing cavern enemies"},it="threat",gp=true},{q="Who do I return the banner to once found?",a="Deliver the recovered banner to Lieutenant Haggerdin, the Alliance officer stationed outside the entrance in the Alterac Mountains.",al={"turn in banner","banner hand in"},it="next_step",gp=true},{q="What is the Stormpike Banner?",a="The Stormpike Banner is a military standard representing the Stormpike Guard, the dwarven expedition currently waging war across Alterac Valley. Planted deep inside the perilous, harpy-infested Icewing Caverns southwest of Dun Baldar, the banner serves as a trial marker. Recruits must venture into the frozen depths, brave the feral beasts lurking within, and recover the colors to prove their mettle and worthiness to wear the Stormpike insignia.",al={"what is stormpike banner","stormpike banner lore","about stormpike banner"},it="identity",add=true}},ang={["faction:Alliance"]="Retrieving the banner marks your formal entrance into the Stormpike Guard, earning you the right to carry their battle insignia against the Frostwolf Clan.",["race:Dwarf"]="The banner represents Ironforge's sovereign claim and the Stormpike clan's sacred mission to uncover titan relics throughout the valley."},kw={"alterac valley","dun baldar","haggerdin","icewing caverns","insignia","proving grounds","stormpike banner"},rel={"quest:7161","npc:lieutenant-haggerdin","zone:alterac","topic:alliance","zone:hillsbrad"},src={"Stormpike Banner","Proving Grounds (Alterac Valley) (Alliance)"}}
E["item:tainted-keg"] = {t="item",n="Tainted Keg",z="hillsbrad",s="The Tainted Keg is a barrel of stolen dwarven stout laced with a lethal Forsaken brew concocted by Apothecary Lydon. Delivered under the guise of refreshments to imprisoned human farmers in Tarren Mill, it serves as a gruesome field test for the Royal Apothecary Society's developing poisons.",h="The Tainted Keg is a barrel of stolen dwarven stout laced with a lethal Forsaken brew concocted by Apothecary...",sec={{t="A Deadly Vintage",b="The keg began its existence as a barrel of Shindigger Stout, plundered from the dwarven riflemen entrenched at Dun Garok. Rather than drinking it, Apothecary Lydon contaminated the hearty ale with his newly refined Elixir of Agony. By lacing an ordinary beverage, the Forsaken crafted an insidious vector designed to slip past suspicion, turning a familiar comforts of the living into a swift death sentence.",sp=0},{t="Testing on the Condemned",b="Held upstairs in the Tarren Mill inn, several human farmers were captured after High Executor Darthalia suspected a Stormwind military strategist had hidden among them. When word arrived that the strategist had perished elsewhere, the captive laborers became expendable. Darthalia handed them over to Lydon, who staged a cruel celebration by having the poisoned keg placed on the rug in their holding room. Parched and desperate, the prisoners drank freely, proving the elixir's immediate, fatal potency.",sp=1}},faq={{q="What is inside the Tainted Keg?",a="It contains Shindigger Stout—a rich dwarven ale stolen from Dun Garok—mixed with the Elixir of Agony, an experimental toxin created by Apothecary Lydon in Tarren Mill.",al={"tainted keg contents","what poison is in the keg","what is in the barrel"},it="item"},{q="Where did the ale originally come from?",a="The base brew was taken from the dwarven mountaineers and riflemen occupying Dun Garok, a heavily defended dwarven fortress situated in southeastern Hillsbrad Foothills.",al={"who made the ale","where was the stout stolen from","shindigger stout source"},it="origin"},{q="Who drinks from the keg?",a="A group of human farmers held hostage in the upstairs room of the Tarren Mill inn drink from the barrel, collapsing and dying almost instantly from the tainted brew.",al={"who drinks it","tainted keg victims","captured farmers"},sp=1,it="target"},{q="Why were the farmers being held prisoner?",a="High Executor Darthalia arrested them under suspicion that an Alliance military strategist from Stormwind was hiding in their ranks. Once that strategist was confirmed dead in the Plaguelands, the captive farmers were deemed useless and handed to the apothecaries.",al={"why captive farmers","why did darthalia capture farmers","why are farmers in tarren mill"},it="motive"},{q="What is the Tainted Keg?",a="The Tainted Keg is a vessel of stolen dwarven Shindigger Stout that has been laced with a deadly concoction brewed by the Forsaken. Apothecary Lydon created this lethal batch of tainted brew to serve as a practical trial for his ongoing alchemical research.",al={"what is tainted keg","tainted keg item","what is this keg"},it="identity",add=true,nx={6}},{q="Why does Apothecary Lydon want the Tainted Keg used?",a="Apothecary Lydon wants the keg delivered to test the efficacy of his newly finished Elixir of Agony. With the captured human farmers handed over to his disposal by High Executor Darthalia, offering them poisoned stout provides the Royal Apothecary Society a convenient means to observe the toxin's fatal effects firsthand.",al={"why use the tainted keg","why does lydon want tainted keg","purpose of tainted keg"},it="why_wanted",add=true}},ang={["race:Undead"]="For the Royal Apothecary Society, the tainted stout is a practical milestone in engineering biological weapons capable of eradicating humanity.",["race:Human"]="The slaughter of captured rural laborers by laced ale shows the harrowing, merciless tactics facing the living remnants throughout Hillsbrad."},kw={"apothecary lydon","captured farmers","dun garok","elixir of agony","shindigger stout","tainted keg","tarren mill"},rel={"quest:509","item:keg-of-shindigger-stout","subzone:dun-garok","npc:high-executor-darthalia","zone:hillsbrad","topic:stormwind-kingdom","topic:horde","topic:human"},src={"Tainted Keg","Elixir of Agony (5)"}}
E["item:worn-stone-token"] = {t="item",n="Worn Stone Token",z="hillsbrad",s="Worn Stone Tokens are small magical talismans carried by personnel and mages associated with Dalaran in the Alterac Mountains. Though their ambient magic has largely faded, they were crafted to help the Kirin Tor bind and command elemental servants.",h="Worn Stone Tokens are small magical talismans carried by personnel and mages associated with Dalaran in the...",sec={{t="Tokens of Elemental Mastery",b="The magi of Dalaran have long possessed a formidable command over elemental entities, using specialized talismans to bend these extradimensional beings to their will. Worn Stone Tokens represent depleted or exhausted versions of these implements. Carried not only by theurgists and summoners but even by Dalaran laborers and guards stationed around the ruins and internment camps of Alterac, they demonstrate how deeply elemental binding is integrated into Dalaran's everyday operations.",sp=0},{t="Forsaken Curiosity",b="From their outpost in Tarren Mill, the Forsaken keep a watchful eye on the nearby wizards. Magus Voidglare sought specimens of these tokens to decipher Dalaran's methods of elemental enslavement. Keeper Bel'varil directs agents to collect worn, inert tokens first, allowing the Magus to safely analyze the foundational enchanting techniques before experimenting with more potent, volatile conduits.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What were these tokens used for?",a="Dalaran's wizards use these magical stone tokens to command and bind elementals summoned from other realms to serve as laborers, guards, and defenders.",al={"worn stone token purpose","what are stone tokens","why do dalaran carry tokens"},it="purpose"},{q="Why are the tokens described as worn?",a="Their active enchantments have faded over time and heavy use. Keeper Bel'varil considers these inert specimens safer for Magus Voidglare's initial research into Dalaran's binding rituals.",al={"why worn","are tokens magical","inert tokens"}},{q="Who carries these tokens?",a="They are found on various Dalaran personnel operating in the southern Alterac Mountains, ranging from high-ranking summoners and theurgists to ordinary laborers, shield guards, and Warden Belamoore at the internment camp.",al={"who drops worn stone tokens","where to get tokens","dalaran token drops"},it="residents"},{q="Why does the Forsaken want them?",a="Magus Voidglare wishes to study Dalaran's arcane techniques for controlling elementals, seeking to unravel the secrets behind their summoning and subjugation arts.",al={"why does belvaril want tokens","magus voidglare tokens"},it="why_wanted"},{q="What is a Worn Stone Token?",a="A Worn Stone Token is a faded magical artifact crafted by the mages of Dalaran. These enchanted stones serve as arcane implements used to bind, command, and control elemental servants summoned from other dimensions. Over time or through extensive handling, their innate magic has dulled into an inert state, yet they still retain the structural secrets of Dalaran's elemental craft.",al={"what is worn stone token","worn stone token","stone tokens"},it="identity",add=true},{q="Where do the Worn Stone Tokens come from, and who made them?",a="The tokens are created by the wizards and artificers of Dalaran, a magocracy renowned for its mastery over extradimensional magic. You will find them carried by Dalaran's forces stationed across the Alterac Mountains, including summoners, theurgists, shield guards, workers, and Warden Belamoore at the nearby internment camps.",al={"who made worn stone token","origin of stone tokens","where do stone tokens come from"},it="origin",add=true}},ang={["class:Mage"]="Mages recognize these tokens as the practical focus items the Kirin Tor uses to keep conjured elementals stable and obedient in the field.",["faction:Horde"]="Securing these tokens aids the Forsaken at Tarren Mill in studying the arcane defenses and practices of the hostile Kirin Tor presence in Alterac."},kw={"alterac mountains","dalaran","elementals","keeper bel'varil","magus voidglare","stone tokens","tarren mill","worn stone token"},rel={"quest:556","npc:keeper-bel-varil","subzone:dalaran","zone:alterac","subzone:tarren-mill","zone:hillsbrad"},src={"Worn Stone Token","Stone Tokens"}}
E["npc:chef-jessen"] = {t="npc",n="Chef Jessen",z="hillsbrad",s="Chef Jessen is Southshore's resident meat vendor and culinarian, working to keep the coastal town fed amidst constant border tensions. Known for his short temper regarding noise while preparing meals, he is best remembered for his famous turtle bisque.",h="Chef Jessen is Southshore's resident meat vendor and culinarian, working to keep the coastal town fed amidst...",sec={{t="A Cook in Southshore",b="Operating out of Southshore in the southern Hillsbrad Foothills, Chef Jessen provides provisions and meat to locals and visiting Alliance soldiers alike. Though he grumbles about disturbances while trying to work, he possesses notable culinary expertise. Years past, before plague and war disrupted northern Lordaeron, he regularly ventured north past Dalaran to the shores of Lordamere Lake. There, he harvested meat from native snapjaw turtles to concoct his prized Soothing Turtle Bisque, a hearty recipe he is willing to share with aspiring travelers who assist him in gathering ingredients.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Chef Jessen?",a="Chef Jessen is a human butcher and cook located in Southshore within the Hillsbrad Foothills. He sells meats and shares local culinary recipes with travelers supporting the Alliance.",al={"jessen","chef jessen southshore","who is jessen"},it="identity"},{q="What is Chef Jessen's famous dish?",a="His signature recipe is Soothing Turtle Bisque. Historically, he harvested fresh turtle meat from the snapjaws dwelling around Lordamere Lake, just north past Dalaran, to craft the hearty broth.",al={"turtle bisque recipe","jessen specialty","soothing turtle bisque"},it="fame"},{q="Why does Chef Jessen ask travelers for help?",a="Gathering snapjaw turtle meat around Lordamere Lake has grown dangerous due to regional instability and nearby Forsaken presence. Jessen relies on capable adventurers to collect turtle meat so he can prepare his bisque.",al={"jessen quest","turtle meat quest"},it="wants"},{q="Does Chef Jessen sell anything unusual?",a="Aside from standard roasted fowl, Jessen has been known to concoct his own 'Special Slop,' alongside training others in the regional preparation of turtle bisque.",al={"jessens special slop","jessen food vendor"},gp=true},{q="Whose side is Chef Jessen on?",a="Chef Jessen is loyal to the Alliance. He lives and works in Southshore, the primary human refuge and Alliance stronghold along the southern coast of the Hillsbrad Foothills, catering to locals and travelers fighting to hold the line in Lordaeron.",al={"chef jessen alliance or horde","is chef jessen alliance","chef jessen faction"},it="side",add=true},{q="Why is Chef Jessen in Southshore?",a="Chef Jessen operates as a local meat vendor and cook in Southshore. While he once traveled up past Dalaran and out to Lordamere Lake to hunt snapjaws himself, these days he stays safely behind in the town, relying on adventurous passersby to bring in fresh ingredients.",al={"why is chef jessen in southshore","chef jessen why here","what brought chef jessen to hillsbrad"},it="why_here",add=true}},ang={["profession:Cooking"]="Jessen is a valuable contact for cooks passing through Hillsbrad, as his turtle bisque recipe provides a substantial meal for hardy travelers.",["faction:Alliance"]="Operating in Southshore, Jessen helps sustain the Alliance soldiers and adventurers holding the defensive line against northern threats."},kw={"chef jessen","cooking","hillsbrad foothills","jessen","lordamere lake","snapjaw","southshore","turtle bisque"},rel={"subzone:southshore","quest:555","zone:hillsbrad","subzone:lordamere-lake","subzone:dalaran","topic:alliance"},src={"Chef Jessen"}}
E["npc:christoph-jeffcoat"] = {t="npc",n="Christoph Jeffcoat",z="hillsbrad",s="Christoph Jeffcoat is a Forsaken merchant stationed in the settlement of Tarren Mill within the Hillsbrad Foothills. He supplies local crafters and travelers with essential trade goods, cooking seasonings, and specialty recipes. In an active war zone contested by the Alliance and the Syndicate, his mundane wares keep the northern Horde war effort running.",h="Christoph Jeffcoat is a Forsaken merchant stationed in the settlement of Tarren Mill within the Hillsbrad...",sec={{t="A Merchant on the Front Lines",b="While Tarren Mill stands as the Forsaken's military stronghold in Hillsbrad Foothills, a garrison cannot fight on malice alone. Christoph Jeffcoat handles the quiet, practical side of occupation, vending reagents, tools, threads, and spices to soldiers and traveling artisans. From the soothing spices required for local culinary recipes like turtle bisque to rare schematics and alchemical vials, Jeffcoat ensures that Horde forces passing through southern Lordaeron are fully provisioned for the battles against Southshore and the regional perils.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Where can I find Christoph Jeffcoat?",a="Christoph Jeffcoat resides in Tarren Mill, the primary Forsaken and Horde stronghold located in central Hillsbrad Foothills.",al={"christoph jeffcoat location","where is jeffcoat","tarren mill trade vendor"},it="place",gp=true},{q="What kinds of goods does he sell?",a="He is a trade supplies merchant stocking tailoring threads, blacksmithing hammers, fluxes, vials for alchemy, and culinary spices such as soothing spices and hot spices, alongside select specialty recipes.",al={"what does jeffcoat sell","christoph jeffcoat wares","jeffcoat items"},it="purpose",gp=true},{q="Why is he important for local cooks?",a="Jeffcoat sells Soothing Spices, an ingredient in Soothing Turtle Bisque, and he teaches Horde cooks the bisque himself once they bring him turtle meat from the snapjaws.",al={"soothing spices vendor hillsbrad","soothing turtle bisque ingredients","jeffcoat cooking"},gp=true},{q="Who is Christoph Jeffcoat?",a="Christoph Jeffcoat is an undead merchant stationed at Tarren Mill in the Hillsbrad Foothills. He serves the Forsaken by providing trade supplies, raw materials, and crafting components to travelers, artisans, and defenders holding the Horde's front lines in the region.",al={"who is christoph jeffcoat","christoph jeffcoat identity","who is jeffcoat"},it="identity",add=true},{q="Whose side is Christoph Jeffcoat on?",a="Christoph Jeffcoat is firmly loyal to the Forsaken and the Horde. Stationed inside the heavily contested outpost of Tarren Mill, he caters directly to Horde adventurers and champions battling the nearby Alliance forces from Southshore.",al={"christoph jeffcoat faction","is christoph jeffcoat horde","who does christoph jeffcoat serve"},it="side",add=true},{q="Why is Christoph Jeffcoat here in Tarren Mill?",a="With Tarren Mill acting as the northern anchor for Horde operations in Hillsbrad Foothills, crafters and fighters constantly run low on everyday supplies. Christoph Jeffcoat is stationed here to ensure trade goods, vials, threads, and spices remain readily available to those defending the post.",al={"why is christoph in tarren mill","christoph jeffcoat why here","why is jeffcoat in hillsbrad"},it="why_here",add=true}},ang={["profession:Cooking"]="Christoph Jeffcoat is an essential stop for aspiring chefs in Hillsbrad, as he stocks the Soothing Spices required to complete Chef Jessen's recipe for Soothing Turtle Bisque.",["faction:Horde"]="For Horde champions campaigning in Hillsbrad Foothills, Jeffcoat provides indispensable crafting materials and common tools right in the heart of Tarren Mill."},kw={"christoph jeffcoat","forsaken merchant","hillsbrad","soothing spices","tarren mill","trade supplies","trade vendor"},rel={"subzone:tarren-mill","zone:hillsbrad","quest:555","topic:forsaken","topic:horde"},src={"Christoph Jeffcoat"}}
E["npc:deathguard-humbert"] = {t="npc",n="Deathguard Humbert",z="hillsbrad",s="Deathguard Humbert is a Forsaken sentry stationed in Tarren Mill within the Hillsbrad Foothills. Assigned to monitor the encroaching Alliance presence, he finds himself in an embarrassing predicament after losing his military gear to the dwarves of Dun Garok.",h="Deathguard Humbert is a Forsaken sentry stationed in Tarren Mill within the Hillsbrad Foothills.",sec={{t="A Guard Relieved of His Steel",b="While tasked with maintaining Tarren Mill's perimeter against regional threats, Deathguard Humbert suffered a humiliating setback at the hands of the Dun Garok mountaineers. The dwarves garrisoning Dun Garok stripped Humbert of his prized sword and assorted equipment, leaving the undead soldier desperate to salvage his pride and armament before high command takes notice.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Deathguard Humbert?",a="Deathguard Humbert is a Forsaken warrior stationed as a scout and guard in Tarren Mill. His duties involve keeping an eye on hostile Alliance operations throughout the Hillsbrad Foothills.",al={"humbert lore","who is humbert","humbert tarren mill"},it="identity"},{q="What happened to Humbert's sword and armor?",a="While scouting the southern foothills, Humbert crossed paths with the dwarves stationed in the fortress of Dun Garok. The dwarves overpowered him and made off with his personal arms and armor, including his trusty blade.",al={"humberts sword stolen","who took humberts gear","why does humbert need help"}},{q="Why doesn't Humbert just recover his gear himself?",a="Dun Garok is heavily fortified with disciplined dwarven riflemen and mountaineers. A lone scout standing outside its trenches stands little chance, and Humbert cannot easily leave his post without answering for how he lost his kit in the first place.",al={"why cant humbert fight","humbert dun garok"},it="motive"},{q="Whose side is Deathguard Humbert on?",a="Deathguard Humbert serves the Forsaken and, by extension, the Horde. As a member of the Deathguard, he stands as a sentry and soldier sworn to the defense of Lordaeron and the will of the Banshee Queen, Lady Sylvanas Windrunner.",al={"deathguard humbert faction","humbert allegiance","who does humbert serve"},it="side",add=true},{q="What does Deathguard Humbert want?",a="Humbert wants the return of his personal military equipment, particularly his sword and armor pieces. They were stripped from him by the Stormpike dwarves entrenched nearby, leaving him empty-handed and desperate for someone capable to venture into enemy territory and reclaim them.",al={"humbert goal","what does humbert need","why does humbert give quests"},it="wants",add=true},{q="Why is Deathguard Humbert stationed here?",a="Humbert is stationed at Tarren Mill to monitor the hostile Alliance presence in the Hillsbrad Foothills, specifically keeping an eye on the dwarven forces holed up at Dun Garok. His post ensures the Forsaken settlement remains alerted to movements from the south.",al={"why is humbert in tarren mill","humbert mission","what is humbert doing here"},it="why_here",add=true}},ang={["faction:Horde"]="Recovering Humbert's lost sword strikes back against the bold dwarven foothold in Hillsbrad while preserving the dignity of Tarren Mill's garrison.",["race:Undead"]="Forsaken soldiers are expected to serve the Dark Lady with unyielding vigilance, making Humbert's lapse of attention against the living an embarrassing blemish on the Deathguard."},kw={"deathguard humbert","dun garok","hillsbrad foothills","humbert","humbert's sword","stormpike","tarren mill"},rel={"subzone:tarren-mill","quest:547","subzone:dun-garok","zone:hillsbrad","topic:forsaken","topic:horde"},src={"Deathguard Humbert"}}
E["npc:deathguard-samsa"] = {t="npc",n="Deathguard Samsa",z="hillsbrad",s="Deathguard Samsa is a Forsaken sentry stationed in Tarren Mill within the Hillsbrad Foothills. Tasked with maintaining Horde vigilance on a tense frontier, he directs traveling champions to strike at local threats encroaching on the settlement.",h="Deathguard Samsa is a Forsaken sentry stationed in Tarren Mill within the Hillsbrad Foothills.",sec={{t="Frontier Sentry of Tarren Mill",b="Standing watch in Tarren Mill, Deathguard Samsa represents the defensive backbone of the Forsaken in the contested Hillsbrad Foothills. Tarren Mill serves as the Horde's primary outpost in the region, facing immediate pressure from Alliance outposts like Southshore as well as savage local wildlife. Samsa's duties involve securing the perimeter and directing capable adventurers to eliminate threats before they endanger the encampment.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Deathguard Samsa?",a="Deathguard Samsa is an undead soldier serving the Forsaken military in Tarren Mill. He stands guard over the town and issues orders to visiting adventurers to help secure the region from nearby perils.",al={"samsa","who is samsa","deathguard samsa role"},it="identity"},{q="Where can I find Deathguard Samsa?",a="He is located in Tarren Mill, the major Horde settlement situated in the northern part of the Hillsbrad Foothills.",al={"samsa location","where is deathguard samsa","tarren mill guard location"},it="place",gp=true},{q="What tasks does Deathguard Samsa give out?",a="Samsa commissions adventurers to venture into the Hillsbrad wilderness, including collecting the skulls of Hillsbrad humans slain during the Horde's campaign against them.",al={"samsa quests","souvenirs of death quest giver"},it="purpose",gp=true},{q="Whose side is Deathguard Samsa on?",a="Deathguard Samsa serves the Forsaken and the Horde. As a deathguard stationed in Tarren Mill, he acts under the authority of Queen Sylvanas Windrunner, guarding Forsaken holdings in the Hillsbrad Foothills and securing the region against nearby threats.",al={"deathguard samsa faction","is samsa horde","who does samsa serve"},it="side",add=true},{q="Why is Deathguard Samsa here in Tarren Mill?",a="Deathguard Samsa is posted in Tarren Mill as part of the Forsaken military presence guarding the settlement. Tarren Mill serves as a critical northern bastion in the Hillsbrad Foothills, requiring steadfast guards to watch over the town and monitor dangerous wildlife and enemy movements in the surrounding lands.",al={"why is samsa in tarren mill","deathguard samsa purpose hillsbrad","why is deathguard samsa here"},it="why_here",add=true}},ang={["race:Undead"]="For the Forsaken, Deathguard Samsa represents the pragmatic and grim defense required to hold Lordaeron's southern border against hostile neighbors.",["faction:Horde"]="Horde travelers coming through Hillsbrad Foothills rely on sentries like Samsa to coordinate defenses against nearby Alliance aggression from Southshore."},kw={"deathguard samsa","forsaken","hillsbrad","samsa","souvenirs of death","tarren mill"},rel={"subzone:tarren-mill","zone:hillsbrad","quest:546","topic:forsaken","topic:horde","subzone:southshore"},src={"Deathguard Samsa"}}
E["npc:deathstalker-lesh"] = {t="npc",n="Deathstalker Lesh",z="hillsbrad",s="Deathstalker Lesh is a Forsaken rogue serving as a forward scout at Southpoint Tower in the Hillsbrad Foothills. Operating directly under High Executor Darthalia, she keeps watch over the human farms in the Hillsbrad Fields to gauge when the Forsaken should strike.",h="Deathstalker Lesh is a Forsaken rogue serving as a forward scout at Southpoint Tower in the Hillsbrad...",sec={{t="Eyes on the Fields",b="Perched at Southpoint Tower on the southern road through the Hillsbrad Foothills, Deathstalker Lesh monitors the human farmers and town militia working the nearby Hillsbrad Fields. As an operative of the Deathstalkers—the Forsaken's secretive intelligence and assassination network—Lesh tracks enemy movements and numbers for High Executor Darthalia in Tarren Mill. When the human defenses show weakness, Lesh coordinates targeted raids to keep the Alliance population destabilized and pave the way for Forsaken expansion southward.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Deathstalker Lesh?",a="Lesh is a Forsaken scout stationed at Southpoint Tower. She answers to High Executor Darthalia in Tarren Mill and monitors the human activity across the Hillsbrad Fields.",al={"deathstalker lesh","who is lesh","lesh hillsbrad"},it="identity"},{q="What are the Deathstalkers?",a="The Deathstalkers serve Queen Sylvanas Windrunner as scouts, spies, and assassins. They function as the covert arm of the Forsaken military, gathering intelligence and eliminating high-value targets across Lordaeron.",al={"what are deathstalkers","deathstalker order","forsaken rogues"}},{q="What is Lesh's role at Southpoint Tower?",a="She acts as a forward lookout. From Southpoint Tower, she watches the Hillsbrad Fields and directs Horde travelers to strike the human farmers and militia when opportunity arises.",al={"southpoint tower scout","lesh quest","why is lesh here"},it="why_here"},{q="Who does Lesh report to?",a="She reports to High Executor Darthalia, the Forsaken commander stationed at Tarren Mill who oversees the offensive against the human forces in Hillsbrad.",al={"lesh boss","who commands lesh","high executor darthalia"},it="ties"},{q="Whose side is Deathstalker Lesh on?",a="Deathstalker Lesh is loyal to Lady Sylvanas Windrunner and the Forsaken, operating as part of the Horde forces in Hillsbrad Foothills. As an operative stationed at Southpoint Tower under the command of Tarren Mill, she works tirelessly to secure Forsaken supremacy in the region.",al={"deathstalker lesh faction","lesh alliance or horde","who does lesh serve"},it="side",add=true},{q="What does Deathstalker Lesh want?",a="Lesh wants to cripple human resistance in the Hillsbrad Fields. Stationed as a scout on the front lines, she observes enemy movements and seeks capable adventurers to strike directly at the local human settlements, furthering the Forsaken campaign to control the foothills.",al={"what does lesh want","lesh goal","deathstalker lesh objective"},it="wants",add=true}},ang={["race:Undead"]="For the Forsaken, scouts like Lesh represent the vital frontier work of securing Lordaeron from Alliance resurgents.",["class:Rogue"]="Deathstalker Lesh demonstrates the essential military function of covert operatives within the Horde war effort."},kw={"deathstalker lesh","high executor darthalia","hillsbrad fields","hillsbrad foothills","southpoint tower","tarren mill","time to strike"},rel={"subzone:southpoint-tower","quest:494","subzone:hillsbrad-fields","npc:high-executor-darthalia","zone:hillsbrad","topic:forsaken"},src={"Deathstalker Lesh"}}
E["npc:drum-fel"] = {t="npc",n="Drum Fel",z="hillsbrad",s="Drum Fel is an orc commander stationed at the Horde outpost of Hammerfall in the Arathi Highlands. Alongside his wife, Korin, he directs military efforts to secure the refuge against encroaching trolls, ogres, and human remnants. His strategic push is vital to carving out a lasting foothold for the Horde in Arathi.",h="Drum Fel is an orc commander stationed at the Horde outpost of Hammerfall in the Arathi Highlands.",sec={{t="Warden of Hammerfall",b="Situated within the fortified refuge of Hammerfall, Drum Fel oversees the defense and territorial expansion of the Horde in Arathi. Surrounded by rival factions, he coordinates military strikes against the Witherbark forest trolls and the Boulderfist ogre clan holding Boulder'gor and Boulderfist Hall. Drum recognizes that Hammerfall cannot merely survive through isolation; it must break its neighbors' strength to thrive. To that end, he regularly directs veteran champions into hostile territory to disrupt regional threats before they can mount an assault on the Horde encampment.",sp=0},{t="The Threat in Stromgarde",b="Drum Fel's campaign extends into the ruins of Stromgarde Keep, where Boulderfist ogres have entrenched themselves amidst the fallen human kingdom. Years ago, Drum defeated the ogre brute Or'Kalar, earning an enduring grudge. Unknown to Drum, Or'Kalar waits within Stromgarde seeking vengeance. To protect her husband from falling into an ambush fueled by this rivalry, his wife Korin quietly takes measures to obscure Or'Kalar's presence, relying on outside adventurers to eliminate the threat before Drum charges in himself.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Who is Drum Fel?",a="Drum Fel is an orc leader located in Hammerfall in the Arathi Highlands. He coordinates the stronghold's military campaigns against rival factions in the region.",al={"drum fel","who is drum fel","hammerfall drum"},it="identity"},{q="Where can Drum Fel be found?",a="He is located inside the Horde settlement of Hammerfall, situated in northeastern Arathi Highlands just east of the main road heading north into the Hinterlands.",al={"drum fel location","where is drum fel","find drum fel"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Who is Korin Fel?",a="Korin Fel is Drum's wife. She also resides in Hammerfall.",al={"korin fel","drum fel wife"},it="ties"},{q="Why does the ogre Or'Kalar want Drum Fel dead?",a="Years ago, Drum Fel defeated Or'Kalar in battle. Deeply humiliated, the ogre now lurks within the ruins of Stromgarde Keep, plotting vengeance against the orc commander.",al={"orkalar grudge","why does orkalar hate drum fel","or'kalar drum fel"},it="conflict"},{q="What threats does Drum Fel target?",a="Drum Fel directs strikes against the Boulderfist ogres at Boulder'gor, Boulderfist Hall, and Stromgarde Keep, as well as the Witherbark troll tribe nearby.",al={"drum fel quests","drum fel enemies","who does drum fel fight"},it="threat"},{q="Whose side is Drum Fel on?",a="Drum Fel is a stalwart leader within the Horde. Stationed at the outpost of Hammerfall, he directs military efforts to secure the safety and dominance of the Horde across the Arathi Highlands.",al={"drum fel faction","who does drum fel serve","drum fel horde"},it="side",add=true},{q="What does Drum Fel want?",a="Drum Fel wants to ensure that Hammerfall survives and thrives amidst hostile territory. To protect the settlement, he orders decisive campaigns against rival forces threatening the region, including the Boulderfist ogres, the Witherbark trolls, and hostile occupants within the ruins of Stromgarde Keep.",al={"drum fel goals","what does drum fel need","drum fel motive"},it="wants",add=true},{q="Why is Drum Fel in Hammerfall?",a="Drum Fel oversees military operations from Hammerfall to safeguard the Horde's foothold in the Arathi Highlands. From this bastion, he coordinates the defense of his people against surrounding threats that seek to wipe the settlement out.",al={"why is drum fel here","drum fel arathi","drum fel purpose arathi"},it="why_here",add=true}},ang={["faction:Horde"]="For Horde warriors advancing through the Eastern Kingdoms, Drum Fel serves as a primary military coordinator securing the fragile lifeline between the Undercity and southern territories.",["race:Orc"]="Drum Fel embodies the practical military grit required to rebuild orcish lives in the Eastern Kingdoms, holding fast in the very land where the internment camps once stood."},kw={"arathi highlands","boulderfist","drum fel","hammerfall","korin fel","orkalar","witherbark"},rel={"subzone:hammerfall","zone:arathi","npc:tallow","subzone:stromgarde-keep","subzone:boulder-gor","subzone:boulderfist-hall","quest:676","topic:horde"},src={"Drum Fel"}}
E["npc:high-executor-darthalia"] = {t="npc",n="High Executor Darthalia",z="hillsbrad",s="High Executor Darthalia is a high-ranking Forsaken military commander stationed at Tarren Mill in the Hillsbrad Foothills. Acting under the direct authority of Lady Sylvanas Windrunner and Varimathras, she directs Forsaken operations against the human stronghold of Southshore and local Syndicate brigands. Her leadership is central to securing the Horde's southern flank in Lordaeron.",h="High Executor Darthalia is a high-ranking Forsaken military commander stationed at Tarren Mill in the...",sec={{t="Commander of Tarren Mill",b="Operating out of Tarren Mill, High Executor Darthalia serves as the operational commander for Forsaken forces throughout the Hillsbrad Foothills. Her primary strategic concern is halting the expansion of human resistance, keeping the Alliance forces in Southshore contained, and hunting down the lawless Syndicate rogues infesting the surrounding countryside. Every offensive push into southern Hillsbrad flows directly through her command.",sp=0},{t="The War for Hillsbrad",b="Under direct orders originating from the Undercity's high leadership—the Banshee Queen and her dreadlord lieutenant, Varimathras—Darthalia oversees the relentless attrition war across Hillsbrad. She coordinates scouting missions, targeted strikes against human leadership, and bounties on dangerous outlaws who threaten the Forsaken hold on northern Lordaeron.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is High Executor Darthalia?",a="High Executor Darthalia is a Forsaken military leader stationed in Hillsbrad Foothills. She is responsible for directing Horde and Forsaken military efforts against the human town of Southshore and eliminating hostile regional threats.",al={"who is darthalia","darthalia identity","executor darthalia"},it="identity"},{q="Where can Darthalia be found?",a="In classic Hillsbrad Foothills, she commands Forsaken forces from Tarren Mill, organizing troops and coordinating strikes across the central region of Lordaeron.",al={"darthalia location","where is darthalia","executor darthalia map"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Who does Darthalia answer to?",a="Darthalia operates under the direct military hierarchy of the Undercity, answering to Lady Sylvanas Windrunner and the dreadlord Varimathras as they coordinate the defense and expansion of Forsaken territory.",al={"darthalia boss","darthalia faction","who commands darthalia"},it="ties"},{q="What tasks does Darthalia give to adventurers?",a="Darthalia tasks Horde champions with striking directly against human settlements, executing dangerous outlaws, and hunting down members of the Syndicate operating throughout the Hillsbrad Foothills.",al={"darthalia quests","quests from darthalia","what does darthalia want"},it="purpose"},{q="Why is Darthalia fighting the humans of Southshore?",a="Southshore represents the primary Alliance military foothold in Lordaeron. Darthalia's mission is to suppress the human presence, protect Tarren Mill, and prevent the Alliance from pushing north toward the Undercity.",al={"why attack southshore","southshore war","hillsbrad conflict"},it="motive"},{q="What is Darthalia's rank in the Forsaken military?",a="As a High Executor, Darthalia holds one of the highest field-grade ranks within the Forsaken military hierarchy, granting her operational command over regional forces, outposts, and war strategy in the zone.",al={"high executor rank","darthalia title"}},{q="Whose side is High Executor Darthalia on?",a="High Executor Darthalia serves the Forsaken and the Horde. She operates as a high-ranking military commander under the authority of Lady Sylvanas Windrunner and Varimathras, directing Horde operations in Hillsbrad Foothills to secure the region against Alliance encroachment.",al={"darthalia faction","who does darthalia fight for","is darthalia horde"},it="side",add=true},{q="What does High Executor Darthalia want?",a="Darthalia seeks to halt the spread of humanity and root out Alliance influence across the Hillsbrad Foothills. She coordinates strikes against nearby human strongholds like Southshore and eliminates rival threats such as the Syndicate to ensure unchallenged Forsaken control over the territory.",al={"darthalia goals","what is darthalia trying to do","darthalia purpose"},it="wants",add=true},{q="Why is High Executor Darthalia here?",a="She is stationed in Tarren Mill to oversee the Forsaken campaign in the Hillsbrad Foothills. From this central vanguard, she organizes war efforts against the hostile human settlements to the south and secures the southern approaches to Tirisfal Glades and the Undercity.",al={"why is darthalia in tarren mill","darthalia hillsbrad why","reason darthalia is here"},it="why_here",add=true}},ang={["race:Undead"]="For the Forsaken, Darthalia represents the iron will of the Undercity, ensuring that Lordaeron remains firmly in the hands of the free-willed undead.",["faction:Horde"]="Horde adventurers report to Darthalia to check Alliance aggression and hold the contested frontier of Hillsbrad Foothills.",["faction:Alliance"]="To the humans of Southshore and their allies, Darthalia is the ruthless architect behind the relentless assaults threatening their last foothold in Lordaeron."},kw={"darthalia","high executor","hillsbrad","hillsbrad foothills","southshore","sylvanas","syndicate","tarren mill","varimathras"},rel={"subzone:tarren-mill","zone:hillsbrad","topic:forsaken","subzone:southshore","npc:varimathras","npc:sylvanas-windrunner","quest:494","quest:549"},src={"High Executor Darthalia"}}
E["npc:huraan"] = {t="npc",n="Huraan",z="hillsbrad",s="Huraan is a mysterious traveler staying within the tavern at Southshore in the Hillsbrad Foothills. He seeks the aid of Alliance adventurers to recover a valuable shipment of stolen crystals seized by the nearby Forsaken.",h="Huraan is a mysterious traveler staying within the tavern at Southshore in the Hillsbrad Foothills.",sec={{t="A Foreign Guest in Southshore",b="Amid the worried human townsfolk and weary soldiers stationed in Southshore, Huraan cuts an unusual figure within the town's inn. Rather than concerning himself with the regional border skirmishes or the local syndicate brigands, his focus is trained squarely on a specific cargo: a cache of precious crystals that fell into the hands of the Forsaken. Determined to recover what was taken, he turns to capable travelers willing to venture near enemy territory to reclaim the lost stones.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Where can Huraan be found?",a="Huraan stays inside the inn in Southshore, the Alliance's primary coastal port and stronghold in the Hillsbrad Foothills.",al={"huraan location","where is huraan","southshore inn npc"},it="place",gp=true},{q="What does Huraan want?",a="Huraan seeks the recovery of a shipment of crystals that was stolen by the Forsaken operating out of the Hillsbrad region.",al={"huraan quest","what does huraan need","missing crystals task"},it="wants"},{q="Who took Huraan's crystals?",a="The crystals were intercepted and stolen by the Forsaken, the undead faction based to the north in Tarren Mill and the ruins of Lordaeron.",al={"who stole the crystals","who has huraan crystals"},it="target"},{q="Who is Huraan?",a="Huraan is an enigmatic draenei visitor residing at the inn in Southshore. Draenei are an exceedingly rare sight across the Eastern Kingdoms, making his presence among the Alliance townfolk in the Hillsbrad Foothills unusual and striking.",al={"who is huraan","huraan lore","what race is huraan"},it="identity",add=true},{q="Whose side is Huraan on?",a="Huraan aligns himself with the Alliance. Taking shelter within Southshore's inn, he seeks aid from Alliance travelers to oppose the local Forsaken who have interfered with his affairs.",al={"is huraan alliance","huraan faction","who does huraan serve"},it="side",add=true},{q="Why is Huraan in Southshore?",a="Huraan has traveled to the Hillsbrad Foothills concerning a valuable shipment of crystals. Unfortunately for him, the nearby Forsaken intercepted and seized the shipment, leaving him stranded in Southshore trying to recover them.",al={"why is huraan here","why is huraan in hillsbrad","huraan purpose in southshore"},it="why_here",add=true}},ang={["faction:Alliance"]="For Alliance champions based in Southshore, aiding Huraan provides another crucial opportunity to strike back against Forsaken operations in Hillsbrad."},kw={"crystals","hillsbrad","huraan","inn","missing crystals","southshore"},rel={"subzone:southshore","zone:hillsbrad","topic:forsaken","subzone:tarren-mill"},src={"Huraan"}}
E["npc:keeper-bel-varil"] = {t="npc",n="Keeper Bel'varil",z="hillsbrad",s="Keeper Bel'varil is a Forsaken caretaker and researcher stationed at Tarren Mill in the Hillsbrad Foothills. Working closely alongside Wordeen Voidglare, he directs Horde adventurers to gather magical relics and binding materials from the surrounding lands to further their occult studies.",h="Keeper Bel'varil is a Forsaken caretaker and researcher stationed at Tarren Mill in the Hillsbrad Foothills.",sec={{t="Study in Tarren Mill",b="Amid the besieged village of Tarren Mill, Keeper Bel'varil quietly supports the Forsaken's magical and alchemical research. While royal apothecaries and soldiers occupy themselves with the Alliance garrison down the road at Southshore, Bel'varil focuses on practical sorcery, dispatching travelers to recover stone tokens and binding bracers from nearby elemental and enchanted threats.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Keeper Bel'varil?",a="Keeper Bel'varil is a Forsaken scholar stationed in Tarren Mill in the Hillsbrad Foothills. He aids fellow researcher Wordeen Voidglare in examining magical artifacts and reagents found across the contested territory.",al={"keeper belvaril","who is belvaril","belvaril tarren mill"},it="identity"},{q="Where can I find Keeper Bel'varil?",a="He can be found standing in the Forsaken settlement of Tarren Mill, situated in northern Hillsbrad Foothills.",al={"belvaril location","where is keeper bel'varil","find keeper bel'varil"},it="place",gp=true},{q="What tasks does Keeper Bel'varil offer?",a="He enlists Horde adventurers to collect magical remnants such as stone tokens and bracers of binding, helping his circle understand and manipulate elemental forces.",al={"belvaril quests","keeper bel'varil tasks"},it="purpose",gp=true},{q="Whose side is Keeper Bel'varil on?",a="Keeper Bel'varil is loyal to the Forsaken and the broader Horde. Stationed in Tarren Mill, he works alongside his undead brethren to secure the Hillsbrad Foothills against Alliance aggression and assist in the strategic research being carried out by his fellow Forsaken.",al={"bel'varil faction","is bel'varil horde","bel'varil allegiance"},it="side",add=true},{q="What does Keeper Bel'varil want?",a="Bel'varil seeks mystical components and artifacts to assist with specialized arcane research. To aid Wordeen Voidglare's work in Tarren Mill, he enlists travelers to retrieve enchanted remnants, such as stone tokens and bracers of binding, from the elementals and ruins in the surrounding regions.",al={"bel'varil goal","what does bel'varil need","why help bel'varil"},it="wants",add=true},{q="Why is Keeper Bel'varil here in Tarren Mill?",a="Keeper Bel'varil remains stationed in Tarren Mill to support the Forsaken's territorial and arcane interests in Hillsbrad Foothills. Working in concert with researchers like Wordeen Voidglare, he coordinates the gathering of magical supplies needed to bolster their hold against nearby enemies.",al={"why is bel'varil in tarren mill","bel'varil hillsbrad purpose","why is keeper bel'varil here"},it="why_here",add=true},{q="Who is Keeper Bel'varil tied to?",a="Keeper Bel'varil works closely with Wordeen Voidglare, another Forsaken scholar stationed in Tarren Mill. Bel'varil acts as an assistant and coordinator, organizing adventurers to gather the specific materials and tokens Wordeen requires for his ongoing studies.",al={"bel'varil associates","who does bel'varil work for","bel'varil connections"},it="ties",add=true}},ang={["faction:Horde"]="For Horde champions fighting in the Hillsbrad Foothills, Bel'varil offers practical rewards in exchange for subduing elemental threats and recovering binding charms.",["race:Undead"]="Bel'varil's work reflects the Forsaken pursuit of arcane mastery and resourcefulness, securing an edge in Lordaeron through careful study of regional relics."},kw={"bel'varil","bracers of binding","hillsbrad foothills","keeper bel'varil","stone tokens","tarren mill","wordeen voidglare"},rel={"subzone:tarren-mill","zone:hillsbrad","quest:556","topic:forsaken","topic:horde","subzone:southshore"},src={"Keeper Bel'varil"}}
E["npc:krusk"] = {t="npc",n="Krusk",z="hillsbrad",s="Krusk is an orc scout stationed at Tarren Mill in the Hillsbrad Foothills. Dispatched directly under Warchief Thrall's orders to investigate the Syndicate and recover relics from the ruins of Durnholde Keep, he now coordinates reconnaissance and rescue efforts after his initial infiltration was ambushed.",h="Krusk is an orc scout stationed at Tarren Mill in the Hillsbrad Foothills.",sec={{t="A Mission Gone Wrong",b="When Warchief Thrall turned his attention back to the ruins of Durnholde Keep, he dispatched Krusk and a small strike team to scout Syndicate activity and retrieve relics tied to the fortress's grim past. However, the human outlaws proved more entrenched and coordinated than anticipated. An ambush inside Durnholde's crumbling walls overwhelmed the orcish scout squad. Krusk managed to fight his way out, but his three companions—Gol'dir, Drull, and Tog'thar—were captured and locked away deep within the ruins. Regrouping at Tarren Mill, Krusk now directs Horde adventurers to breach Durnholde, recover the lost items, and liberate his trapped comrades.",sp=0},{t="Eyes on the Syndicate",b="Beyond recovering his scouts, Krusk remains fixated on dismantling the Syndicate's hold over Hillsbrad. The fallen nobles of Alterac represent a volatile threat, operating out of Durnholde Keep and scheming against both Horde outposts and their former Alliance brethren. Working from Tarren Mill, Krusk tracks the movements of Syndicate leaders, such as Lord Aliden Perenolde, hoping to sever their leadership before they can threaten the tenuous Horde foothold in Lordaeron.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Krusk?",a="Krusk is an orc scout sent to Tarren Mill by Warchief Thrall. He was tasked with investigating Syndicate operations around the ruins of Durnholde Keep and recovering historic relics.",al={"krusk","who is krusk","krusk tarren mill"},it="identity"},{q="What happened to Krusk's squad?",a="Krusk and his team were ambushed by the Syndicate inside Durnholde Keep. While Krusk escaped, his companions Gol'dir, Drull, and Tog'thar were captured and imprisoned within the ruined fortress.",al={"krusk squad","what happened to krusk","durnholde ambush"},it="conflict"},{q="Why is the Horde interested in Durnholde Keep?",a="Durnholde holds deep personal and historical significance to Warchief Thrall, who was raised as a captive gladiator there by Aedelas Blackmoore before leading the orcish rebellion that razed the keep.",al={"why durnholde","thrall durnholde","durnholde relics"},it="motive"},{q="Where can I find Krusk?",a="Krusk is stationed outdoors in the Horde settlement of Tarren Mill in northern Hillsbrad Foothills.",al={"krusk location","where is krusk"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Whose side is Krusk on?",a="Krusk is a loyal operative of the Horde. Dispatched directly under orders from Warchief Thrall, he operates out of Tarren Mill to serve Orgrimmar's strategic interests across the Hillsbrad Foothills.",al={"krusk faction","is krusk horde","who does krusk serve"},it="side",add=true},{q="What does Krusk want?",a="Krusk needs capable champions to rescue his captured companions—Gol'dir, Drull, and Tog'thar—from the Syndicate within the ruins of Durnholde Keep. He also seeks to uncover Syndicate operations and secure an item of great importance tied to Durnholde's history.",al={"what does krusk need","krusk goals","what is krusk looking for"},it="wants",add=true},{q="Why is Krusk here in Tarren Mill?",a="Warchief Thrall personally sent Krusk and his squad into Hillsbrad to investigate Syndicate activities around Durnholde Keep. After an ambush left his scouts imprisoned, Krusk fell back to Tarren Mill to regroup and recruit aid to finish the mission.",al={"why is krusk in hillsbrad","krusk tarren mill why","why did thrall send krusk"},it="why_here",add=true},{q="Who is Krusk tied to?",a="Krusk answers directly to Warchief Thrall and leads a vanguard of orc scouts consisting of Gol'dir, Drull, and Tog'thar. From Tarren Mill, he coordinates his efforts alongside the local Horde garrison.",al={"krusk companions","krusk allies","who does krusk work with"},it="ties",add=true}},ang={["faction:Horde"]="Krusk represents Warchief Thrall's direct interests in Lordaeron, focusing on securing Durnholde's history and ensuring no captured orc is left in the hands of the Syndicate.",["race:Orc"]="Helping Krusk rescue his fellow scouts touches upon the honor and painful history of the orcish internment camps, specifically the fortress where Thrall broke his people's chains."},kw={"drull","durnholde keep","gol'dir","hillsbrad","krusk","syndicate","tarren mill","thrall","tog'thar"},rel={"subzone:tarren-mill","subzone:durnholde-keep","topic:syndicate","npc:thrall","quest:498","zone:hillsbrad","topic:horde","quest:1361"},src={"Krusk"}}
E["npc:lieutenant-farren-orinelle"] = {t="npc",n="Lieutenant Farren Orinelle",z="hillsbrad",s="Lieutenant Farren Orinelle is an officer of the Stormwind army currently stationed at the Southshore inn in the Hillsbrad Foothills. Deeply unhappy with his frontier posting, he spends most of his time drinking while outsourcing his duties to passing travelers. His primary military assignment is dealing with the encroaching murlocs along the coast, a chore he eagerly delegates in hopes of securing a transfer back south.",h="Lieutenant Farren Orinelle is an officer of the Stormwind army currently stationed at the Southshore inn in...",sec={{t="Exile in Southshore",b="Lieutenant Farren Orinelle did not choose Southshore. Dispatched far from Stormwind City, the lieutenant finds the damp, contested shores of Hillsbrad a miserable step down from the civilized comforts of the capital. Instead of patrolling the fields or coordinating defenses with his commanding officer, Marshal Redpath, Orinelle has practically taken up permanent residence inside Southshore's inn. His days are spent sulking, drinking, and dreaming of an official transfer order that will return him to the south.",sp=0},{t="Outsourcing Duty",b="Despite his comfortable seat at the tavern, Orinelle still answers to Marshal Redpath, who tasked the lieutenant with clearing out the murlocs swarming the nearby shoreline. Unwilling to soil his boots in coastal mud, Orinelle relies on wandering adventurers to cull the creatures and gather proof of their demise. He hopes that presenting tangible results back to his superiors will show his duty is accomplished, hastening his eventual recall to Stormwind.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Lieutenant Farren Orinelle?",a="He is an officer of the Stormwind military stationed in Southshore, a town in the Hillsbrad Foothills. He can be found drinking inside the Southshore inn, grumbling about his posting.",al={"farren orinelle","who is orinelle","southshore lieutenant"},it="identity"},{q="Why is he in Southshore?",a="He was transferred north from Stormwind City to bolster the local garrison and support Marshal Redpath. He thoroughly dislikes the assignment and longs to return home.",al={"why is farren in southshore","orinelle transfer"},it="why_here"},{q="What is his official assignment?",a="Marshal Redpath ordered him to deal with the hostile murlocs infesting the Hillsbrad coast, though Orinelle prefers paying traveling mercenaries to do the fighting for him.",al={"farren duty","orinelle mission","farren murlocs"},it="purpose"},{q="Does he ever leave the Southshore inn?",a="No. Orinelle spends almost all of his time lingering by the inn's bar, reluctant to brave the muddy beaches or hostile elements outside.",al={"where to find farren","farren location","orinelle inn"},gp=true},{q="What is Farren's ultimate goal?",a="He wants nothing more than to secure an official reassignment back to Stormwind City, away from the dangers and bleakness of Lordaeron's coast.",al={"what does farren want","reassignment"},it="wants"},{q="Who is Orinelle's commander?",a="He reports to Marshal Redpath, who commands the Alliance military detachment defending Southshore.",al={"farren superior","farren boss","who commands farren"},it="ties"},{q="Whose side is Lieutenant Farren Orinelle on?",a="Lieutenant Orinelle serves the Grand Alliance and answers directly to the military forces of Stormwind. Though he detests his current assignment in the Hillsbrad Foothills, his post under Marshal Redpath places him squarely on the side of Southshore's defenders against both regional terrors and Horde aggression.",al={"orinelle faction","farren orinelle alliance","who does farren serve"},it="side",add=true}},ang={["faction:Alliance"]="For Alliance champions, Orinelle represents the disgruntled Southern troops holding a lonely Northern outpost, willing to offer coin and commendation to anyone handling his duties.",["race:Human"]="As a Stormwind soldier stuck far from Elwynn Forest, Orinelle's disdain for northern frontier duty highlights the rift between comfortable capital life and harsh overseas deployments."},kw={"farren","hillsbrad","marshal redpath","murloc","orinelle","reassignment","southshore","stormwind"},rel={"subzone:southshore","zone:hillsbrad","quest:536","quest:559","quest:562","quest:563","topic:stormwind-kingdom","topic:murloc"},src={"Lieutenant Farren Orinelle"}}
E["npc:lieutenant-haggerdin"] = {t="npc",n="Lieutenant Haggerdin",z="hillsbrad",s="Lieutenant Haggerdin is a dwarven officer stationed upon the Headland in the Alterac Mountains. Standing watch outside the fortified gate to Alterac Valley, he acts as the primary recruitment and liaison officer for the Stormpike Guard. He evaluates aspiring Alliance champions and rewards those who prove their valor against the Frostwolf Clan.",h="Lieutenant Haggerdin is a dwarven officer stationed upon the Headland in the Alterac Mountains.",sec={{t="Gatekeeper of the Headland",b="Perched in the snowy heights of the Headland above the Hillsbrad Foothills, Lieutenant Haggerdin oversees the muster point for the Alliance's ongoing campaign in Alterac Valley. Dwarven banners flutter beside the massive wooden gate as recruits and veterans assemble under his watchful eye, preparing to plunge into the frigid warzone.",sp=0},{t="Voice of the Stormpike Guard",b="Serving the Stormpike Expedition, Haggerdin ensures that only tested warriors represent Ironforge and the Grand Alliance in the valley. Through challenges like the Proving Grounds, he tasks recruits with recovering banners and relics, and bestows official commendations, insignias, and rank recognitions as soldiers rise through the ranks of the Stormpike Guard.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Lieutenant Haggerdin?",a="Lieutenant Haggerdin is a dwarf officer representing the Stormpike Guard. Stationed at the entrance to Alterac Valley on the Headland in the Alterac Mountains, he oversees Alliance recruitment and rewards battlefield honors.",al={"haggerdin","who is haggerdin","lieutenant haggerdin alterac"},it="identity"},{q="Where can I find Lieutenant Haggerdin?",a="He is located in the northern Alterac Mountains on the Headland, standing just outside the portal and gates leading directly into Alterac Valley.",al={"haggerdin location","where is lieutenant haggerdin","alterac valley entrance alliance"},it="place",gp=true},{q="What role does Haggerdin play in the Stormpike Guard?",a="He serves as a field liaison and quartermaster officer, administering recruitment trials such as the Proving Grounds and rewarding Alliance fighters with higher ranks and insignia as their reputation with the Stormpike Guard grows.",al={"what does haggerdin do","haggerdin quests","stormpike guard officer"},it="purpose"},{q="Why is the Alliance fighting in Alterac Valley?",a="The Stormpike Expedition journeyed into the valley to excavate ancient relics and dwarven history, but their arrival sparked a fierce territorial conflict with the indigenous Frostwolf orcs and their Horde allies.",al={"why alterac valley","stormpike expedition goal","alterac conflict"},it="conflict"},{q="Can Horde players interact with Lieutenant Haggerdin?",a="No. Lieutenant Haggerdin is an active Alliance officer and will attack any Horde champions who venture near the Headland gate.",al={"is haggerdin hostile to horde","horde haggerdin","can horde talk to haggerdin"},it="hostile",gp=true},{q="What is the Proving Grounds trial?",a="The Proving Grounds is an introductory assignment Haggerdin gives to prospective Alliance soldiers to verify their competence and resolve before committing fully to the Alterac Valley war effort.",al={"proving grounds quest","proving grounds alterac","haggerdin proving grounds"}},{q="Whose side is Lieutenant Haggerdin on?",a="Lieutenant Haggerdin is thoroughly loyal to the Alliance, serving specifically within the Stormpike Guard. Operating at the northern edge of the foothills near Alterac Valley, he acts as an officer and muster agent for Alliance forces rallying against the Frostwolf orcs.",al={"haggerdin faction","is haggerdin alliance","haggerdin allegiance"},it="side",add=true},{q="What does Lieutenant Haggerdin want?",a="Haggerdin wants capable Alliance champions to bolster the Stormpike Guard's ranks in Alterac Valley. He tests new recruits to ensure they can survive the freezing wilderness, recognizes seasoned veterans with ranks and insignias as their deeds grow, and seeks the downfall of threats like the Winterax troll champion, Korrak.",al={"what does haggerdin want","haggerdin goals","haggerdin purpose"},it="wants",add=true},{q="Why is Lieutenant Haggerdin here in the Alterac foothills?",a="Lieutenant Haggerdin is stationed at the Headland overlooking the gate to Alterac Valley to organize and vet incoming Alliance forces. Because the ongoing clash between the Stormpike Expedition and the Frostwolf Clan demands constant reinforcement, he stands guard at the staging grounds to recruit and honor those willing to fight in the snow.",al={"why is haggerdin here","why is haggerdin in alterac","haggerdin post"},it="why_here",add=true},{q="Who is Lieutenant Haggerdin tied to?",a="Haggerdin is tied directly to the Stormpike Guard, the military arm of Ironforge's Stormpike Expedition led by General Vanndar Stormpike. He serves as an officer linking Alliance recruits arriving through the Alterac Mountains to the regiment fighting deep within Alterac Valley.",al={"haggerdin ties","haggerdin stormpike guard","who does haggerdin serve"},it="ties",add=true}},ang={["faction:Alliance"]="Lieutenant Haggerdin is your primary contact outside Alterac Valley, offering the credentials and official honors earned while clashing with the Frostwolf Clan.",["race:Dwarf"]="A proud officer of the Stormpike clan, Haggerdin embodies Ironforge's resolute determination to uncover their titan heritage in the snowy crags of Alterac.",["faction:Horde"]="A stalwart sentinel guarding the Alliance portal into Alterac Valley, Haggerdin directs the reinforcements sent to crush the Frostwolf orcs."},kw={"alterac","dwarf","frostwolf","haggerdin","headland","ironforge","lieutenant","proving grounds","stormpike"},rel={"quest:7161","zone:alterac","topic:dwarf","topic:alliance","topic:horde","zone:hillsbrad","topic:alterac-kingdom"},src={"Lieutenant Haggerdin"}}
E["npc:magistrate-henry-maleb"] = {t="npc",n="Magistrate Henry Maleb",z="hillsbrad",s="Magistrate Henry Maleb oversees civic administration in the port town of Southshore, the Alliance's primary coastal bastion in the Hillsbrad Foothills. Tasked with maintaining order amid constant threats, he focuses much of his authority on hunting down the Syndicate conspirators targeting the town's leadership.",h="Magistrate Henry Maleb oversees civic administration in the port town of Southshore, the Alliance's primary...",sec={{t="Guardian of Southshore's Order",b="Operating from the town hall in Southshore, Magistrate Henry Maleb handles civil governance for one of the last true Alliance settlements in Lordaeron. The town sits under constant siege from the Forsaken to the north and West, while ruthless highwaymen prowl the foothills. Maleb stepped into his current station after the mysterious assassination of the prior magistrate, an act he attributes directly to the Syndicate. Determined not to suffer the same fate, he coordinates active investigations to root out hidden assassins, dismantle Syndicate supply networks, and unmask the rogue nobles pulling the strings from the ruins of Alterac.",sp=0},{t="A Web of Noble Treachery",b="Maleb's enquiries into the Syndicate reveal a bitter regional conflict. The assassins creeping through the orchards outside Southshore are not mere bandits, but paid operatives taking contracts from fallen Alteraci aristocrats. Maleb directs trusted Alliance scouts to intercept their coded plans and eliminate their leaders, working relentlessly to break the Syndicate's hold before their plots can fully cripple the town's defenses.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Who is Magistrate Henry Maleb?",a="He is the chief civic magistrate of Southshore in the Hillsbrad Foothills, responsible for keeping civil order and protecting the coastal Alliance haven from domestic threats.",al={"henry maleb","southshore magistrate","who is maleb"},it="identity"},{q="Why is Maleb investigating the Syndicate?",a="Maleb assumed his post following the assassination of Southshore's previous magistrate. His investigations point to hired Syndicate assassins sent by fallen nobles of Alterac, and he actively commissions Alliance adventurers to preempt another assassination attempt on his life.",al={"why syndicate","maleb syndicate","southshore assassins"},it="motive"},{q="Where can Magistrate Maleb be found?",a="He can be found inside the town hall building in Southshore, situated in the southern reaches of the Hillsbrad Foothills.",al={"maleb location","where is henry maleb","find magistrate maleb"},it="place",gp=true},{q="What threats does Maleb face in Hillsbrad?",a="Aside from the ever-present threat of Forsaken expansion from the north and west, Maleb is specifically menaced by shadowy Syndicate killers stalking the town perimeter and plotting the downfall of Southshore's governance.",al={"southshore threats","maleb enemies"},it="threat"},{q="Whose side is Magistrate Henry Maleb on?",a="Magistrate Henry Maleb is devoted entirely to the Alliance. As the civil magistrate of Southshore, he serves the local township and answers to the Alliance authorities, working to keep the remaining free humans of Hillsbrad united and safe against surrounding hostiles.",al={"magistrate maleb faction","maleb alliance or horde","is henry maleb alliance"},it="side",add=true},{q="What does Magistrate Henry Maleb want?",a="Maleb wants to safeguard Southshore from destruction and bring an end to the Syndicate's predation. Having stepped into office after his predecessor was assassinated, he is determined to identify the conspirators, track down their shadowy assassins, and punish the Alteraci nobles directing the plots against the town.",al={"henry maleb goals","what does maleb need","magistrate maleb objective"},it="wants",add=true},{q="Why is Magistrate Henry Maleb in Southshore?",a="Maleb was recently assigned as the magistrate of Southshore following the assassination of the town's previous leader. He presides in the Southshore town hall to govern the settlement, oversee town defense, and coordinate Alliance investigations into the threats lurking across the Hillsbrad Foothills.",al={"why is maleb in southshore","maleb southshore reason","magistrate maleb town hall"},it="why_here",add=true}},ang={["faction:Alliance"]="For Alliance champions arriving in Hillsbrad, Magistrate Maleb represents legitimate civic authority in a lawless borderland, offering bounties on Syndicate cutthroats destabilizing the town.",["class:Rogue"]="Rogues will find Maleb deeply concerned with the arts of stealth and assassination, relying on keen-eyed operatives to outmaneuver the Syndicate's concealed killers."},kw={"alterac","assassins","henry maleb","hillsbrad","magistrate maleb","southshore","syndicate"},rel={"subzone:southshore","zone:hillsbrad","topic:syndicate","topic:alterac-kingdom","topic:alliance","topic:lordaeron"},src={"Magistrate Henry Maleb"}}
E["npc:major-samuelson"] = {t="npc",n="Major Samuelson",z="hillsbrad",s="Major Samuelson is a high-ranking officer in the Stormwind City Guard stationed within the throne room of Stormwind Keep. As an experienced military commander, he oversees vital personnel matters and previously mentored junior officers such as Lieutenant Farren Orinelle.",h="Major Samuelson is a high-ranking officer in the Stormwind City Guard stationed within the throne room of...",sec={{t="A Pillar of Stormwind's Guard",b="Standing within Stormwind Keep before the royal court, Major Samuelson represents the leadership of the Stormwind City Guard. He oversees officer postings and administrative military orders across the realm. Notably, he mentored Lieutenant Farren Orinelle, an officer stationed far north at Southshore in the Hillsbrad Foothills. When junior commanders find themselves overwhelmed or seeking transfer from distant frontier garrisons, their requests and official reports travel directly across the kingdom to Major Samuelson's desk in the capital.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Major Samuelson?",a="Major Samuelson is an officer of the Stormwind City Guard stationed in the throne room of Stormwind Keep. He serves as an administrative commander handling officer deployments and personnel.",al={"samuelson","major samuelson identity","who is the major in keep"},it="identity"},{q="Where can Major Samuelson be found?",a="He is located inside Stormwind Keep within Stormwind City, standing in the throne room near the boy-king Anduin Wrynn and Highlord Bolvar Fordragon.",al={"samuelson location","where is major samuelson","find samuelson"},it="place",gp=true},{q="What is his connection to Southshore?",a="Major Samuelson served as the mentor to Lieutenant Farren Orinelle, an officer stationed at Southshore in the Hillsbrad Foothills. Orinelle seeks a reassignment from the stressful northern posting through Samuelson.",al={"samuelson southshore","lieutenant farren orinelle mentor","samuelson hillsbrad"},it="ties"},{q="Why do adventurers seek him out?",a="Adventurers traveling from the northern front in Hillsbrad carry Lieutenant Farren Orinelle's official request for reassignment to Major Samuelson in Stormwind Keep.",al={"stormwind ho quest turnin","reassignment quest","why talk to samuelson"},it="purpose"},{q="Whose side is Major Samuelson on?",a="Major Samuelson serves the Kingdom of Stormwind and the Alliance. As an officer within the Stormwind City Guard stationed directly inside Stormwind Keep, his duty is to defend the capital, maintain military order, and carry out the commands of the city's leadership.",al={"samuelson faction","who does major samuelson serve","is samuelson alliance"},it="side",add=true}},ang={["faction:Alliance"]="Serving within the royal throne room, Major Samuelson represents the administrative backbone of Stormwind's military, directing personnel across contested territories like Hillsbrad."},kw={"farren orinelle","major samuelson","reassignment","samuelson","southshore","stormwind guard","stormwind keep"},rel={"subzone:stormwind-keep","zone:stormwind","npc:lieutenant-farren-orinelle","quest:562","quest:563","zone:hillsbrad","topic:stormwind-kingdom"},src={"Major Samuelson"}}
E["npc:marcus-redpath"] = {t="npc",n="Marcus Redpath",z="hillsbrad",s="Marshal Marcus Redpath is the senior military authority defending the Alliance town of Southshore in the Hillsbrad Foothills. Having served the town since before the Second War, he now organizes patrols and bounty contracts to hold off surrounding ogres, murlocs, and naga. His leadership is essential to maintaining Lordaeron's last southern bastion on the coast.",h="Marshal Marcus Redpath is the senior military authority defending the Alliance town of Southshore in the...",sec={{t="A Sentinel of Southshore",b="Marcus Redpath's service to Southshore spans decades. Years ago, before the Second War engulfed the north, he served as the village headman who received Lord Anduin Lothar, the young mage Khadgar, and thousands of exhausted refugees fleeing the sack of Stormwind. Recognizing the gravity of their plight, he dispatched his swiftest courier north to alert King Terenas Menethil II, playing an early role in forging the Grand Alliance of Lordaeron. Through the fall of the capital and the devastating Scourge invasion, Redpath remained at his post, transitioning from civil administrator to military marshal to guard the port's beleaguered survivors.",sp=0},{t="Holding the Coast",b="In the wake of the Third War, Southshore stands virtually alone against hostile forces pressing in from every side. Marshal Redpath coordinates defense operations across the Hillsbrad Foothills, enlisting seasoned adventurers to push back the Crushridge ogres creeping down from Alterac and purge dangerous naga and murloc encampments along the coastline. With the Forsaken occupying the north and Tarren Mill heavily fortified nearby, Redpath's vigilance is one of the few barriers preventing the regional Alliance presence from collapsing entirely.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Marcus Redpath?",a="Marcus Redpath is the marshal and military commander of Southshore in the Hillsbrad Foothills. He was originally the town's headman during the Second War and now oversees local defense against surrounding wilderness threats and hostile neighbors.",al={"marcus redpath lore","who is the marshal in southshore","marcus redpath info"},it="identity"},{q="What role did he play in the Second War?",a="When the Kingdom of Stormwind fell to the Orcish Horde, refugees led by Anduin Lothar and Khadgar made landfall at Southshore. Redpath welcomed them ashore and immediately sent his rider, Willem, to notify King Terenas Menethil II in Capital City.",al={"second war marcus","did marcus redpath meet lothar"},it="history"},{q="What threats does he focus on fighting?",a="Redpath organizes military efforts against local predators and invaders encroaching on Southshore. He issues bounties and missions targeting the Crushridge ogre tribe in the Alterac foothills, coastal murlocs, and raiding naga.",al={"marcus redpath quests","what does redpath want killed"},it="threat"},{q="Is he related to the Redpaths of Darrowshire?",a="While he shares the Redpath surname made famous by Captain Joseph Redpath of Darrowshire in the Eastern Plaguelands, no direct kinship has been formally established beyond their shared heritage in the Kingdom of Lordaeron.",al={"redpath family","is marcus related to joseph redpath","redpath relatives"},it="ties"},{q="Why does he wear Stormwind-style armor?",a="Following the First War, many southern refugees settled permanently in Southshore, creating deep historical and military ties between the port and Stormwind. Local garrison forces often utilize standardized Alliance arms and uniforms derived from those southern traditions.",al={"marcus redpath armor","why stormwind gear southshore"}},{q="Where can Marcus Redpath be found?",a="Marshal Redpath is stationed in the center of Southshore, an Alliance haven situated on the southern coast of the Hillsbrad Foothills.",al={"where is marcus redpath","marcus redpath location"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Whose side is Marcus Redpath on?",a="Marshal Marcus Redpath serves the Alliance and the survivors of Lordaeron who have gathered under Southshore's banner. As Southshore's town marshal, he stands staunchly with the human defenders holding the Hillsbrad line against hostile threats across the foothills.",al={"marcus redpath faction","what faction is marcus redpath","who does redpath serve"},it="side",add=true},{q="What does Marcus Redpath want?",a="Redpath wants to secure Southshore and its surrounding lands from encroaching perils. He actively directs soldiers and adventurers to eliminate regional dangers, pushing back the Crushridge ogre tribes from the northern mountains and eradicating the murloc and naga infestations plaguing the coast.",al={"marcus redpath goals","what does redpath need","marcus redpath purpose"},it="wants",add=true},{q="Why is Marcus Redpath here?",a="Marcus Redpath has long called Southshore home, having served as its headman since the days of the Second War. Following the fall of Lordaeron in the Third War, he took on the duties of town marshal to organize local defenses and keep order in one of the Alliance's last strongholds in the region.",al={"why is marcus redpath in southshore","redpath southshore reason","what is redpath doing here"},it="why_here",add=true}},ang={["faction:Alliance"]="Marshal Redpath provides Alliance champions with vital tasks to secure Hillsbrad against encroaching ogres and coastal hazards.",["race:Human"]="Redpath is a living link to the opening days of the Grand Alliance, having greeted Anduin Lothar and the refugees of Stormwind when they first fled north."},kw={"anduin lothar","crushridge","headman","hillsbrad","marcus redpath","marshal","southshore","terenas"},rel={"subzone:southshore","zone:hillsbrad","topic:anduin-lothar","topic:terenas-menethil-ii","npc:willem","quest:559","topic:second-war","topic:third-war"},src={"Marcus Redpath"}}
E["npc:master-apothecary-lydon"] = {t="npc",n="Master Apothecary Lydon",z="hillsbrad",s="Apothecary Lydon is a morbid researcher of the Royal Apothecary Society stationed in Tarren Mill. Chronically depressed and intensely bored, he finds joy only in refining lethal concoctions and watching the living suffer. He spearheads the research into potent new toxins aimed at securing Hillsbrad for the Forsaken and furthering Sylvanas's New Plague.",h="Apothecary Lydon is a morbid researcher of the Royal Apothecary Society stationed in Tarren Mill.",sec={{t="The Recluse of Tarren Mill",b="Stationed inside the chapel turned laboratory of Tarren Mill, Apothecary Lydon represents the cold, calculating ethos of the Royal Apothecary Society. He is afflicted by a profound, languid melancholy, disgusted by the blooming flowers and crisp air of Hillsbrad Foothills. The only diversion that lifts his perpetual gloom is the art of deathcraft. When left unattended, he passes the time poisoning, dissecting, and reanimating his unfortunate pet frog, Umpi, repeatedly waiting for new reagents to arrive.",sp=0},{t="Concoctions of Agony",b="Working in coordination with Master Apothecary Faranell in the Undercity, Lydon conducts extensive field experiments across Hillsbrad. His work escalates from the Elixir of Suffering to the virulent Elixir of Agony. To verify their potency, Lydon dispatches adventurers to test brews on local targets, ranging from innocent wildlife and domesticated animals to captured human farmers. His ultimate loyalty lies entirely with the Dark Lady, longing for the day when their finished New Plague cleanses the living world.",sp=1},{t="Venom of the Loa",b="Beyond his standard concoctions, Lydon's intellectual curiosity extends to esoteric poisons. When mysterious venom bottles surface in the region, he consults with troll mystics such as Master Gadrin to trace their origin. This investigation unearths a trail leading directly to the spider goddess Shadra in the Hinterlands. Once secured, such primeval venom is shipped directly to the Apothecarium in the Undercity to further advance the Forsaken plague initiative.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Who is Apothecary Lydon?",a="He is an alchemist of the Royal Apothecary Society operating out of Tarren Mill in Hillsbrad Foothills. He oversees the development of various experimental plagues and toxins on behalf of Lady Sylvanas Windrunner.",al={"who is lydon","lydon tarren mill","apothecary lydon lore"},it="identity"},{q="Why is Lydon so depressed?",a="Lydon suffers from profound melancholy and finds the natural beauty and fresh air of Hillsbrad repulsive. The only things that lift his spirits are cruel experimentation, the suffering of the living, and the aroma of alchemical embalming fluids.",al={"why is he sad","lydon depression","why is lydon gloomy"}},{q="Who is Umpi?",a="Umpi is a frog that Lydon keeps in his workshop, wryly referring to her as his assistant. In reality, he relieves his extreme boredom by repeatedly poisoning, killing, and reanimating the helpless amphibian.",al={"lydon frog","who is the frog","umpi lore"}},{q="What is the Elixir of Agony?",a="It is a potent experimental poison brewed by Lydon using ingredients from across the Eastern Kingdoms, including syndicate charms, dwarven ale, and creeper venom. Lydon ultimately tests it on captive humans in Hillsbrad to confirm its lethal effectiveness.",al={"elixir of agony quest","what is elixir of agony","lydon elixir"},sp=1},{q="How did Lydon become Forsaken?",a="He was a young human alchemist in Lordaeron who fell to the Scourge during the Third War. When Sylvanas broke the Lich King's control, Lydon rallied behind her, fully discarding his former human identity to dedicate his undead existence to the Dark Lady.",al={"lydon past","was lydon human","lydon third war"},it="origin"},{q="What does Lydon send to the Undercity?",a="After discovering ancient venom vessels in the Hinterlands and coordinating the downfall of the troll spider god Shadra, Lydon collects her concentrated, divine venom and ships it straight to Master Apothecary Faranell to bolster the Society's plague research.",al={"lydon undercity venom","shadra venom quest"},sp=1},{q="Whose side is Apothecary Lydon on?",a="Apothecary Lydon is fiercely loyal to Lady Sylvanas Windrunner, the Forsaken, and the Horde. He is a ranking researcher in the Royal Apothecary Society, taking direct guidance from Master Apothecary Faranell in the Undercity. Everything he concocts serves Sylvanas's grand designs to secure the realm for the undead.",al={"lydon faction","who does lydon serve","is lydon forsaken"},it="side",add=true},{q="What does Apothecary Lydon want?",a="Lydon is consumed by the creation and perfection of the New Plague for the Dark Lady. He seeks potent toxins, predator blood, and lethal venoms from across the region to refine his brews—including the Elixir of Suffering and Elixir of Agony—aiming to bring misery and death to the living.",al={"what is lydon trying to do","lydon goal","why does lydon want poisons"},it="wants",add=true},{q="Why is Apothecary Lydon in Tarren Mill?",a="Lydon is stationed at the Tarren Mill apothecary lab to gather regional reagents and test lethal alchemical formulas close to enemy territory. Hillsbrad Foothills offers fertile testing grounds against local wildlife, hostile dwarven incursions, and the human town of Southshore just down the road.",al={"why is lydon in hillsbrad","lydon tarren mill purpose","why is apothecary lydon here"},it="why_here",add=true},{q="Who is Apothecary Lydon tied to?",a="Lydon answers directly to Master Apothecary Faranell and the Royal Apothecary Society. He collaborates closely with colleagues across Azeroth, supplying Apothecary Zamah in the Stonetalon Mountains with potent toxins and coordinating research with other Forsaken apothecaries stationed throughout Lordaeron.",al={"lydon connections","who works with lydon","lydon allies"},it="ties",add=true}},ang={["race:Undead"]="Lydon embodies the Royal Apothecary Society's singular mission: developing the New Plague to secure a future for the Forsaken and eradicate the living.",["faction:Alliance"]="To the humans of Southshore, Lydon is a horrific monster who brews lethal diseases and tests them indiscriminately on captive Hillsbrad farmers and wildlife.",["profession:Herbalism"]="Lydon's workshop is packed with reagents, cauldrons, and rotting flora, demonstrating how traditional gathering arts are weaponized by the Apothecary Society."},kw={"apothecary","elixir of agony","faranell","hillsbrad","lydon","royal apothecary society","tarren mill","umpi"},rel={"npc:master-apothecary-faranell","npc:umpi","npc:master-gadrin","subzone:tarren-mill","zone:hillsbrad","topic:royal-apothecary-society","quest:509"},src={"Master Apothecary Lydon"}}
E["npc:tallow"] = {t="npc",n="Tallow",z="hillsbrad",s="Tallow is a Forsaken warrior stationed in the fortified settlement of Tarren Mill within the Hillsbrad Foothills. Serving the Dark Lady and the Horde, he watches over the contested front lines, helping organize strikes against local Alliance threats.",h="Tallow is a Forsaken warrior stationed in the fortified settlement of Tarren Mill within the Hillsbrad...",sec={{t="A Blade in Tarren Mill",b="Situated in the heart of Tarren Mill, Tallow stands among the Forsaken and Horde forces holding the line in the Hillsbrad Foothills. The region is a powder keg of conflict, caught between nearby Southshore humans, wandering Syndicate outlaws, and hostile wildlife. Tallow helps direct capable adventurers into the field, testing their strength against the Boulderfist ogres of the Arathi Highlands before sending them on to aid the besieged outpost of Hammerfall.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Tallow?",a="Tallow is a Forsaken warrior based in Tarren Mill in the Hillsbrad Foothills, acting as an organizer and quest giver for Horde champions fighting in the area.",al={"who is tallow","tallow lore","tallow tarren mill"},it="identity"},{q="Where can I find Tallow?",a="He can be found standing in the Forsaken-held town of Tarren Mill, located in the northern half of the Hillsbrad Foothills.",al={"where is tallow","tallow location","find tallow"},it="place",gp=true},{q="What quests does Tallow offer?",a="Tallow is known for directing Horde adventurers in the mission 'The Hammer May Fall', sending fighters to prove themselves against the Boulderfist ogres of the Arathi Highlands before reporting to Drum Fel at the besieged Hammerfall outpost.",al={"tallow quests","the hammer may fall quest"},it="purpose",gp=true},{q="What is Tarren Mill's role in the conflict?",a="Tarren Mill serves as the primary northern Horde stronghold in the Hillsbrad Foothills, facing constant skirmishes and open warfare against the human bastion of Southshore to the south.",al={"why is tarren mill important","tarren mill role"},it="conflict"},{q="Whose side is Tallow on?",a="Tallow serves the Forsaken and the broader Horde. Stationed in Tarren Mill, he stands with the undead defenders holding the line in Hillsbrad against the hostile human forces of Southshore and the regional threats pressing against the Horde's southern borders.",al={"tallow faction","is tallow horde","tallow allegiance"},it="side",add=true},{q="What does Tallow want?",a="As a warrior stationed at the front lines of Tarren Mill, Tallow seeks to secure the Forsaken settlement and weaken their enemies across Hillsbrad. He directs capable Horde champions to strike at looming threats, including sending adventurers on dangerous missions like 'The Hammer May Fall' to undermine rival forces.",al={"tallow goal","what is tallow doing","tallow motive"},it="wants",add=true},{q="Why is Tallow in Tarren Mill?",a="Tarren Mill is the primary stronghold of the Forsaken in the Hillsbrad Foothills, constantly under pressure from the Alliance in Southshore and other hostile factions. Tallow is garrisoned here as a warrior to defend the town, coordinate martial strikes, and enlist passing Horde fighters to bolster their front lines.",al={"why is tallow here","tallow tarren mill","tallow purpose hillsbrad"},it="why_here",add=true}},ang={["faction:Horde"]="Tallow provides essential frontline tasks for Horde champions looking to weaken the human presence throughout the Hillsbrad Foothills.",["race:Undead"]="Like many Forsaken in Tarren Mill, Tallow fights to expand Undercity's dominion south of the Alterac Mountains."},kw={"forsaken","hillsbrad foothills","horde warrior","tallow","tarren mill","the hammer may fall"},rel={"subzone:tarren-mill","quest:676","zone:hillsbrad","subzone:southshore","topic:forsaken","topic:horde"},src={"Tallow"}}
E["npc:umpi"] = {t="npc",n="Umpi",z="hillsbrad",s="Umpi is a frog residing in Tarren Mill as the unwitting laboratory assistant of Apothecary Lydon. Kept inside the Royal Apothecary Society's workshop, she serves as a recurring test subject for experimental toxins and plague concoctions.",h="Umpi is a frog residing in Tarren Mill as the unwitting laboratory assistant of Apothecary Lydon.",sec={{t="A Life of Perpetual Testing",b="Within the dark laboratories of Tarren Mill, the Forsaken work tirelessly to brew concoctions of death and torment. For Apothecary Lydon, scientific rigor requires living flesh to test his formulas, and Umpi bears the brunt of these trials. Lydon regularly tests lethal brews—such as the Elixir of Suffering and the Elixir of Agony—directly on her. Once the poisons take their inevitable toll and kill her, the apothecary re-animates the amphibian, ensuring she is ready to endure the next lethal dose for the glory of the Royal Apothecary Society.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Umpi?",a="Umpi is a frog kept by Apothecary Lydon in Tarren Mill. She acts as an assistant and prime test subject for Lydon's noxious alchemical experiments.",al={"umpi who","what is umpi","frog tarren mill"},it="identity"},{q="Why does Apothecary Lydon keep killing Umpi?",a="Apothecary Lydon uses Umpi to gauge the potency of his newly brewed toxins. After feeding her fatal concoctions like the Elixir of Suffering, he re-animates her so she can be poisoned all over again in future trials.",al={"why kill umpi","umpi poisoned","lydon frog"},it="why_here"},{q="Is Umpi alive or undead?",a="Biologically, she walks the line between both. While technically functioning as a beast, Apothecary Lydon openly admits to raising her from the dead after each lethal poisoning experiment.",al={"is umpi undead","umpi zombie","frog undead"}},{q="Where can Umpi be found?",a="Umpi is located inside the apothecary workshop in Tarren Mill within the Hillsbrad Foothills, right beside Apothecary Lydon's workbench.",al={"where is umpi","umpi location"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Whose side is Umpi on?",a="Umpi is essentially the captive assistant and test subject of Apothecary Lydon and the Royal Apothecary Society. Rather than having any political loyalty to the Forsaken or the Horde, she simply endures whatever concoctions Lydon decides to pour down her throat.",al={"umpi faction","is umpi horde","who does umpi serve"},it="side",add=true},{q="Who is Umpi tied to?",a="Umpi is tied directly to Apothecary Lydon, serving as his unwilling laboratory assistant in Tarren Mill. Her entire existence revolves around testing his lethal concoctions, dying to their venomous effects, and being dragged back from death to undergo the process again.",al={"umpi apothecary lydon","who owns umpi","umpi master"},it="ties",add=true}},ang={["race:Undead"]="Umpi exemplifies the ruthless, pragmatic research methods of the Royal Apothecary Society, where life and death are merely variables in perfecting the Forsaken arsenal."},kw={"apothecary lydon","elixir of agony","elixir of suffering","frog","hillsbrad foothills","tarren mill","umpi"},rel={"subzone:tarren-mill","quest:496","quest:509","zone:hillsbrad"},src={"Umpi"}}
E["npc:vanndar-stormpike"] = {t="npc",n="Vanndar Stormpike",z="hillsbrad",s="Vanndar Stormpike is a fierce dwarf mountain king who commands the Stormpike Expedition from the northern fortress of Dun Baldar. Searching the frozen peaks of Alterac Valley for ancient relics and raw resources, he leads the Alliance's unyielding war against the Frostwolf orcs.",h="Vanndar Stormpike is a fierce dwarf mountain king who commands the Stormpike Expedition from the northern...",sec={{t="Lord of Dun Baldar",b="A veteran mountain king of Ironforge, Vanndar Stormpike spearheads the dwarven excavation into Alterac Valley. Following the Third War, he marched the Stormpike Guard into the northern mountains seeking hidden mineral riches and long-lost titan artifacts. Settling into the fortified redoubt of Dun Baldar, Vanndar views the valley as an ancestral right and rightful Alliance territory. He directs military outposts, defensive bunkers, and frontline pushes with grim dwarven resolve, determined that no retreat will ever be sounded under his watch.",sp=0},{t="War for the Frozen Pass",b="Vanndar's relentless mining and prospecting encroached directly onto the home of the Frostwolf clan, sparking brutal mountain warfare. Despite orcish demands to withdraw, Vanndar refuses to yield an inch of ground, vowing that Alterac Valley will belong to the dwarves. From his throne room deep within Dun Baldar, flanked by his marshals and bodyguards, he personally oversees the defense against Frostwolf incursions while dispatching Alliance champions to break the enemy lines and claim the valley once and for all.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Vanndar Stormpike?",a="Vanndar Stormpike is a dwarf mountain king and the supreme commander of the Stormpike Expedition. Based in Dun Baldar, he leads the Alliance war effort within Alterac Valley.",al={"who is vanndar","vanndar stormpike lore","stormpike leader"},it="identity"},{q="Why is Vanndar fighting in Alterac Valley?",a="Vanndar led the Stormpike Expedition to Alterac Valley to uncover ancient relics and extract natural resources. His refusal to abandon these claims brought the dwarves into a bloody conflict with the native Frostwolf orcs.",al={"why are dwarves in alterac","vanndar motive","stormpike purpose"},it="why_here"},{q="Where does Vanndar stay?",a="He commands his forces from the northern stronghold of Dun Baldar in Alterac Valley, protected by dwarven bunkers, marshals, and elite guards.",al={"where is vanndar","vanndar location","dun baldar boss"},it="place"},{q="Who is Vanndar's main enemy?",a="His primary adversary is Drek'Thar, the chieftain and elder shaman of the Frostwolf clan, who seeks to purge the dwarven interlopers from their ancestral homeland.",al={"vanndar rival","who does vanndar fight","frostwolf leader"},it="threat"},{q="Whose side is Vanndar Stormpike on?",a="Vanndar Stormpike is a proud dwarven mountain king who fights fiercely for Ironforge and the Grand Alliance. As supreme commander of the Stormpike Guard and the expedition into Alterac Valley, he directs all Alliance military and excavation efforts against the Frostwolf orcs and their Horde allies.",al={"vanndar stormpike faction","is vanndar alliance","who does vanndar fight for"},it="side",add=true},{q="What does Vanndar Stormpike want?",a="Vanndar wants nothing less than total dwarven dominion over Alterac Valley. His expedition came seeking natural resources, ancestral history, and titan relics buried in the mountains, but with the Frostwolf clan resisting their claim, his goal is to completely drive out the orcs and secure the entire valley for the Alliance.",al={"vanndar stormpike goal","what does vanndar want","vanndar stormpike purpose"},it="wants",add=true},{q="Who is Vanndar Stormpike tied to?",a="Vanndar is the head of the Stormpike Expedition and leads the Stormpike Guard, an elite dwarven military force tied directly to King Magni Bronzebeard and the kingdom of Ironforge. He also shares a clan and potential kinship with General Lena Stormpike, who commands dwarven interests elsewhere in the Eastern Kingdoms.",al={"vanndar stormpike clan","who is vanndar related to","vanndar stormpike connections"},it="ties",add=true}},ang={["race:Dwarf"]="For dwarves of Ironforge, Vanndar exemplifies the indomitable spirit of the Mountain Kings, fighting to claim ancient heritage and honor the Explorer's Guild.",["faction:Alliance"]="Vanndar serves as the premier commander on the Alterac front, holding the northern ramparts and pushing Alliance territory into the wild mountains."},kw={"alterac","dun baldar","dwarf","frostwolf","mountain king","stormpike","vanndar"},rel={"topic:dwarf","topic:alliance","zone:hillsbrad","topic:alterac-kingdom","topic:third-war"},src={"Vanndar Stormpike"}}
E["npc:warmaster-laggrond"] = {t="npc",n="Warmaster Laggrond",z="hillsbrad",s="Warmaster Laggrond is a seasoned orc commander stationed outside the Horde entrance to Alterac Valley in the Alterac Mountains. He oversees recruitment and frontline recognition for warriors answering the call to aid the Frostwolf clan. Through his trials, fighters prove their mettle and earn the respect of the Horde vanguard.",h="Warmaster Laggrond is a seasoned orc commander stationed outside the Horde entrance to Alterac Valley in the...",sec={{t="Frontline Commander",b="Standing watch in the bitter cold at the threshold of Alterac Valley, Warmaster Laggrond organizes the Horde's war effort against the Stormpike Expedition. He ensures that only capable fighters enter the valley to represent the Frostwolf clan and the wider Horde.",sp=0},{t="The Path of Honor",b="Laggrond tests arriving combatants through the Proving Grounds before directing them into the thick of battle. As warriors spill blood across the frozen peaks, it is Laggrond who measures their standing, bestowing honors upon those who earn renown among the Frostwolves.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Where is Warmaster Laggrond located?",a="Warmaster Laggrond is posted near the Horde encampment at the entrance portal to Alterac Valley, high in the snowy passes of the Alterac Mountains north of Hillsbrad Foothills.",al={"laggrond location","where is laggrond","alterac valley entrance warmaster"},it="place",gp=true},{q="What is Warmaster Laggrond's role?",a="He serves as a recruitment officer and battlemaster for the Horde's Alterac Valley war effort, assessing recruits through initial combat trials and rewarding those who achieve standing with the Frostwolf clan.",al={"what does laggrond do","laggrond purpose","why talk to laggrond"},it="purpose",gp=true},{q="What is the Proving Grounds quest?",a="The Proving Grounds is the trial given by Laggrond to prospective fighters, directing them into the valley to prove their capability in battle before they fully join the clan's campaigns.",al={"proving grounds horde","laggrond initial quest"},gp=true},{q="Why is the Horde fighting in Alterac Valley?",a="The Frostwolf clan has long claimed the valley as their home after being exiled during the First War. The Stormpike Guard, an Alliance dwarven expedition, has pushed into the region searching for relics and territory, sparking a bitter territorial war.",al={"why alterac valley","frostwolf war","alterac valley conflict"},it="conflict"},{q="Does Warmaster Laggrond offer reputation rewards?",a="Yes. As you earn renown fighting beside the Frostwolves, Laggrond provides successive honors, acknowledging warriors as they advance from recognized fighters to exalted legends of the valley.",al={"frostwolf reputation turn in","rise and be recognized","laggrond rep"},gp=true},{q="Can Alliance players interact with Warmaster Laggrond?",a="No. Warmaster Laggrond is a devoted champion of the Horde and will attack any Alliance trespassers who approach his outpost in the mountains.",al={"can alliance talk to laggrond","laggrond hostile"},gp=true},{q="Who is Warmaster Laggrond?",a="Warmaster Laggrond is an orc officer stationed at the entrance to Alterac Valley in the snowy reaches of the Alterac Mountains. He serves the Frostwolf clan and the broader Horde war effort, evaluating arriving champions and directing capable soldiers toward the battle against the Stormpike dwarves.",al={"who is laggrond","warmaster laggrond lore","laggrond alterac"},it="identity",add=true},{q="Whose side is Warmaster Laggrond on?",a="Laggrond stands firmly with the Horde, specifically representing the interests of the Frostwolf clan. He regards the Alliance—especially the encroaching Stormpike Expedition—as invaders trespassing on ancestral Frostwolf territory.",al={"is laggrond horde","warmaster laggrond faction","laggrond alliance or horde"},it="side",add=true},{q="What does Warmaster Laggrond want?",a="Laggrond seeks stalwart champions willing to prove themselves in the harsh conflict of Alterac Valley. He wants the Frostwolf lands defended, the dwarven expedition crushed, and Horde fighters to earn standing and honor among the clan through blood and duty.",al={"what does laggrond want","laggrond goal","laggrond objective"},it="wants",add=true},{q="Why is Warmaster Laggrond here?",a="Stationed right outside the portal to the valley, Laggrond acts as a gatekeeper and recruiter for the frontline. He inspects those who answer the Frostwolves' call to arms, ensuring only determined fighters carry the clan's banner into battle.",al={"why is laggrond in alterac","laggrond location purpose","why is warmaster laggrond here"},it="why_here",add=true},{q="Who is Warmaster Laggrond tied to?",a="Laggrond answers to the leadership of the Frostwolf clan, fighting on behalf of General Drek'Thar and the Horde forces committed to holding Alterac Valley against dwarven excavation and conquest.",al={"laggrond ties","laggrond frostwolf","who does laggrond work for"},it="ties",add=true}},ang={["faction:Horde"]="Warmaster Laggrond serves as your initial point of contact for the Alterac Valley war effort, acknowledging your battlefield achievements on behalf of the Frostwolf clan.",["race:Orc"]="For orcs, answering Laggrond's summons is a matter of heritage, defending the ancestral refuge of the venerable Frostwolf clan from dwarven intrusion.",["class:Warrior"]="Laggrond values raw frontline courage and tests prospective champions to ensure they can hold the line against heavy dwarven armor and vanguard charges."},kw={"alterac mountains","alterac valley","frostwolf","laggrond","proving grounds","pvp","stormpike","warmaster laggrond"},rel={"zone:alterac","quest:7161","topic:horde","zone:hillsbrad"},src={"Warmaster Laggrond"}}
E["npc:winstone-wolfe"] = {t="npc",n="Winstone Wolfe",z="hillsbrad",s="Winstone Wolfe is a human operative affiliated with the secretive Ravenholdt organization, stationed at their secluded estate nestled between Hillsbrad and the Alterac Mountains. He keeps watch over the estate's grounds and groundskeepers, serving as one of the trusted contacts within the hidden league of thieves and assassins.",h="Winstone Wolfe is a human operative affiliated with the secretive Ravenholdt organization, stationed at their...",sec={{t="A Fixer in the Mountains",b="Tucked away in the hidden valley of Ravenholdt Manor, Winstone Wolfe operates among the ranks of Lord Jorach Ravenholdt's syndicate. Quiet, watchful, and practical, Wolfe is one of the capable hands who handles business around the manor, ensuring that only those with proper discretion and talent walk the grounds undisturbed.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Winstone Wolfe?",a="Winstone Wolfe is a human rogue operating within Ravenholdt Manor, the secluded headquarters of the League of Assassins tucked high above Hillsbrad Foothills and the Alterac Mountains.",al={"who is wolfe","winstone wolfe lore","ravenholdt wolfe"},it="identity"},{q="Where can I find Winstone Wolfe?",a="He is located at Ravenholdt Manor, which can be reached via a hidden path winding north through the mountains from the Durnholde Keep area in Hillsbrad Foothills.",al={"wolfe location","where is winstone wolfe","find winstone wolfe"},it="place",gp=true},{q="What is his role in Ravenholdt?",a="Wolfe acts as an operative and guard around the manor, keeping watch over the grounds and assisting in the syndicate's shadowy logistical affairs.",al={"what does wolfe do","wolfe purpose"},it="purpose"},{q="Whose side is Winstone Wolfe on?",a="Winstone Wolfe is aligned with Ravenholdt, the secretive league of thieves and assassins operating out of Ravenholdt Manor. Tucked away in the hidden foothills overlooking Hillsbrad and Alterac, he serves the guild rather than either the Alliance or the Horde.",al={"winstone wolfe faction","who does winstone wolfe work for","is winstone wolfe ravenholdt"},it="side",add=true},{q="Why is Winstone Wolfe here?",a="Wolfe operates out of Ravenholdt Manor as part of the hidden league of rogues based in the mountains. Whether watching the grounds or assisting fellow guild operatives, he remains where the guild's business is conducted.",al={"why is winstone wolfe at ravenholdt","winstone wolfe ravenholdt manor why"},it="why_here",add=true}},ang={["class:Rogue"]="As an operative at Ravenholdt Manor, Wolfe is a familiar face to rogues who travel into the mountains to hone their craft with the syndicate."},kw={"alterac","hillsbrad","ravenholdt","ravenholdt manor","rogue","winstone wolfe"},rel={"subzone:ravenholdt-manor","topic:ravenholdt","zone:hillsbrad","zone:alterac"},src={"Winstone Wolfe"}}
E["quest:2480"] = {t="quest",n="Hinott's Assistance",z="hillsbrad",s="Hinott's Assistance is the culmination of a Horde rogue's journey to overcome Zanzil's deadly creeping poison. Waiting upon apothecary Serge Hinott in Tarren Mill, the afflicted operative receives an antidote to the toxin alongside foundational training in alchemical venomcraft.",h="Hinott's Assistance is the culmination of a Horde rogue's journey to overcome Zanzil's deadly creeping poison.",sec={{t="A Toxic Masterpiece",b="After contracting a virulent, mind-altering toxin during an assignment in the Barrens, Horde rogues are directed north to Tarren Mill to consult Serge Hinott. A Forsaken chemist of singular focus, Hinott displays professional awe toward the poison concocted by the jungle troll exile Zanzil. While unconcerned with the troll's identity or lineage, Hinott openly commends the brew's vicious efficacy, eager to study its mechanism before formulating an antidote.",sp=0},{t="The Antidote and the Trade",b="Developing the remedy requires only patience while Hinott isolates the active agents. The finished concoction halts the creeping madness, even if the chemist admits he cannot wash out the lingering stench. Once purged of the debilitating venom, rogues transition from victims to practitioners, using Hinott's insights into Zanzil's handiwork to master the preparation of their own tactical poisons.",sp=1}},faq={{q="What happens during Hinott's Assistance?",a="You simply need to wait a few moments in Tarren Mill while Serge Hinott prepares the anti-toxin. Once he finishes concocting the mixture, speak with him to ingest the cure and cleanse Zanzil's poison.",al={"what do i do here","hinott assistance walk","how to finish quest"},it="purpose"},{q="Who is Serge Hinott?",a="Serge Hinott is a Forsaken alchemist and poison expert stationed at Tarren Mill in the Hillsbrad Foothills. He lends his specialized craft to Horde rogues seeking to cure exotic afflictions and learn the intricacies of venom preparation.",al={"serge hinott lore","who is hinott","tarren mill apothecary"},it="identity"},{q="Why is Serge Hinott impressed by the poison?",a="Hinott considers Zanzil's formula a marvel of alchemical design due to its potent mixture of creeping madness and physical debilitation. Even while working to neutralize it, he openly praises the craft behind such a destructive concoction.",al={"zanzil poison reaction","why does hinott like it"},it="motive"},{q="What is the lingering smell Hinott mentions?",a="Zanzil's mixture possesses a pungent, sickly odor that permeates the victim's pores. While Hinott's anti-toxin successfully halts the poison's progression and clears the mind, it does not immediately neutralize the offensive stench left behind.",al={"why do i smell","madness smell","quest smell"}},{q="What is the reward for completing this quest?",a="Completing this task clears the persistent debuff contracted during the rogue class questline and opens the way to learning the Rogue Poisons skill, allowing players to brew their own debilitating coatings.",al={"what do rogues get","hinotts assistance reward"},it="for_you",gp=true},{q="Where is this quest turned in?",a="The quest begins and completes directly with Serge Hinott at Tarren Mill, located in the northern Hillsbrad Foothills.",al={"where is hinott","turn in location"},it="place",gp=true}},ang={["class:Rogue"]="This rite of passage cures the debilitating affliction suffered during your initiation and unlocks the knowledge needed to concoct tactical poisons.",["faction:Horde"]="Forsaken alchemy proves indispensable to the Horde's stealth operatives, transforming exotic jungle troll toxins into standard field knowledge.",["race:Undead"]="Apothecary Hinott exemplifies the Royal Apothecary Society's detached scientific admiration for any poison that shows genuine craftsmanship, regardless of origin."},kw={"anti-toxin","cure","hillsbrad","hinott","poisons","rogue quest","serge hinott","tarren mill","zanzil"},rel={"npc:serge-hinott","quest:2479","zone:hillsbrad"},m={start="Serge Hinott",level="21",faction="Horde",id=2480},src={"Hinott's Assistance (2)"}}
E["quest:493"] = {t="quest",n="Journey to Hillsbrad Foothills",z="hillsbrad",s="Journey to Hillsbrad Foothills is a Horde courier task connecting the Forsaken research efforts in Silverpine Forest with their outpost in Tarren Mill. Entrusted with sensitive notes from Apothecary Renferrel, the traveler journeys south into the disputed Hillsbrad Foothills to deliver vital biological research to Apothecary Lydon. This dispatch reflects the intense pressure Lady Sylvanas Windrunner places upon the Royal Apothecary Society to produce a weapon of mass devastation.",h="Journey to Hillsbrad Foothills is a Horde courier task connecting the Forsaken research efforts in Silverpine...",sec={{t="A Plague of Their Own",b="Since breaking free from the Lich King's iron grip, Lady Sylvanas Windrunner has harbored a single-minded ambition: the development of a New Plague engineered to eradicate both living enemies and the Scourge. To achieve this, the Royal Apothecary Society operates under relentless pressure from the Banshee Queen. Because distance isolates their laboratories, researchers scattered across Lordaeron must continuously share raw chemical data and test findings to accelerate their sinister breakthrough.",sp=0},{t="The Road South",b="Apothecary Renferrel, operating out of the Sepulcher in Silverpine Forest, directs couriers to deliver his recent findings to his colleague, Apothecary Lydon. The trek winds south through the shadowed pine woods, past Dalaran's shimmering magical dome, and down into the open, rolling pastures of Hillsbrad Foothills. There, nestled beneath the Alterac Mountains, lies Tarren Mill—a vital Forsaken hub and laboratory staging ground.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is inside Renferrel's findings?",a="Renferrel's findings consist of research documentation detailing his experiments on local fauna, flora, and biological toxins. They serve as pieces of the broader formula the Royal Apothecary Society is compiling toward their prized New Plague.",al={"what are the findings","renferrel research","what am i delivering"},it="item"},{q="Why is the Royal Apothecary Society in such a rush?",a="Lady Sylvanas Windrunner demands immediate results. Surrounded by hostile human remnants, the fanatical Scarlet Crusade, and wandering Scourge, the Forsaken believe only a definitive biological weapon can guarantee their survival and exact revenge upon Arthas.",al={"why rush plague","why under pressure","sylvanas pressure"},it="conflict"},{q="Who is Apothecary Lydon?",a="Apothecary Lydon is a senior researcher of the Royal Apothecary Society stationed in Tarren Mill. Highly respected by his peers like Renferrel, Lydon oversees lethal biological experiments in Hillsbrad Foothills, refining plague strains using local supplies and captives.",al={"who is lydon","apothecary lydon lore"},it="identity"},{q="Where is Tarren Mill?",a="Tarren Mill is located in northern Hillsbrad Foothills, situated south of the Alterac Mountains and east of Silverpine Forest. Following the primary roads south from Silverpine and turning east at the crossroads leads directly to the settlement.",al={"tarren mill location","how to get to tarren mill","where is hillsbrad"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Why do the Forsaken have to share findings via foot couriers?",a="The Forsaken cannot risk arcane transmission that Kirin Tor mages or rival factions might intercept. Physical couriers traveling established, guarded roads provide a discreet means of moving lethal alchemical notes across regional borders.",al={"why foot messenger","why courier delivery"},it="why_me"},{q="What happens after Lydon gets the research?",a="Upon receiving the package, Apothecary Lydon immediately begins studying Renferrel's notes to integrate them into his own concoctions, eventually tasking adventurers with testing improved strains on the local human population.",al={"what next after delivering","lydon reaction"},sp=1,it="next_step"},{q="Why does Apothecary Renferrel want his findings delivered?",a="The Royal Apothecary Society is under severe pressure from Lady Sylvanas to develop a New Plague to secure the Forsaken's survival. Renferrel knows that their alchemical breakthroughs can only succeed quickly if the apothecaries pool their research rather than working in isolation. By sending his latest discoveries to Apothecary Lydon in Tarren Mill, he hopes to accelerate the Society's collective progress.",al={"why send findings to lydon","renferrel motive","why deliver the plague research"},it="motive",add=true}},ang={["race:Undead"]="For the Forsaken, delivering these findings is a direct contribution to their people's survival and vengeance against the living and the Scourge alike.",["faction:Horde"]="While orcs and tauren generally disfavor underhanded poisons, helping establish Forsaken dominance in Hillsbrad secures the Horde's foothold in the Eastern Kingdoms.",["profession:Herbalism"]="The research conducted by both Renferrel and Lydon relies heavily on the study and harvest of virulent, mutated flora across Lordaeron's soils."},kw={"hillsbrad","lydon","new plague","renferrel","royal apothecary society","silverpine","sylvanas","tarren mill"},rel={"npc:apothecary-renferrel","subzone:tarren-mill","zone:hillsbrad","topic:royal-apothecary-society","quest:367"},m={start="Apothecary Renferrel",["end"]="Apothecary Lydon",level="20",faction="Horde",id=493},src={"Journey to Hillsbrad Foothills"}}
E["quest:494"] = {t="quest",n="Time to Strike",z="hillsbrad",s="\"Time to Strike\" is a Horde reconnaissance mission that transitions scouts across the Hillsbrad Foothills border to the military hub of Tarren Mill. Delivering Deathstalker Lesh's coded signal to High Executor Darthalia marks the transition from quiet surveillance to coordinated offensive operations against the local human populace.",h="\"Time to Strike\" is a Horde reconnaissance mission that transitions scouts across the Hillsbrad Foothills...",sec={{t="A Watcher at the Border",b="Perched along the high ground near the border between Silverpine Forest and the Hillsbrad Foothills, Deathstalker Lesh monitors the movements of human settlers and militia in the valley below. The Deathstalkers operate as the eyes and ears of the Undercity, surveying enemy settlements before any military deployment. Rather than risk abandoning his watchpost, Lesh entrusts passing Horde travelers to relay his gathered intelligence down the road to Tarren Mill.",sp=0},{t="A Coded Beckon",b="The message Lesh sends is deliberately veiled: \"The raven's cry from the west doth beckon.\" Carried east down the beaten roads, this signal informs High Executor Darthalia that human defenses around the town of Hillsbrad are vulnerable. To Darthalia and the dreadlord Varimathras, this confirms that the hour has arrived to mobilize Forsaken forces and execute their campaigns against Hillsbrad's human defenders.",sp=1}},faq={{q="What does Deathstalker Lesh's message mean?",a="The phrase \"The raven's cry from the west doth beckon\" is a coded reconnaissance update. It signals to High Executor Darthalia that the western approaches to Hillsbrad are inadequately guarded and ripe for an immediate offensive.",al={"raven's cry meaning","what does the raven cry mean","lesh message"}},{q="Who is High Executor Darthalia?",a="High Executor Darthalia serves as the supreme Forsaken military commander in the Hillsbrad Foothills. Operating from the fortified hamlet of Tarren Mill, she directs offensive operations against the Southshore humans and coordinates strategy closely with Varimathras in the Undercity.",al={"who is darthalia","darthalia role"},it="identity"},{q="Why does Lesh send a courier instead of going himself?",a="Lesh is actively engaged in a critical reconnaissance mission on Hillsbrad's western edge. Leaving his post would create a blind spot in Forsaken surveillance, so he relies on passing Horde travelers to deliver urgent dispatches.",al={"why doesn't lesh leave","why couriers"},it="why_me"},{q="Where is this message meant to be delivered?",a="The message must be carried along the main road eastward through the Hillsbrad Foothills to Tarren Mill, the primary Horde stronghold in the region.",al={"where do i go","message destination"},it="place"},{q="Why is Varimathras involved in Hillsbrad's affairs?",a="As Sylvanas Windrunner's chief lieutenant and dreadlord advisor, Varimathras oversees significant portions of the Forsaken military and strategic planning from the Royal Quarter in Undercity. High Executor Darthalia executes his campaign directives on the regional front.",al={"varimathras hillsbrad","why varimathras"},it="ties"},{q="What happens after this message is received?",a="Once Darthalia receives confirmation that Hillsbrad is vulnerable, she authorizes aggressive offensive strikes, sending Horde champions to dismantle the farms, militia, and infrastructure of the town of Hillsbrad.",al={"what happens next","after time to strike"},it="next_step"},{q="Why does Deathstalker Lesh want this message delivered?",a="Deathstalker Lesh is stationed near the border on a covert reconnaissance mission to monitor the human settlement of Hillsbrad. Having observed that the town is vulnerable, he needs his coded assessment rushed immediately to High Executor Darthalia at Tarren Mill so the Forsaken leadership can initiate their coordinated offensive.",al={"why send message","deathstalker lesh motive","time to strike motive"},it="motive",add=true}},ang={["race:Undead"]="For Forsaken operatives, carrying Lesh's dispatch helps secure the eastern frontier of Lordaeron against remnants of the human Alliance.",["class:Rogue"]="Lesh's covert watch post and coded messaging reflect the tradecraft of the Deathstalkers, the Undercity's elite guild of assassins and scouts.",["faction:Horde"]="This dispatch draws non-Undead Horde allies deeper into the strategic conflict unfolding between the Forsaken and the southern human settlements."},kw={"deathstalker lesh","high executor darthalia","hillsbrad","hillsbrad foothills","scouting","tarren mill","varimathras"},rel={"npc:deathstalker-lesh","npc:high-executor-darthalia","subzone:tarren-mill","zone:hillsbrad","zone:silverpine","npc:varimathras","topic:horde"},m={start="Deathstalker Lesh",["end"]="High Executor Darthalia",level="20",faction="Horde",id=494},src={"Time To Strike"}}
E["quest:496"] = {t="quest",n="Elixir of Suffering",z="hillsbrad",s="In Tarren Mill, Apothecary Lydon pursues the Royal Apothecary Society's grim mandate to engineer lethal concoctions against the living. To advance his morbid experiments, he enlists travelers to harvest animal reagents from the surrounding foothills.",h="In Tarren Mill, Apothecary Lydon pursues the Royal Apothecary Society's grim mandate to engineer lethal...",sec={{t="A Toxic Enterprise",b="While Tarren Mill serves as a military stronghold for the Forsaken in the Hillsbrad Foothills, it also functions as an active research station for the Royal Apothecary Society. Stationed amidst the scenic greenery, Apothecary Lydon despises the pristine countryside and yearns to see the human settlements poisoned and conquered. To manufacture his experimental 'Elixir of Suffering', he requires local biological agents known for their potency and virulence.",sp=0},{t="Gathering Reagents",b="Developing alchemical plagues demands precise ingredients. Lydon directs hunters into the wilds surrounding Tarren Mill to collect the tongues of native Gray Bears alongside rare ichor secreted by Moss Creepers. Once refined through unholy alchemy, these organic fluids form the foundation for a lethal mixture intended to eradicate living trespassers across Hillsbrad.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Apothecary Lydon?",a="Apothecary Lydon is a member of the Royal Apothecary Society stationed in Tarren Mill. True to Forsaken alchemical tradition, he despises the clean, living landscape of Hillsbrad and dedicates his time to synthesizing potent poisons to annihilate human populations.",al={"apothecary lydon","who gives elixir of suffering","lydon tarren mill"},it="identity"},{q="Why does Lydon need bear tongues and creeper ichor?",a="Lydon is researching virulent killing agents to brew into lethal concoctions. The biological properties of Gray Bear tongues and the caustic secretions of Moss Creepers provide the volatile alchemical base required for his new Elixir of Suffering.",al={"why bear tongues","what is creeper ichor for","elixir ingredients lore"},it="item"},{q="Where does this quest lead next?",a="Once the base reagents are delivered, Lydon blends them into a prototype brew. He then demands that the concoction be tested to measure its lethal efficacy on living subjects.",al={"next quest elixir of suffering","what happens after elixir of suffering"},sp=1,it="next_step"},{q="What is the goal of the Royal Apothecary Society in Hillsbrad?",a="The Society operates under Lady Sylvanas Windrunner's command to devise an alchemical plague capable of wiping out humanity and the Scourge alike. Tarren Mill serves as an ideal frontier outpost to harvest biological matter and test prototypes against local Alliance forces.",al={"why are apothecaries in hillsbrad","forsaken poison goals","hillsbrad plague"},it="purpose"},{q="Where can the necessary creatures be found?",a="Gray Bears roam widely throughout the central fields and forests of the Hillsbrad Foothills, while Moss Creepers skulk in the brush and wooded areas just outside Tarren Mill.",al={"where are gray bears","where are moss creepers","bear and spider locations"},gp=true},{q="Why is Lydon in such a bad mood?",a="Like many Forsaken alchemists, Lydon is disgusted by vitality, clean air, and thriving nature. He finds joy only in death, decay, and the successful distillation of deadly toxins.",al={"why is lydon unhappy","lydon clean air"}},{q="Why does Apothecary Lydon want this done?",a="Apothecary Lydon despises the pristine, living landscape of Hillsbrad Foothills and longs to see the local humans wiped out. He is conducting rigorous research to develop lethal chemical agents for the Royal Apothecary Society, striving to craft a concoction potent enough to unleash widespread death across the region.",al={"why does lydon want this done","lydon motive","why make the elixir of suffering"},it="motive",add=true},{q="Why does Apothecary Lydon need you to gather the ingredients?",a="Lydon is consumed by the meticulous theoretical work of compounding and refining new killing agents at his laboratory in Tarren Mill. With his research demanding constant oversight, he lacks the time to personally scour the surrounding wilds hunting bears and tracking elusive creepers.",al={"why cant lydon gather them","why does lydon need me","why hire an adventurer"},it="why_me",add=true}},ang={["race:Undead"]="For Forsaken operatives, assisting Lydon advances the Royal Apothecary Society's central ambition: creating a devastating weapon to secure their people's survival against living humanity.",["faction:Horde"]="While other Horde allies might balk at the cold ruthlessness of biological experimentation, securing Tarren Mill's frontier against Southshore necessitates trusting the Forsaken's alchemical warfare."},kw={"apothecary lydon","creeper ichor","elixir of suffering","gray bear tongue","hillsbrad foothills","royal apothecary society","tarren mill"},rel={"subzone:tarren-mill","zone:hillsbrad"},m={start="Apothecary Lydon",level="22",faction="Horde",id=496,ri={"Creeper Ichor","Gray Bear Tongue"}},src={"Elixir of Suffering (quest)"}}
E["quest:498"] = {t="quest",n="The Rescue",z="hillsbrad",s="The Rescue is an early Horde quest initiated by Krusk in Tarren Mill, tasking heroes with infiltrating Durnholde Keep to liberate captured orc scouts. Thrall's handpicked scouts were ambushed while seeking a relic of the Warchief's past, leaving them captive to the ruthless human criminals of the Syndicate.",h="The Rescue is an early Horde quest initiated by Krusk in Tarren Mill, tasking heroes with infiltrating...",sec={{t="A Scout Mission Gone Wrong",b="Warchief Thrall sent a select detachment of orc warriors to the Hillsbrad Foothills with orders to quietly investigate the rising Syndicate threat and recover an item tied closely to Durnholde Keep's history. Under the leadership of Gol'dir, the scouting party approached the fortress ruins. However, the Syndicate's sheer numbers overwhelmed them in an ambush. While the warrior Krusk managed to break free and limp back across the river to Tarren Mill, his companions Drull, Tog'thar, and Gol'dir were taken alive into human chains.",sp=0},{t="Chains in the Ruins",b="Durnholde holds bitter memories for the orcish people, having once served as the headquarters of Aedelas Blackmoore's internment camps where captive orcs were forced into lethargy and gladiatorial slavery. Finding their own warriors once again bound in iron within Durnholde's cracked stone walls is an unbearable insult to the Horde. To free Drull and Tog'thar, rescuers must confront the Syndicate jailors holding the keys to their shackles before uncovering what has become of their commanding scout, Gol'dir.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Why were orcs sent into Durnholde Keep in the first place?",a="Warchief Thrall dispatched Gol'dir and his scout cadre to investigate the Syndicate bandits and to secure an item from Durnholde's past that holds great personal significance to the Warchief.",al={"why were they there","why durnholde","krusk mission"},it="purpose"},{q="Who are the captives being rescued?",a="Drull and Tog'thar are orcish scouts sent by the Horde under the command of Gol'dir. They were overwhelmed and placed in ball-and-chain bonds by Syndicate brigands inside the ruins.",al={"who is drull","who is togthar","who are the hostages"},it="people"},{q="Where is the squad's leader, Gol'dir?",a="When Drull and Tog'thar are freed, Krusk discovers that their commander, Gol'dir, was separated from the main contingent and relocated by the Syndicate to an unknown second location.",al={"where is goldir","find goldir","what happened to goldir"},sp=1},{q="Who is holding the scouts captive?",a="They are held by the Syndicate, an aristocratic criminal network operating out of the ruins of Lordaeron and Alterac, guarded directly by Syndicate jailors inside Durnholde.",al={"who captured them","who are the jailors","who runs durnholde"},it="target"},{q="Where does this quest chain lead?",a="Freeing the scouts leads directly into a mission to track down and infiltrate the Syndicate to rescue Gol'dir, eventually uncovering Lord Aliden Perenolde's schemes and a token belonging to Taretha Foxton.",al={"what comes next","after the rescue","rescue chain"},sp=1,it="next_step"},{q="Why does Durnholde Keep hold special meaning to the Horde?",a="Durnholde was the fortress where Aedelas Blackmoore raised Thrall as a gladiator and commanded the Alliance internment camp system following the Second War until Thrall raised a rebellion and laid waste to the keep.",al={"history of durnholde","why horde cares about durnholde"},it="history"},{q="Why does Krusk need the captives rescued?",a="Krusk was part of the very reconnaissance squad ambushed inside Durnholde Keep. While he managed to fight his way free and flee back to Tarren Mill, his comrades Drull and Tog'thar were captured alive. He fears the Syndicate plans to reduce them to slaves—an intolerable fate in the very fortress where orcs were once held in bondage—and cannot abandon his fellow warriors to captivity and torture.",al={"why rescue drull and tog'thar","krusk motive","why help krusk"},it="motive",add=true}},ang={["race:Orc"]="Seeing orc warriors bound in shackles within Durnholde Keep cuts straight to the painful history of internment, making the mission to free them deeply personal.",["faction:Horde"]="The mission marks an early push by the Horde to counter Syndicate expansion across the contested hills of Lordaeron.",["class:Warrior"]="Breaking fellow frontline fighters out of captivity reinforces martial brotherhood against dishonorable human bandits."},kw={"drull","durnholde keep","gol'dir","hillsbrad","krusk","syndicate","tarren mill","tog'thar"},rel={"npc:krusk","subzone:durnholde-keep","subzone:tarren-mill","topic:syndicate","quest:549","topic:horde","zone:hillsbrad"},m={start="Krusk",level="22",faction="Horde",id=498},src={"The Rescue"}}
E["quest:499"] = {t="quest",n="Elixir of Suffering",z="hillsbrad",s="In Tarren Mill, Apothecary Lydon brews a venomous concoction intended to further the Royal Apothecary Society's sinister work. To confirm its lethality, he orders an immediate live trial on his unfortunate companion nearby.",h="In Tarren Mill, Apothecary Lydon brews a venomous concoction intended to further the Royal Apothecary...",sec={{t="A Toxic Test",b="Apothecary Lydon works tirelessly out of Tarren Mill to develop chemical weapons capable of fulfilling the Dark Lady's grand ambitions: a blight that will annihilate both the living humans of the Alliance and the undead horrors of the Scourge. Once the necessary reagents are gathered and steeped, Lydon mixes the foul brew into what he dubs the Elixir of Suffering, eager to witness its raw potency before deploying it on a broader scale.",sp=0},{t="The Fate of Umpi",b="Rather than seeking out an enemy captive or an escaped beast, Lydon turns directly to the creature beside him. He directs the adventurer to administer the freshly brewed poison to his assistant, Umpi—a harmless toad sitting quietly at his feet. A single dose of the elixir proves swiftly catastrophic, killing the amphibian on the spot and satisfying the apothecary that his deadly formula functions precisely as intended.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Who is Apothecary Lydon?",a="Apothecary Lydon is an alchemist representing the Royal Apothecary Society, stationed in the Forsaken settlement of Tarren Mill within the Hillsbrad Foothills. He spends his days refining poisons and alchemical mixtures designed to wipe out enemies of the Forsaken.",al={"lydon","who is lydon","apothecary lydon tarren mill"},it="identity"},{q="Who is Umpi?",a="Umpi is a simple toad perched right beside Apothecary Lydon's work table in Tarren Mill, jokingly designated by Lydon as his assistant.",al={"what is umpi","umpi the toad","who is the assistant"},it="target"},{q="What is the purpose of the Elixir of Suffering?",a="The Elixir of Suffering is an experimental chemical weapon developed to test toxic formulas meant to eradicate both living humans and the undead Scourge on behalf of Lady Sylvanas Windrunner.",al={"what does the elixir do","why make elixir of suffering"},it="purpose"},{q="What happens when you feed the potion to Umpi?",a="Upon drinking the toxic brew, Umpi croaks once and promptly drops dead, confirming the lethal efficacy of Lydon's creation.",al={"does umpi die","what happens to the toad"},sp=1},{q="Where does this test take place?",a="The test occurs inside the Forsaken town of Tarren Mill, located in northern Hillsbrad Foothills, right by Lydon's brewing station.",al={"where is lydon located","where do i find umpi"},it="place"},{q="Why does the Royal Apothecary Society test poisons on small animals?",a="Forsaken apothecaries routinely use small creatures and vermin for preliminary trials to verify the speed and lethality of their chemical compounds before advancing to field tests on larger targets or living captives.",al={"why test on toads","apothecary society animal testing"},it="history"},{q="Why does Apothecary Lydon want to test the Elixir of Suffering?",a="Apothecary Lydon seeks to verify whether his newly brewed concoction achieves its intended lethal effect. The Royal Apothecary Society works tirelessly under Lady Sylvanas to develop plagues capable of annihilating both the Scourge and living humanity, and field tests like this confirm whether their dark formulas are progressing as planned.",al={"why test the elixir of suffering","apothecary lydon motive","why does lydon want this done"},it="motive",add=true}},ang={["race:Undead"]="For the Forsaken, testing lethal toxins is essential business in fulfilling Lady Sylvanas's decree to eradicate both the Scourge and the living.",["faction:Horde"]="Allies visiting Tarren Mill get a chilling, firsthand glimpse into the ruthless alchemical methods practiced by the Royal Apothecary Society.",["class:Druid"]="A druid might find the casual, callous poisoning of a harmless amphibian in the name of Forsaken warfare deeply unsettling."},kw={"apothecary lydon","elixir of suffering","hillsbrad foothills","poison","royal apothecary society","tarren mill","toad","umpi"},rel={"quest:496","npc:umpi","subzone:tarren-mill","zone:hillsbrad","topic:scourge"},m={start="Apothecary Lydon",["end"]="Umpi",level="22",faction="Horde",id=499},src={"Elixir of Suffering (2)"}}
E["quest:501"] = {t="quest",n="Elixir of Pain",z="hillsbrad",s="Commissioned by Apothecary Lydon in Tarren Mill, this assignment tasks Horde adventurers with harvesting mountain lion blood to brew a lethal new concoction. It highlights the Royal Apothecary Society's grim dedication to perfecting their New Plague while despising the natural vitality of the Hillsbrad Foothills.",h="Commissioned by Apothecary Lydon in Tarren Mill, this assignment tasks Horde adventurers with harvesting...",sec={{t="A Bitter Outlook in Tarren Mill",b="While stationed inside Tarren Mill, Apothecary Lydon finds little joy in the surrounding landscape. Looking out past his window at the blooming meadows and brisk mountain air of Hillsbrad, he views the region's enduring life as an offense. Like many within the Royal Apothecary Society, his personal devotion is bound to Lady Sylvanas Windrunner and the perfection of the New Plague, an engineered scourge intended to bring death to the living and retribution to their enemies.",sp=0},{t="Ingredients for Misery",b="To engineer his latest poisonous mixture, Lydon turns to the local fauna prowling the foothills and the slopes toward the Alterac Mountains. Believing that mountain lion blood possesses specific properties vital for crafting what he calls an Elixir of Pain, he sends agents into the wilds to claim ten vials. The collection serves as the foundation for the Society's ongoing chemical trials along the contested southern front.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who gives the quest Elixir of Pain?",a="The quest is assigned by Apothecary Lydon, a Forsaken alchemist stationed within the settlement of Tarren Mill in the Hillsbrad Foothills.",al={"quest giver elixir of pain","who starts elixir of pain","apothecary lydon quest"},it="identity"},{q="Why does Apothecary Lydon need mountain lion blood?",a="Lydon's alchemical research suggests that mountain lion blood is an essential reagent for brewing a lethal new concoction, an elixir designed to advance the Royal Apothecary Society's plague experiments against their living enemies.",al={"why mountain lion blood","lion blood purpose","what is the blood for"},it="item"},{q="Where can the mountain lions be found?",a="Mountain lions prowl throughout the open fields and rolling hills of Hillsbrad Foothills, as well as along the higher bluffs leading into the Alterac Mountains.",al={"where are mountain lions","mountain lion locations hillsbrad","lion blood farming"},gp=true},{q="What is the New Plague Lydon mentions?",a="The New Plague is a biological weapon being meticulously researched and developed by the Forsaken's Royal Apothecary Society under the orders of Lady Sylvanas Windrunner, meant to eradicate both the Scourge and the living.",al={"what is the new plague","royal apothecary society plague","forsaken plague"},it="purpose"},{q="What comes next after completing this quest?",a="Handing in the ten vials of mountain lion blood leads directly into a follow-up task where Apothecary Lydon begins putting his newly brewed elixir to the test.",al={"elixir of pain next quest","follow up elixir of pain","what follows elixir of pain"},it="next_step"},{q="Why does Lydon despise Hillsbrad's scenery?",a="As an undead servant of the Dark Lady, Lydon resents the blooming flora, fresh air, and persistent vitality of the region, desiring instead to see the living world smothered by his Society's toxic creations.",al={"why does lydon hate hillsbrad","why is lydon brooding","lydon window quote"},it="motive"}},ang={["race:Undead"]="For Forsaken travelers, gathering reagents for Apothecary Lydon directly serves the mandate of the Dark Lady and the Royal Apothecary Society as they stake their claim in Lordaeron.",["faction:Horde"]="Allies of the Forsaken must navigate the grim methods of Tarren Mill's alchemists, aiding in the harvest of wild beasts to fortify Horde footholds against nearby human threats."},kw={"apothecary lydon","elixir of pain","hillsbrad foothills","mountain lion blood","new plague","royal apothecary society","tarren mill"},rel={"subzone:tarren-mill","zone:hillsbrad","topic:royal-apothecary-society","zone:alterac","subzone:hillsbrad-fields","topic:horde"},m={start="Apothecary Lydon",level="24",faction="Horde",id=501,ri={"Mountain Lion Blood"}},src={"Elixir of Pain (quest)"}}
E["quest:502"] = {t="quest",n="Elixir of Pain",z="hillsbrad",s="Commissioned by Apothecary Lydon in Tarren Mill, this quest tasks Horde agents with testing a newly brewed biological concoction known as the Elixir of Pain. The Forsaken apothecary selects Stanley, a pet dog belonging to Farmer Ray in the Hillsbrad Fields, as an unsuspecting test subject.",h="Commissioned by Apothecary Lydon in Tarren Mill, this quest tasks Horde agents with testing a newly brewed...",sec={{t="Apothecary Science",b="Operating out of Tarren Mill, Apothecary Lydon conducts experiments on behalf of the Royal Apothecary Society and Lady Sylvanas Windrunner. Utilizing fresh blood gathered from the local wildlife, Lydon concocts a volatile mixture he dubs the Elixir of Pain. Rather than relying purely on theoretical alchemy, the society requires empirical field data to observe the physiological effects of their experimental poisons and mutagens.",sp=0},{t="Testing on Stanley",b="To evaluate the draught without alarming the human defenders of Hillsbrad, Lydon directs his agents to target the northern farm in Hillsbrad Fields. There lives Stanley, a seemingly harmless pet dog kept by Farmer Ray. Approaching the unsuspecting canine with the draft poured into an open hand, the agent administers the dose under the guise of an ordinary treat.",sp=0},{t="Violent Mutation",b="The true nature of the Elixir of Pain manifests immediately upon ingestion. Instead of a straightforward lethal toxin, the concoction acts as a horrific mutagen, triggering instantaneous agony and violently warping Stanley's body into a savage, enraged wolf. The beast turns violently on anything nearby, proving the volatile efficacy of Lydon's alchemical formula.",sp=1}},faq={{q="What is the purpose of the Elixir of Pain?",a="Apothecary Lydon brewed the Elixir of Pain as part of the Royal Apothecary Society's ongoing efforts to engineer biological weapons and potent mutagens for Lady Sylvanas and the Forsaken.",al={"elixir of pain goal","why make elixir of pain","lydon elixir purpose"},it="purpose"},{q="Who is Stanley?",a="Stanley is a pet dog belonging to Farmer Ray, residing outside the large farmhouse at the northern end of Hillsbrad Fields.",al={"who is stanley","farmer ray dog","stanley the dog"},it="identity"},{q="What happens when you feed Stanley the elixir?",a="Consuming the elixir causes Stanley to mutate violently into a ferocious, rabid wolf that immediately turns hostile and attacks.",al={"stanley transformation","what does elixir do to dog","stanley wolf"},sp=1},{q="Where is Stanley located?",a="Stanley wanders outside the large house on the northern farm within the Hillsbrad Fields, southwest of Tarren Mill.",al={"find stanley","stanley location","where is farmer ray dog"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Who gives the quest to test the elixir?",a="Apothecary Lydon, stationed in the Forsaken settlement of Tarren Mill in the Hillsbrad Foothills, offers the quest after you gather the necessary reagents.",al={"elixir of pain questgiver","who gives elixir of pain","apothecary lydon quest"},it="in_charge",gp=true},{q="Why test the potion on a farmer's dog instead of humans?",a="Testing on a domestic pet in Hillsbrad Fields provides a quiet, accessible trial run without immediately alerting Hillsbrad's town militia or armed guards to the nature of the alchemical trial.",al={"why test on dog","why stanley","why poison dog"},it="motive"},{q="Why does Apothecary Lydon want the Elixir of Pain tested?",a="Apothecary Lydon believes this concoction could be the start of something monumental for Lady Sylvanas and the Royal Apothecary Society. Having mixed fresh mountain lion blood with his own vile additives, he needs practical field testing to prove whether his calculations hold true and see how living flesh reacts to the brew.",al={"why test the elixir of pain","apothecary lydon motive","why does lydon want this done"},it="motive",add=true},{q="Who are you sent to target with the elixir?",a="Your target is Stanley, a small pet dog belonging to Farmer Ray. Stanley resides on the northern homestead within the contested Hillsbrad Fields southwest of Tarren Mill. Instead of striking at the human farmers directly, Lydon has chosen this unsuspecting pet as an expendable subject to observe the elixir's volatile effects.",al={"who do i give the elixir to","elixir of pain target","who is the target"},it="target",add=true}},ang={["race:Undead"]="This experiment highlights the ruthless methodology of the Royal Apothecary Society, which seeks biological weapons to ensure the Forsaken's survival regardless of collateral damage.",["faction:Horde"]="Allies of the Forsaken are drawn directly into their grim chemical trials against the neighboring human farmlands of Hillsbrad.",["class:Hunter"]="Watching a gentle domestic pet violently warp into a savage, mutated predator illustrates the unnatural perversion of beast nature through Forsaken alchemy."},kw={"apothecary lydon","elixir of pain","farmer ray","hillsbrad fields","royal apothecary society","stanley","tarren mill"},rel={"quest:501","subzone:hillsbrad-fields","zone:hillsbrad"},m={start="Apothecary Lydon",["end"]="Stanley",level="24",faction="Horde",id=502},src={"Elixir of Pain (2)"}}
E["quest:509"] = {t="quest",n="Elixir of Agony",z="hillsbrad",s="In Tarren Mill, Apothecary Lydon enlists Horde adventurers to gather toxic fungi from an overrun farmstead in Hillsbrad Foothills. These virulent Mudsnout Blossoms serve as vital raw material for the Royal Apothecary Society's grim chemical experimentation. The resulting concoction is meant to aid Lady Sylvanas's long-term design to eradicate both the living and the Scourge.",h="In Tarren Mill, Apothecary Lydon enlists Horde adventurers to gather toxic fungi from an overrun farmstead in...",sec={{t="A Plague in the Making",b="While the Scourge ravages the north and the Alliance clings to towns like Southshore, the Forsaken pursue their own calculated solution: the development of a tailored, lethal plague. Operating from the chapel laboratories of Tarren Mill, Apothecary Lydon labors under the mandate of the Dark Lady. Though personally cynical about the tedious toil of alchemy, Lydon diligently gathers potent organic toxins from the surrounding countryside to brew elixirs capable of speeding along the mutual destruction of Sylvanas's enemies.",sp=0},{t="The Fields of Nethander Stead",b="South of Tarren Mill and east of the river lies Nethander Stead, an abandoned human farmstead now overrun by the vicious Mudsnout gnolls. Amid the filth and neglected soil, strange and foul-smelling mushrooms known as Mudsnout Blossoms flourish. These large, pungent growths hold concentrated organic poisons prized by the Royal Apothecary Society. Procuring them requires cutting through gnoll packs or quietly weaving past their ramshackle camps.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Apothecary Lydon?",a="Apothecary Lydon is an alchemist of the Royal Apothecary Society stationed at Tarren Mill in Hillsbrad Foothills. Working on behalf of Lady Sylvanas Windrunner, his duties focus on refining lethal mixtures and developing a new plague to defeat both living mortals and the Scourge.",al={"lydon","who is lydon","apothecary lydon lore"},it="identity"},{q="What are Mudsnout Blossoms used for?",a="Mudsnout Blossoms are noxious, foul-smelling mushrooms harvested from Nethander Stead. Apothecary Lydon uses their potent, natural toxic properties as a base ingredient to brew the Elixir of Agony, part of the Forsaken's broader chemical and biological warfare research.",al={"mudsnout blossoms","what are the mushrooms for","blossom use"},it="item"},{q="Where is Nethander Stead located?",a="Nethander Stead is an overgrown farmstead situated south of Tarren Mill, east of the major river that runs past Southshore. The farm has been claimed by aggressive Mudsnout gnolls who guard the fields where the mushrooms grow.",al={"nethander stead location","where is nethander stead","where are the gnolls"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Why do the Forsaken want to create a new plague?",a="Lady Sylvanas and the Forsaken seek a weapon powerful enough to eliminate both the relentless Scourge and the hostile living races of the Alliance. By engineering their own plague, the Royal Apothecary Society aims to secure the sovereignty and survival of the Forsaken in Lordaeron.",al={"why make a plague","forsaken plague reason","sylvanas plague"},it="history"},{q="Why does Lydon complain about having to brew these elixirs?",a="Lydon is somewhat weary and morbid, observing that the humans and the Scourge are already bent on slaughtering each other without outside help. However, because Lady Sylvanas wants to accelerate their mutual destruction, he follows orders and continues concocting deadly brews.",al={"lydon attitude","why is lydon cynical"},it="motive"},{q="What happens after collecting the blossoms?",a="Once Lydon receives the Mudsnout Blossoms, he proceeds with brewing the toxic mixture and soon requires additional ingredients and field testing to ensure the elixir reaches maximum lethal potency.",al={"next quest","what follows elixir of agony"},it="next_step"},{q="Who guards the Mudsnout Blossoms at Nethander Stead?",a="The fields of Nethander Stead have been overrun by Mudsnout gnolls. These filthy creatures cultivate or fiercely guard the pungent fungi growing across the farmstead, making any gathering run a hazardous venture into their claimed territory.",al={"what guards mudsnout blossoms","nethander stead enemies","mudsnout gnolls"},it="target",add=true}},ang={["race:Undead"]="For Forsaken agents, assisting Lydon contributes directly to the Royal Apothecary Society's vital work in defending Lordaeron from humanity and the Lich King alike.",["profession:Herbalism"]="Herbalists and foragers will recognize the Mudsnout Blossom as a rare, extraordinarily toxic fungal specimen thriving in unworked soil tainted by gnoll habitation.",["faction:Horde"]="Horde emissaries operating in Tarren Mill must balance assisting their Forsaken allies with the unsettling reality of their chemical experimentation."},kw={"apothecary lydon","elixir of agony","hillsbrad","mudsnout blossom","nethander stead","new plague","royal apothecary society","tarren mill"},rel={"zone:hillsbrad","subzone:tarren-mill","subzone:nethander-stead","quest:367","topic:gnoll","topic:scourge","subzone:southshore","topic:horde"},m={start="Apothecary Lydon",["end"]="Apothecary Lydon",level="28",faction="Horde",id=509,ri={"Mudsnout Blossom"}},src={"Elixir of Agony"}}
E["quest:517"] = {t="quest",n="Elixir of Agony",z="hillsbrad",s="This quest is the fourth chapter in Apothecary Lydon's relentless development of a devastating Forsaken poison in Tarren Mill. With the deadly Elixir of Agony finally brewed, Lydon dispatches Horde champions to Dun Garok to steal a keg of dwarven Shindigger Stout for delivery.",h="This quest is the fourth chapter in Apothecary Lydon's relentless development of a devastating Forsaken...",sec={{t="A Bitter Brew",b="In the damp reaches of Tarren Mill, Apothecary Lydon works tirelessly on behalf of the Royal Apothecary Society and Lady Sylvanas. Having gathered lethal ingredients from across Hillsbrad, his new concoction is complete. Lydon has no interest in wasting such a potent strain on trivial creatures like frogs or stray dogs; he seeks a real, tangible test against living adversaries.",sp=0},{t="Infiltrating Dun Garok",b="To stage his experiment, Lydon needs an inconspicuous delivery vehicle. South of Hillsbrad, the Ironforge dwarves have fortified the stronghold of Dun Garok. Lydon directs agents of the Horde to infiltrate the underground barracks and mess halls, slipping past dwarven rifles and axes to purloin a prized keg of Shindigger Stout.",sp=0},{t="A Recipe for Disaster",b="Lydon intends to blend his lethal toxin straight into the dwarves' favorite brew. Once infused into the stolen keg, the elixir can be unleashed upon an unwitting target under the guise of festive refreshment, turning a beloved dwarven stout into an instrument of horrific agony.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Who is Apothecary Lydon?",a="Apothecary Lydon is a Forsaken alchemist stationed in Tarren Mill. Representing the Royal Apothecary Society, he conducts experiments to develop deadly plagues and elixirs for the Banshee Queen, Lady Sylvanas.",al={"lydon","who gives this quest","apothecary lydon lore"},it="identity"},{q="Why does Lydon need a keg of Shindigger Stout?",a="Lydon wants to test the finished Elixir of Agony on living targets. By blending the toxin into a keg of popular dwarven ale, he creates a covert and potent delivery method to poison his victims.",al={"why dwarven beer","why shindigger stout","purpose of the keg"},it="item"},{q="Where is Dun Garok located?",a="Dun Garok is a heavily fortified dwarven redoubt situated in southeastern Hillsbrad Foothills, manned by Ironforge mountaineers and riflemen guarding their northern interests.",al={"where is dun garok","dun garok location","where do i find the keg"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Who is Umpi?",a="Umpi is Apothecary Lydon's assistant in Tarren Mill. Lydon playfully notes that opening jars of formaldehyde around the lab tends to make Umpi visibly nervous.",al={"umpi","who is umpi","lydon assistant"},it="allies"},{q="What is the ultimate goal of the Elixir of Agony?",a="The Elixir of Agony is an experimental poison engineered by the Royal Apothecary Society to eradicate the living, serving the Forsaken's campaign to secure Lordaeron from human and dwarven footholds.",al={"what does elixir of agony do","plague purpose","forsaken poison goal"},it="motive"},{q="What comes next after retrieving the keg?",a="Once the keg is in hand, Lydon laces the Shindigger Stout with the toxic elixir and tasks you with delivering the tainted ale to an unsuspecting test subject.",al={"next quest","what after dun garok","elixir part 5"},sp=1,it="next_step"},{q="Who are you sent against at Dun Garok?",a="You are sent to infiltrate Dun Garok, a heavily fortified dwarf outpost in the southeastern Hillsbrad Foothills. The Stormpike mountaineers and riflemen stationed there belong to the Alliance, defending dwarven interests in the region and posing an ongoing threat to the Forsaken presence in Tarren Mill.",al={"dun garok dwarves","who is at dun garok","who guards the stout"},it="target",add=true}},ang={["race:Undead"]="Every batch perfected by Lydon brings the Forsaken closer to weaponizing death against the living enemies encroaching on Lordaeron.",["race:Dwarf"]="The desecration of traditional dwarven ale into a vessel for chemical slaughter represents a profound insult to Ironforge craftsmanship.",["faction:Horde"]="Undermining the Alliance presence at Dun Garok helps Tarren Mill maintain a delicate foothold against relentless southern threats.",["class:Rogue"]="Slipping through the crowded mess halls of Dun Garok unseen is a masterclass in covert thievery right under the mountaineers' noses."},kw={"apothecary lydon","dun garok","dwarves","elixir of agony","hillsbrad","shindigger stout","tarren mill","umpi"},rel={"quest:509","subzone:tarren-mill","subzone:dun-garok","zone:hillsbrad","npc:umpi","topic:horde"},m={start="Apothecary Lydon",level="30",faction="Horde",id=517,ri={"Keg of Shindigger Stout"}},src={"Elixir of Agony (4)"}}
E["quest:524"] = {t="quest",n="Elixir of Agony",z="hillsbrad",s="Elixir of Agony is the culmination of Apothecary Lydon's sinister brewing experiments in Tarren Mill. Tasked by the Royal Apothecary Society, Lydon seeks to test a deadly poison disguised as stolen dwarven ale on human prisoners held within the settlement.",h="Elixir of Agony is the culmination of Apothecary Lydon's sinister brewing experiments in Tarren Mill.",sec={{t="A Deadly Vintage",b="Throughout the Hillsbrad Foothills, Apothecary Lydon gathers foul ingredients and purloined dwarven ale from the mountain fortress of Dun Garok. His purpose is singular and ruthless: concocting a virulent new brew known as the Elixir of Agony under the mandate of the Royal Apothecary Society. Once mixed, the dark mixture sits inside a seemingly innocent keg of mountain stout, waiting to demonstrate its potency.",sp=0},{t="Unfortunate Guests",b="The Deathguards in Tarren Mill recently rounded up local human farmers, originally suspecting an elusive military strategist from Stormwind was hiding among their ranks. When news arrived that the strategist had perished out in the Plaguelands, High Executor Darthalia deemed the surviving farm folk useless to military intelligence. Rather than setting them free, she gifted them to Lydon to serve as guinea pigs for his chemical trials.",sp=1},{t="Testing the Brew",b="Carried upstairs to the holding room, the tainted keg is set upon a dusty rug before the parched captives. Thirsty and completely unaware of Lydon's cruelty, the farmers eagerly rush the barrel to drink. The poison acts with terrifying speed: mere moments after partaking of the dwarven brew, the unfortunate captives collapse and die instantly, proving the elixir's devastating lethality.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Why were the human farmers captured in the first place?",a="Deathguards detained them under suspicion that a military strategist from the Kingdom of Stormwind had embedded himself within their community. Once the strategist turned up dead in the Plaguelands, the captives lost any intelligence value to High Executor Darthalia.",al={"why prisoners","why farmers locked up","tarren mill prisoners"},it="target"},{q="Who is Apothecary Lydon?",a="Apothecary Lydon is a member of the Forsaken's Royal Apothecary Society stationed in Tarren Mill. He develops and tests lethal blights and poisons intended to eradicate the living, often using captured locals as live subjects.",al={"apothecary lydon lore","who is lydon","lydon tarren mill"},it="identity"},{q="Where did the ale inside the keg come from?",a="The ale was stolen directly from the dwarves of Dun Garok, a stout mountain stronghold in southern Hillsbrad Foothills. Lydon tainted the stolen barrel with his noxious reagents so the deadly poison appeared to be ordinary dwarven brew.",al={"source of the ale","dun garok ale","keg origin"},it="item"},{q="What happens when you deliver the tainted keg?",a="When the tainted keg is placed on the rug in their holding room, the thirsty human farmers immediately rush toward it and drink. Within seconds, the toxic concoction takes effect, killing all of them on the spot.",al={"what happens to the farmers","farmers drink keg","plagued brew result"},sp=1},{q="Who authorized using the prisoners as test subjects?",a="High Executor Darthalia, commander of the Forsaken forces in Tarren Mill, handed the surviving prisoners over to Apothecary Lydon once she had no military use for them.",al={"who let lydon test on farmers","darthalia role","darthalia prisoners"},it="in_charge"},{q="What is the Royal Apothecary Society trying to achieve here?",a="The Royal Apothecary Society works relentlessly to craft a deadly blight capable of annihilating both the Scourge and the living. Field experiments like the Elixir of Agony test new chemical delivery methods and determine toxicity levels on human biology.",al={"apothecary goals hillsbrad","why make elixir of agony","forsaken blight testing"},it="purpose"},{q="Why does Apothecary Lydon want to poison the prisoners?",a="Apothecary Lydon needs live human subjects to verify the lethal efficacy of his newly completed Elixir of Agony. The Royal Apothecary Society constantly strives to refine deadly plagues and toxins to eradicate humanity and the Scourge alike. Now that High Executor Darthalia no longer needs the captured farmers for interrogation, Lydon views them as convenient, expendable test subjects to confirm that his brew functions as intended before reporting his success.",al={"why poison the farmers","lydon motive","why test the elixir of agony","why does lydon want this done"},it="motive",add=true}},ang={["race:Undead"]="For the Forsaken, perfecting the Royal Apothecary Society's poisons is paramount to survival, securing Hillsbrad Foothills from human resurgence by any means necessary.",["race:Human"]="The slaughter of helpless Lordaeron farmers highlights the cold, calculated ruthlessness with which the Forsaken treat their former living kin.",["faction:Horde"]="This grim experiment showcases the darker, unvarnished aspects of Forsaken operations, testing the moral stomach of other Horde races assisting Tarren Mill."},kw={"apothecary lydon","captured farmers","dun garok","elixir of agony","high executor darthalia","hillsbrad","tainted keg","tarren mill"},rel={"quest:509","npc:high-executor-darthalia","zone:hillsbrad","subzone:dun-garok","topic:stormwind-kingdom","topic:horde"},m={start="Apothecary Lydon",["end"]="Dusty Rug",level="30",faction="Horde",id=524},src={"Elixir of Agony (5)"}}
E["quest:527"] = {t="quest",n="Battle of Hillsbrad",z="hillsbrad",s="Battle of Hillsbrad is the opening strike in the Forsaken campaign to eradicate the human settlement of Hillsbrad. Handed down by High Executor Darthalia under orders from Varimathras, this mission targets the farmers and infrastructure of the northern Hillsbrad Fields to sever the town's food supply.",h="Battle of Hillsbrad is the opening strike in the Forsaken campaign to eradicate the human settlement of...",sec={{t="Starving the Resistance",b="Tarren Mill stands as the southern spearhead of the Forsaken empire, facing an entrenched human populace clinging to the Hillsbrad Foothills. High Executor Darthalia operates under strict directives straight from Varimathras in the Undercity. Her strategy is total attrition: before marching directly on the heavily defended town of Hillsbrad, she orders the systematic disruption of its agriculture. Striking the northern fields deprives the human militia of critical provisions while sowing chaos across their homesteads.",sp=0},{t="A Delaying Action",b="The broader campaign against the human presence in Hillsbrad serves a grim tactical purpose. While the Forsaken armies pin down and bleed the local defenders, the Royal Apothecary Society works tirelessly to concoct a new plague capable of eradicating the living and Scourge alike. High Executor Darthalia views these early skirmishes—and the deaths of local landowners like Farmer Ray and Farmer Getz—as necessary steps to suppress the human infestation until that ultimate weapon is ready to deploy.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Why are the Forsaken attacking simple farmers?",a="The human farmers and farmhands in the Hillsbrad Fields form the logistical foundation of the town of Hillsbrad. By burning through their workforce and slaying prominent landowners like Farmer Ray and Farmer Getz, the Forsaken cut off the human garrison's food supply and weaken their defenses before a direct assault.",al={"why kill farmers","hillsbrad farm targets","why attack farms"},it="motive"},{q="Who orders this attack?",a="High Executor Darthalia, the Forsaken military commander stationed at Tarren Mill, issues the mission. She serves under the direct command of the dreadlord Varimathras and Lady Sylvanas Windrunner.",al={"who gives quest","darthalia orders","who is darthalia"},it="in_charge"},{q="What is the Royal Apothecary Society's role in this campaign?",a="Darthalia notes that conventional warfare against the humans is meant to quell the living population and buy time while Forsaken apothecaries develop a new plague designed to eliminate their enemies entirely.",al={"why the new plague","apothecaries hillsbrad","forsaken plague plan"},it="ties"},{q="Where are Farmer Ray and Farmer Getz located?",a="Both landowners oversee the northern section of the Hillsbrad Fields. Farmer Ray is typically found near the large farmhouse or working in the garden just east of it, while Farmer Getz frequents the barn, the secondary house, or the surrounding tilled plots.",al={"find farmer ray","find farmer getz","ray and getz location"},it="place",gp=true},{q="What happens after completing this raid?",a="Returning victorious to Darthalia advances the assault onto the southern fields and the town of Hillsbrad itself, while also opening side operations like collecting grim trophies in Souvenirs of Death.",al={"battle of hillsbrad follow up","what comes next","chain progression"},it="next_step"},{q="Why does Darthalia threaten her soldiers?",a="High Executor Darthalia demands absolute discipline and ruthlessness. She views any hesitation or levity regarding the war with the Alliance as treason punishable by immediate execution on the spot.",al={"darthalia dialogue","darthalia beheading threat"}},{q="Who are you sent against in Hillsbrad Fields?",a="You are dispatched against the human farmers and farmhands working the northern plots of Hillsbrad Fields, specifically targeting landowners Farmer Ray and Farmer Getz. These residents form the backbone of the region's agricultural infrastructure, cultivating crops and livestock that sustain the nearby human settlement of Hillsbrad and the Alliance forces holding the area.",al={"battle of hillsbrad targets","who are we attacking in hillsbrad","who are farmer ray and getz"},it="target",add=true}},ang={["race:Undead"]="For the Forsaken, reclaiming Lordaeron means wiping away every surviving pocket of the living who treat their homeland as stolen ground.",["faction:Horde"]="While Thrall preaches honor, the northern campaign run out of Tarren Mill reveals the uncompromising brutality of Sylvanas's war against the Alliance.",["faction:Alliance"]="The slaughter of the northern homesteaders demonstrates the terrifying reality facing the remaining human enclaves in Lordaeron."},kw={"battle of hillsbrad","darthalia","farmer getz","farmer ray","hillsbrad fields","new plague","tarren mill","varimathras"},rel={"npc:high-executor-darthalia","subzone:hillsbrad-fields","subzone:tarren-mill","zone:hillsbrad","npc:varimathras","quest:546","topic:horde","topic:alliance"},m={start="High Executor Darthalia",level="24",faction="Horde",id=527},src={"Battle of Hillsbrad (quest)"}}
E["quest:528"] = {t="quest",n="Battle of Hillsbrad",z="hillsbrad",s="Battle of Hillsbrad is a Forsaken military mission directed by High Executor Darthalia from Tarren Mill. Following the initial strikes on the northern human farms, Horde operatives are sent south to slaughter the fleeing Hillsbrad Peasants seeking refuge in the orchards.",h="Battle of Hillsbrad is a Forsaken military mission directed by High Executor Darthalia from Tarren Mill.",sec={{t="Sowing Terror in the Fields",b="The campaign against the human presence in Hillsbrad Foothills moves with cold deliberation. After Horde forces strike the northern farms, panic sweeps through the settlement. Rather than taking up arms, many laborers flee southward into the orchards and pastures of Hillsbrad Fields, hoping to hide from the advancing undead. High Executor Darthalia views their terror not with mercy, but as a strategic opening to break Hillsbrad's remaining labor force and morale completely.",sp=0},{t="The Dark Lady's Advance",b="Under direct orders from Tarren Mill, champions of the Horde hunt down these displaced laborers in the fields. Deprived of protection, the peasants are systematically eliminated to choke off Hillsbrad's food supply and shatter civilian resolve. For Darthalia and the Forsaken, every human felled tightens the grip of death around the surviving township, ensuring that Lordaeron remains firmly in the hands of the Forsaken.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Why are the Forsaken targeting simple peasants?",a="Targeting the peasants destroys the agrarian backbone that feeds the Hillsbrad settlement. By killing the laborers hiding in the southern orchards, High Executor Darthalia ensures the town descends further into panic and starves, making ultimate conquest far easier.",al={"why kill peasants","why target farmers","darthalia peasant plan"},it="motive"},{q="Who orders this assault?",a="High Executor Darthalia, the Forsaken commander stationed at Tarren Mill, commands the entire military effort against the local human settlements in the name of Lady Sylvanas Windrunner.",al={"who gives battle of hillsbrad 2","quest giver battle of hillsbrad","darthalia orders"},it="in_charge"},{q="Where did these peasants flee from?",a="They fled from the northern farms of Hillsbrad following earlier Horde strikes. Panicked and defenseless, they took refuge among the trees and pastures of the southern Hillsbrad Fields.",al={"where are peasants coming from","northern farms hillsbrad"},it="origin"},{q="Where can the fleeing peasants be found?",a="The peasants are scattered across the southern orchards and pastures of Hillsbrad Fields, just south of the main road running through the foothills.",al={"hillsbrad peasant location","where are hillsbrad peasants"},it="place",gp=true},{q="What comes after killing the peasants?",a="With the southern fields cleared of laborers, High Executor Darthalia escalates the campaign to target Blacksmith Verringtan and the smithy arming Hillsbrad's defenders, bringing the fight ever closer to the town center.",al={"what is next after peasants","battle of hillsbrad next step"},sp=1,it="next_step"},{q="Why is the Horde fighting so ruthlessly here?",a="The human town of Hillsbrad represents one of the final remaining Alliance strongholds in Lordaeron. The Forsaken regard the region as their rightful sovereign territory and seek to expel or eliminate any Alliance enclaves that threaten their southern border.",al={"why horde attacking hillsbrad","forsaken vs hillsbrad war"},it="conflict"},{q="Who are the Hillsbrad Peasants?",a="They are the human commoners of Hillsbrad who fled the initial assault on the northern farms. Terrified by the advancing Forsaken, they scattered south into the orchards of the Hillsbrad Fields hoping to hide from the slaughter, but Darthalia's scouts quickly uncovered their refuge.",al={"hillsbrad peasants","who are the peasants","peasants in orchards"},it="target",add=true}},ang={["race:Undead"]="For the Forsaken, this purge is practical and uncompromising: eliminating the living laborers denies the Alliance sustenance and cements the Dark Lady's dominion over southern Lordaeron.",["faction:Horde"]="Tarren Mill serves as the Horde's vital bastion in the foothills. Breaking Hillsbrad ensures Horde lines of communication and supply remain secure against Alliance incursions.",["faction:Alliance"]="The slaughter of unarmed refugees in the southern orchards underscores the ruthless, total war waged by the Forsaken against Lordaeron's remaining living subjects."},kw={"battle of hillsbrad","dark lady","darthalia","deathstalkers","forsaken","hillsbrad fields","hillsbrad peasants","tarren mill"},rel={"npc:high-executor-darthalia","subzone:hillsbrad-fields","subzone:tarren-mill","zone:hillsbrad"},m={start="High Executor Darthalia",["end"]="High Executor Darthalia",level="25",faction="Horde",id=528},src={"Battle of Hillsbrad (2)"}}
E["quest:529"] = {t="quest",n="Battle of Hillsbrad",z="hillsbrad",s="This operation represents a critical phase in the Forsaken campaign to conquer the Hillsbrad Foothills. High Executor Darthalia orders the destruction of the local smithy in Hillsbrad Fields to cut off the weapons arming the stubborn human populace.",h="This operation represents a critical phase in the Forsaken campaign to conquer the Hillsbrad Foothills.",sec={{t="Breaking the Anvil",b="The Forsaken push across the Hillsbrad Foothills faced fiercer resistance than High Executor Darthalia anticipated. The rural humans refused to simply scatter or yield to the Deathstalkers and soldiers sent from Tarren Mill. Investigation revealed that the local peasantry were not fighting with simple pitchforks and scythes; they were actively being outfitted for war right in the fields.",sp=0},{t="Severing the Supply Line",b="At the southwest edge of the Hillsbrad Fields, Blacksmith Verringtan and his apprentices worked tirelessly at their forge, turning raw ore into blades and armor for the militia. By dispatching an operative to eliminate Verringtan, butcher his apprentices, and seize their stockpiled iron shipment, Darthalia aimed to cripple the settlement's defense while redirecting their metal toward the eventual assault on Southshore.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Why does High Executor Darthalia target the blacksmith specifically?",a="The human townsfolk and farmers are offering unexpected military resistance to the Forsaken advance. Darthalia discovered that Blacksmith Verringtan and his apprentices are actively forging weapons for the militia, turning ordinary peasants into an armed threat.",al={"why kill verringtan","blacksmith objective","verringtan quest"},it="motive"},{q="Where is the smithy located?",a="The smithy stands on the southwestern side of the Hillsbrad Fields, surrounded by working apprentices, guards, and local patrols.",al={"verringtan location","where is the blacksmith","hillsbrad smithy"},it="place",gp=true},{q="What is the shipment of iron used for?",a="Darthalia confiscates the iron to feed the Forsaken war machine. She intends to use these captured raw materials to forge weapons and supplies for the planned assault against the Alliance harbor town of Southshore.",al={"what happens to the iron","iron shipment lore"},it="item"},{q="How does this fit into the broader Battle of Hillsbrad campaign?",a="It marks the third stage of Darthalia's systematic effort to dismantle the human presence in the foothills, transitioning from culling rural laborers and farmers to stripping away their leadership, logistics, and production capacity.",al={"battle of hillsbrad chain","darthalia campaign"},it="purpose"},{q="Are the people in Hillsbrad Fields part of the Alliance military?",a="While culturally aligned with Southshore and the Alliance, the inhabitants of the fields are primarily local farmers, laborers, and townsfolk who formed an ad-hoc militia to defend their homes from the Forsaken.",al={"are hillsbrad farmers alliance","hillsbrad militia"},it="people"},{q="Who orders this strike?",a="High Executor Darthalia, the commanding military officer overseeing Forsaken operations from the stronghold of Tarren Mill.",al={"quest giver","who is darthalia"},it="leader"},{q="Who is Blacksmith Verringtan?",a="Blacksmith Verringtan is the local metalworker stationed at the smithy on the southwest edge of the Hillsbrad Fields. Alongside his apprentices, he manufactures weapons and tools for the local human populace, fueling their fierce resistance against the Forsaken push into the foothills.",al={"who is verringtan","blacksmith verringtan","hillsbrad blacksmith"},it="target",add=true}},ang={["race:Undead"]="For the Forsaken, breaking the human smithy is a pragmatic step toward securing Lordaeron's southern borders and stockpiling metal for their own struggling war effort.",["faction:Alliance"]="The slaughter of Verringtan and the theft of the settlement's iron strips Southshore's outlying farms of their only means of self-defense.",["profession:Blacksmithing"]="Verringtan's forge served as the beating heart of local resistance, proving that an anvil can be as dangerous to an invading army as a regiment of footmen."},kw={"apprentice blacksmith","battle of hillsbrad","darthalia","hillsbrad fields","shipment of iron","tarren mill","verringtan"},rel={"npc:high-executor-darthalia","subzone:hillsbrad-fields","subzone:tarren-mill","subzone:southshore","zone:hillsbrad"},m={start="High Executor Darthalia",level="26",faction="Horde",id=529,ri={"Shipment of Iron"}},src={"Battle of Hillsbrad (3)"}}
E["quest:532"] = {t="quest",n="Battle of Hillsbrad",z="hillsbrad",s="This critical phase of the Forsaken campaign against Southshore's surrounding holdings targets the civic leadership of Hillsbrad town. Directed by High Executor Darthalia from Tarren Mill, Horde forces strike at Magistrate Burnside, his council, and their administrative records to completely shatter human governance in the foothills.",h="This critical phase of the Forsaken campaign against Southshore's surrounding holdings targets the civic...",sec={{t="Decapitating the Town Council",b="Even after suffering severe casualties across their fields and patrols, the human defenders of Hillsbrad cling to their remaining civil authority. High Executor Darthalia recognizes that ordinary peasants and militia rally behind their civic leaders. To ensure the town completely collapses, Forsaken operatives are dispatched directly into the Town Hall to execute Magistrate Burnside and five of his councilmen, severing the chain of command.",sp=0},{t="Erasing the Civic Record",b="Beyond physical assassinations, Darthalia seeks the total psychological and administrative dismantling of Hillsbrad. Operatives must burn the Hillsbrad Proclamation, a revered political document that symbolizes the settlement's charter and pride. Alongside its destruction, the town registry is seized, depriving the surviving Alliance loyalists of their official records and citizen registries while giving Undercity intelligence detailed insight into the local populace.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who orders this strike?",a="High Executor Darthalia, the Forsaken commander stationed at Tarren Mill, orchestrates the assault as part of her broader campaign to wipe Alliance settlements from the foothills.",al={"who gives this quest","quest giver battle of hillsbrad","darthalia hillsbrad"},it="in_charge"},{q="Who is Magistrate Burnside?",a="Magistrate Burnside is the magistrate and political leader of the human town of Hillsbrad. Stationed inside the town hall alongside his councilors, he uses arcane magic to defend the remaining authority of the settlement.",al={"magistrate burnside","who is burnside","hillsbrad leader"},it="identity"},{q="What is the Hillsbrad Proclamation?",a="The Hillsbrad Proclamation is an esteemed political charter kept prominently within the Town Hall. It embodies the legal governance and spirit of the town's people, making its destruction a devastating blow to civic morale.",al={"what is the proclamation","hillsbrad proclamation lore","destroy proclamation"}},{q="Why does Darthalia want the town registry?",a="The town registry contains a full census and civic documentation of Hillsbrad's population. Stealing it strips the surviving humans of their administrative memory while offering the Forsaken vital intelligence on who remains in the area.",al={"why steal registry","hillsbrad town registry","what does registry do"},it="why_wanted"},{q="Where does this fight take place?",a="The targets reside in and around the large Town Hall building situated within the human settlement of Hillsbrad, located in the southern foothills between Tarren Mill and Southshore.",al={"where is magistrate burnside","hillsbrad town hall location","where are councilmen"},it="place",gp=true},{q="What role do the councilmen play?",a="The Hillsbrad Councilmen serve as the governing body aiding Magistrate Burnside. They are capable spellcasters who defend both the interior of the Town Hall and its surrounding grounds.",al={"hillsbrad councilmen","who are councilmen"},it="threat"},{q="Why does High Executor Darthalia want this done?",a="The town of Hillsbrad is in disarray after repeated Forsaken strikes, but its human defenders refuse to surrender so long as their local leadership holds. High Executor Darthalia intends to break their spirit entirely and wipe them from the foothills forever. By assassinating Magistrate Burnside and the council, destroying their revered Hillsbrad Proclamation, and seizing their records, she aims to shatter the remaining structure keeping Hillsbrad Fields organized.",al={"why attack hillsbrad leadership","darthalia motive battle of hillsbrad","why does darthalia want burnside dead"},it="motive",add=true},{q="Who are you sent against in Hillsbrad?",a="You are sent to assassinate Magistrate Burnside and five of his councilmen within the Hillsbrad town hall. Despite severe casualties across the fields and orchards, Burnside and his council continue to organize the local defense and rally the human populace against Tarren Mill. Striking down their magistrate and political council strips the town of its governing authority.",al={"who are we killing in hillsbrad","battle of hillsbrad target","who is magistrate burnside and council"},it="target",add=true},{q="What is the Hillsbrad Town Registry for?",a="The Hillsbrad Town Registry is the official civic record documenting the local populace and property of Hillsbrad. Seizing it deprives the surviving humans of their administrative census while granting High Executor Darthalia comprehensive intelligence on every resident, property owner, and taxpayer in the settlement.",al={"what is hillsbrad town registry","hillsbrad registry purpose","why steal town registry"},it="item",add=true}},ang={["faction:Horde"]="Striking the town hall cripples the Alliance's ability to coordinate local militia, firmly securing Tarren Mill's southern frontier against human counterattacks.",["race:Undead"]="For the Forsaken, eradicating Hillsbrad's human governance is both strategic expansion and ruthless retribution against the living who dispute Lordaeron's borders.",["faction:Alliance"]="The slaughter of Magistrate Burnside and the burning of the town charter mark the catastrophic fall of Hillsbrad's last legitimate local government."},kw={"battle of hillsbrad","darthalia","hillsbrad councilmen","hillsbrad proclamation","hillsbrad town registry","magistrate burnside","tarren mill","town hall"},rel={"npc:high-executor-darthalia","subzone:tarren-mill","zone:hillsbrad"},m={start="High Executor Darthalia",level="26",faction="Horde",id=532,ri={"Hillsbrad Town Registry"}},src={"Battle of Hillsbrad (4)"}}
E["quest:536"] = {t="quest",n="Down the Coast",z="hillsbrad",s="Down the Coast is an Alliance task given by Lieutenant Farren Orinelle in Southshore. Deeply unhappy with his frontier transfer from Stormwind, the guard lieutenant prefers drinking ale to patrolling and hires adventurers to clear out the Torn Fin murlocs encroaching along the Western Strand.",h="Down the Coast is an Alliance task given by Lieutenant Farren Orinelle in Southshore.",sec={{t="A Reluctant Posting",b="Lieutenant Farren Orinelle was reassigned from the polished stone streets of the Stormwind city guard to the remote, salty port of Southshore. Finding the town dreary and its fishy harbor odor unbearable, Orinelle spends his days nursing drinks at the local inn rather than patrolling the frontlines. When ordered by Marshal Marcus Redpath to protect Southshore from the surrounding dangers, Orinelle chooses to subcontract his duties to passing sellswords instead.",sp=0},{t="The Torn Fin Threat",b="The task itself focuses on the Western Strand, the coastline stretching west from Southshore. While Orinelle scoffs at the threat of 'overgrown fish,' the Torn Fin tribe of murlocs poses a genuine hazard to coastal travel and local shipping. Gathering in tightly packed camps along the breakers, their tidehunters and mystical oracles readily ambush anyone straying too far from town walls, making clearing the shoreline a bloody undertaking.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Why doesn't Farren Orinelle deal with the murlocs himself?",a="Farren considers Southshore an unwanted exile from his former life in the Stormwind city guard. Resentful of his posting and disgusted by the coastal town, he would rather sit in the tavern drinking ale than march into the surf to fight murlocs, prompting him to pay adventurers to do his job.",al={"why is farren drinking","farren orinelle personality","why hire adventurers"},it="why_me"},{q="Who is 'ol Redpath' mentioned by Orinelle?",a="He is referring to Marshal Marcus Redpath, the marshal of Southshore. Redpath is responsible for maintaining order and defense in the embattled settlement, which includes issuing military directives that Lieutenant Orinelle blatantly seeks to evade.",al={"who is redpath","magistrate redpath","orinelle commander"}},{q="Where are the Torn Fin murlocs located?",a="The Torn Fin murlocs dwell along the Western Strand, the coastal beaches stretching directly west of Southshore in the Hillsbrad Foothills.",al={"where are torn fin","murloc location hillsbrad","western strand location"},it="place",gp=true},{q="What kinds of murlocs need to be eliminated?",a="The order requires slaying Torn Fin Tidehunters, the frontline fighters of the tribe, along with Torn Fin Oracles, who wield elemental and aquatic magic to bolster their brethren.",al={"murloc targets","which murlocs kill","tidehunter oracle"},it="target",gp=true},{q="What happens after clearing the beach for Orinelle?",a="Upon completing the sweep, Orinelle realizes he needs tangible evidence to satisfy Marshal Redpath's scrutiny, kicking off a series of tasks aimed at gathering physical proof of the slain murlocs.",al={"next quest after down the coast","down the coast chain","farrens proof next"},sp=1,it="next_step",gp=true},{q="Is the murloc threat actually serious or just an excuse?",a="While Farren mocks the creatures as harmless overgrown fish, the Torn Fin are numerous, aggressive, and situated uncomfortably close to Southshore's docks, threatening trade routes and fishermen.",al={"are murlocs dangerous hillsbrad","southshore murloc danger"},it="threat"},{q="Why does Lieutenant Farren Orinelle want the murlocs killed?",a="Lieutenant Orinelle despises Southshore and feels exiled after being transferred from the Stormwind city guard. His superior, Marshal Redpath, ordered him to secure the coastline against the local murlocs. Farren considers the assignment beneath him and mocks the overgrown fish as a trivial chore. By having you thin out their ranks, he hopes to present the illusion that he is actively obeying orders and keeping Southshore safe, all while nursing his ale and longing for a transfer back to the capital.",al={"farren motive","why kill murlocs farren","why does farren want murlocs dead"},it="motive",add=true},{q="What are the Torn Fin murlocs along the coast?",a="The Torn Fin are an aggressive tribe of murlocs infesting the Western Strand and southern shores of the Hillsbrad Foothills. Clustered in fishing encampments along the water, their tidehunters and mystic oracles raid the shoreline and pose a persistent annoyance to the town of Southshore. Though Lieutenant Orinelle scoffs at them as mere fish, their sheer numbers along the surf make them a continuous nuisance to the local harbor and travelers venturing along the coast.",al={"who are torn fin","torn fin murlocs","hillsbrad murlocs"},it="target",add=true}},ang={["faction:Alliance"]="Southshore stands as the Alliance's primary coastal bastion in the north, making even petty negligence among the garrison a hazard to the town's survival.",["race:Human"]="The contrast between Stormwind's sheltered core and the gritty survival of northern settlements is made painfully clear by Orinelle's indolence."},kw={"down the coast","farren orinelle","hillsbrad","murloc","redpath","southshore","torn fin","western strand"},rel={"npc:lieutenant-farren-orinelle","quest:559","subzone:southshore","zone:hillsbrad","topic:murloc","quest:562","quest:563","topic:alliance"},m={start="Lieutenant Farren Orinelle",level="30",faction="Alliance",id=536},src={"Down the Coast"}}
E["quest:539"] = {t="quest",n="Battle of Hillsbrad",z="hillsbrad",s="This campaign order from High Executor Darthalia directs Horde agents to strike deep into Azurelode Mine, a vital iron excavation south of Hillsbrad Fields. By eliminating Foreman Bonds and his crew, the Forsaken aim to sever iron shipments to Alliance armories and seize the tunnels for themselves.",h="This campaign order from High Executor Darthalia directs Horde agents to strike deep into Azurelode Mine, a...",sec={{t="Severing the Iron Supply",b="Having seized the Hillsbrad Town Registry during earlier raids, High Executor Darthalia identified Azurelode Mine as a linchpin of human military endurance in the region. The mine operates just south of the contested fields, continuously extracting rich veins of iron ore to supply Alliance weaponsmiths and armories. Leaving it untouched would allow Southshore's forces to rearm and bolster their garrisons, rendering Tarren Mill's prior victories moot.",sp=0},{t="A Decisive Message",b="To completely break production, Darthalia targets both leadership and labor. Horde forces are ordered to eliminate Foreman Bonds, the human overseer running the excavation, along with a significant portion of his workforce. Striking into the dark shafts sends an unmistakable message to Southshore: neither their supply lines nor their isolated labor camps are beyond the Forsaken's reach.",sp=0},{t="Spoils for the Dark Lady",b="Beyond denying war material to the Alliance, this assault serves a practical secondary motive for the Undercity. Securing the mine allows Sylvanas Windrunner's forces to claim the rich ore veins for their own foundries. Tarren Mill requires a steady supply of metal to manufacture weapons and plate for the war effort across Lordaeron, turning a former human asset into an engine for Forsaken conquest.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Why is Azurelode Mine so important to the Forsaken?",a="Azurelode Mine provides high-grade iron ore directly to Alliance armories. Seizing it starves human garrisons like Southshore of forging materials while handing a rich source of raw metal over to the Undercity to equip Forsaken forces.",al={"why attack azurelode","azurelode mine purpose","why target the mine"},it="motive"},{q="Who is Foreman Bonds?",a="Foreman Bonds is the human overseer in charge of the Azurelode excavation. He manages the miners and can call upon stalwart dwarven defenders when cornered deep within the lower chambers.",al={"foreman bonds","who is bonds","who leads the mine"},it="target"},{q="Where is the Azurelode Mine located?",a="Azurelode Mine is carved into the hills south of Hillsbrad Fields, sitting west of Southshore along the coastline bluffs.",al={"where is azurelode mine","azurelode location","how to find the mine"},it="place",gp=true},{q="How did Darthalia find out about the mine's operations?",a="Darthalia discovered the mine's logistical value and active status by reviewing the Hillsbrad Town Registry, which Horde operatives recovered during previous strikes on the human settlements.",al={"how did darthalia know","town registry mine","hillsbrad intel"},it="history"},{q="What happens after Foreman Bonds is slain?",a="With the mine crippled and its resources marked for Forsaken control, High Executor Darthalia escalates the offensive, turning the Horde's attention toward breaking the remaining infrastructure of Hillsbrad and pushing closer to Southshore itself.",al={"what next battle of hillsbrad","after killing bonds","quest aftermath"},sp=1,it="next_step"},{q="Does the Alliance defend the mine?",a="Yes. Beyond the human miners working the shafts, the Alliance maintains armed guards at the entrance, and Foreman Bonds keeps tough dwarven reinforcements at hand deep within the tunnels.",al={"mine guards","alliance presence in azurelode","dwarves in mine"},it="danger"}},ang={["race:Undead"]="Taking Azurelode Mine secures vital iron for the Deathguard, turning human industry toward arming Sylvanas's armies across Lordaeron.",["faction:Horde"]="Disrupting the Alliance's primary metal supply in Hillsbrad relieves pressure on the Tarren Mill frontline, ensuring human troops cannot easily replace their equipment.",["profession:Mining"]="Azurelode Mine is one of the richest iron operations in the foothills, making it a natural flashpoint for anyone competing over valuable ore veins."},kw={"azurelode","bonds","darthalia","hillsbrad","iron","miners","southshore","tarren mill","undercity"},rel={"npc:high-executor-darthalia","subzone:azurelode-mine","subzone:hillsbrad-fields","subzone:tarren-mill","subzone:southshore","zone:hillsbrad","topic:alliance"},m={start="High Executor Darthalia",["end"]="High Executor Darthalia",level="28",faction="Horde",id=539},src={"Battle of Hillsbrad (5)"}}
E["quest:541"] = {t="quest",n="Battle of Hillsbrad",z="hillsbrad",s="This critical phase of the Forsaken campaign in Hillsbrad targets the dwarven stronghold of Dun Garok. High Executor Darthalia dispatches Horde champions to dismantle the dwarven garrison assisting the local humans and execute their commanding officer, Captain Ironhill.",h="This critical phase of the Forsaken campaign in Hillsbrad targets the dwarven stronghold of Dun Garok.",sec={{t="Testing the Alliance",b="Having pressured the human farmers and town militia across the foothills, High Executor Darthalia turns Tarren Mill's fury against Ironforge's military contingent. Dwarven troops have taken up arms in support of Southshore, reinforcing the human presence in Lordaeron. To Darthalia, this solidarity is an obstacle that must be shattered, proving to the Alliance that aiding the human remnants will bring only devastation.",sp=0},{t="The Fall of Dun Garok",b="Tucked against the ancient ramparts of Thoradin's Wall in southeastern Hillsbrad, Dun Garok serves as a heavily fortified dwarven bastion. Storming the outpost requires breaking through ranks of disciplined mountaineers, crack riflemen, and battle-hardened priests. The assault culminates in the death of Captain Ironhill, breaking Ironforge's forward tactical command in the region and leaving the remaining human enclaves isolated.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Why are dwarves fighting in Hillsbrad?",a="The dwarves of Ironforge maintain strong ties to the Alliance and have sent armed forces north to Dun Garok to aid the surviving human populations of Southshore and Hillsbrad against Forsaken expansion.",al={"why are there dwarves in hillsbrad","dwarves dun garok","why dwarves helping humans"},it="conflict"},{q="Where is Dun Garok located?",a="Dun Garok is situated in the southeastern corner of Hillsbrad Foothills, built directly into the foundations of Thoradin's Wall.",al={"dun garok location","where is dun garok","find dun garok"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Who is Captain Ironhill?",a="Captain Ironhill is the dwarven commander in charge of the garrison at Dun Garok. His presence keeps the mountaineers organized and operational in the region.",al={"captain ironhill","who is ironhill","dun garok leader"},it="target"},{q="Who gives this order?",a="High Executor Darthalia, the Forsaken military commander stationed at Tarren Mill, issues the mission to crush the dwarven garrison.",al={"who gives quest","questgiver darthalia","darthalia hillsbrad"},it="in_charge"},{q="What happens if Horde forces fail here?",a="High Executor Darthalia makes it clear that failure is intolerable, warning that anyone unable to break Dun Garok will be demoted to digging graves back in Tirisfal Glades.",al={"what if fail","darthalia threat","consequences"},it="danger"},{q="Why is Dun Garok so difficult to assault?",a="Unlike the rural militia of Hillsbrad, Dun Garok is manned by trained dwarven soldiers, rifle squads, and holy priests who fight in tight, fortified formations within their underground and elevated bunker.",al={"dun garok elite","why is dun garok hard","dun garok defense"}},{q="Why does High Executor Darthalia want Dun Garok attacked?",a="The Forsaken are waging an all-out campaign to break human control over Hillsbrad Foothills, but the Stormpike dwarves have intervened to bolster their Alliance allies. High Executor Darthalia intends to break the Alliance's resolve by showing them the cost of coming to Southshore's defense. By crushing their barracks at Dun Garok and slaying their commander, she aims to sever human reinforcements and secure the region entirely under the Dark Lady's dominion.",al={"why attack dun garok","darthalia motive","why kill the dwarves"},it="motive",add=true}},ang={["faction:Horde"]="Striking Dun Garok cuts off vital military reinforcements sent by Ironforge to assist the beleaguered humans of Southshore.",["race:Undead"]="For the Forsaken, eliminating the dwarven garrison secures southeastern Lordaeron and ensures no southern Alliance vanguard can easily march through Thoradin's Wall.",["race:Dwarf"]="Dun Garok represents Ironforge's steadfast loyalty to their human allies, enduring Forsaken siege to hold the northern frontier."},kw={"battle of hillsbrad","captain ironhill","dun garok","high executor darthalia","mountaineer","rifleman","tarren mill","thoradin's wall"},rel={"subzone:dun-garok","npc:high-executor-darthalia","subzone:tarren-mill","zone:hillsbrad","subzone:thoradin-s-wall","zone:tirisfal","topic:alliance"},m={start="High Executor Darthalia",level="30",faction="Horde",id=541},src={"Battle of Hillsbrad (6)"}}
E["quest:546"] = {t="quest",n="Souvenirs of Death",z="hillsbrad",s="Souvenirs of Death is a quest given by Deathguard Samsa in Tarren Mill to Horde champions campaigning against the human settlements of the Hillsbrad Foothills. Envious of those sent to the front lines, Samsa asks for thirty human skulls taken in battle to add to his morbid collection.",h="Souvenirs of Death is a quest given by Deathguard Samsa in Tarren Mill to Horde champions campaigning against...",sec={{t="A Guard's Envy",b="While High Executor Darthalia directs the full military might of the Forsaken against the Hillsbrad human settlements, Deathguard Samsa finds himself stranded on sentry duty in Tarren Mill. Harboring a bitter jealousy toward those dispatched to raid, burn, and pillage, Samsa views the open slaughter of the living as an enviable privilege denied to stationary town guards.",sp=0},{t="A Gruesome Trophy",b="Unable to leave his post, Samsa indulges his hatred by collecting the skulls of Hillsbrad humans slain across the ongoing campaign. Rather than serving an arcane ritual or a tactical strategy, his request for thirty skulls is a purely personal indulgence—trophies of a war he longs to fight firsthand.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who offers this quest and where are they located?",a="Deathguard Samsa offers the task. He is stationed as a sentry within Tarren Mill, the primary Forsaken bastion in the northern Hillsbrad Foothills.",al={"quest giver","who gives souvenirs of death","samsa location"},it="arrival",gp=true},{q="What does Deathguard Samsa want?",a="Samsa asks for thirty Hillsbrad Human Skulls, harvested from the human combatants and townsfolk you slay while fighting across Hillsbrad Fields and the town of Hillsbrad.",al={"quest goal","what items needed","skulls required"},it="wants"},{q="Why does Samsa want human skulls?",a="Samsa is an avid collector of macabre trophies. Stuck on garrison duty in Tarren Mill while others wage total war, he gathers skulls to vicariously share in the slaughter of the living.",al={"why collect skulls","samsa motivation","what are skulls for"},it="motive"},{q="When does this quest become available?",a="Samsa only approaches you after you have enlisted with High Executor Darthalia and completed the opening assault in the Battle of Hillsbrad quest line.",al={"quest prerequisites","how to unlock","prereqs for souvenirs"},gp=true},{q="Are the skulls used for Forsaken alchemy or magic?",a="No. Unlike assignments from the Royal Apothecary Society that seek biological reagents for the New Plague, Samsa's request is entirely personal. He finds the severed skulls beautiful and cherishes them as souvenirs of war.",al={"are skulls for apothecary","magic skulls","necromancy use"},it="item"},{q="Which humans provide the skulls?",a="Any of the human farmers, peasants, militia, and defenders living in Hillsbrad Fields or the town of Hillsbrad can yield the skulls while you fight on behalf of Tarren Mill.",al={"where to farm skulls","which mobs drop skulls","hillsbrad humans"},it="target",gp=true},{q="Why does Deathguard Samsa need an adventurer instead of hunting skulls himself?",a="Deathguard Samsa is bound to his post in Tarren Mill. While the Forsaken wage an active campaign against Hillsbrad, Samsa is stuck standing guard instead of participating in the raid. Since High Executor Darthalia has already enlisted you to join the frontline fighting, Samsa asks you to take pity on an old soldier and collect macabre trophies on his behalf.",al={"why me deathguard samsa","why cant samsa get skulls","why doesnt samsa hunt"},it="why_me",add=true},{q="Who are the humans in Hillsbrad that you are fighting?",a="The targets are the human citizens, laborers, and defenders of Hillsbrad Fields and the town of Hillsbrad. As one of the remaining sovereign human strongholds in Lordaeron, Hillsbrad directly opposes the Forsaken outpost of Tarren Mill. The Forsaken consider their continued existence and Alliance allegiance an unacceptable threat to their territorial dominance.",al={"who are hillsbrad humans","hillsbrad target","hillsbrad humans why here"},it="target",add=true}},ang={["faction:Horde"]="The campaign against Hillsbrad represents the Horde's direct push to dismantle remaining Alliance strongholds in Lordaeron, securing northern supply routes for Tarren Mill.",["race:Undead"]="Deathguard Samsa reflects the casual cruelty and deep-seated animosity many Forsaken hold toward the living humans who view them as monsters.",["faction:Alliance"]="The systematic collection of severed human heads highlights the brutal and existential threat the Forsaken pose to the surviving townsfolk of Hillsbrad."},kw={"battle of hillsbrad","darthalia","deathguard samsa","forsaken","hillsbrad","hillsbrad human skull","souvenirs of death","tarren mill"},rel={"npc:deathguard-samsa","quest:527","subzone:tarren-mill","zone:hillsbrad"},m={start="Deathguard Samsa",level="25",faction="Horde",id=546,ri={"Hillsbrad Human Skull"}},src={"Souvenirs of Death"}}
E["quest:547"] = {t="quest",n="Humbert's Sword",z="hillsbrad",s="While scouting the Ironforge stronghold of Dun Garok under orders from High Executor Darthalia, Deathguard Humbert stepped away from his camp to collect firewood. Dwarven scouts looted his campsite and made off with his personal weapon, leaving the humiliated sentry desperate to recover it before his commanding officer notices.",h="While scouting the Ironforge stronghold of Dun Garok under orders from High Executor Darthalia, Deathguard...",sec={{t="A Scout's Negligence",b="Tasked by High Executor Darthalia with keeping a watchful eye on Dun Garok, Deathguard Humbert took up a concealed vigil near the dwarven fortress. When morning broke, he briefly left his outpost unguarded to gather firewood for boiling water. That lapse was all the opportunistic Ironforge dwarves needed. Upon his return, Humbert found his camp looted and his trusty sword gone, taken deep into the heavily defended bunker.",sp=0},{t="Fear of the Rafters",b="Losing a weapon to the very enemy one is supposed to surveil is an embarrassment punishable by death under Forsaken command. Humbert knows full well that High Executor Darthalia would string him up from the rafters of Tarren Mill if she ever learned of his blunder. Unable to storm the stronghold alone, he depends on passing Horde adventurers to plunge into Dun Garok and reclaim his blade before Darthalia realizes anything is amiss.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Deathguard Humbert?",a="Deathguard Humbert is a Forsaken soldier stationed at Tarren Mill in Hillsbrad Foothills. High Executor Darthalia assigned him to scout and keep watch over Dun Garok, the heavily fortified dwarven outpost in the southeastern foothills.",al={"deathguard humbert","who is humbert","humbert"},it="identity"},{q="How did Humbert lose his sword?",a="While maintaining his observation post near Dun Garok, Humbert stepped away to gather firewood to boil water in the morning. While he was gone, dwarven scouts discovered his camp, pilfered his belongings, and carried off his sword.",al={"how did humbert lose his weapon","who stole humbert's sword","stolen sword"},it="origin"},{q="Why is Humbert so desperate to get his sword back quietly?",a="Humbert's commander, High Executor Darthalia, enforces strict discipline in Tarren Mill. Humbert fears that if she discovers he lost his equipment to the very dwarves he was sent to monitor, she will have him executed and hanged from the rafters.",al={"why humbert worried","darthalia punishment","why fear darthalia"},it="motive"},{q="Where is the sword located?",a="The sword was carried into Dun Garok by the dwarven scouts. It can be found among the ranks of the Ironforge mountaineers, riflemen, and officers occupying the bunker.",al={"sword location","where is humbert's sword","dun garok sword"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Did the dwarves steal anything else from Humbert?",a="Yes. Beyond his sword, various dwarven scouts looted the rest of Humbert's field kit, including his helm, chestpiece, and pants, which remain scattered among the forces of Dun Garok.",al={"humbert other gear","humbert armor pieces","humbert's pants"}},{q="What is Dun Garok?",a="Dun Garok is an Ironforge dwarven stronghold in the southeastern corner of Hillsbrad Foothills, guarding the mountain approach toward the Alterac and Arathi borders. The Alliance garrison there is in direct, hostile confrontation with the Forsaken of Tarren Mill.",al={"dun garok fortress","dun garok lore","dwarves in hillsbrad"},it="place"},{q="Why is Humbert's sword so important to him?",a="To Deathguard Humbert, the weapon is both his personal pride and the badge of his duty. Without it, he stands unarmed while on scout duty for Tarren Mill, completely exposed to the wrath of High Executor Darthalia. It holds no magical powers or grand enchantments; it is simply his prized blade, and having it back restores his dignity and conceals a humiliating blunder from his commander.",al={"what is humbert's sword","why does humbert need his sword","humbert sword purpose"},it="item",add=true},{q="Who are the dwarves holding Humbert's sword?",a="The thieves belong to the dwarven forces stationed at Dun Garok, an Alliance stronghold nestled in southeastern Hillsbrad Foothills. These Stormpike mountaineers and riflemen regularly send scouts through the hills to contest Forsaken expansion and secure the road to the Alterac Mountains. A patrol stumbled upon Humbert's unguarded camp while he gathered firewood, looting his weaponry and carrying it back behind their fortified walls.",al={"who stole humbert's sword","dun garok dwarves","who has the sword"},it="target",add=true},{q="Why does Humbert need you to recover his sword instead of doing it himself?",a="Humbert cannot storm a heavily fortified dwarven bastion alone, nor can he ask his fellow Deathguards for assistance without admitting he abandoned his post to boil water and let his equipment get stolen. If word reaches High Executor Darthalia that he lost his weapon to dwarven thieves, she would make a brutal example of him. An independent adventurer can slip in and recover the blade discreetly.",al={"why can't humbert get his sword","why ask me humberts sword","why humbert needs help"},it="why_me",add=true}},ang={["race:Undead"]="Forsaken soldiers in Hillsbrad understand the brutal discipline enforced by High Executor Darthalia; failure or negligence in Tarren Mill is met with ruthless execution rather than leniency.",["race:Dwarf"]="The mountaineers of Dun Garok have no love for the Forsaken on their doorstep, seizing every opportunity to harass Tarren Mill's sentries and strip their camps bare.",["faction:Horde"]="Every strike into Dun Garok serves the wider campaign to break Ironforge's military grip on Hillsbrad Foothills and protect Tarren Mill from southern incursions."},kw={"darthalia","deathguard","dun garok","firewood","hillsbrad","humbert","sword","tarren mill"},rel={"npc:deathguard-humbert","subzone:dun-garok","npc:high-executor-darthalia","subzone:tarren-mill","zone:hillsbrad","quest:527","quest:509","topic:horde"},m={start="Deathguard Humbert",level="30",faction="Horde",id=547,ri={"Humbert's Sword"}},src={"Humbert's Sword (quest)"}}
E["quest:549"] = {t="quest",n="WANTED: Syndicate Personnel",z="hillsbrad",s="Posted on the Tarren Mill bounty board under the authority of Lady Sylvanas, this decree condemns all members of the Syndicate to death. The Forsaken seek to purge the brigands gathering in the ruins of Durnholde Keep before they threaten Horde operations in the foothills.",h="Posted on the Tarren Mill bounty board under the authority of Lady Sylvanas, this decree condemns all members...",sec={{t="A Standing Execution Order",b="The Syndicate's sudden presence southeast of Tarren Mill has not gone unnoticed by the Forsaken. Rather than offering parley or treating them as mere displaced nobles, Lady Sylvanas Windrunner and her commanders view the Syndicate as an active pestilence. The bounty dictates immediate death, specifying that any prisoners brought in will be executed without trial.",sp=0},{t="The Ruins of Durnholde",b="Once an infamous internment camp fortress, Durnholde Keep now lies shattered and lawless. Syndicate Rogues and Watchmen have crept into its crumbled ramparts and towers, using the historic stronghold as an operations hub. For High Executor Darthalia, ridding the ruins of these armed bandits is essential to securing the road and safeguarding Tarren Mill's southeastern approach.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who posted the bounty for Syndicate personnel?",a="The bounty was issued under the direct authority of Lady Sylvanas Windrunner and posted on the notice board in Tarren Mill. Proof of execution is collected by High Executor Darthalia, the military commander of the settlement.",al={"who posted wanted syndicate personnel","who wants syndicate dead","bounty poster"},it="identity"},{q="Where are these Syndicate members located?",a="They congregate among the shattered stones of Durnholde Keep, situated southeast of Tarren Mill across the river, as well as around the ruined guard tower just south of the main fortress.",al={"where are syndicate rogues","durnholde syndicate location","where to find watchmen"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Why do the Forsaken want them dead instead of captured?",a="The Forsaken view the Syndicate as treacherous pests and an armed threat encroaching on their territory. The decree explicitly orders that any members brought into custody are to be summarily executed, making capture entirely pointless.",al={"why kill syndicate","why no prisoners","darthalia syndicate"},it="motive"},{q="What is the Syndicate doing in Durnholde Keep?",a="Composed primarily of disgraced Alteraci nobility and mercenaries, the Syndicate utilizes abandoned keeps, ruins, and towers across Lordaeron as staging grounds to raid settlements, rob travelers, and rebuild their shattered power base.",al={"why syndicate in durnholde","syndicate purpose hillsbrad","durnholde keep occupiers"},it="target"},{q="What happens after culling these Syndicate operatives?",a="Thinning the ranks of the rogues and watchmen leads High Executor Darthalia to issue a high-priority bounty targeting their local leadership, specifically Baron Vardus.",al={"what quest is next","after wanted syndicate personnel","next bounty"},sp=1,it="next_step"},{q="Why does High Executor Darthalia rely on adventurers for this bounty?",a="High Executor Darthalia oversees Tarren Mill under direct mandate from Lady Sylvanas, but her standing garrison is stretched thin defending Forsaken territory against Southshore and the regional threats of Hillsbrad. As she bluntly reminds visitors, she has far more pressing matters of command than personally handling every encampment of thieves. Offering public bounties draws willing mercenaries and Horde champions to purge pests from Durnholde Keep without depleting the town's front-line defenses.",al={"why send adventurers","why darthalia bounty","why not tarren mill guards"},it="why_me",add=true}},ang={["race:Undead"]="For the Forsaken, clearing out the living remnants of Alterac's nobility is a practical necessity to ensure unchallenged control over the hills of Lordaeron.",["faction:Horde"]="Durnholde Keep holds grim memories as the internment fortress where orcs were once held in captivity; purging the brigands now occupying its ruins carries symbolic weight for the Horde.",["class:Rogue"]="The Syndicate fields skilled cutpurses and ambushers throughout Durnholde, making this contract a direct clash between rival practitioners of stealth."},kw={"durnholde keep","high executor darthalia","hillsbrad foothills","syndicate","syndicate rogue","syndicate watchman","tarren mill","wanted"},rel={"subzone:durnholde-keep","npc:high-executor-darthalia","topic:syndicate","subzone:tarren-mill","zone:hillsbrad","quest:498","topic:horde"},m={start="WANTED",["end"]="High Executor Darthalia",level="22",faction="Horde",id=549},src={"WANTED: Syndicate Personnel"}}
E["quest:555"] = {t="quest",n="Soothing Turtle Bisque",z="hillsbrad",s="Chef Jessen of Southshore prides himself on preparing the finest cuisine north of Stormwind, but recent unrest has cut off his supply of fresh snapjaw turtle meat. To restore his famous Soothing Turtle Bisque to the tavern menu, he asks culinary-minded travelers to brave the dangerous northern waters near Dalaran and Lake Lordamere.",h="Chef Jessen of Southshore prides himself on preparing the finest cuisine north of Stormwind, but recent...",sec={{t="A Northern Delicacy",b="Southshore remains one of the Alliance's last intact coastal towns in Lordaeron, clinging proudly to civilian life amidst mounting regional strife. Chef Jessen claims that his cooking rivals any tavern north of Stormwind, with patrons supposedly trekking from as far as Darkshire in Duskwood just for a taste of his specialty: Soothing Turtle Bisque. The rich, restorative soup depends entirely on fresh meat from the snapjaw turtles indigenous to the rivers and lakes of the northern mountains.",sp=0},{t="Peril on Lordamere",b="In calmer years, Jessen gathered turtle meat himself by journeying up past the magical bubble of Dalaran to the eastern shores of Lordamere Lake. However, rising tensions, hostile wildlife, the Syndicate, and Forsaken incursions have made foraging outside town lethal for ordinary townsfolk. To keep his pot simmering and his patrons satisfied, the chef relies on armed adventurers willing to harvest meat from the snapjaws lurking along the riverbanks and northern shores.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who offers the quest for Soothing Turtle Bisque?",a="Chef Jessen, the culinary master residing in the coastal Alliance town of Southshore in Hillsbrad Foothills, offers this request to visiting cooks.",al={"who gives soothing turtle bisque","where do i start soothing turtle bisque","chef jessen quest"},it="identity"},{q="Why does Chef Jessen need outside help gathering turtle meat?",a="Jessen used to hunt the snapjaw turtles himself near Dalaran and Lordamere Lake, but the region has become far too dangerous due to political unrest and predatory beasts, forcing him to hire adventurers.",al={"why cant jessen get meat","why does jessen need turtles"},it="why_me"},{q="Where are snapjaw turtles found in the region?",a="Snapjaw turtles dwell along the freshwater river flowing between Hillsbrad Foothills and the Alterac Mountains, as well as along the shores of Lordamere Lake north of Dalaran.",al={"turtle meat location","where are snapjaws","where to farm turtle meat"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Do you need to know Cooking to take this quest?",a="Yes. Chef Jessen only shares this request and his culinary secrets with travelers who have trained in the Cooking profession, though it requires no specific skill rank to accept.",al={"is cooking required","cooking profession required","can anyone take soothing turtle bisque"},gp=true},{q="Why is Southshore's cuisine famous?",a="Chef Jessen boasts that Southshore serves the finest cuisine north of Stormwind, and his renowned turtle bisque has supposedly drawn traveling diners from as far away as Darkshire.",al={"southshore food","why is jessen famous","darkshire travel for bisque"},it="fame"},{q="What is the unrest Chef Jessen laments?",a="Hillsbrad and Alterac are caught in open conflict between the Forsaken from the north, Syndicate outlaws roaming the ruins, and wild predators displaced by the fall of Lordaeron, making civilian travel hazardous.",al={"hillsbrad unrest","why is it dangerous now","what unrest"},it="threat"},{q="Why does Chef Jessen want this done?",a="Chef Jessen takes immense pride in Southshore's culinary reputation, boasting that the town offers some of the finest cuisine north of Stormwind. His famed secret recipe for Soothing Turtle Bisque attracts travelers from as far away as Darkshire, but recent violence in the region has cut off his ingredient supply. By gathering the necessary turtle meat, you enable him to resume serving his signature dish and bring comfort to the beleaguered town.",al={"why make turtle bisque","chef jessen motive","why does jessen want turtle meat"},it="motive",add=true},{q="What is the Turtle Meat for?",a="The meat is the essential ingredient in Chef Jessen's secret recipe for Soothing Turtle Bisque. Harvesters typically gather it from snapjaw turtles found in the northern waters, such as Lake Lordamere, allowing the chef to simmer his beloved regional specialty once again.",al={"what is turtle meat used for","why turtle meat","purpose of turtle meat"},it="item",add=true}},ang={["profession:Cooking"]="Chef Jessen shares his craft exclusively with fellow culinarians, rewarding you with the recipe to prepare your own batch of Soothing Turtle Bisque.",["faction:Alliance"]="Restoring Southshore's comforts helps keep local morale high as the town stands isolated against hostile Syndicate outlaws and Forsaken expansion.",["race:Human"]="For humans visiting from the southern kingdoms, Jessen's cooking offers a rare taste of home and hospitality in the embattled north."},kw={"chef jessen","cooking","dalaran","hillsbrad","lordamere lake","snapjaw","soothing turtle bisque","southshore","turtle meat"},rel={"npc:chef-jessen","subzone:southshore","zone:hillsbrad","subzone:lordamere-lake","zone:alterac","subzone:dalaran","subzone:darkshire","topic:alliance"},m={start="Chef Jessen",level="31",faction="Alliance",id=555,ri={"Turtle Meat"}},src={"Soothing Turtle Bisque (Alliance)"}}
E["quest:556"] = {t="quest",n="Stone Tokens",z="hillsbrad",s="Stone Tokens is a Horde assignment issued by Keeper Bel'varil in Tarren Mill to retrieve magical binding artifacts from Dalaran agents in the Alterac region. The Forsaken seek to study the arcane methods Dalaran's mages use to enslave and command powerful elementals. Gathering these inert tokens serves as the foundation for the Magus's research into elemental subjugation.",h="Stone Tokens is a Horde assignment issued by Keeper Bel'varil in Tarren Mill to retrieve magical binding...",sec={{t="Arcane Subjugation",b="The magi of Dalaran have long possessed a formidable command over elemental entities, using specialized conduits and enchanted foci to bind creatures from other dimensions into servitude. While the city itself lies shrouded under a massive violet dome, its agents and remnant forces patrol the surrounding territory, relying on elementals as laborers and defensive shock troops. Magus Voidglare, an arcane researcher working on behalf of the Forsaken in Tarren Mill, seeks to dissect the precise sorcery Dalaran uses to compel these entities into obedience.",sp=0},{t="Inert Specimen Gathering",b="Rather than demanding potent and volatile magical instruments right away, Keeper Bel'varil directs agents to secure worn and faded tokens. By gathering these exhausted charms from Dalaran personnel stationed around the outskirts and the nearby internment camp, Voidglare can safely analyze the lingering enchantments without risking uncontrolled planar backlash. These weathered tokens provide the baseline theoretical knowledge needed before testing more potent binding mechanisms.",sp=1}},faq={{q="What are the stone tokens used for?",a="The wizards of Dalaran craft and carry these stone tokens as magical foci to command and subjugate elementals, forcing creatures from other dimensions to serve as guards, sentries, and laborers.",al={"stone token purpose","why do dalaran wizards have stone tokens","what do the tokens do"},it="item"},{q="Why does Magus Voidglare want worn tokens specifically?",a="Worn stone tokens retain the foundational magical matrix of Dalaran's binding spells while having faded in active arcane power. This makes them far safer for Magus Voidglare to dissect and study without risking violent elemental retaliation or explosive magical feedback during his initial experiments.",al={"why worn stone tokens","why not active tokens"},it="why_wanted"},{q="Who is Keeper Bel'varil?",a="Keeper Bel'varil is a Forsaken questgiver stationed at Tarren Mill in the Hillsbrad Foothills. He oversees tactical operations against human forces in the region and assists researchers like Magus Voidglare by procuring magical artifacts and hostile reagents from nearby territories.",al={"belvaril","who gives stone tokens quest"},it="identity"},{q="Where are the Dalaran forces holding these tokens?",a="The tokens are carried by Dalaran wizards and their personnel occupying the frontier borders between western Hillsbrad and the Alterac Mountains, particularly near the Dalaran bubble and the nearby ruins of the old orc internment camp.",al={"where to find stone tokens","dalaran forces location"},it="place",gp=true},{q="What happens after these tokens are delivered?",a="Once Bel'varil inspects the inert specimens, Magus Voidglare advances his research from theoretical study to physical containment, commissioning the procurement of heavier Bracers of Binding directly from the elementals themselves.",al={"what comes after stone tokens","stone tokens follow up"},sp=1,it="next_step"},{q="Why is the Horde studying Dalaran's magic?",a="The Forsaken view the surviving mages of Dalaran as a direct territorial and magical threat in the Lordaeron region. Deciphering their arcane methods allows Forsaken spellcasters to counter Kirin Tor operations, protect their borders, and potentially turn elemental forces to their own advantage.",al={"why horde wants dalaran magic","forsaken dalaran interest"},it="purpose"},{q="Why does Keeper Bel'varil want these stone tokens collected?",a="Keeper Bel'varil acts on behalf of Magus Voidglare, a Forsaken mage in Tarren Mill seeking to unravel the arcane practices of Dalaran. The Kirin Tor wizards are renowned for their mastery over extra-dimensional elementals, commanding them through enchanted stones. Voidglare intends to study the tokens to unlock their binding secrets, advancing the Forsaken's understanding of elemental control.",al={"why does keeper bel'varil want stone tokens","bel'varil motive stone tokens","why collect worn stone tokens"},it="motive",add=true},{q="Who are the Dalaran forces guarding the internment camp?",a="You are sent against the Kirin Tor wizards and guards occupying the ruined internment camps and lands west of Hillsbrad, along the Alterac border. In the aftermath of the Third War and Dalaran's destruction, these human remnants maintain a stubborn enclave, utilizing elemental servants and wards to secure their holdings against the Forsaken and other regional threats.",al={"who are dalaran forces hillsbrad","why are dalaran wizards at internment camp","dalaran target stone tokens"},it="target",add=true}},ang={["class:Mage"]="Dalaran's conjurers are renowned for binding elementals to their will; examining these tokens reveals how human magi tether extraplanar spirits to material foci.",["race:Undead"]="For the Forsaken of Tarren Mill, unraveling Dalaran's arcane secrets is vital to securing Lordaeron from human sorcerers lurking just beyond the violet dome.",["class:Shaman"]="While shaman revere elementals through reciprocal pacts, Dalaran's wizards use arcane tokens to dominate and enslave them, a practice antithetical to spiritual harmony."},kw={"alterac mountains","binding","dalaran","elementals","hillsbrad foothills","keeper bel'varil","magus voidglare","stone tokens","tarren mill","worn stone token"},rel={"npc:keeper-bel-varil","subzone:tarren-mill","subzone:dalaran","zone:hillsbrad","zone:alterac"},m={start="Keeper Bel'varil",level="32",faction="Horde",id=556,ri={"Worn Stone Token"}},src={"Stone Tokens"}}
E["quest:559"] = {t="quest",n="Farren's Proof",z="hillsbrad",s="Farren's Proof is an Alliance assignment in Southshore given by Lieutenant Farren Orinelle. Tasked with proving his coastal patrol efforts to his superior, Marshal Redpath, Farren sends recruits out to harvest severed murloc heads along the Western Strand.",h="Farren's Proof is an Alliance assignment in Southshore given by Lieutenant Farren Orinelle.",sec={{t="A Grudging Request",b="Following initial sweeps along the coastline in Down the Coast, Lieutenant Farren Orinelle finds himself under scrutiny by Marshal Redpath and town leadership. Claiming credit for clearing out the local murlocs is one thing; presenting undeniable evidence to skeptical superiors is quite another. Unwilling to soil his own hands with gruesome butchery, Farren tasks wandering Alliance adventurers with returning to the shoreline to collect tangible proof of the kill.",sp=0},{t="Grisly Evidence",b="The task takes fighters west of Southshore along the Western Strand, where coastal murlocs nest along the shallows. The lieutenant requires ten severed murloc heads to appease the town garrison's officers. Farren himself detests the creatures, admitting that the repulsive sight and smell of amphibious fish-men has utterly ruined his appetite for Southshore's primary export and staple food.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Lieutenant Farren Orinelle?",a="Lieutenant Farren Orinelle is an Alliance town officer stationed in Southshore. While eager to report success to his superiors, he prefers delegating the violent and filthy aspects of shoreline security to capable adventurers.",al={"farren orinelle","who gives farren's proof","lieutenant farren"},it="identity"},{q="Why does Farren need severed murloc heads?",a="Marshal Redpath and town officials were not satisfied by simple verbal reports that the Western Strand had been cleared. They demanded physical evidence of dead murlocs before officially acknowledging the patrol's success.",al={"why murloc heads","farren proof reason","why collect heads"},it="motive"},{q="Where are these murlocs located?",a="The murlocs inhabit the Western Strand, the coastal beaches stretching directly west of Southshore toward the border of Silverpine Forest.",al={"murloc head location","where is western strand","murloc spots hillsbrad"},it="place",gp=true},{q="What happens after turning in Farren's Proof?",a="Farren's administrative troubles continue. Satisfying Marshal Redpath turns out to be only the first bureaucratic hurdle, leading to further requests for proof and eventually orders tied to Stormwind command.",al={"next quest after farren's proof","farren quest chain","farren's proof followup"},sp=1,it="next_step"},{q="Why is Farren disgusted by the murlocs?",a="Farren finds walking, bipedal fish inherently repulsive. Handling their cold, slimy remains has completely turned his stomach against eating fish, making daily life in Southshore's fishing community miserable for him.",al={"farren fish","why doesn't farren like fish"}},{q="Who is Marshal Redpath?",a="Marshal Redpath is a commanding military officer within the Southshore town defense forces, responsible for holding junior officers like Farren Orinelle accountable for regional security.",al={"captain redpath","who is redpath"},it="identity"},{q="Why does Lieutenant Farren have you collect the heads instead of doing it himself?",a="Lieutenant Farren is utterly revulsed by murlocs. While he is quick to take credit for clearing the coastline, the thought of hacking off cold, slimy heads turns his stomach so badly that he hasn't been able to bring himself to eat fish in weeks. He would rather hire an adventurer to endure the grisly butchery than soil his own hands.",al={"why does farren need me","why doesnt farren get the heads","farren proof why me"},it="why_me",add=true}},ang={["faction:Alliance"]="Holding Southshore requires securing its coastlines against native predators so the outpost can focus on threats from the Syndicate and the Horde.",["profession:Cooking"]="For fish-based cooks in Southshore, Farren's squeamish aversion to seafood is baffling, though fighting along the beach often yields spare raw catches."},kw={"farren","heads","hillsbrad","murloc","orinelle","redpath","southshore","strand"},rel={"npc:lieutenant-farren-orinelle","quest:536","subzone:southshore","zone:hillsbrad","topic:murloc","quest:562","quest:563","topic:stormwind-kingdom"},m={start="Lieutenant Farren Orinelle",level="32",faction="Alliance",id=559,ri={"Murloc Head"}},src={"Farren's Proof"}}
E["quest:560"] = {t="quest",n="Farren's Proof",z="hillsbrad",s="Farren's Proof is a short delivery mission in Southshore where an adventurer carries a grisly bounty of murloc heads from Lieutenant Farren Orinelle to Marshal Redpath. Having let someone else do the bloody work of hunting the coast, the squeamish lieutenant delegates the actual reporting as well. It marks an intermediate step in securing town recognition along the Hillsbrad coast.",h="Farren's Proof is a short delivery mission in Southshore where an adventurer carries a grisly bounty of...",sec={{t="A Squeamish Officer",b="Lieutenant Farren Orinelle is tasked with patrolling and securing the southern coastline of Hillsbrad Foothills, yet he has little stomach for the brutal realities of frontier warfare. After sending an adventurer out to cull the rampant murlocs infesting the beaches, he balks at actually touching the severed heads brought back as proof. Rather than personally marching the dripping trophies to Southshore's town command, Farren gladly dumps the errand right back onto the bearer.",sp=0},{t="Report to Redpath",b="Across Southshore, Marshal Redpath oversees the town's defensive operations and military readiness amidst mounting threats from Tarren Mill and wild beast populations. Receiving a sack of murloc heads via courier rather than directly from his lieutenant hardly surprises him. While recognizing that the adventurer has become Farren's errand runner, Redpath is pragmatic enough to accept the assistance, knowing Southshore requires all the diligent labor it can muster to keep its borders intact.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Why doesn't Lieutenant Farren deliver the murloc heads himself?",a="Lieutenant Farren simply has no desire to handle a dripping sack of severed murloc heads. Having already enlisted an adventurer to do the fighting, he finds it far more comfortable to delegate the messy delivery to Marshal Redpath as well.",al={"why farren not go","farren proof why deliver","why errand boy"},it="why_me"},{q="Who is Marshal Redpath?",a="Marshal Redpath is the senior Alliance military commander stationed in Southshore. He oversees local defense, coordinates town guards, and handles the various regional threats menacing the human settlement in Hillsbrad Foothills.",al={"who is redpath","marshal redpath lore","southshore marshal"},it="identity"},{q="Where does this delivery lead next in the quest chain?",a="Delivering the proof leads to further duties from Marshal Redpath and Lieutenant Farren, culminating in official dispatches regarding troop deployments and paperwork sent back to the capital in Stormwind.",al={"what comes next","farren's proof next quest","redpath next quest"},it="next_step"},{q="Why are murlocs a priority for Southshore's garrison?",a="Murloc tribes nest densely along the beaches of the Hillsbrad coast. Left unchecked, they raid coastal supply routes, harass local fishermen, and threaten the southern approach to Southshore while the town is already preoccupied with the Forsaken to the north.",al={"why kill murlocs","murloc problem southshore","hillsbrad murlocs"},it="danger"},{q="What does Marshal Redpath think of Lieutenant Farren's conduct?",a="Marshal Redpath is well aware of Farren's habits, dryly noting that the courier has become 'Farren's errand boy.' However, Redpath welcomes the help regardless, as Southshore is hard-pressed and needs any capable labor it can get.",al={"redpath opinion on farren","does redpath like farren"}},{q="Where is Marshal Redpath located in Southshore?",a="Marshal Redpath can be found near the town center and council building in Southshore, keeping watch over the settlement's daily defense operations.",al={"find redpath","where is marshal redpath","redpath location"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Why does Lieutenant Farren want the murloc heads delivered to Marshal Redpath?",a="Lieutenant Farren needs concrete proof that the murloc threat along Southshore's coast is actively being dealt with. Presenting the severed heads to Marshal Redpath demonstrates that Farren's patrol orders are being carried out and Southshore's shores are being defended, even if the lieutenant would rather avoid carting a foul-smelling sack across town himself.",al={"farren motive","why deliver murloc heads","farren's proof purpose"},it="motive",add=true}},ang={["faction:Alliance"]="Every minor chore in Southshore contributes to keeping the Alliance's primary bastion in Lordaeron fortified against hostile forces encroaching from the north and sea.",["race:Human"]="For human travelers, dealing with Farren and Redpath offers a candid look at the strained bureaucracy and frontier weariness of the Hillsbrad garrison."},kw={"alliance","errand boy","farren orinelle","farren's proof","hillsbrad foothills","marshal redpath","murloc heads","southshore"},rel={"npc:lieutenant-farren-orinelle","quest:559","subzone:southshore","zone:hillsbrad","quest:536","quest:562","quest:563","topic:murloc"},m={start="Lieutenant Farren Orinelle",["end"]="Marshal Redpath",level="32",faction="Alliance",id=560},src={"Farren's Proof (2)"}}
E["quest:561"] = {t="quest",n="Farren's Proof",z="hillsbrad",s="Farren's Proof is an Alliance courier mission within the harbor town of Southshore. Acting on behalf of Marshal Redpath, an adventurer delivers orders directing Lieutenant Farren Orinelle to focus his military attention on the naga encroaching upon the Eastern Strand.",h="Farren's Proof is an Alliance courier mission within the harbor town of Southshore.",sec={{t="A Shift in Command",b="Southshore's military leadership is hard-pressed by surrounding threats, yet Marshal Redpath remains attentive to maritime dangers along the southern coast. Having received fresh intelligence concerning naga incursions upon the Eastern Strand, Redpath dispatches a runner across town to Lieutenant Farren Orinelle with direct orders: abandon peripheral distractions, eliminate the amphibious menace, and deliver his progress reports directly to the Marshal in person.",sp=0},{t="Rivalry on the Coast",b="Upon receiving the message, Lieutenant Orinelle reveals the quiet friction festering among Southshore's garrison officers. Rather than offering dutiful compliance, Orinelle suspects Redpath is capitalizing on recently shared intelligence to claim credit for pacifying the shoreline. Determined not to let his commanding officer reap a promotion off his soldiers' sweat, Orinelle immediately begins scheming his own avenue to curry favor with the crown.",sp=1}},faq={{q="What is the purpose of this delivery?",a="Marshal Redpath intends to redirect Lieutenant Farren Orinelle's troops toward the naga infesting Hillsbrad's Eastern Strand, requiring Orinelle to report back to him directly once measurable progress is made.",al={"what does redpath want","why send message to farren","farren proof 3 objective"},it="purpose"},{q="Why does Farren Orinelle react bitterly to Redpath's orders?",a="Orinelle believes Redpath is acting on identical military intelligence they both just received. He fears the Marshal intends to take credit for clearing the coast and earn a promotion off Orinelle's hard labor.",al={"farren redpath rivalry","why is orinelle mad","orinelle promotion"},it="conflict"},{q="Where is the Eastern Strand located?",a="The Eastern Strand stretches along the southern saltwater coastline of the Hillsbrad Foothills, situated southeast of Southshore where encroaching naga have established foul encampments on the sand.",al={"eastern strand location","where are the naga","hillsbrad coast"},it="place",gp=true},{q="What comes next after delivering this message?",a="Following this encounter, Orinelle hatches his own scheme rather than submitting cleanly to Redpath's authority, pointing adventurous couriers down the coast and toward high command in the quest 'Stormwind Ho!'.",al={"next quest","what happens next","stormwind ho follow up"},sp=1,it="next_step"},{q="Who are the leaders involved in this exchange?",a="Marshal Redpath serves as Southshore's primary garrison commander, while Lieutenant Farren Orinelle serves under him as a field lieutenant overseeing coastal defense efforts.",al={"who are farren and redpath","southshore officers","farren orinelle and redpath"},it="leader"},{q="Does this assignment require any combat?",a="No. This specific step is purely an internal communication errand between officers within Southshore, though it deals directly with the military response to naga hostiles along the shore.",al={"is there fighting","do i fight naga","farrens proof combat"},gp=true},{q="Why does Marshal Redpath send you to Lieutenant Farren?",a="Marshal Redpath oversees Southshore's defense and wants Lieutenant Farren Orinelle to stop wasting time on murlocs and turn his attention to the naga threatening the Eastern Strand. He needs Farren to produce real tactical results and answer directly to him rather than pursuing petty personal initiatives.",al={"why does redpath send this message","redpath motive farren","why refocus on naga"},it="motive",add=true}},ang={["faction:Alliance"]="The exchange offers a glimpse into the bureaucratic and career rivalries simmering inside Southshore's garrison, showing that even in besieged northern outposts, officers jockey for prestige.",["class:Warrior"]="Navigating the petty jealousies of officer politics is a familiar frustration for soldiers serving the Alliance banner, where battlefield prowess often clashes with command ambition."},kw={"eastern strand","farren orinelle","farren's proof","hillsbrad","marshal redpath","naga","promotion","southshore"},rel={"npc:lieutenant-farren-orinelle","quest:562","quest:559","subzone:southshore","subzone:eastern-strand","zone:hillsbrad","topic:naga","quest:536"},m={start="Marshal Redpath",["end"]="Lieutenant Farren Orinelle",level="32",faction="Alliance",id=561},src={"Farren's Proof (3)"}}
E["quest:562"] = {t="quest",n="Stormwind Ho!",z="hillsbrad",s="Lieutenant Farren Orinelle is desperate to escape his posting in Southshore and return south to Stormwind City. Sensing a career opportunity after hearing Alliance High Command fears the rising threat of the naga, he hires an adventurer to exterminate the serpent-folk so he can claim the credit and secure a reassignment.",h="Lieutenant Farren Orinelle is desperate to escape his posting in Southshore and return south to Stormwind...",sec={{t="A Ticket Out of Southshore",b="Southshore sits on the knife-edge of Lordaeron, hemmed in by Forsaken forces, syndicate brigands, and relentless sea fiends. For Lieutenant Farren Orinelle, an ordinary guardsman accustomed to city drunks and petty brawls in Stormwind, the posting is nothing short of miserable. When word arrives from his former mentor that Alliance High Command is increasingly anxious about the naga encroaching on the coasts, Farren spots his golden opportunity to leave the north behind.",sp=0},{t="Stolen Valor on the Coast",b="Despite his lofty ambitions, Farren is candid about his cowardice: facing ferocious Daggerspine sirens and shorehunters in open combat is far beyond his courage and ability. Instead of risking his neck, he commissions an adventurer to scour the beaches southeast of Southshore, cull the naga ranks, and provide the martial feats he needs to draft an impressive dispatch to Major Samuelson in Stormwind.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Why does Farren Orinelle want to kill the naga?",a="He does not personally care about the naga; he wants out of Southshore. Farren learned from his mentor that Alliance High Command is worried about the naga threat, making successful operations against them a fast track for promotion or reassignment back to Stormwind City.",al={"why naga","farren motive","why kill naga in southshore"},it="motive"},{q="Can Lieutenant Farren Orinelle fight the naga himself?",a="No. Farren openly admits he is merely an urban guardsman suited for breaking up drunken tavern brawls or arresting rowdy beggars. The savage Daggerspine naga terrify him, forcing him to rely entirely on visiting adventurers to do his fighting.",al={"why doesn't farren fight","is farren weak","farren combat"},it="why_me"},{q="Where are the Daggerspine naga located?",a="The Daggerspine shorehunters and sirens have established encampments along the coastline directly southeast of the town of Southshore, prowling the shores of the Great Sea in Hillsbrad Foothills.",al={"where are naga","daggerspine location","southshore naga beach"},it="target",gp=true},{q="Who is Major Samuelson?",a="Major Samuelson is Farren Orinelle's former mentor in the Stormwind City Guard. Farren prepares reports for him detailing the culled naga in hopes that Samuelson will pull the strings necessary to grant him a transfer back south.",al={"major samuelson","samuelson stormwind","who gets the letter"},it="people"},{q="What happens after completing this task?",a="Once the naga threat is mitigated and Farren takes credit for your work, he sends you south to Stormwind Keep to personally deliver his report and reassignment plea to Major Samuelson.",al={"what comes next","next quest after stormwind ho","reassignment quest"},sp=1,it="next_step"},{q="Why does Farren hate Southshore so much?",a="Farren views Southshore as a dismal, dangerous frontier outpost far removed from the civilized safety of Stormwind. Between undead neighbors and coastal monsters, he refers to it bitterly as a 'Light-forsaken port.'",al={"why does farren hate southshore","light forsaken port"},it="motive"},{q="Who are the Daggerspine naga threatening Southshore?",a="The Daggerspine are serpentine monstrous humanoids encroaching along the eastern coastline of Hillsbrad Foothills. Alliance High Command has grown increasingly alarmed by their organized presence along the shores. Ferocious shorehunters patrol the beaches alongside sirens wielding ocean magics, harassing the regional fisheries and threatening to overwhelm Southshore's fragile defenses if left unchecked.",al={"daggerspine naga","who are the naga in southshore","daggerspine shorehunters"},it="target",add=true}},ang={["faction:Alliance"]="The Alliance command structure in Hillsbrad is stretched thin, leaving ordinary city watchmen out of their depth against monstrous threats like the Daggerspine naga.",["race:Human"]="For humans serving in Lordaeron, Southshore is a grim reminder of lost northern glory, contrasting sharply with the rebuilt grandeur and safety of Stormwind to the south."},kw={"daggerspine","farren orinelle","hillsbrad foothills","naga","reassignment","samuelson","southshore","stormwind ho"},rel={"npc:lieutenant-farren-orinelle","quest:563","quest:559","npc:major-samuelson","subzone:southshore","zone:hillsbrad","topic:naga","zone:stormwind"},m={start="Lieutenant Farren Orinelle",level="32",faction="Alliance",id=562},src={"Stormwind Ho!"}}
E["quest:563"] = {t="quest",n="Reassignment",z="hillsbrad",s="Reassignment is the culmination of Lieutenant Farren Orinelle's campaign to escape his posting in Southshore. Having compiled an exaggerated report of his deeds against the coastal naga, Farren dispatches an adventurer all the way to Stormwind Keep to deliver the documents to his former mentor, Major Samuelson.",h="Reassignment is the culmination of Lieutenant Farren Orinelle's campaign to escape his posting in Southshore.",sec={{t="A Ticket Out of Southshore",b="Lieutenant Farren Orinelle has made no secret of his disdain for his station in the Hillsbrad Foothills. Tucked away in Southshore, far from the comforts of the capital and under the stern watch of Marshal Redpath, Farren has spent his days scheming for a transfer back south. By taking credit for clearing out the nearby Daggerspine naga, he hopes to present himself as an indispensable, battle-hardened officer ripe for promotion.",sp=0},{t="Keep Connections",b="To secure his reassignment without arousing the suspicion of Marshal Redpath, Farren bypasses the local chain of command entirely. He relies instead on his personal ties to Major Samuelson, a senior officer in Stormwind Keep who once mentored him. Delivering the polished report directly into Samuelson's hands ensures that Farren's alleged accomplishments land on the desk of someone with the authority to reassign garrison personnel.",sp=0},{t="Bureaucracy at Work",b="Upon receiving the dossier in Stormwind Keep, Major Samuelson expresses mild approval of his former pupil's initiative regarding the naga menace. However, military bureaucracy grinds slowly. Rather than issuing an immediate transfer, Samuelson merely promises to weigh the report during next month's routine personnel reviews, leaving Farren's fate in Southshore hanging in the balance.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Why does Farren Orinelle want a reassignment?",a="Lieutenant Farren Orinelle loathes being stationed in Southshore, viewing the remote northern outpost as dull, dangerous, and beneath him. He longs to return to the relative luxury and safety of Stormwind City, and seeks to use his reports on the naga to justify a transfer.",al={"why leave southshore","farren motive","why does farren want to leave"},it="motive"},{q="Who is Major Samuelson?",a="Major Samuelson is a high-ranking officer in Stormwind Keep who oversees city guard assignments. Prior to his current post, he served as Lieutenant Farren Orinelle's mentor during Farren's early career in the capital.",al={"who is samuelson","samuelson lore"},it="identity"},{q="Why can't Farren deliver the report himself?",a="Farren is on active duty in Southshore and cannot abandon his post without permission. Furthermore, he is attempting to bypass his immediate superior, Marshal Redpath, who would likely obstruct a self-serving transfer request.",al={"why do i have to deliver it","why not deliver himself"},it="why_me"},{q="Did Farren actually defeat the naga himself?",a="No. Farren tasked independent adventurers with hunting the Daggerspine naga along the coast and collecting heads, scales, and intelligence. He then compiled their hard work into a formal dispatch that framed the campaign as his own strategic triumph.",al={"did farren kill naga","farren report truth"},it="history"},{q="Does Farren actually get transferred back to Stormwind?",a="Not immediately. Major Samuelson promises only to consider the report during the next month's personnel review. Farren remains stationed in Southshore for the foreseeable future while the wheels of the kingdom's military bureaucracy slowly turn.",al={"does farren get reassigned","does transfer work"},sp=1,it="next_step"},{q="Where is Major Samuelson located?",a="Major Samuelson stands inside Stormwind Keep, the fortress at the heart of Stormwind City where the high command and regency council reside.",al={"samuelson location","where is major samuelson"},it="place",gp=true}},ang={["faction:Alliance"]="This errand illustrates the everyday bureaucratic politics of the Alliance military, where distant frontier garrisons like Southshore often clash with the comfortable ambitions of officers looking to return to Stormwind.",["race:Human"]="The delivery reveals the contrast between the embattled human refugees and defenders holding the line in Lordaeron and the political maneuvering inside the high halls of Stormwind Keep."},kw={"daggerspine","farren orinelle","major samuelson","reassignment","redpath","southshore","stormwind keep"},rel={"quest:562","npc:lieutenant-farren-orinelle","npc:major-samuelson","subzone:southshore","subzone:stormwind-keep","quest:559","quest:536","zone:hillsbrad"},m={start="Lieutenant Farren Orinelle",["end"]="Major Samuelson",level="32",faction="Alliance",id=563},src={"Reassignment"}}
E["quest:567"] = {t="quest",n="Dangerous!",z="hillsbrad",s="Posted on the wanted board in Tarren Mill, this bounty marks four prominent Hillsbrad humans for execution. High Executor Darthalia has declared them dangerous enemies of the Forsaken due to specific assassinations and supply ambushes.",h="Posted on the wanted board in Tarren Mill, this bounty marks four prominent Hillsbrad humans for execution.",sec={{t="A Matter of Retribution",b="The front lines across the Hillsbrad Foothills are brutal and personal. To High Executor Darthalia and the Forsaken garrison at Tarren Mill, ordinary citizens of Hillsbrad have become lethal combatants. The wanted notice singles out four specific figures whose resistance has cost Forsaken lives and valuable shipments from the Undercity.",sp=0},{t="Targets of Tarren Mill",b="The bounty names Clerk Horrace Whitesteed for the killing of Deathguard Toma, Citizen Wilkes for the murder of Apothecary Eli, Miner Hackett for taking the life of Deathstalker Fry, and Farmer Kalaba for sabotaging supply convoys sent from the Undercity. Each target operates from different pockets of Hillsbrad resistance, remaining elusive amid the chaos of the broader conflict.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who posted the Dangerous! bounty?",a="High Executor Darthalia, commander of the Forsaken forces stationed at Tarren Mill, issued the bounty against four prominent Hillsbrad humans.",al={"who posted dangerous","who gave dangerous quest","darthalia bounty"},it="identity"},{q="Why are these specific humans wanted?",a="Each has struck a blow against the Forsaken: Clerk Horrace Whitesteed killed Deathguard Toma, Citizen Wilkes murdered Apothecary Eli, Miner Hackett slew Deathstalker Fry, and Farmer Kalaba ambushed essential supplies sent from the Undercity.",al={"why are they dangerous","what did they do","hillsbrad targets crime"},it="why_wanted"},{q="Where are the targets located?",a="All four targets are entrenched across the human settlements and worksites of Hillsbrad Foothills, hiding among the townsfolk, farms, and mines.",al={"where to find targets","dangerous quest locations","hackett location"},it="place",gp=true},{q="What is the strategic purpose of this contract?",a="Beyond raw vengeance, eliminating these leaders cripples local human resistance and protects Forsaken patrols and supply lines traveling between Tarren Mill and the Undercity.",al={"why kill them","hillsbrad bounty goal","tarren mill strategy"},it="purpose"},{q="Does this connect to the Battle of Hillsbrad?",a="Yes. The targets of this bounty reside in the very farms, mines, and town centers that Forsaken forces assault during the broader Battle of Hillsbrad offensive.",al={"battle of hillsbrad connection","darthalia battle","hillsbrad offensive"},it="conflict"},{q="Who turns in the bounty once they are slain?",a="Proof of their elimination is delivered directly to High Executor Darthalia in Tarren Mill.",al={"who completes dangerous","dangerous turn in","darthalia turn in"},it="next_step",gp=true},{q="Why does High Executor Darthalia want these four humans eliminated?",a="High Executor Darthalia posted the bounty because these four individuals struck direct, crippling blows against Tarren Mill's key operations. Clerk Whitesteed, Citizen Wilkes, and Miner Hackett each assassinated vital Forsaken personnel—a Deathguard, an Apothecary, and a Deathstalker scout. Farmer Kalaba intercepted crucial supply caravans arriving from the Undercity. Eliminating them avenges fallen comrades, secures the supply lines, and removes dangerous guerrilla threats from the Hillsbrad front.",al={"why kill them","darthalia motive","why are they wanted dead"},it="motive",add=true},{q="Who are the targets marked on the Dangerous! bounty?",a="Your targets are four influential Hillsbrad residents who have taken up arms against the Forsaken: Clerk Horrace Whitesteed, Citizen Wilkes, Miner Hackett, and Farmer Kalaba. While they appear to be ordinary townsfolk, miners, and laborers, each has proven exceptionally deadly and resourceful, operating from concealment across the foothills and fields to wage irregular warfare against Tarren Mill.",al={"who are the targets","dangerous bounty targets","who to kill"},it="target",add=true},{q="Why does High Executor Darthalia rely on adventurers instead of her own Deathguards?",a="Tarren Mill's military forces are already stretched thin holding defensive perimeters and waging pitched skirmishes across Hillsbrad. Furthermore, the targets are not marching in the open; they have gone into hiding across civilian farms, mines, and backroads. Darthalia relies on roving bounty hunters and capable adventurers who can move independently, track down evasive targets, and root them out behind enemy lines without drawing away entire garrison units.",al={"why not use guards","why me dangerous","why send adventurers"},it="why_me",add=true}},ang={["race:Undead"]="Avenging fallen Deathguards, Apothecaries, and Deathstalkers is a point of grim pride for any loyal servant of the Dark Lady.",["faction:Horde"]="Securing Hillsbrad Foothills requires breaking the human militia's fiercest figures, ensuring the safety of Horde movements through the region.",["class:Rogue"]="Tracking down concealed leaders in hostile territory mirrors the covert trade of Deathstalker Fry, whose death this contract avenges."},kw={"apothecary eli","citizen wilkes","clerk horrace whitesteed","dangerous","deathguard toma","deathstalker fry","farmer kalaba","high executor darthalia","hillsbrad","miner hackett","tarren mill","undercity"},rel={"npc:high-executor-darthalia","subzone:tarren-mill","quest:527","zone:hillsbrad","zone:undercity"},m={start="Dangerous!",level="28",faction="Horde",id=567},src={"Dangerous! (quest)"}}
E["quest:676"] = {t="quest",n="The Hammer May Fall",z="hillsbrad",s="Dispatched by Tallow from Tarren Mill, Horde champions are directed across the mountains into the Arathi Highlands to relieve the embattled settlement of Hammerfall. Before reporting to Drum Fel, adventurers must prove their battle readiness against the brutish Boulderfist ogres lurking near the ruins of Stromgarde.",h="Dispatched by Tallow from Tarren Mill, Horde champions are directed across the mountains into the Arathi...",sec={{t="A Gruff Summons",b="In Tarren Mill, Tallow harbors little patience for untested adventurers wandering through the Foothills. Seeing undisciplined recruits standing idle while distant allies bleed, he directs capable fighters east through Thoradin's Wall into the Arathi Highlands. The Horde outpost of Hammerfall stands besieged on multiple fronts, but Tallow refuses to send warm bodies unless they have proven their worth against substantial opposition first.",sp=0},{t="Trial by Boulderfist",b="Rather than allowing recruits to stumble blindly into Hammerfall, Tallow demands a demonstration of martial strength at the ogre mound northeast of Stromgarde. The Boulderfist tribe maintains a heavy presence in Arathi, their hulking ogres and enforcers posing an immediate threat to anyone traveling the highland trails. Slaying these brutes serves both to thin the hostile forces flanking the road and to ensure that only capable warriors arrive at the outpost.",sp=0},{t="Reporting to Hammerfall",b="Upon clearing out the Boulderfist encampment, the path leads northeast to Hammerfall, an outpost named in memory of Warchief Orgrim Doomhammer. There, commander Drum Fel accepts fresh arrivals with weary skepticism. Whether Tallow intended to bolster the garrison or simply send fools to their deaths, Drum Fel wastes no time turning proven fighters toward the endless skirmishes threatening the outpost's survival.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Where does this quest begin and end?",a="The quest is offered by Tallow in Tarren Mill, located in the Hillsbrad Foothills. After completing the required kills in Arathi Highlands, it is turned in to Drum Fel inside the Horde outpost of Hammerfall.",al={"where do i start the hammer may fall","quest turn in location","who gives the hammer may fall"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Where are the Boulderfist ogres located?",a="The Boulderfist ogres inhabit a prominent dirt mound and surrounding camp located northeast of the ruins of Stromgarde in the Arathi Highlands.",al={"boulderfist ogre location","where are the ogres in arathi","boulderfist mound"},it="target",gp=true},{q="What is the outpost of Hammerfall?",a="Hammerfall is a fortified Horde settlement in northeastern Arathi Highlands. It is named in honor of former Warchief Orgrim Doomhammer, who fell in battle nearby during the liberation of the orc internment camps.",al={"what is hammerfall","hammerfall lore","who founded hammerfall"},it="place"},{q="Why does Tallow make you fight ogres before reporting to Hammerfall?",a="Hammerfall is under constant attack and desperate for capable fighters. Tallow sends recruits against the Boulderfist ogres as a harsh proving ground, ensuring that anyone arriving to reinforce Drum Fel can actually fight rather than becoming an added burden.",al={"why kill ogres first","tallow motive","why test me"},it="motive"},{q="Who is Drum Fel?",a="Drum Fel is a veteran orc warrior and commander stationed at Hammerfall in the Arathi Highlands, tasked with organizing defense forces against hostile wildlife, ogres, trolls, and Alliance remnants.",al={"drum fel identity","hammerfall commander","who is drum fel"},it="identity"},{q="What follows this assignment?",a="Reporting to Drum Fel leads directly into the Call to Arms campaign, a sequence of military operations aimed at clearing surrounding threats, including the Witherbark troll tribes threatening the highlands.",al={"next quest","hammer may fall followup","what comes after"},it="next_step"},{q="Who are the Boulderfist ogres you are sent against?",a="The Boulderfist tribe is a brutish clan of ogres claiming territory across the Arathi Highlands, centered around their mound northeast of the ruins of Stromgarde. Fierce, stubborn, and physically imposing, they dominate the highlands' rocky hills and contest the surrounding territory. Tallow sends you to their mound to see if you can survive their frontline enforcers, ensuring you have the strength required before you throw yourself into the meat grinder of the Arathi war zone.",al={"boulderfist ogres","who are boulderfist","ogres arathi"},it="target",add=true}},ang={["faction:Horde"]="This task marks the primary transition from the localized disputes of Hillsbrad into the wider defense of Arathi Highlands, reinforcing Hammerfall's vital foothold in the region.",["race:Orc"]="Hammerfall holds profound sentimental and historical value for orcs, having been founded where Warchief Orgrim Doomhammer gave his life during the liberation campaigns.",["class:Warrior"]="Facing hulking Boulderfist enforcers serves as a classic proving ground for frontline fighters looking to earn the respect of veteran orc commanders like Drum Fel."},kw={"arathi highlands","boulderfist enforcer","boulderfist ogre","drum fel","hammerfall","hillsbrad foothills","stromgarde","tallow","tarren mill","the hammer may fall"},rel={"npc:tallow","npc:drum-fel","subzone:hammerfall","subzone:tarren-mill","zone:arathi","zone:hillsbrad","topic:troll"},m={start="Tallow",["end"]="Drum Fel",level="32",faction="Horde",id=676},src={"The Hammer May Fall"}}
E["quest:7161"] = {t="quest",n="Proving Grounds",z="hillsbrad",s="Proving Grounds is an initiation rite required of any Horde warrior who seeks to join the Frostwolf Clan's campaign in Alterac Valley. To prove their worth, recruits must brave the gnoll-infested Wildpaw Cavern and recover a lost clan standard.",h="Proving Grounds is an initiation rite required of any Horde warrior who seeks to join the Frostwolf Clan's...",sec={{t="The Call to Arms",b="Before any soldier of the Horde is trusted to fight alongside General Drek'Thar's forces in Alterac Valley, they must prove their spirit is primed for war. Warmaster Laggrond tests newly arrived champions by sending them straight into hostile territory. This trial separates ordinary travelers from true warriors capable of answering the ancient call to battle and channeling the clan's ancestral fury.",sp=0},{t="Trial in the Wildpaw Cavern",b="The initiation demands braving the Wildpaw Cavern, a cold cave system south of the Frostwolf stronghold swarming with aggressive local gnolls. Somewhere deep inside the burrows lies an abandoned Frostwolf banner. Recovering this emblem under the fangs and claws of the Wildpaw beasts demonstrates courage, resilience, and battle readiness to the warmasters.",sp=0},{t="Earning the Insignia",b="Returning the retrieved banner to Laggrond completes the rite. With their spirit deemed fully awakened to the conflict, the recruit receives a Frostwolf initiate's insignia. This trinket serves as a badge of honor and a symbol of allegiance, marking the warrior's first official step toward rising through the clan's esteemed ranks.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is the purpose of the Proving Grounds rite?",a="The rite tests newly arrived Horde soldiers to verify they possess the martial spirit and grit necessary to endure the brutal war against the Stormpike dwarves in Alterac Valley.",al={"why do proving grounds","frostwolf initiation","purpose of quest"},it="purpose"},{q="Who gives the quest and where do I find them?",a="Warmaster Laggrond gives the quest. He is stationed by the Horde entrance to Alterac Valley in the Alterac Mountains, ready to test and induct recruits who seek to join the Frostwolf Clan's ranks.",al={"who starts proving grounds","warmaster laggrond location","where is laggrond"},it="in_charge",gp=true},{q="Where is the Frostwolf Banner located?",a="The banner is hidden deep inside the Wildpaw Cavern, a gnoll-infested cave situated southeast of the main Frostwolf base in Alterac Valley.",al={"frostwolf banner location","where is banner","wildpaw cavern banner"},it="place",gp=true},{q="What creatures dwell inside the Wildpaw Cavern?",a="The cavern is held by the Wildpaw gnolls, a hostile tribe adapted to the freezing mountains that savagely defends its underground dens from intruders.",al={"wildpaw gnolls","what is in cave","wildpaw enemies"},it="danger"},{q="What is the significance of the Frostwolf insignia?",a="The insignia marks an adventurer as an accepted initiate of the Frostwolf Clan. As recruits prove themselves further and rise in standing, the warmaster replaces it with more prestigious badges of rank.",al={"frostwolf insignia use","what is the insignia","rank insignia"},it="power"},{q="What is the Frostwolf Clan's stake in Alterac Valley?",a="Alterac Valley has long been the ancestral sanctuary of the Frostwolf orcs since their exile during the First War. They fiercely guard its valleys against the intrusion of the dwarven Stormpike Guard.",al={"why are frostwolves in alterac","frostwolf lore alterac","alterac valley conflict"},it="conflict"},{q="Why does Warmaster Laggrond want this done?",a="Warmaster Laggrond needs every warrior entering Alterac Valley to prove their mettle before marching alongside the Frostwolf Clan. War against the Stormpike dwarves demands absolute resolve, and the warmaster requires newcomers to awaken their inner battle rage and spirit through trial before he will entrust them with a place in the clan's ranks.",al={"warmaster laggrond motive","why laggrond sends you","why proving grounds rite"},it="motive",add=true},{q="What is the Frostwolf Banner for?",a="The Frostwolf Banner serves as the objective for your rite of initiation. Deep inside the Wildpaw gnoll den, the standard stands as a test of courage and strength; recovering it proves to Warmaster Laggrond that your fighting spirit is awake and worthy of bearing the Frostwolf name.",al={"what is frostwolf banner","frostwolf banner purpose","why get the banner"},it="item",add=true},{q="Who are you sent against in Wildpaw Cavern?",a="You are sent against the Wildpaw gnolls, an indigenous tribe that has claimed the caves southeast of the Frostwolf stronghold. Their lair holds the banner, making their fierce, territorial pack the primary obstacle standing between you and proving your worth to the clan.",al={"wildpaw gnolls target","who are the wildpaw gnolls","what are wildpaw gnolls"},it="target",add=true}},ang={["faction:Horde"]="Every soldier of the Horde must earn their place in the eyes of the Frostwolves before marching out across the icy plains of Alterac.",["race:Orc"]="For orcs, returning the banner to the Frostwolf Clan honors the venerable traditions and ancestral home established by Chieftain Durotan.",["class:Warrior"]="The trial is designed to stir martial fury and hone instincts, ensuring recruits are ready for the brutal clash of arms against the Stormpike vanguard."},kw={"alterac valley","frostwolf banner","frostwolf insignia","proving grounds","warmaster laggrond","wildpaw cavern","wildpaw gnolls"},rel={"npc:warmaster-laggrond","topic:gnoll","zone:hillsbrad","topic:alterac-kingdom"},m={start="Warmaster Laggrond",faction="Horde",id=7161,ri={"Frostwolf Banner"}},src={"Proving Grounds (Alterac Valley) (Horde)"}}
E["quest:7162"] = {t="quest",n="Proving Grounds",z="hillsbrad",s="Proving Grounds is an initiation rite given by Lieutenant Haggerdin to Alliance recruits enlisting with the Stormpike Guard in Alterac. To earn an official Stormpike Insignia, aspirants must venture into the harpy-infested Icewing Caverns and recover a planted battle standard. Proving one's courage in the cavern marks the first step toward rising through the expedition's military ranks.",h="Proving Grounds is an initiation rite given by Lieutenant Haggerdin to Alliance recruits enlisting with the...",sec={{t="A Measure of Courage",b="The Stormpike Guard wages a relentless campaign in Alterac Valley against the Frostwolf Clan. Lieutenant Haggerdin, coordinating forces from the Alliance encampment in the Alterac Mountains, refuses to send green recruits onto the battlefield without a test. Before granting any soldier an official place in the guard, Haggerdin demands proof of skill and nerve by sending them into the treacherous Icewing Caverns southwest of Dun Baldar.",sp=0},{t="The Icewing Caverns",b="The trial is straightforward in concept but deadly in execution: a Stormpike banner stands planted deep within the subterranean ice tunnels. The caverns are not empty; vicious frost harpies nest in the frostbitten recesses and eagerly tear apart unwary trespassers. Returning with the banner intact demonstrates that a recruit can navigate dangerous terrain, withstand brutal predators, and maintain discipline under pressure.",sp=0},{t="The Stormpike Insignia",b="Surviving the cavern and returning the standard earns a soldier the Stormpike initiate's insignia, welcoming them officially into the expeditionary force. As Haggerdin promises, the insignia is not merely a trinket—it is a mark of rank that can be enhanced as a soldier earns greater honor on the battlefield, aspiring toward legendary honors such as the Eye of Command.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Lieutenant Haggerdin?",a="Lieutenant Haggerdin is an Alliance officer stationed in the Alterac Mountains who oversees recruitment and field recognition for the Stormpike Guard. He tests prospective fighters and rewards their service with military insignias.",al={"lieutenant haggerdin","haggerdin","who gives proving grounds"},it="identity"},{q="Where are the Icewing Caverns?",a="The Icewing Caverns lie southwest of the Alliance stronghold of Dun Baldar inside the frozen reaches of Alterac Valley. They are labyrinthine subterranean tunnels carved out of ice and stone.",al={"icewing caverns location","where is icewing caverns","banner location"},it="place",gp=true},{q="What threats dwell inside the Icewing Caverns?",a="The caverns are inhabited by ferocious ice harpies. Lieutenant Haggerdin warns recruits that these savage creatures will not hesitate to ambush trespassers and tear out their throats.",al={"harpies","what is in icewing caverns","icewing harpies"},it="danger"},{q="Why does the Stormpike Guard require this test?",a="The battle against the Frostwolf orcs is brutal and unforgiving. Haggerdin insists on weeding out untested recruits before they join the main lines, ensuring every soldier bearing their banner can fight under harsh conditions.",al={"why proving grounds","why do the banner trial","stormpike initiation"},it="motive"},{q="What is the reward for completing the proving ground?",a="Completing the trial rewards the recruit with a Stormpike initiate's insignia. Haggerdin upgrades this insignia to more powerful versions as the soldier accumulates honor in Alterac Valley.",al={"stormpike insignia","eye of command","proving grounds reward"},gp=true},{q="Who are the Frostwolves mentioned by Haggerdin?",a="The Frostwolf Clan is an orcish clan that has inhabited Alterac Valley since their exile decades ago. The Stormpike Guard considers them hostile savages standing in the way of Alliance interests and excavation in the valley.",al={"frostwolf savages","who are the frostwolves","frostwolf clan"},it="threat"},{q="What is the purpose of the Stormpike Banner in the caverns?",a="Planted deep inside the dangerous Icewing Caverns, the Stormpike Banner serves as a trial marker for recruits seeking to enlist in the expeditionary force. To claim it, you must brave the feral wildkin and vicious harpies that infest the caves, demonstrating the courage, resourcefulness, and grit required of a true Stormpike soldier before ever setting foot on the open battlefield.",al={"what is stormpike banner","why banner in icewing caverns","stormpike banner purpose"},it="item",add=true}},ang={["faction:Alliance"]="The Stormpike expedition represents the Alliance's primary military endeavor in Alterac, blending dwarven archaeological ambitions with territorial defense against the Horde.",["race:Dwarf"]="The Stormpike Guard is predominantly led by Ironforge dwarves seeking ancestral relics and titan mysteries, making this trial an entry into one of your race's proudest military units."},kw={"dun baldar","haggerdin","harpies","icewing caverns","insignia","proving grounds","stormpike","stormpike banner"},rel={"npc:lieutenant-haggerdin","zone:alterac","zone:hillsbrad","topic:alterac-kingdom"},m={start="Lieutenant Haggerdin",faction="Alliance",id=7162,ri={"Stormpike Banner"}},src={"Proving Grounds (Alterac Valley) (Alliance)"}}
E["quest:7321"] = {t="quest",n="Soothing Turtle Bisque",z="hillsbrad",s="Soothing Turtle Bisque is a culinary task offered by Christoph Jeffcoat in Tarren Mill. The Forsaken cook aims to disprove the notion that the undead lack culinary talent by preparing a hearty broth from local snapjaw meat. Players must hunt freshwater turtles around the waterways of Hillsbrad Foothills and the shores of Lordamere Lake to master his prized recipe.",h="Soothing Turtle Bisque is a culinary task offered by Christoph Jeffcoat in Tarren Mill.",sec={{t="Forsaken Gastronomy",b="It is widely assumed that the Forsaken have entirely abandoned the comforts of life, including the art of fine dining. Christoph Jeffcoat, stationed in Tarren Mill, vigorously rejects that assumption. Boasting that his rich, soothing turtle bisque is good enough to tempt souls back from beyond the grave, Jeffcoat seeks to prove that undead hands are capable of delicate, heartwarming craft even in a land tainted by plague and war.",sp=0},{t="Hunting the Snapjaws",b="Ordinarily, Jeffcoat gathered his own ingredients from the waterways of Hillsbrad Foothills and the eastern shores of Lordamere Lake in neighboring Alterac. However, duties in Tarren Mill and the encroaching presence of Alliance forces have pinned him down. He relies on passing Horde cooks to hunt the snapjaws, harvest their meat, and bring it back so the culinary tradition can endure.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Why does a Forsaken cook care about making hot bisque?",a="While the Forsaken do not require sustenance in the same manner as living mortals, individuals like Christoph Jeffcoat take great pride in their trade. Jeffcoat aims to disprove the prejudice that undead lack refined skill, joking that his signature broth is good enough to bring the deceased back to life.",al={"undead cooking","why make bisque","undead eat food"},it="motive"},{q="Where can turtle meat be found for this recipe?",a="Turtle meat is harvested from the aggressive snapjaws dwelling along the rivers running through Hillsbrad Foothills and Alterac, as well as along the shores of Lordamere Lake.",al={"where are turtles","turtle locations","snapjaw locations"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Why can't Christoph Jeffcoat gather his own ingredients?",a="Jeffcoat claims he is tied down with responsibilities in Tarren Mill. He also expresses irritation at the encroaching Alliance forces nearby, which make personal hunting excursions far more hazardous.",al={"why doesn't christoph go","jeffcoat stuck in town"},it="why_me"},{q="Is cooking knowledge required to take this quest?",a="Yes. Christoph Jeffcoat will only share his craft and recipe with fellow practitioners of the cooking profession, though it does not demand any advanced mastery to begin.",al={"do i need cooking","cooking profession requirement"},gp=true},{q="What is Tarren Mill's importance to the Horde in Hillsbrad?",a="Tarren Mill serves as the primary Horde stronghold in the Hillsbrad Foothills. Formerly a human village, it now functions as a fortified base for the Forsaken and their allies, facing frequent clashes against Southshore and the regional Alliance presence.",al={"what is tarren mill","tarren mill lore"},it="place"},{q="Is turtle bisque unique to the Horde?",a="Alliance cooks can acquire the recipe from local human chefs in Southshore who also make use of the local turtle population, but Christoph Jeffcoat's personal quest and perspective are exclusive to the Horde.",al={"alliance version","can alliance get turtle bisque"}},{q="What is the Turtle Meat for?",a="Christoph Jeffcoat needs the turtle meat to brew his signature soothing turtle bisque. While the undead may not feel the cold or hunger like the living, Jeffcoat takes immense pride in his culinary craft. He claims his secret recipe is so good that people would return from the dead just to savor a hot bowl.",al={"turtle meat use","why turtle meat","what is turtle meat used for"},it="item",add=true},{q="What are the snapjaws you hunt for this bisque?",a="Snapjaws are vicious, hard-shelled freshwater turtles native to the waterways of Lordaeron, particularly plentiful along the shores of Lake Lordamere and the local riverbanks. While feral and dangerous to unwary travelers, their tough flesh provides the vital, rich meat Christoph requires for his bisque.",al={"snapjaws hillsbrad","lake lordamere snapjaws","who do i hunt"},it="target",add=true}},ang={["profession:Cooking"]="This task allows cooks to master Soothing Turtle Bisque, turning the aggressive reptiles of Lordamere Lake and Hillsbrad's rivers into a restorative meal.",["race:Undead"]="Christoph Jeffcoat represents a lighter, craft-driven side of the Forsaken, insisting that death has not dulled his culinary passion.",["faction:Horde"]="Supporting the garrison at Tarren Mill involves more than defending its borders; keeping provisions and morale high helps secure the Horde's footing in contested Hillsbrad."},kw={"christoph jeffcoat","cooking","hillsbrad foothills","lordamere lake","snapjaw","soothing turtle bisque","tarren mill","turtle meat"},rel={"npc:christoph-jeffcoat","subzone:tarren-mill","zone:hillsbrad","subzone:lordamere-lake","zone:alterac","topic:horde","topic:alliance","quest:555"},m={start="Christoph Jeffcoat",level="31",faction="Horde",id=7321,ri={"Turtle Meat"}},src={"Soothing Turtle Bisque (Horde)"}}
E["quest:8249"] = {t="quest",n="Junkboxes Needed",z="hillsbrad",s="At Ravenholdt Manor, Winstone Wolfe maintains an endless demand for sturdy, locked containers to train the guild's rising rogues. Because the practice locks provided by the manor's own craftsman are too simple for advanced students, Wolfe trades specialized throwing knives to anyone willing to supply authentic heavy junkboxes.",h="At Ravenholdt Manor, Winstone Wolfe maintains an endless demand for sturdy, locked containers to train the...",sec={{t="Sharpening Ravenholdt's Talons",b="Within the hidden redoubt of Ravenholdt Manor, nestled in the mountains above Hillsbrad Foothills, training never ceases. Master thief Winstone Wolfe oversees instruction for the guild's operatives, placing high value on practical lockpicking mastery. While Zan provides practice contraptions for new recruits, Wolfe considers that crude work entirely unfit for experienced operatives who must crack real, stubborn mechanisms in the field.",sp=0},{t="A Curiously Open Arrangement",b="To keep the manor supplied with real-world mechanisms, Wolfe contracts out for heavy junkboxes swiped from dangerous targets across Azeroth. Though only skilled thieves can lift these boxes from marks in the wild, Wolfe does not restrict his business solely to rogues. Anyone who delivers batches of these locked chests—even if already picked clean of major valuables—earns Wolfe's favor and a supply of the manor's lethally balanced throwing blades, provided a token coin remains inside to motivate the initiates.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Why does Winstone Wolfe want these junkboxes?",a="Ravenholdt's apprentice rogues need realistic mechanisms to practice lockpicking. Wolfe finds the practice chests made by the manor's resident craftsman, Zan, far too elementary for anyone past rank beginners, requiring true lockboxes harvested from dangerous marks.",al={"why junkboxes","junkboxes purpose","why wolfe wants boxes"},it="motive"},{q="Where does this task take place?",a="The exchange takes place at Ravenholdt Manor, a secret refuge for the guild of thieves concealed within the mountains north of the Hillsbrad Foothills.",al={"junkboxes needed location","where is winstone wolfe","ravenholdt location"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Can only rogues turn in this quest?",a="While the heavy junkboxes themselves are originally procured through the rogue art of pickpocketing, Winstone Wolfe accepts deliveries from anyone capable of bringing them to the manor.",al={"is this rogue only","can anyone do junkboxes needed","other classes junkboxes"},it="why_me",gp=true},{q="Why must there still be coins left inside the boxes?",a="Wolfe insists that a few coins remain inside each chest because even rogues in training need practical incentive and tangible reward to spur their lockpicking efforts.",al={"why leave coins in box","do boxes need loot","empty junkboxes"},it="purpose"},{q="What does Ravenholdt offer in exchange?",a="Wolfe rewards contributors with guild standing and finely crafted throwing knives, which he sardonically wishes will find a place directly in someone's heart.",al={"junkboxes needed reward","what does wolfe give","ravenholdt throwing knives"},it="for_you"},{q="Who is Zan that Wolfe complains about?",a="Zan is Ravenholdt's in-house locks supplier. Wolfe considers Zan's practice mechanisms crude and suitable only for the rawest neophytes rather than serious operatives.",al={"who is zan","zan ravenholdt","zan locks"},it="people"},{q="Why does Winstone Wolfe need an outside rogue to gather junkboxes?",a="Ravenholdt's current trainees are still cutting their teeth and simply lack the skill to obtain intricate locks on their own. The practice mechanisms crafted by their in-house tinker, Zan, are far too crude for advanced training. Wolfe relies on accomplished operatives like you to venture into perilous territory and filch genuine, high-security lockboxes that pose a real challenge.",al={"why ask me for junkboxes","why winstone wolfe needs me","why doesn't ravenholdt get their own junkboxes"},it="why_me",add=true}},ang={["class:Rogue"]="Sourcing these heavy chests relies entirely on the art of pickpocketing seasoned adversaries, cementing Ravenholdt as the ultimate clearinghouse for a rogue's illicit skills.",["faction:Alliance"]="Though hidden in contested Lordaeron territory, Ravenholdt operates independently, accepting contracts from Alliance wanderers without regard for faction lines.",["faction:Horde"]="Horde operatives who brave the trek into the Hillsbrad mountains find Ravenholdt strictly indifferent to faction loyalties, prizing useful illicit goods above all else."},kw={"heavy junkbox","hillsbrad","junkboxes","lockpicking","pickpocket","ravenholdt","winstone wolfe","zan"},rel={"npc:winstone-wolfe","topic:ravenholdt","zone:hillsbrad"},m={start="Winstone Wolfe",["end"]="Winstone Wolfe",id=8249},src={"Junkboxes Needed"}}
E["subzone:alterac-mountains"] = {t="subzone",n="Alterac Mountains",z="hillsbrad",s="The Alterac Mountains are a rugged, snow-capped range rising directly above the rolling pastures of Hillsbrad. Once the heart of a proud human kingdom, the slopes now harbor ruined settlements, bandit factions, and dangerous wilderness where travelers rarely walk unguarded.",h="The Alterac Mountains are a rugged, snow-capped range rising directly above the rolling pastures of Hillsbrad.",sec={{t="A Fallen Realm",b="Long before the hills fell into chaos, these highlands formed the sovereign nation of Alterac, one of the seven kingdoms born from ancient Arathor. That legacy shattered during the Second War when King Aiden Perenolde struck a clandestine pact with the Old Horde, allowing orcish forces passage through the peaks in exchange for his kingdom's safety. The Alliance of Lordaeron uncovered the betrayal and deposed Perenolde, leaving the region fractured by martial law and territorial disputes.",sp=0},{t="Wilderness and Bandits",b="Following the devastation of the Third War, the mountains collapsed into complete lawlessness. The disinherited nobles of the realm banded together to form the Syndicate, operating out of the ruins of Strahnbrad and plotting to reclaim their lost dominion through sabotage and assassination. Between ruthless Crushridge ogres occupying the shattered capital, marauding gnolls, and the shattered magical ruins around Dalaran, the passes of Alterac remain some of the most perilous pathways in Lordaeron.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What kingdom used to rule these mountains?",a="The human kingdom of Alterac held these mountains for generations after the splintering of the Empire of Arathor. Its capital sat among the highest peaks, commanding the roads between Lordaeron, Dalaran, and the Arathi highlands until its fall during the Second War.",al={"who owned alterac","what was alterac","alterac kingdom lore"},it="history"},{q="Why is Alterac in ruins?",a="During the Second War, King Aiden Perenolde betrayed the Alliance of Lordaeron by assisting the Horde. When the treason was exposed, Alliance armies crushed Alterac's forces and deposed the crown. With no legitimate ruler and subsequent devastation from the Third War, the nation collapsed into rubble.",al={"what happened to alterac","who destroyed alterac","ruins of alterac backstory"},it="ruin"},{q="Who are the Syndicate lurking in the hills?",a="The Syndicate is an outlaw syndicate made up of former Alteraci nobility and their retainers. Led by Aliden Perenolde, they employ brigands, assassins, and rogue mercenaries to destabilize the region in hopes of violently restoring their kingdom.",al={"who is the syndicate","what is the syndicate","why are there bandits in alterac"},it="people"},{q="What threats wander the snowy peaks?",a="Travelers brave enough to climb the slopes must contend with the brutal Crushridge ogres, packs of Highland gnolls, scavenging kobolds, and opportunistic Syndicate brigands patrolling the passes.",al={"what lives in alterac","alterac monsters","threats in alterac"},it="danger"},{q="What are the Alterac Mountains?",a="The Alterac Mountains are a rugged, snow-capped range rising in central Lordaeron just north of the Hillsbrad Foothills. Once the sovereign territory of the human kingdom of Alterac, these heights held fortified cities, mountain keeps, and remote valleys. Today, the nation is broken and its towns lie shattered in the snow, leaving the freezing peaks a battleground for lingering outcasts, warring clans, and predatory monsters.",al={"what is alterac mountains","alterac mountains lore","alterac region overview"},it="place",add=true},{q="Who rules the Alterac Mountains today?",a="No legitimate government holds the Alterac Mountains. The kingdom collapsed after its treason in the Second War, and whatever order remained vanished during the Scourge's onslaught. Today, the Syndicate—dispossessed human nobles and outlaws led by the Perenolde bloodline—claims ancestral rights to the ruins. However, they violently contend with brutish Crushridge ogres, wandering undead, and entrenched Frostwolf orcs hidden in the high valleys.",al={"who controls alterac","who lives in alterac mountains","alterac leadership"},it="residents",add=true}},ang={["faction:Alliance"]="For the Alliance, Alterac stands as a bitter monument to betrayal, where Perenolde's treachery nearly doomed humanity during the Second War.",["class:Rogue"]="The mountain passes are rife with Syndicate agents and hired cutthroats, making the hills a prime testing ground for survival and counter-espionage."},kw={"alterac","crushridge","hillsbrad","mountains","perenolde","strahnbrad","syndicate"},rel={"zone:hillsbrad","zone:alterac","subzone:ruins-of-alterac","subzone:strahnbrad","topic:alterac-kingdom","topic:syndicate","topic:alliance-of-lordaeron","subzone:dalaran"},src={"Alterac Mountains"}}
E["subzone:azurelode-mine"] = {t="subzone",n="Azurelode Mine",z="hillsbrad",s="Azurelode Mine is an active Alliance iron mine nestled in the southwestern hills of Hillsbrad Foothills. Guarded by Southshore's militia and worked by human laborers, its steady supply of ore fuels the local human war effort against the Forsaken of Tarren Mill.",h="Azurelode Mine is an active Alliance iron mine nestled in the southwestern hills of Hillsbrad Foothills.",sec={{t="Veins of the Foothills",b="Situated southwest of the open farmland and just west of Southshore, Azurelode Mine has long tapped into the mineral-rich ridges along the coast. Before the Greymane Wall was sealed, these hills were considered part of Gilnean territory. Today, human miners labor deep underground under the watchful eye of Foreman Bonds, extracting iron to forge arms and armor for the Alliance defenders holding the region against the Undercity.",sp=0},{t="A Vital Military Target",b="Because Azurelode Mine supplies the bulk of the raw iron needed to maintain Southshore's garrisons and town militia, it sits directly in the crosshairs of the Horde. Tarren Mill has targeted its workforce and guards in an effort to shatter the supply lines that sustain Hillsbrad's human strongholds.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who controls Azurelode Mine?",a="Azurelode Mine is controlled by the Alliance and operated by human miners affiliated with Southshore and the Hillsbrad township, overseen on-site by Foreman Bonds.",al={"who runs azurelode","azurelode mine faction","who owns azurelode"},it="in_charge"},{q="Why is the mine important to the Horde?",a="The mine supplies vital iron to the armories of Southshore and local Alliance militia. Tarren Mill's leadership targets the miners and overseers to cripple human weapon production in the Foothills.",al={"why attack azurelode","battle of hillsbrad mine","horde interest in mine"},it="purpose"},{q="Was Azurelode Mine always part of Hillsbrad?",a="Historically, the rugged ridge holding Azurelode Mine fell within the outer borders of Gilneas before King Genn Greymane erected the Greymane Wall, walling his kingdom off from the rest of Lordaeron.",al={"greymane wall history","was azurelode gilneas","gilneas mine"},it="origin"},{q="What metals are mined here?",a="The mine primarily produces iron ore for nearby human armories, though its name also reflects historical deposits of azurite along the coastal hills.",al={"what ore in azurelode","azurelode resources"},it="item"},{q="What is Azurelode Mine?",a="Azurelode Mine is an active iron-mining operation carved into the hills of southwestern Hillsbrad Foothills, situated south of the Hillsbrad Fields and west of Southshore. It serves as a vital strategic asset for the local human population, supplying vital iron to Alliance armories across the region to fuel their ongoing struggle against hostile forces.",al={"azurelode mine","what is azurelode","azurelode mine info"},it="place",add=true},{q="What happened at Azurelode Mine?",a="Originally, Azurelode Mine and its surrounding hillside were claimed as part of the kingdom of Gilneas before the construction of the Greymane Wall sealed that nation off from the world. Left outside the wall, the site was eventually integrated into the Hillsbrad territory. Today, it remains fully garrisoned and operational under Alliance control, though it faces escalating pressure as the Forsaken contest Hillsbrad.",al={"azurelode history","history of azurelode mine","azurelode past"},it="history",add=true},{q="Who lives in or runs Azurelode Mine?",a="The mine is operated by human laborers from the nearby Hillsbrad Fields, directed by Foreman Bonds. Due to the constant danger posed by the Horde and local wildlife, Hillsbrad sentries and armed guards are stationed throughout the tunnels and exterior to defend the miners while they dig.",al={"who runs azurelode mine","azurelode overseer","who works in azurelode"},it="residents",add=true},{q="Is Azurelode Mine dangerous?",a="Yes. Beyond the standard hazards of subterranean excavation, Azurelode Mine is a military target caught in the broader Battle for Hillsbrad. The site is heavily fortified with vigilant human sentries, and Horde operatives frequently probe its tunnels seeking to disrupt ore production, assassinate Foreman Bonds, and slaughter the workforce.",al={"is azurelode dangerous","azurelode threats","danger at azurelode mine"},it="danger",add=true}},ang={["profession:Mining"]="The tunnels inside and the ridges around Azurelode are rich in iron deposits, though Alliance miners guard the interior fiercely.",["faction:Horde"]="Striking at Azurelode Mine cuts off Southshore's supply of fresh iron, directly supporting the Forsaken offensive in the Foothills."},kw={"azurelode mine","foreman bonds","hillsbrad foothills","hillsbrad miners","iron mine","southshore"},rel={"zone:hillsbrad","quest:527","subzone:southshore","subzone:hillsbrad-fields","subzone:greymane-wall","topic:forsaken","topic:alliance"},src={"Azurelode Mine"}}
E["subzone:chillwind-point"] = {t="subzone",n="Chillwind Point",z="hillsbrad",s="Chillwind Point is a rocky rise and ancient troll ruin sitting on the high frontier between the Alterac Mountains, Hillsbrad Foothills, and the Western Plaguelands. It gets its name from the freezing drafts howling through the mountain pass out of the blighted north. Today, it serves as a lonely vantage point inhabited primarily by a lone troll mystic.",h="Chillwind Point is a rocky rise and ancient troll ruin sitting on the high frontier between the Alterac...",sec={{t="A Bitter Crossroads",b="Perched on the borderlands where Hillsbrad gives way to Alterac and the plagued north, Chillwind Point looks out over the mountain ravine leading directly into the Western Plaguelands. Long before Lordaeron claimed these passes, ancient trolls built stone structures upon these heights, the remnants of which still stand weather-beaten against the elements. Today, cold winds blow south through the ravine, carrying the chill of the fallen north into the foothill valleys below.",sp=0},{t="The Windwatcher",b="Despite its bleak exposure and proximity to Scourge-ravaged lands, Chillwind Point is not entirely deserted. The ancient masonry provides shelter for Bath'rah the Windwatcher, a jungle troll hermit who communes with the violent gales coursing through the gap. Travelers and shamans venturing north often seek out his solitary camp amid the ruins to learn the secrets of the mountain currents.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is Chillwind Point?",a="Chillwind Point is an ancient troll ruin situated on a high rise overlooking the pass between Hillsbrad, Alterac, and the Western Plaguelands. It takes its name from the biting drafts that constantly whistle through the adjacent gorge.",al={"chillwind point overview","where is chillwind point","what is this place"},it="place"},{q="Is Chillwind Point the same as Chillwind Camp?",a="No, though they are frequently confused. Chillwind Camp is the fortified Alliance and Argent Dawn outpost just north across the border inside the Western Plaguelands, whereas Chillwind Point is the ruined troll rise slightly to the south.",al={"chillwind point vs camp","chillwind camp difference","is this chillwind camp"}},{q="Who lives at Chillwind Point?",a="The solitary occupant of the ruins is Bath'rah the Windwatcher, a friendly jungle troll who studies the winds and aids elemental seekers and shamans who brave the mountain pass.",al={"who is here","who is the troll","bathrah"},it="residents"},{q="Why is it so cold here?",a="The point sits directly adjacent to a narrow mountain ravine that funnels freezing drafts down from the high northern regions and the blighted expanse of the Western Plaguelands into the lower foothills.",al={"why is it chilly","chill winds","freezing wind"},it="name"},{q="What happened to Chillwind Point in the past?",a="This elevated pass once formed part of the prosperous human kingdom of Lordaeron. Long before Lordaeron's fall, however, trolls established the ancient stone structure that still crowns the hill. Today, it stands as an abandoned relic caught between the troubled lands of Alterac and the blight creeping down from the north.",al={"chillwind point history","past of chillwind point","what happened at chillwind point"},it="history",add=true},{q="Why is Chillwind Point in ruins?",a="The stone edifice atop the rise is an ancient troll ruin that fell into decay long before the recent wars. With the collapse of Lordaeron and the devastation wrought across the surrounding mountains, no civilized power maintains the pass, leaving only weathered stonework open to the bitter elements.",al={"why is chillwind point ruined","chillwind point ruins","why is chillwind point abandoned"},it="ruin",add=true},{q="Is Chillwind Point dangerous?",a="The hill itself is relatively calm, home only to the solitary hermit Bath'rah the Windwatcher. However, danger looms directly nearby: the pass funnels bitter drafts down from the plagued horrors of the Western Plaguelands just to the north, and the surrounding wilderness is rife with mountain predators and bandits.",al={"is chillwind point safe","chillwind point danger","threats chillwind point"},it="danger",add=true}},ang={["class:Shaman"]="The wild, funneling gusts of the pass make Chillwind Point a place of elemental focus, drawing practitioners to study with the hermit Bath'rah the Windwatcher.",["faction:Alliance"]="Lying just south of the border post at Chillwind Camp, these ancient ruins mark the transition between the contested foothills and the terrifying territory of the Plaguelands."},kw={"alterac","bath'rah","chillwind","chillwind point","hillsbrad","plaguelands","troll ruins","windwatcher"},rel={"npc:bath-rah-the-windwatcher","subzone:chillwind-camp","zone:westernplaguelands","zone:alterac","zone:hillsbrad","quest:1791","topic:troll","topic:lordaeron"},src={"Chillwind Point"}}
E["subzone:corrahn-s-dagger"] = {t="subzone",n="Corrahn's Dagger",z="hillsbrad",s="Corrahn's Dagger is the second ridge among the four mountainous fingers towering over northern Hillsbrad Foothills. This high ground serves as a hideout for rogue Syndicate operatives.",h="Corrahn's Dagger is the second ridge among the four mountainous fingers towering over northern Hillsbrad...",sec={{t="A Northern Strongpoint",b="Rising steeply in northern Hillsbrad Foothills, Corrahn's Dagger is the second of the four rocky projections known locally as the fingers of Hillsbrad. The ridge is overrun by cutthroats belonging to the Syndicate, who use the elevated perch to overlook the valley below.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who controls Corrahn's Dagger?",a="The ridge is held by rogue humans of the Syndicate, who keep the heights as a hideout.",al={"who is at corrahn's dagger","corrahns dagger faction","who lives here"},it="in_charge"},{q="What are the fingers of Hillsbrad?",a="The fingers of Hillsbrad are four prominent, finger-like mountain ridges projecting southward from the northern mountain range into the Hillsbrad valley. Corrahn's Dagger is the second of these formations.",al={"four fingers hillsbrad","four ridges hillsbrad","hillsbrad fingers"}},{q="What is Corrahn's Dagger?",a="Corrahn's Dagger is the second of the four prominent mountain ridges known as the fingers of Hillsbrad, rising along the northern edge of the foothills. Rogue humans of the Syndicate hold the high ground as a hideout overlooking the valley below.",al={"what is corrahns dagger","corrahns dagger lore","corrahn dagger hill"},it="place",add=true},{q="Is Corrahn's Dagger dangerous?",a="Yes. The ridge is held by Syndicate cutthroats who use the heights as a hideout, and they attack travelers of both the Alliance and the Horde who wander too close.",al={"is corrahns dagger safe","danger corrahns dagger","corrahns dagger enemies"},it="danger",add=true}},ang={["race:Dwarf"]="The ridge is a Syndicate hideout, so dwarven travelers crossing the northern foothills should expect bandits rather than allies.",["race:Undead"]="The Syndicate cutthroats on the ridge are hostile to the Forsaken working in Hillsbrad."},kw={"corrahn","corrahn's dagger","dagger","four fingers","hillsbrad","syndicate"},rel={"zone:hillsbrad","topic:forsaken","topic:syndicate"},src={"Corrahn's Dagger"}}
E["subzone:darrow-hill"] = {t="subzone",n="Darrow Hill",z="hillsbrad",s="Darrow Hill is an elevated expanse of rugged grassland nestled in northern Hillsbrad Foothills directly beneath the Headland. While mountain lions and stags graze across its open slopes, feral yetis lurk inside the Foothill Caverns that pit the hillside. Rich with veins of Alterac Granite, it serves as a treacherous frontier where natural beasts and rival travelers constantly clash.",h="Darrow Hill is an elevated expanse of rugged grassland nestled in northern Hillsbrad Foothills directly...",sec={{t="A Treacherous Frontier",b="Rising along the base of the northern mountains below the Headland, Darrow Hill bridges the rolling pasture of southern Hillsbrad with the jagged, colder heights of Alterac. Mountain lions and stags stalk through the tall grasses, sharing the rocky slopes with towering yetis that spill out from the Foothill Caverns. Beyond its feral wildlife, the cavern walls hide deposits of dense Alterac Granite, drawing quarry workers, miners, and adventurers straight into harm's way. Caught between contentious regional claims, its trails remain notoriously dangerous for travelers of either faction caught unawares.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Where is Darrow Hill located?",a="Darrow Hill lies in the northern reaches of Hillsbrad Foothills, sitting immediately south of the rocky bluffs known as the Headland and east of the main mountain road into Alterac.",al={"darrow hill location","where is darrow hill","darrow hill map"},it="place",gp=true},{q="What creatures threaten travelers around Darrow Hill?",a="The open slopes are prowled by stags and mountain lions, while savage yetis roam the area surrounding and inside the Foothill Caverns.",al={"darrow hill mobs","what lives on darrow hill","monsters darrow hill"},it="threat"},{q="What can be found inside the Foothill Caverns?",a="The Foothill Caverns are infested by feral yetis and contain veins of prized Alterac Granite embedded in their rocky stone walls.",al={"foothill caverns","darrow hill cave","what is in the cave"},it="place"},{q="Why is this area considered so dangerous for travelers?",a="Aside from fierce wildlife and yeti dens, the open geography directly adjacent to contested roadways makes Darrow Hill a notorious skirmish point where Alliance and Horde wanderers frequently ambushed one another.",al={"why is darrow hill dangerous","darrow hill pvp","danger at darrow hill"},it="danger"},{q="What is Darrow Hill?",a="Darrow Hill is an elevated, rugged expanse nestled in the northern reaches of the Hillsbrad Foothills, resting directly beneath the towering heights of the Headland. Its open slopes are home to roaming wildlife, while the nearby Foothill Caverns cut into the stone, harboring subterranean dangers beneath the tranquil surface.",al={"what is darrow hill","darrow hill hillsbrad","darrow hill info"},it="place",add=true}},ang={["profession:Mining"]="The cave networks puncturing Darrow Hill, particularly the Foothill Caverns, are rich with Alterac Granite and regional mineral veins, provided you can handle the yetis nesting nearby.",["class:Hunter"]="The hills provide prime hunting grounds for mountain lions and stags moving between the Alterac tree line and the lower grasslands."},kw={"alterac granite","darrow hill","foothill caverns","headland","hillsbrad foothills","yetis"},rel={"zone:hillsbrad","topic:alterac-kingdom"},src={"Darrow Hill"}}
E["subzone:dun-garok"] = {t="subzone",n="Dun Garok",z="hillsbrad",s="Dun Garok is a fortified dwarven mountain bastion situated in the southeastern heights of the Hillsbrad Foothills. Commanded by Captain Ironhill, the outpost's stalwart garrison defends regional Alliance interests and nearby operations like the Azurelode Mine against hostile encroachment. To the Forsaken of Tarren Mill, this entrenched dwarven stronghold stands as a constant military threat bordering their domain.",h="Dun Garok is a fortified dwarven mountain bastion situated in the southeastern heights of the Hillsbrad...",sec={{t="A Bastion in the Foothills",b="Carved into the craggy southeastern hills of Hillsbrad Foothills, Dun Garok stands as a heavily defended redoubt of Ironforge mountaineers and riflemen. Commanded by Captain Ironhill, the dwarves here maintain a critical defensive perimeter, shielding human settlements in Hillsbrad and securing vital operations at the Azurelode Mine. Their sturdy stone architecture and deep entrenchments provide the Alliance with an anchor against nearby threats.",sp=0},{t="Target of Tarren Mill",b="Because of its close proximity to Tarren Mill, Dun Garok is viewed by the Forsaken as an intolerable intrusion on their southern border. Sylvanas Windrunner's forces loathe the presence of heavily armed dwarven troops so close to their stronghold, routinely plotting to infiltrate the fortress, break its defenses, and eliminate Captain Ironhill's garrison to secure Forsaken dominion over Hillsbrad.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is Dun Garok?",a="Dun Garok is a fortified dwarven outpost located in the southeastern mountains of the Hillsbrad Foothills. It is manned by troops from Ironforge dedicated to defending regional Alliance holdings.",al={"dun garok location","what is this dwarven keep","hillsbrad dwarf fort"},it="place"},{q="Who commands Dun Garok?",a="The stronghold is commanded by Captain Ironhill, who leads the local mountaineers and riflemen in safeguarding Hillsbrad and the nearby Azurelode Mine.",al={"dun garok leader","who leads dun garok","captain ironhill"},it="residents"},{q="Why do the Forsaken want to destroy Dun Garok?",a="The Forsaken view an active, fortified dwarven stronghold right on their southern border as a major security threat to Tarren Mill and actively dispatch agents to eradicate the garrison.",al={"why horde attack dun garok","forsaken dun garok","tarren mill dun garok conflict"},it="conflict"},{q="What is Dun Garok's strategic value to the Alliance?",a="Dun Garok serves as a key military anchor in Hillsbrad, helping maintain Alliance security in the region and protecting the nearby Azurelode Mine from hostile takeovers.",al={"why is dun garok important","alliance purpose dun garok"},it="purpose"},{q="What happened at Dun Garok?",a="Dun Garok was built as a dwarven stronghold nestled in the southeastern hills to defend nearby human settlements and the Azurelode Mine. Ever since the Forsaken established their dominion in Lordaeron, they have viewed the dwarven fortress as a severe military threat, regularly sending soldiers and mercenaries to harass and attempt to purge its defenders.",al={"dun garok history","what happened here","dun garok lore"},it="history",add=true},{q="Is Dun Garok dangerous?",a="Yes. The stronghold is heavily fortified and garrisoned by disciplined dwarven soldiers under Captain Ironhill. For members of the Horde and the Forsaken, entering Dun Garok invites immediate hostility from elite riflemen and mountain guards who defend their ramparts with stubborn tenacity.",al={"is dun garok safe","dun garok danger","threats in dun garok"},it="danger",add=true}},ang={["race:Dwarf"]="Dun Garok is a proud symbol of Ironforge's reach into Lordaeron, where Captain Ironhill and his mountaineers stand resolute in defense of their human allies.",["faction:Horde"]="This well-defended dwarven enclave poses an ongoing danger to Forsaken expansion and border security around Tarren Mill, making its garrison a priority target."},kw={"azurelode mine","dun garok","dwarf","hillsbrad","ironforge","ironhill","keep","mountaineer"},rel={"zone:hillsbrad","subzone:azurelode-mine","topic:dwarf","zone:ironforge","topic:alliance","topic:forsaken","topic:horde"},src={"Dun Garok"}}
E["subzone:durnholde-keep"] = {t="subzone",n="Durnholde Keep",z="hillsbrad",s="Durnholde Keep is a shattered fortress situated east of Tarren Mill in the Hillsbrad Foothills. Once the nerve center of the Alliance's orc internment camps and the place where Warchief Thrall was raised as a captive gladiator, it now lies in ruin, occupied by outlaws of the Syndicate.",h="Durnholde Keep is a shattered fortress situated east of Tarren Mill in the Hillsbrad Foothills.",sec={{t="A Crucible of Captivity",b="Built by the Alliance, Durnholde served as the headquarters overseeing the southern internment camps following the Second War. Commanded by the ambitious and corrupt Lieutenant General Aedelas Blackmoore, it functioned as both an administrative fortress and a gladiatorial arena. It was here that Blackmoore raised the orphaned infant Go'el, naming him Thrall and training him to fight for sport and profit. Aided by Taretha Foxton, Thrall escaped captivity and later united the dispersed orc clans under the banner of the new Horde. Returning to Durnholde, Thrall laid siege to the fortress, slew Blackmoore, and called upon the earth spirits to shatter its walls.",sp=0},{t="In the Clutches of the Syndicate",b="Since its collapse prior to the Third War, Durnholde Keep has remained a scarred heap of masonry. In the vacuum left by Lordaeron's fall, the aristocratic bandits of the Syndicate took refuge among the ramparts. Operating out of the broken bailey and towers, these dispossessed Alterac nobles and cutthroats prey upon travelers across the Hillsbrad Foothills, turning a former instrument of martial law into a heavily fortified rogue outpost.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Why is Durnholde Keep in ruins?",a="Thrall returned to Durnholde at the head of the liberated Horde to defeat his former master, Lieutenant General Aedelas Blackmoore. After slaying Blackmoore, Thrall communed with the spirits of the earth to demolish the fortress so it could never again cage his people.",al={"who destroyed durnholde","what happened to durnholde keep","why is durnholde destroyed"},it="ruin"},{q="Who currently occupies Durnholde Keep?",a="The stronghold is held by the Syndicate, a faction of exiled Alterac nobles turned outlaws. They use the crumbling ramparts as a fortified redoubt to conduct banditry and launch attacks across Hillsbrad.",al={"who lives in durnholde","durnholde mobs","syndicate at durnholde"},it="residents"},{q="What was Thrall's connection to this place?",a="Aedelas Blackmoore discovered the orphaned orc as a child and raised him at Durnholde as a slave. Thrall was educated in tactics and forced to fight as a gladiator in the arena before he managed to break out with help from a human woman named Taretha Foxton.",al={"did thrall live here","thrall durnholde history","was thrall a prisoner here"},it="people"},{q="What purpose did the keep serve during the Second War?",a="Beyond serving as an Alliance stronghold, it was used as a prison facility. During the conflict, the forest troll warlord Zul'jin was held captive here until Orgrim Doomhammer breached the fortress to liberate him.",al={"durnholde second war","what was durnholde used for"},it="purpose"},{q="What is Durnholde Keep?",a="Durnholde Keep is a shattered fortress situated east of Tarren Mill in the Hillsbrad Foothills. Once a bustling military stronghold featuring barracks, an arena, and a mage tower, it served as the administrative command center for the Alliance's orc internment camps following the Second War. Today, it stands as a sprawling ruin, occupied by outlaws and scavengers.",al={"what is durnholde","durnholde keep overview","where is durnholde"},it="place",add=true},{q="What happened at Durnholde Keep?",a="Originally an Alliance prison where Zul'jin was once rescued during the Second War, Durnholde became infamous under Lieutenant General Aedelas Blackmoore, who raised the captive orc Thrall here as a gladiator. After escaping, Thrall returned at the head of a reformed Horde to liberate his people. He defeated Blackmoore in combat and invoked the earth spirits to shatter the fortress to the ground.",al={"history of durnholde","durnholde lore","siege of durnholde"},it="history",add=true},{q="Is Durnholde Keep dangerous?",a="Yes. The crumbled walls and surrounding grounds are heavily infested with operatives of the Syndicate, an aggressive criminal organization composed of former Alterac nobility and brigands. They guard the wreckage fiercely and attack any travelers or adventurers who wander too close to their encampments.",al={"is durnholde dangerous","threats in durnholde keep","what dangers are at durnholde"},it="danger",add=true}},ang={["race:Orc"]="The ruined stones of Durnholde mark the forge where Warchief Thrall threw off his chains, ending decades of orcish captivity and kindling the rebirth of the Horde.",["faction:Alliance"]="Once a linchpin of Lordaeron's defense and justice, Durnholde's shattered ramparts now serve only as a wretched lair for Syndicate outlaws and cutthroats."},kw={"blackmoore","durnholde keep","hillsbrad","internment","syndicate","taretha foxton","tarren mill","thrall"},rel={"npc:thrall","zone:hillsbrad","topic:syndicate","npc:orgrim-doomhammer","subzone:tarren-mill","topic:alterac-kingdom","topic:second-war","topic:horde"},src={"Durnholde Keep"}}
E["subzone:eastern-strand"] = {t="subzone",n="Eastern Strand",z="hillsbrad",s="The Eastern Strand is a stretch of southern coastline in Hillsbrad Foothills, lying to the southeast toward the border of the Arathi Highlands. Once peaceful shores, the beaches and shallows have been overrun by hostile Daggerspine naga establishing a coastal beachhead.",h="The Eastern Strand is a stretch of southern coastline in Hillsbrad Foothills, lying to the southeast toward...",sec={{t="A Hostile Shoreline",b="Running along the southeastern edge of Hillsbrad Foothills, the Eastern Strand complements the Western Strand across the bay. While the region is primarily known for human farming settlements and territorial clashes between Southshore and Tarren Mill, these sandy flats and tidelines are dominated entirely by the Daggerspine naga. Creeping out of the Great Sea, the serpent folk slither across the sandbars and dwell among the rocky outcrops, watching the mainland closely.",sp=0},{t="Signs of an Invasion",b="The presence of the Daggerspine on the Eastern Strand is more than simple scavengers seeking land. Scouting patrols carry written battle orders and attack plans, signaling an organized campaign to push further inland. The threat forces both local human defenders and Horde forces inland to cast a wary eye toward the coast, lest the serpentine tide wash over the foothill settlements.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Where is the Eastern Strand located?",a="The Eastern Strand encompasses the coastal sands and shallows in the southeastern corner of Hillsbrad Foothills, sitting eastward along the water toward the borders of the Arathi Highlands.",al={"eastern strand location","where is eastern strand","eastern strand map"},it="place",gp=true},{q="What creatures inhabit the Eastern Strand?",a="The beach and nearby waters are overrun by the Daggerspine tribe of naga, including foot soldiers, raiders, and spellcasters prowling the tideline.",al={"eastern strand mobs","who lives on eastern strand","eastern strand enemies"},it="threat"},{q="Why are the naga gathering on this beach?",a="The Daggerspine naga are preparing an offensive against the mainland. Orders and attack plans discovered among their coastal forces reveal they are coordinating incursions into the surrounding foothills.",al={"why are naga in hillsbrad","daggerspine attack plans","what are the naga doing here"},it="purpose"},{q="How does the Eastern Strand differ from the Western Strand?",a="Both strands are occupied by Daggerspine naga, but they bracket the southern coast of Hillsbrad on opposite sides, with the Western Strand sitting southwest toward Silverpine and the Eastern Strand lying southeast toward Arathi.",al={"western strand vs eastern strand","two beaches in hillsbrad"}},{q="What is the Eastern Strand?",a="The Eastern Strand is the windswept southeastern coastline of Hillsbrad Foothills, facing the cold waters of the Great Sea. While it mirrors the Western Strand across the region's coast, this beach is distinguished by a heavy infestation of Daggerspine naga who prowl the shallows and gather along the surf.",al={"what is eastern strand","eastern strand lore","tell me about eastern strand"},it="place",add=true},{q="Is the Eastern Strand dangerous?",a="Yes, it is very hazardous for lone travelers. The shoreline crawls with aggressive Daggerspine naga, including shoreline hunters and sorceresses who fiercely protect their foothold on the coast. Furthermore, recovered orders among their ranks reveal they are preparing organized assault plans against nearby inland settlements.",al={"eastern strand danger","is eastern strand safe","how dangerous is eastern strand"},it="danger",add=true},{q="Why is it called the Eastern Strand?",a="It is named simply for its geography. 'Strand' is an old term for a shore or beach, and this stretch forms the eastern half of the coast bordering Hillsbrad Foothills, sitting in natural contrast to the Western Strand situated past Southshore.",al={"why called eastern strand","eastern strand name origin","where does eastern strand get its name"},it="name",add=true}},ang={["faction:Alliance"]="The naga encamped on the Eastern Strand pose a direct, creeping flank threat to Southshore's maritime security and nearby patrols.",["faction:Horde"]="Any organized naga expansion moving inland from the coast threatens to destabilize Horde movements and supply lines crossing lower Hillsbrad."},kw={"beach","coast","daggerspine","eastern strand","hillsbrad foothills","naga","preemptive strike"},rel={"zone:hillsbrad","topic:naga"},src={"Eastern Strand"}}
E["subzone:growless-cave"] = {t="subzone",n="Growless Cave",z="hillsbrad",s="Growless Cave is a frigid cavern carved into the crags of the Alterac Mountains, overrun by ferocious mountain yetis. It is best known as the resting place of the Flame of Uzel, an unholy ceremonial pyre tied to the dark necromancy of Helcular.",h="Growless Cave is a frigid cavern carved into the crags of the Alterac Mountains, overrun by ferocious...",sec={{t="A Den of Beasts and Dark Magic",b="Tucked away in the snow-dusted heights overlooking the foothills, Growless Cave serves primarily as a den for the territorial mountain yetis that roam Alterac. Travelers navigating the treacherous slopes often steer clear of its mouth, especially when the notorious yeti Skhowl is sighted prowling outside. Beyond the primal danger of the beasts, the cave harbors a sinister past: inside lies the Flame of Uzel, an arcane brazier left behind by the ambitious human mage Helcular. Before his demise, Helcular intended to use the pyre in a dark ritual to achieve lichdom, and its foul warmth once drew the massive predator Frostmaw out from the frozen wastes.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What creatures live in Growless Cave?",a="The cave is occupied by wild mountain yetis native to Alterac. Occasionally, a dangerous rare yeti named Skhowl wanders just outside the entrance.",al={"who lives here","growless cave mobs","what is inside growless cave"},it="residents"},{q="What is the Flame of Uzel?",a="The Flame of Uzel is a ceremonial pyre established by Helcular, a former mage of Dalaran turned necromancer. He created the pyre as part of a forbidden ritual meant to transform himself into an undying lich.",al={"flame of uzel","pyre in growless cave","helcular flame"}},{q="Who is Frostmaw?",a="Frostmaw is a massive, exceptionally fierce yeti that roams the Alterac peaks. In the past, burning fresh meat upon the Flame of Uzel would lure the ravenous beast directly to the cavern.",al={"frostmaw yeti","frostmaw"}},{q="Why would travelers venture here?",a="Adventurers braving the cave typically seek to hunt the dangerous yetis for their pelts or pursue the lingering necromantic artifacts tied to Helcular's legacy in Alterac.",al={"why go to growless cave","growless cave quests"},it="purpose"},{q="What is Growless Cave?",a="Growless Cave is a cavern hollowed into the frigid slopes of the Alterac Mountains. Far from civilized settlements, it serves primarily as a den for savage mountain yetis, shielded from the brutal highland winds.",al={"what is growless cave","growless cave info","about growless cave"},it="place",add=true},{q="What happened at Growless Cave?",a="In the past, the ambitious human mage Helcular chose this remote den to establish the Flame of Uzel. He intended this dark ceremonial pyre to serve as an instrument in his necromantic rituals to ascend into lichdom.",al={"growless cave history","what happened here","helcular growless cave"},it="history",add=true},{q="Is Growless Cave dangerous?",a="Yes. The cave is crawling with ferocious mountain yetis that aggressively defend their lair. On occasion, the wandering beast Skhowl prowls just outside its threshold, and the formidable yeti Frostmaw has been known to frequent the cavern.",al={"how dangerous is growless cave","growless cave danger","is growless cave safe"},it="danger",add=true}},ang={["race:Undead"]="The cave holds grim significance for the Forsaken assisting in the vengeance of Helcular, whose dark rites and relics remain scattered across the fallen realm of Alterac.",["class:Mage"]="The remnants of the Flame of Uzel stand as a stark warning of what happens when Kirin Tor wizardry is perverted into necromantic pursuits."},kw={"alterac","flame of uzel","frostmaw","growless cave","helcular","skhowl","yeti"},rel={"zone:alterac","zone:hillsbrad","topic:alterac-kingdom"},src={"Growless Cave"}}
E["subzone:hillsbrad-fields"] = {t="subzone",n="Hillsbrad Fields",z="hillsbrad",s="The Hillsbrad Fields encompass the cultivated farmlands and rustic settlement of Hillsbrad in western Hillsbrad Foothills. As one of the few surviving human communities in former Lordaeron that refused to succumb to the Scourge or join the fanatical Scarlet Crusade, its farmers and militia now face constant assaults from the nearby Forsaken at Tarren Mill.",h="The Hillsbrad Fields encompass the cultivated farmlands and rustic settlement of Hillsbrad in western...",sec={{t="A Defiant Bastion of Lordaeron",b="Spanning orchards, pumpkin patches, and pastures between Darrow Hill and the Azurelode Mine, the Hillsbrad Fields supply essential provisions to Southshore and the surviving Alliance resistance. While much of Lordaeron fell to the plague of undeath, the people of Hillsbrad endured, proudly retaining the royal tabard and heraldry of their fallen kingdom. Led by Magistrate Burnside and the Council of Hillsbrad, the township operates as an independent civic body under constant siege. The local blacksmith Verringtan and his apprentices keep the populace armed, ensuring every farmer and laborer is prepared to defend their land.",sp=0},{t="Front Line of the Undead Advance",b="The fertile fields are a prime target for High Executor Darthalia and the Forsaken forces entrenched at Tarren Mill. Viewing the thriving human settlement as an existential threat on their southern flank, the Undercity has orchestrated continuous raids against the community's infrastructure, targeting crops, livestock, councilors, and civilian farmers alike. In response, Hillsbrad's defenders have formed a hardened militia. Far from helpless peasants, local landowners like Farmer Ray and Farmer Getz organize ambushes and fight fiercely against undead incursions to preserve their homes.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Why are there still living humans farming here?",a="Hillsbrad and neighbouring Southshore are among the very few settlements in Lordaeron that avoided complete destruction by the Scourge during the Third War. Unlike other survivors who fled south or joined the fanatical Scarlet Crusade, these residents remained to rebuild their lives and maintain their homeland.",al={"why are humans in hillsbrad","who lives in hillsbrad fields","are the farmers alive"},it="people"},{q="Who rules over the town and fields?",a="The town and farmlands are governed by Magistrate Burnside, aided by Clerk Horrace Whitesteed and the Council of Hillsbrad from the local town hall. Landowners such as Farmer Ray and Farmer Getz manage the surrounding estates, while local blacksmith Verringtan equips the town watch.",al={"who leads hillsbrad","hillsbrad leadership","magistrate of hillsbrad"},it="in_charge"},{q="Why are the Forsaken attacking the farms?",a="High Executor Darthalia at Tarren Mill considers Hillsbrad a dangerous Alliance foothold on the Forsaken border. Undercity orders direct soldiers to break the human supply lines by destroying food stores, slaughtering livestock, and eliminating town leaders to clear the way for Forsaken dominance in the foothills.",al={"why forsaken attack hillsbrad","battle of hillsbrad reason","tarren mill attacks"},it="threat"},{q="What happened to Hillsbrad during the Second War?",a="During the Second War, Warchief Orgrim Doomhammer ordered a devastating assault on Hillsbrad to break human morale while building up Horde forces in the Southshore region. Hillsbrad was destroyed in a gruesome show of force, but the Alliance drove the orcs out and the town was subsequently rebuilt.",al={"hillsbrad second war","orcs destroyed hillsbrad","history of hillsbrad fields"},it="history"},{q="What is Hillsbrad Fields?",a="Hillsbrad Fields is the fertile agricultural heartland surrounding the township of Hillsbrad in the western foothills. Its sprawling orchards, pumpkin patches, and pastures provide food not only for the local populace, but for the nearby port of Southshore and Alliance outposts across the region. Unlike much of northern Lordaeron, its farmlands survived the Scourge largely intact, remaining one of the few places where living human farmers still cultivate crops under the banner of the fallen kingdom.",al={"what is hillsbrad fields","hillsbrad fields overview","about hillsbrad fields"},it="place",add=true},{q="Is Hillsbrad Fields dangerous?",a="Extremely so, depending on who you are. The fields are currently a primary battleground in the war between the living humans of Hillsbrad and the Forsaken garrison at Tarren Mill. The farmers, peasants, and town guards are heavily armed, organized, and vigilant against undead incursions, staging vicious ambushes against trespassers. For Forsaken champions sent by High Executor Darthalia, clearing these fortified farmsteads is a bloody and hotly contested campaign.",al={"is hillsbrad fields safe","hillsbrad fields danger","how dangerous is hillsbrad fields"},it="danger",add=true}},ang={["faction:Alliance"]="The Hillsbrad Fields are a vital breadbasket and a poignant symbol of Lordaeron's enduring spirit, warranting protection against Forsaken extermination.",["faction:Horde"]="High Executor Darthalia demands the systematic dismantling of Hillsbrad's farms and militia to secure the southern frontier for the Forsaken."},kw={"battle of hillsbrad","darthalia","farmer getz","farmer ray","hillsbrad","hillsbrad fields","magistrate burnside","southshore","tarren mill","verringtan"},rel={"quest:527","quest:567","zone:hillsbrad","subzone:southshore","subzone:tarren-mill","subzone:azurelode-mine","npc:high-executor-darthalia","topic:lordaeron"},src={"Hillsbrad Fields"}}
E["subzone:lordamere-lake"] = {t="subzone",n="Lordamere Lake",z="hillsbrad",s="Lordamere Lake is one of the largest bodies of freshwater in the Eastern Kingdoms, bordered by Tirisfal Glades, Silverpine Forest, and the Alterac Mountains. Once the bustling aquatic heart of human civilization in the north, its cold waters and islands are now haunted by Scourge necromancers, feral murlocs, and the spreading shadow of the undead.",h="Lordamere Lake is one of the largest bodies of freshwater in the Eastern Kingdoms, bordered by Tirisfal...",sec={{t="Heart of the Fallen Kingdoms",b="In the golden age of the Alliance of Lordaeron, Lordamere Lake sat at the crossroads of human power. The Capital City of Lordaeron guarded its northern shores, the sorcerous city-state of Dalaran rose near its southern reach, and the kingdom of Alterac lined its mountainous eastern edge. Merchant vessels and fishing boats once crossed its broad, mist-covered expanse without fear. Following the devastation of the Third War, the lake was transformed from a hub of commerce into a natural barrier dividing the Forsaken-held lands of Tirisfal and Silverpine from the treacherous heights of Alterac.",sp=0},{t="A Contested Expanse",b="Today, navigating the dark waters of Lordamere is fraught with peril. At the center of the lake sits Fenris Isle, where Scourge necromancer Thule Ravenclaw and his undead thralls hold out against the Forsaken, while vicious worgen prowl the vicinity. Further east lie the Dawning Isles, completely overrun by aggressive Vile Fin murlocs. From the ruins around Dalaran to the shoreline of the Undercity, the lake is no longer a peaceful highway, but a drowned frontier contested by remnant monsters and the armies of the dead.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What kingdoms historically bordered Lordamere Lake?",a="Lordamere Lake was bordered by three major human kingdoms during the height of the Alliance of Lordaeron: the Kingdom of Lordaeron to the north and west, Dalaran to the south, and Alterac along its eastern mountain bluffs.",al={"who lived on lordamere lake","lordamere lake history","kingdoms around lordamere"},it="history"},{q="Who controls Fenris Isle in the middle of the lake?",a="Fenris Isle is currently held by agents of the Scourge under the command of the necromancer Thule Ravenclaw, though they face relentless assaults from the Forsaken and constant pressure from ravenous worgen.",al={"who is on fenris isle","fenris island lordamere","fenris isle ruler"},it="residents"},{q="What are the Dawning Isles?",a="The Dawning Isles are a cluster of small islands situated in the eastern portion of Lordamere Lake, east of Fenris Isle. They have been overrun and claimed by hostile Vile Fin murlocs.",al={"dawning isles location","islands in lordamere lake","dawning isles monsters"},it="place"},{q="How did the lake get its name?",a="The lake was named in conjunction with the nearby Capital City and kingdom of Lordaeron, which took their name from the ancient human general Lordain.",al={"lordamere name origin","why is it called lordamere"},it="name"},{q="What is Lordamere Lake?",a="Lordamere Lake is one of the largest bodies of freshwater in the Eastern Kingdoms, rivaled only by Darrowmere Lake to the east. Spanning the borders between Tirisfal Glades, Silverpine Forest, and the Alterac Mountains, its waters historically connected the great human realms of Lordaeron, Dalaran, and Alterac. Today, it serves as a natural dividing line between Forsaken territory and the contested mountain highlands.",al={"what is lordamere lake","about lordamere lake","lordamere lake overview"},it="place",add=true},{q="Is Lordamere Lake dangerous?",a="Yes, its waters and shores harbor severe dangers. The Vile Fin murlocs have infested the Dawning Isles on the lake's eastern waters, attacking anyone who draws near. Farther out, Fenris Isle has fallen to the Scourge and dark magics, making travel across the water perilous for unwary travelers venturing between Silverpine and the Alterac foothills.",al={"is lordamere lake safe","dangers in lordamere lake","threats lordamere lake"},it="danger",add=true}},ang={["race:Undead"]="For the Forsaken, Lordamere Lake serves as both a defensive moat protecting Tirisfal and an active frontline where Scourge remnants on Fenris Isle must be purged.",["race:Human"]="The quiet, foggy waters of Lordamere are a somber reminder of the ruined glory of the northern human kingdoms, which once traded freely across its shores."},kw={"alterac mountains","dawning isles","fenris isle","lake lordamere","lordamere lake","silverpine forest","thule ravenclaw","tirisfal glades","vile fin"},rel={"subzone:fenris-isle","subzone:dawning-isles","zone:silverpine","zone:tirisfal","zone:alterac","subzone:dalaran","topic:lordaeron","quest:446"},src={"Lordamere Lake"}}
E["subzone:misty-shore"] = {t="subzone",n="Misty Shore",z="hillsbrad",s="Misty Shore is the quiet northern shoreline of Hillsbrad Foothills, skirting the southern edge of Lordamere Lake. Stretching between Dandred's Fold and the perimeter of Dalaran Crater, it offers wide, foggy views of the Dawning Isles and the sinister silhouette of Fenris Keep.",h="Misty Shore is the quiet northern shoreline of Hillsbrad Foothills, skirting the southern edge of Lordamere...",sec={{t="A Fog-Shrouded Waterline",b="Running along the southern margin of Lordamere Lake, the Misty Shore sits caught between ancient ruins and active warzones. To the east lie the perimeter domes and remains of Dalaran, while to the west rises Dandred's Fold. Thick, damp air regularly drifts off the lake, obscuring the local wildlife of snapping turtles and the occasional zealous fanatic who wanders down from regional strongholds.",sp=0},{t="Watching the Lake",b="From the banks of the Misty Shore, travelers look out across the waters toward the Dawning Isles and the imposing shadow of Fenris Keep. Because of its vantage point across Lordamere Lake and its proximity to both Dalaran's magical warding and Scarlet-controlled pockets, travelers along the bank often keep a low profile to avoid unwanted attention.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Where is the Misty Shore located?",a="Misty Shore forms the northern waterline of Hillsbrad Foothills, running along the southern bank of Lordamere Lake between Dandred's Fold and the Dalaran Crater perimeter.",al={"misty shore location","where is misty shore","misty shore map"},it="place"},{q="What can be seen across the water from here?",a="Looking north across the waters of Lordamere Lake, you can see the Dawning Isles and the looming structure of Fenris Keep out in the fog.",al={"what is across the water","misty shore view","lake view"}},{q="What threats are typically found along the shore?",a="The shoreline is inhabited by lake beasts like snapjaw turtles, but travelers also risk encountering zealots aligned with the Scarlet Crusade or scouts roaming from neighboring farmsteads and ruins.",al={"misty shore danger","enemies at misty shore","creatures on misty shore"},it="threat"},{q="What is Misty Shore?",a="Misty Shore is a quiet, fog-shrouded stretch of shoreline bordering the southern waters of Lordamere Lake in the Hillsbrad Foothills. It extends roughly between Dandred's Fold and the perimeter of Dalaran, offering a clear view across the lake toward the Dawning Isles and the distant towers of Fenris Keep.",al={"what is misty shore","about misty shore","misty shore overview"},it="place",add=true},{q="Is Misty Shore dangerous?",a="While it appears placid at first glance, the shore is far from safe. The waters and banks teem with aggressive snapjaw turtles, and travelers must watch for hostile humans aligned with the Scarlet Crusade who patrol nearby, attacking anyone they perceive as tainted or trespassers.",al={"how dangerous is misty shore","misty shore dangers","is misty shore safe"},it="danger",add=true}},ang={["profession:Cooking"]="The shores of Lordamere Lake provide an abundant hunting ground for snapping turtles, yielding tender meat valuable to cooks traveling through Hillsbrad.",["faction:Horde"]="The misty bank provides a natural approach between the Forsaken-held lands near Tarren Mill and the northern lakeshore, keeping travelers sheltered from open patrols."},kw={"dandred's fold","dawning isles","fenris keep","hillsbrad foothills","lordamere lake","misty shore","turtles"},rel={"subzone:lordamere-lake","zone:hillsbrad","subzone:dandred-s-fold","subzone:fenris-isle","subzone:fenris-keep","subzone:dawning-isles","topic:scarlet-crusade"},src={"Misty Shore"}}
E["subzone:nethander-stead"] = {t="subzone",n="Nethander Stead",z="hillsbrad",s="Nethander Stead is an abandoned farmstead lying along the road just east of Southshore in the Hillsbrad Foothills. Once a working human farm, it has fallen into ruin and is completely overrun by the Mudsnout gnoll pack. The fields are overgrown with giant white mushrooms known as Mudsnout Blossoms, attracting the interest of Forsaken alchemists.",h="Nethander Stead is an abandoned farmstead lying along the road just east of Southshore in the Hillsbrad...",sec={{t="A Ruined Homestead",b="Situated within sight of Southshore's eastern borders, Nethander Stead was once an active piece of the region's agricultural belt. Like much of the eastern foothills, the farm was abandoned as regional security eroded and wild packs moved in. Today, it serves as the sole enclave of the Mudsnout gnolls in the foothills. The brutes dwell among the ruined fences and outbuildings, aggressively driving off any travelers who wander too close to their claimed territory.",sp=0},{t="The Mudsnout Blossoms",b="The untended soil of the stead provides fertile ground for unusual fungal growth. Giant, pale mushrooms known as Mudsnout Blossoms carpet the abandoned plots. These fungi harbor potent natural toxins, drawing the attention of the Royal Apothecary Society in Tarren Mill. Apothecaries seek samples harvested directly from the gnolls' grounds to distill caustic concoctions, making this otherwise petty farmstead a target of covert Horde expeditions into Alliance territory.",sp=1}},faq={{q="What is Nethander Stead?",a="Nethander Stead is an abandoned human farm located just east of Southshore in the Hillsbrad Foothills. It has been entirely overrun by a hostile pack of Mudsnout gnolls.",al={"what is this farm","nethander stead info","where is nethander stead"},it="place"},{q="Who controls Nethander Stead right now?",a="The farmstead is occupied by the Mudsnout gnoll tribe. It is the only place in the Hillsbrad Foothills where this particular pack makes its camp.",al={"who lives here","who is at nethander stead","what mobs are here"},it="residents"},{q="What are the giant white mushrooms growing in the fields?",a="They are Mudsnout Blossoms, large white fungi that thrive in the unworked soil of the stead. They contain toxic properties that make them valuable to Forsaken alchemists researching poisons.",al={"white mushrooms","mudsnout mushrooms","mudsnout blossoms"},it="item"},{q="Why does the Horde care about this ruined farm?",a="Apothecary Lydon in Tarren Mill seeks the Mudsnout Blossoms that grow in the stead's fields. Their potent juices are an essential reagent in brewing the Elixir of Agony.",al={"why go here horde","forsaken interest","horde quest nethander"},it="motive"},{q="What happened to Nethander Stead?",a="Once a peaceful human farmstead supporting Hillsbrad and Southshore, Nethander Stead fell to ruin when the Mudsnout gnolls moved in. The original human farmers were displaced or slain, leaving the fields neglected and overgrown with strange fungi while the gnolls claimed the homestead as their own.",al={"nethander stead history","what happened at nethander stead","why is nethander stead abandoned"},it="history",add=true},{q="Why is Nethander Stead abandoned?",a="The farm was overrun by the Mudsnout gnoll tribe. Unable to hold their land against the aggressive scavengers, the peasant caretakers were driven out or slaughtered, leaving the barns and homes to decay under gnoll occupation.",al={"why is nethander stead ruined","why did farmers leave nethander stead","who ruined nethander stead"},it="ruin",add=true},{q="Is Nethander Stead dangerous?",a="Yes. It is occupied by the Mudsnout gnolls, who fiercely defend their territory from outsiders. Anyone wandering off the road east of Southshore into these overgrown fields risks being swarmed by savage gnolls.",al={"is nethander stead safe","nethander stead danger","threats at nethander stead"},it="danger",add=true}},ang={["faction:Alliance"]="The overrun farm is an unsettling reminder of how fragile Southshore's perimeter remains, with feral gnolls entrenched just down the eastern road.",["faction:Horde"]="Infiltrating this farmstead near Southshore is required to gather the Mudsnout Blossoms needed by the Royal Apothecary Society for their lethal research."},kw={"blossoms","gnolls","hillsbrad","mudsnout","mushrooms","nethander","southshore","stead"},rel={"zone:hillsbrad","subzone:southshore","quest:509","topic:gnoll"},src={"Nethander Stead"}}
E["subzone:purgation-isle"] = {t="subzone",n="Purgation Isle",z="hillsbrad",s="Purgation Isle is a spiraling, rocky island lying off the southern coast of the Hillsbrad Foothills. Crowned with a cemetery and a ruined scout tower, the desolate rock is cursed and swarming with the restless, condemned spirits of fallen humans and dwarves.",h="Purgation Isle is a spiraling, rocky island lying off the southern coast of the Hillsbrad Foothills.",sec={{t="A Haunted Sanctuary",b="Rising abruptly from the sea south of Hillsbrad, Purgation Isle is a grim sight marked by winding paths that lead past tombstones to an abandoned watchtower. Long before modern conflicts, the island was associated with the maritime kingdom of Kul Tiras. Today, however, no living nation claims it. Instead, the isle is plagued by condemned souls—former paladins, priests, mages, and judges who wander among the graves, unable to find peace in death.",sp=0},{t="Dark Associations",b="The lingering souls trapped upon the island have made it a site of sinister interest. Dark spellcasters, such as the ogre necromancer Kormok, are said to have delighted in drawing upon the island's anguished dead, summoning forth its spirits to do their bidding.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Where is Purgation Isle located?",a="Purgation Isle is an isolated island off the southern coast of the Hillsbrad Foothills, sitting out in the bay south of the mainland.",al={"purgation isle location","where is purgation isle","how to find purgation isle"},it="place",gp=true},{q="What haunts the island?",a="The island is overrun by powerful condemned spirits, including cursed paladins, justiciars, clerics, acolytes, and writhing mages of human and dwarven descent.",al={"who is on purgation isle","mobs on purgation isle","purgation isle ghosts"},it="residents"},{q="Who originally owned Purgation Isle?",a="Prior to the First War, Purgation Isle was considered an outlying territory belonging to the island kingdom of Kul Tiras before falling into ruin and ghostly neglect.",al={"history of purgation isle","who built purgation isle tower"},it="history"},{q="Who is Kormok and why does he care about this island?",a="Kormok is a notorious ogre necromancer who mastered summoning forth the condemned spirits of Purgation Isle to perform his bidding using specialized dark artifacts.",al={"kormok connection","brazier of invocation ghosts"},it="threat"},{q="What is Purgation Isle?",a="Rising from the waters south of Hillsbrad Foothills, Purgation Isle is a spiraling, ominous crag crowned by an overgrown cemetery and the shattered remnants of an old scout tower. Once an offshore holding of the seafaring kingdom of Kul Tiras, it has long fallen into ruin and desolation, cut off from the mainland and avoided by living sailors.",al={"what is purgation isle","purgation isle","tell me about purgation isle"},it="place",add=true},{q="Is Purgation Isle dangerous?",a="It is exceedingly dangerous. The island swarms with the restless, tormented specters of condemned paladins, clerics, mages, and judges who violently lash out at any living soul who steps ashore. Even darker forces seek to exploit them; the ogre necromancer Kormok is infamous for binding these tortured spirits to his dark will.",al={"how dangerous is purgation isle","is purgation isle safe","dangers of purgation isle"},it="danger",add=true}},ang={["class:Paladin"]="The tragic sight of cursed paladins and justiciars wandering Purgation Isle serves as a somber reminder of what happens when holy defenders fall to dark curses and are denied eternal rest.",["race:Dwarf"]="Among the cursed specters haunting the cemetery are dwarven spirits, binding your kin to this lonely, windswept rock far from the mountains of Khaz Modan."},kw={"arados the damned","hillsbrad","judge thelgram","kormok","kul tiras","purgation isle","spirits"},rel={"zone:hillsbrad","topic:kul-tiras","topic:first-war","topic:dwarf","topic:light"},src={"Purgation Isle"}}
E["subzone:ravenholdt-manor"] = {t="subzone",n="Ravenholdt Manor",z="hillsbrad",s="Tucked away high in the mountains above Hillsbrad Foothills, Ravenholdt Manor serves as the secluded headquarters for the guild of thieves and assassins known as Ravenholdt. Overseen by Lord Jorach Ravenholdt, the estate provides a discreet haven where practitioners of stealth hone their craft far from the eyes of authorities.",h="Tucked away high in the mountains above Hillsbrad Foothills, Ravenholdt Manor serves as the secluded...",sec={{t="A Sanctuary in the Shadows",b="Hidden behind a narrow mountain pass and a winding cave northwest of Durnholde Keep, Ravenholdt Manor sits isolated on the borderlands of the Alterac Mountains. The property belongs to Lord Jorach Ravenholdt, a nobleman who maintains a disciplined enclave of rogues, assassins, and intelligence operatives. The grounds feature a tranquil garden and an outdoor training arena overseen by martial experts like Master Kang, providing a disciplined space to practice lockpicking, poison-crafting, and close-quarters combat. While the manor welcomes those with a talent for skullduggery, clumsy outsiders and unwanted visitors are treated with cold suspicion by the manor's watchful sentries.",sp=0},{t="A Bitter Feud in the Foothills",b="Prior to the First War, the land surrounding the manor was part of the kingdom of Alterac, reflected in the weathered orange tiles of the manor's roof. In the turbulent wake of Alterac's ruin, the fallen nobles of the Syndicate sought to control the region, placing them in direct conflict with Ravenholdt. Ravenholdt maintains an uneasy association with Stormwind's SI:7 intelligence service, cooperating where interests align to purge Syndicate influences from the surrounding highlands. For Jorach's followers, every skirmish fought across Hillsbrad and Alterac is part of a silent war to maintain their sovereign haven.",sp=0}},faq={{q="How do you reach Ravenholdt Manor?",a="To reach the manor, travel to the plateau northwest of Durnholde Keep in Hillsbrad Foothills. Near where the plateau meets the northern mountains, an obscure dirt path twists upward and passes through a hidden cave, emerging directly onto the manor's grounds.",al={"where is ravenholdt manor","how to get to ravenholdt","ravenholdt path"},it="arrival",gp=true},{q="Who owns Ravenholdt Manor?",a="The estate belongs to Lord Jorach Ravenholdt, who leads an elite brotherhood of thieves and assassins known simply as Ravenholdt. He commands deep respect among rogues throughout Azeroth.",al={"who leads ravenholdt","lord ravenholdt","manor owner"},it="residents"},{q="Why does Ravenholdt hate the Syndicate?",a="Both factions claim roots in the shattered lands of Alterac. While the displaced nobles of the Syndicate resort to banditry and lawlessness across the hills, Ravenholdt operates with strict discipline and actively works to thwart the Syndicate's ambitions.",al={"ravenholdt vs syndicate","syndicate feud","why fight syndicate"},it="conflict"},{q="Can anyone visit the manor?",a="Any traveler can physically walk into the grounds, but the guards and assassins stationed there are openly hostile in tone to outsiders. Rogues and trusted operatives find a warm welcome and extensive training, while others receive chilling warnings to leave.",al={"non-rogue in ravenholdt","are outsiders allowed in ravenholdt"}},{q="What is Ravenholdt Manor?",a="Ravenholdt Manor is the secluded mountain headquarters of the Ravenholdt guild, an enigmatic league of thieves and assassins. Tucked away high in the hills above Hillsbrad and the Alterac border, the estate serves as a sanctuary and training ground where rogues hone their arts, craft subtle poisons, and coordinate covert operations far from the prying eyes of the Alliance and Horde.",al={"what is this place","ravenholdt manor lore","what is ravenholdt"},it="place",add=true},{q="What is the history of Ravenholdt Manor?",a="Before the First War, this land was part of the ancient human kingdom of Alterac, reflected in the manor's traditional orange-tiled roof. Following the kingdom's downfall and the rise of criminal factions, Lord Jorach Ravenholdt established the estate as an independent stronghold. Over the years, the manor has stood as a bastion against the lawless Syndicate, quietly housing clandestine figures dedicated to the subtle arts.",al={"ravenholdt history","manor history","who built ravenholdt manor"},it="history",add=true},{q="Is Ravenholdt Manor dangerous?",a="It depends entirely on who you are. The estate is fortified with watchful sentries, seasoned lookouts, and lethal assassins lurking in the shadows. While practitioners of stealth and shadowcraft are tolerated or welcomed to seek instruction, uninvited intruders or careless wanderers who meddle where they do not belong will find the shadows turning deadly very quickly.",al={"is ravenholdt safe","will ravenholdt attack me","is it safe here"},it="danger",add=true},{q="Why is it called Ravenholdt Manor?",a="The estate derives its name directly from its master and ancestral noble family, Lord Jorach Ravenholdt. The manor serves as the personal estate and sovereign seat of Lord Ravenholdt, lending both his noble moniker and crest to the brotherhood of rogues operating within its walls.",al={"ravenholdt manor name","why ravenholdt","where does the name ravenholdt come from"},it="name",add=true}},ang={["class:Rogue"]="Ravenholdt Manor is the premier sanctuary for your profession, offering rigorous trials, specialized training, and a deep network of underground contacts.",["profession:Engineering"]="Discerning engineers venture through the mountain pass specifically to acquire the rare schematic for the Gnomish Cloaking Device from the manor's supply."},kw={"alterac","assassin","hillsbrad","jorach ravenholdt","manor","ravenholdt","rogue guild","syndicate","thief"},rel={"npc:lord-jorach-ravenholdt","topic:ravenholdt","topic:syndicate","zone:hillsbrad","zone:alterac","subzone:durnholde-keep","topic:alterac-kingdom","quest:2300"},src={"Ravenholdt Manor"}}
E["subzone:ruins-of-southshore"] = {t="subzone",n="Ruins of Southshore",z="hillsbrad",s="In the current era of Year 25 ADP, the town of Southshore stands fully intact as the Alliance's primary coastal port and stronghold in the Hillsbrad Foothills. Constant threats from the Forsaken and lurking shoreline monsters keep the settlement under ceaseless siege.",h="In the current era of Year 25 ADP, the town of Southshore stands fully intact as the Alliance's primary...",sec={{t="A Bulwark Still Standing",b="Southshore is far from a ruin in this age. As one of the few remaining bastions of the fallen Kingdom of Lordaeron, it serves as an indispensable port and haven for the Alliance in the northern subcontinent. Positioned directly between the encroaching Forsaken forces from Tarren Mill and the encroaching horrors of the coastline, Southshore's garrisons remain vigilant against any assault seeking to reduce their home to ash.",sp=0},{t="Threats on the Eastern Strand",b="The most immediate peril stems from the sea. Along the Eastern Strand just outside the town, hostile Daggerspine naga have gathered in force. Alliance patrols frequently discover scouting parties and attack orders suggesting these serpent-kin covet Southshore's docks and waterways, hoping to seize the town whenever the defenders falter.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Is Southshore currently in ruins?",a="No. In Year 25 ADP, Southshore is a bustling, fully functional human port town and the Alliance's central outpost in the Hillsbrad Foothills. It has not fallen into ruin, despite relentless conflict with the Forsaken and local threats.",al={"is southshore destroyed","ruins of southshore status","is southshore a ruin"},it="ruin"},{q="What is the danger on the beaches near Southshore?",a="Hostile Daggerspine naga have colonized the Eastern Strand east of the town docks. These naga continually probe Southshore's defenses and plot incursions against the harbor, posing a constant danger to local fishermen and patrols.",al={"eastern strand danger","naga southshore","who is attacking the beach"},it="threat"},{q="Who controls Southshore right now?",a="Southshore is firmly under Alliance control. It remains one of the last major human settlements in Lordaeron, defended by human guards and allied troops acting as a base against the Horde and the Scourge.",al={"who owns southshore","is southshore alliance or horde","southshore faction"},it="in_charge"},{q="Why is Southshore so critical to the Alliance?",a="With Lordaeron shattered by the plague and the Scourge, Southshore provides the Alliance with a vital deep-water harbor and land base in the north, allowing troops and supplies to travel directly into the Hillsbrad Foothills.",al={"why southshore matters","southshore importance","why defend southshore"},it="purpose"},{q="What is the town of Southshore?",a="Southshore is a bustling port town along the southern coast of the Hillsbrad Foothills. It stands as one of the last major human bastions in northern Lordaeron, offering harbor and harbor defense to Alliance ships traveling across the Great Sea.",al={"what is southshore","southshore town","about southshore"},it="place",add=true},{q="What happened to Southshore historically?",a="Historically a tranquil coastal haven, Southshore endured the Second War and later survived the devastation of the Scourge plague that consumed the rest of Lordaeron. Today, it remains a thriving haven and garrison, holding firm against nearby undead and hostile forces.",al={"southshore history","history of southshore","what happened at southshore"},it="history",add=true},{q="Who lives in and runs Southshore?",a="Southshore is populated by human refugees, townspeople, fishermen, and an active detachment of Alliance guards and militia. Local authorities and commanders oversee the port, maintaining vigilance against surrounding threats.",al={"who lives in southshore","southshore inhabitants","who runs southshore"},it="residents",add=true},{q="Is Southshore dangerous to visit?",a="For members of the Alliance, Southshore is a secure refuge offering commerce, shelter, and strong harbor fortifications. For members of the Horde, it is intensely hostile territory heavily guarded by vigilant Alliance sentries who attack trespassers on sight.",al={"is southshore dangerous","southshore safety","danger southshore"},it="danger",add=true}},ang={["faction:Alliance"]="Southshore stands as your vital lifeline in the northern kingdoms; protecting its docks and defending its borders against the Forsaken is crucial to maintaining a foothold in Lordaeron.",["faction:Horde"]="Southshore represents the last major bastion of human power in Hillsbrad, acting as an obstinate barrier to securing total control over the region."},kw={"alliance","daggerspine","eastern strand","hillsbrad","lordaeron","naga","ruins","southshore"},rel={"subzone:southshore","zone:hillsbrad","subzone:eastern-strand","topic:lordaeron","topic:alliance","topic:horde","topic:naga"},src={"Ruins of Southshore"}}
E["subzone:slaughter-hollow"] = {t="subzone",n="Slaughter Hollow",z="hillsbrad",s="Slaughter Hollow is a secluded ogre mound tucked away in the snowy heights of the Alterac Mountains. Controlled by the brutish Crushridge clan, it stands as a rough camp rather than a bustling settlement. Travelers rarely have reason to trespass unless hunting ogres or exploring the frozen mountain passes.",h="Slaughter Hollow is a secluded ogre mound tucked away in the snowy heights of the Alterac Mountains.",sec={{t="A Den of Ogres",b="Hidden high in the peaks bordering Hillsbrad and Alterac, Slaughter Hollow serves as an encampment for the local Crushridge ogres. Like many ogre mounds scattered across the highlands, it is littered with makeshift bonfires, discarded bones, and crude shelters. While other ogre dens in the mountains see frequent conflicts over territory or stolen supplies, Slaughter Hollow remains largely quiet and bypassed by major military campaigns.",sp=0},{t="Captives and Travelers",b="Due to its seclusion, the mound occasionally serves as a holding place for unlucky prisoners taken along the mountain trails. Word among travelers tells of an unfortunate gnome named Rizz Loosebolt who has found himself locked in a crude cage here, attempting to barter with anyone passing by. Such unfortunate captives rarely fare well against the appetite of the Crushridge clan.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is Slaughter Hollow?",a="Slaughter Hollow is an ogre encampment in the Alterac Mountains inhabited by the Crushridge clan. It features primitive mound dwellings and fires typical of highland ogre settlements.",al={"slaughter hollow lore","what is this place","slaughter hollow hillsbrad"},it="place"},{q="Who lives in Slaughter Hollow?",a="The hollow is inhabited entirely by Crushridge ogres, the same clan that holds the nearby ruins of Alterac City and various surrounding outposts.",al={"who is here","slaughter hollow mobs","who controls slaughter hollow"},it="residents"},{q="Are there any quests here?",a="No formal quests send adventurers directly to Slaughter Hollow. It is largely an out-of-the-way den discovered while exploring the mountainous terrain.",al={"slaughter hollow quests","any quests in slaughter hollow","why come here"},gp=true},{q="Who was the gnome caged here?",a="A gnome named Rizz Loosebolt is held captive in a cage inside the hollow, hawking wares to anyone who finds him.",al={"rizz loosebolt","gnome in cage","slaughter hollow vendor"}},{q="Is Slaughter Hollow dangerous?",a="Yes, Slaughter Hollow is exceptionally hazardous. Deep in the snowy passes of the Alterac Mountains, this hollow serves as an ogre mound crawling with hostile Crushridge ogres. Wandering into their camp without preparation will quickly draw the wrath of multiple hulking brutes.",al={"is slaughter hollow safe","slaughter hollow danger","how dangerous is slaughter hollow"},it="danger",add=true}},ang={["race:Gnome"]="The unfortunate capture of Rizz Loosebolt by the Crushridge serves as a stark warning to tinkerers and scouts who wander the Alterac passes unprepared."},kw={"alterac","crushridge","hillsbrad","ogre mound","rizz loosebolt","slaughter hollow"},rel={"zone:alterac","zone:hillsbrad","topic:gnome","topic:alterac-kingdom"},src={"Slaughter Hollow"}}
E["subzone:southpoint-tower"] = {t="subzone",n="Southpoint Tower",z="hillsbrad",s="Southpoint Tower is a ruined Lordaeron scout tower situated at the western border of Hillsbrad Foothills, overlooking the road to Silverpine Forest. Once a human sentry post, the shattered structure is now utilized by Forsaken scouts keeping watch over Alliance movements in the region.",h="Southpoint Tower is a ruined Lordaeron scout tower situated at the western border of Hillsbrad Foothills...",sec={{t="A Ruined Sentinel",b="Standing just south of the highway linking Silverpine Forest and Hillsbrad Foothills, Southpoint Tower was originally built by the Kingdom of Lordaeron to guard traffic moving between the eastern farmlands and the western woods. Following the Third War and the Scourge's destruction of the kingdom, the stonework fell into ruin. Today, it stands roofless and crumbling, an isolated relic of human dominion in a fractured territory.",sp=0},{t="Eyes on the Hills",b="Despite its collapsed state, the vantage point remains tactically valuable. The Forsaken maintain an outpost here, stationing agents such as Deathstalker Lesh to spy on local Alliance patrols, the nearby human settlements of Hillsbrad Fields, and travelers passing along the primary road. Because of its lonely location right near hostile territory, the tower frequently becomes a flashpoint for skirmishes.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Where is Southpoint Tower located?",a="Southpoint Tower sits at the western edge of Hillsbrad Foothills, directly south of the road leading into Silverpine Forest and just west of the Hillsbrad Fields.",al={"southpoint tower location","where is southpoint tower","find southpoint tower"},gp=true},{q="Who controls Southpoint Tower right now?",a="The tower is controlled by the Forsaken. An operative named Deathstalker Lesh is stationed within its ruined walls, observing the road and monitoring nearby Alliance forces.",al={"who is at southpoint tower","who owns southpoint tower","southpoint tower faction"},it="in_charge"},{q="Why is the tower in ruins?",a="The tower was battered and abandoned during the fall of Lordaeron when the Scourge ravaged the region. It has never been repaired, leaving only broken stone walls.",al={"why is southpoint tower broken","who destroyed southpoint tower"},it="ruin"},{q="Why do Alliance players attack this outpost?",a="The post holds a solitary Forsaken scout watching human territory. Its isolated position near the border makes it an easy and tempting target for Alliance travelers passing between Southshore and the western roads.",al={"why kill deathstalker lesh","alliance attacking southpoint tower"},gp=true},{q="What is Southpoint Tower?",a="Southpoint Tower is a crumbling human watchtower situated along the western edge of the Hillsbrad Foothills, overlooking the road leading into Silverpine Forest. Once a standing fortification for human defenders, it now lies largely broken and exposed, serving as a tactical forward surveillance post.",al={"what is southpoint tower","southpoint tower purpose","about southpoint tower"},it="place",add=true},{q="Who lives in or runs Southpoint Tower?",a="The tower is not a permanent settlement, but it currently hosts Deathstalker Lesh, an operative of the Forsaken. Hidden among the shattered stonework, she uses the elevation to spy on Alliance movements between Southshore and the western borders.",al={"who is at southpoint tower","southpoint tower residents","who lives at southpoint tower"},it="residents",add=true},{q="Is Southpoint Tower dangerous?",a="It can be treacherous depending on your allegiance. Deathstalker Lesh will readily strike down Alliance travelers venturing along the road to Silverpine, while Alliance scouts and adventurers frequently target her isolated post to disrupt Forsaken intelligence.",al={"is southpoint tower dangerous","how dangerous is southpoint tower","southpoint tower threats"},it="danger",add=true}},ang={["race:Undead"]="The tower offers the Forsaken an indispensable reconnaissance perch near the Silverpine border to monitor human troop movements out of Hillsbrad.",["faction:Alliance"]="The ruined tower harbors an enemy spy watching the road to Silverpine, making it a natural target for scouts protecting Hillsbrad's human settlements."},kw={"deathstalker lesh","hillsbrad fields","hillsbrad foothills","scout tower","silverpine forest","southpoint tower"},rel={"npc:deathstalker-lesh","zone:hillsbrad","zone:silverpine","subzone:hillsbrad-fields","topic:forsaken","subzone:southshore"},src={"Southpoint Tower"}}
E["subzone:southshore"] = {t="subzone",n="Southshore",z="hillsbrad",s="Southshore is a coastal human port in the Hillsbrad Foothills and one of the Alliance's few surviving strongholds in fallen Lordaeron. Once a sleepy fishing village, it now stands as an embattled bastion facing constant hostility from the Forsaken garrison at Tarren Mill, rogue Syndicate bandits, and shoreline monsters.",h="Southshore is a coastal human port in the Hillsbrad Foothills and one of the Alliance's few surviving...",sec={{t="A Beacon in Lordaeron",b="Southshore first rose to prominence during the First War when refugee boats carrying survivors from the fallen kingdom of Stormwind landed upon its beaches. Though contested and overrun during the Second War, it was rebuilt and later endured the horrors of the Third War. Today, while the rest of Lordaeron lies in ruins or under the rule of the Forsaken, Southshore remains fiercely loyal to the Grand Alliance. It offers shelter to displaced human survivors, veteran paladins of the Silver Hand, and scholars of the Kirin Tor.",sp=0},{t="Besieged on All Fronts",b="Despite its scenic docks and famous turtle bisque, life in Southshore is perilous. Led by Magistrate Henry Maleb and Marshal Redpath, the town struggles against relentless pressure. To the north, the Forsaken of Tarren Mill wage a bitter border conflict for dominance over Hillsbrad. Inland, the aristocratic outlaws of the Syndicate raid supply lines and assassinate local leaders, while ogres, murlocs, and naga constantly harass the town's borders.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Why is Southshore still aligned with the Alliance when Lordaeron fell?",a="Southshore was spared total destruction during the Scourge's invasion. Its surviving human populace reaffirmed their historic oaths to the Grand Alliance, receiving military and logistical backing from Stormwind to maintain a foothold in the north.",al={"why is southshore alliance","who controls southshore","southshore alliance lordaeron"},it="side"},{q="Why is there such intense fighting between Southshore and Tarren Mill?",a="Tarren Mill is held by the Forsaken, while Southshore is the primary Alliance bastion in the region. Both factions claim rightful dominion over the Hillsbrad Foothills, resulting in near-constant border skirmishes, raids, and sabotage.",al={"southshore tarren mill war","why do southshore and tarren mill fight","hillsbrad conflict"},it="conflict"},{q="Who leads the town of Southshore?",a="Civil governance is handled by Magistrate Henry Maleb, who took over after the previous magistrate was assassinated by the Syndicate. Military defense and town security are directed by Marshal Redpath.",al={"southshore leader","who runs southshore","magistrate maleb"},it="in_charge"},{q="What threats does Southshore face other than the Forsaken?",a="Beyond the Forsaken, Southshore must fend off coastal murlocs and naga, Crushridge ogres descending from the Alterac Mountains, and the criminal Syndicate based out of Durnholde Keep.",al={"southshore enemies","threats to southshore"},it="threat"},{q="What is Southshore?",a="Southshore is a bustling port town on the southern coast of the Hillsbrad Foothills. It serves as one of the last remaining bastions of human civilization and Alliance authority in Lordaeron following the Scourge's destruction of Capital City. Despite being surrounded by hostile factions, it maintains a functioning harbor, civic leadership, and a steadfast garrison.",al={"what is southshore","southshore town","about southshore"},it="place",add=true},{q="What happened at Southshore historically?",a="Originally a simple fishing village, Southshore welcomed the refugees fleeing Stormwind during the First War. In the Second War, it became a strategic seaport coveted for offshore oil, falling briefly to the Horde before being retaken and rebuilt. During the Third War, Thrall's fledgling Horde infiltrated the town to seize ships for their voyage to Kalimdor.",al={"southshore history","southshore lore","history of southshore"},it="history",add=true},{q="Is Southshore dangerous?",a="For the Alliance, Southshore offers a well-guarded sanctuary, but the surrounding countryside is fraught with danger. Skirmishes with the Forsaken from Tarren Mill frequently spill across the foothills, while coastal murlocs and naga threaten the harbor. Additionally, Syndicate rogues, Crushridge ogres, and lingering undead lurk just outside the town's perimeter.",al={"how dangerous is southshore","is southshore safe","threats in southshore"},it="danger",add=true}},ang={["faction:Alliance"]="Southshore serves as your primary haven, quest hub, and military redoubt in northern Lordaeron, offering essential support against both the Forsaken and the Syndicate.",["faction:Horde"]="For the Horde—especially the Forsaken at nearby Tarren Mill—Southshore represents an obstinate Alliance enclave trespassing on land reclaimed by the dead."},kw={"hillsbrad","jessen","lordaeron","maleb","redpath","southshore","syndicate","tarren mill"},rel={"zone:hillsbrad","subzone:tarren-mill","npc:magistrate-henry-maleb","npc:chef-jessen","quest:555","subzone:durnholde-keep","topic:syndicate","topic:forsaken"},src={"Southshore"}}
E["subzone:southshore-town-hall"] = {t="subzone",n="Southshore Town Hall",z="hillsbrad",s="Southshore Town Hall serves as the administrative seat of the southern coast of Hillsbrad Foothills, standing as one of the last functioning centers of Lordaeron's civil authority. From inside, Magistrate Henry Maleb coordinates local defenses and governs the town's surviving populace. The hall is a vital hub for the Alliance as they struggle to maintain a foothold in the plagued north.",h="Southshore Town Hall serves as the administrative seat of the southern coast of Hillsbrad Foothills, standing...",sec={{t="A Bastion of Civil Rule",b="While much of Lordaeron lies shattered under Scourge corruption and Forsaken expansion, Southshore's town hall maintains the semblance of an intact human government. Magistrate Henry Maleb oversees daily governance from his office here, working alongside officials like Kundric Zanden to secure resources and preserve civic order. In a region surrounded by aggressive undead, Syndicate rogues, and Hillsbrad's fierce border skirmishes, the hall is the nerve center directing the town's survival against constant threats.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who leads the town from the Southshore Town Hall?",a="Magistrate Henry Maleb serves as the primary civil leader in Southshore and conducts town business from inside the town hall, directing the defense and administration of the surviving human settlement.",al={"who is in charge here","southshore mayor","who runs southshore"},it="in_charge"},{q="What is the strategic importance of Southshore Town Hall?",a="It represents one of the final seats of Lordaeron's rightful civil leadership in the north. Alliance members look to the town hall for direction, bounties, and coordination against the encroaching Forsaken and Syndicate bandits.",al={"why does the town hall matter","southshore importance"},it="purpose"},{q="Who else works inside the town hall?",a="Alongside Magistrate Henry Maleb, civil servants such as Kundric Zanden are stationed within the town hall to assist in managing local affairs and supporting town operations.",al={"who is inside southshore town hall","kundric zanden","town hall npcs"},it="residents"},{q="How does the town hall maintain ties with the wider Alliance?",a="Though historically part of the Kingdom of Lordaeron, Southshore and its leadership now rely heavily on the Alliance, receiving reinforcements and supplies to defend this isolated coastal bastion against surrounding hostile forces.",al={"is southshore alliance","ties to stormwind"},it="ties"},{q="What is Southshore Town Hall?",a="This sturdy stone building stands as the administrative heart of Southshore and a vital center of governance for the surviving remnants of Lordaeron. Within its walls, local civic leaders coordinate the settlement's defense, maintain civil order, and manage the daily needs of a refuge surrounded by hostile forces.",al={"southshore town hall","what is southshore town hall","what building is this southshore"},it="place",add=true},{q="What happened at Southshore Town Hall?",a="Following the fall of Lordaeron to the Scourge during the Third War, Southshore became one of the last major refuges for the kingdom's survivors. The town hall was established as the primary seat of civic authority, where Magistrate Henry Maleb and his councilors took up the monumental task of preserving lawful human society along the southern coast.",al={"history of southshore town hall","what happened here town hall"},it="history",add=true},{q="Is Southshore Town Hall dangerous?",a="For champions of the Alliance, the town hall is a safe and fortified haven guarded by vigilant town guards. For members of the Horde, however, entering the building is perilous; the town officials and nearby sentries will immediately attack any intruders who breach the town's perimeter.",al={"is southshore town hall safe","is it dangerous in southshore town hall"},it="danger",add=true}},ang={["faction:Alliance"]="For Alliance champions arriving in the north, Southshore Town Hall is the primary civic outpost providing regional authority and vital missions against nearby threats.",["race:Human"]="Human travelers view the town hall as a poignant reminder of Lordaeron's lost glory, where a functioning magistrate still flies the banners of a shattered kingdom."},kw={"henry maleb","hillsbrad","kundric zanden","lordaeron","magistrate","southshore","town hall"},rel={"subzone:southshore","npc:magistrate-henry-maleb","zone:hillsbrad","topic:lordaeron","topic:forsaken","topic:third-war","subzone:fenris-isle"},src={"Southshore Town Hall"}}
E["subzone:strahnbrad"] = {t="subzone",n="Strahnbrad",z="hillsbrad",s="Strahnbrad is a ruined human settlement nestled in the northeastern heights of the Alterac Mountains, near the border of the Western Plaguelands. Once famous as the site of Prince Arthas Menethil's early defense against Blackrock orc raiders, the town has since fallen into decay and serves as a fortified stronghold for the criminal Syndicate.",h="Strahnbrad is a ruined human settlement nestled in the northeastern heights of the Alterac Mountains, near...",sec={{t="A Town of Tragedy",b="Originally a holding of the Kingdom of Alterac before being absorbed into Lordaeron following the Second War, Strahnbrad's misfortune began on the eve of the Third War. Blackrock clan orcs raided the settlement to take human sacrifices for the Burning Legion, leading Prince Arthas Menethil and the Knights of the Silver Hand to ride to its defense. Though Arthas drove the raiders away and slew their slave master, the town was heavily bloodied. When Lordaeron crumbled beneath the Scourge shortly thereafter, Strahnbrad was abandoned to the elements.",sp=0},{t="The Syndicate's Grip",b="Today, Strahnbrad has become a crucial operations hub for the Syndicate, the organization of displaced Alteraci nobility and outlaws plotting to reclaim their fallen realm. Patrolled by human rogues and brigands, its abandoned town hall and blacksmith now serve as hideouts and staging grounds. The Syndicate uses the ruined town to house supplies and captive labor, including unfortunate prisoners like the orc Gol'dir, whom Horde scouts from Tarren Mill actively seek to liberate.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Why is Strahnbrad significant in history?",a="Strahnbrad was the site of the opening clash of the Third War for Prince Arthas Menethil. Sent by Uther the Lightbringer to protect the settlement from rampaging Blackrock orcs, Arthas made his first celebrated stand here, rescuing townsfolk and cutting down the orc raiders.",al={"why does strahnbrad matter","arthas strahnbrad","strahnbrad history"},it="history"},{q="Who controls Strahnbrad now?",a="The Syndicate holds Strahnbrad. These human brigands, loyal to the fallen noble bloodlines of Alterac, have fortified the ruined town hall and blacksmith to use as a primary staging ground for their ambitions in the mountains.",al={"who owns strahnbrad","strahnbrad mobs","who lives in strahnbrad"},it="residents"},{q="Which kingdom did Strahnbrad belong to originally?",a="Strahnbrad was originally part of the Kingdom of Alterac before the First War. After Alterac betrayed the Alliance during the Second War, the town was integrated under the domain of the Kingdom of Lordaeron.",al={"is strahnbrad alterac or lordaeron","strahnbrad kingdom"},it="history"},{q="Why does the Horde care about this town?",a="The Syndicate captured an orc named Gol'dir and forced him into brutal slave labor within Strahnbrad's ruins. Horde operatives from Tarren Mill, directed by Krusk, send adventurers here to breach the Syndicate's defenses and break Gol'dir out.",al={"horde quests in strahnbrad","krusk strahnbrad","gol'dir strahnbrad"},it="purpose"},{q="What is Strahnbrad?",a="Strahnbrad is a ruined settlement nestled in the northeastern foothills of the Alterac Mountains, near the pass into the Western Plaguelands. Originally a human town that passed from the Kingdom of Alterac to Lordaeron, it now stands derelict, its streets deserted of innocent life and occupied by dangerous outlaws.",al={"what is this place","strahnbrad overview","tell me about strahnbrad"},it="place",add=true},{q="Why is Strahnbrad ruined and abandoned?",a="Strahnbrad suffered brutal devastation just prior to the Third War when renegade Blackrock orcs raided the settlement to capture sacrifices for the Burning Legion. Though Prince Arthas Menethil arrived to drive the raiders off, many townsfolk perished. Following the fall of Lordaeron to the Scourge, the surviving populace scattered or died, leaving the abandoned structures to be seized by bandits.",al={"why is strahnbrad destroyed","who destroyed strahnbrad","why is strahnbrad a ghost town"},it="ruin",add=true},{q="Is Strahnbrad dangerous to visit?",a="Yes, Strahnbrad is very dangerous. The abandoned town serves as an active stronghold for the Syndicate, a ruthless criminal network of former Alterac nobility and brigands. They attack trespassers on sight and have even been known to take captives for forced labor, making the area hazardous for any lone traveler passing through the mountains.",al={"is strahnbrad safe","strahnbrad hostile","strahnbrad dangers"},it="danger",add=true}},ang={["class:Paladin"]="Walking the cobblestones of Strahnbrad recalls the early, untainted days of Prince Arthas Menethil and Uther the Lightbringer, serving as a bitter reminder of how far Lordaeron's heroes have fallen.",["faction:Horde"]="The Syndicate's enslavement of the orc Gol'dir makes Strahnbrad an urgent target for Horde champions seeking to strike at human brigands and rescue their kin."},kw={"alterac","arthas","blackrock","gol'dir","krusk","lordaeron","strahnbrad","syndicate"},rel={"zone:alterac","topic:syndicate","topic:arthas-menethil","topic:alterac-kingdom","topic:lordaeron","npc:krusk","subzone:tarren-mill","zone:westernplaguelands"},src={"Strahnbrad"}}
E["subzone:tarren-mill"] = {t="subzone",n="Tarren Mill",z="hillsbrad",s="Tarren Mill is a beleaguered Forsaken outpost nestled in the northern reaches of the Hillsbrad Foothills beneath the Alterac Mountains. Once a peaceful human farming village, it now serves as the primary bastion of the Horde in Hillsbrad, locked in constant conflict with the Alliance town of Southshore to the south.",h="Tarren Mill is a beleaguered Forsaken outpost nestled in the northern reaches of the Hillsbrad Foothills...",sec={{t="From Grain to Grave",b="Before the Third War, Tarren Mill was a thriving agricultural township loyal to the Kingdom of Lordaeron. During the Second War, it earned renown when Alliance forces rescued captured high elven archers from nearby orc encampments, securing Quel'Thalas's full commitment to the Alliance of Lordaeron. Today, however, the town's original living inhabitants are gone, replaced by the Forsaken. The town's architecture stands weathered and decayed, its fields barren, and its old mill silent as the new undead occupants fortify the settlement against constant threats from mountain beasts, Syndicate outlaws, and Alliance skirmishers.",sp=0},{t="Front Line of Hillsbrad",b="Tarren Mill functions as the Horde's vital forward operations base in the region. Directly opposed to the Alliance port of Southshore, the road between the two settlements has devolved into an open warzone. Horde travelers use Tarren Mill to push back against the human farmers and soldiers occupying Hillsbrad, coordinate strikes against dwarven excavators at Dun Garok, and secure the treacherous roads leading up into the snowy crags of the Alterac Mountains.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who controls Tarren Mill right now?",a="Tarren Mill is controlled entirely by the Forsaken and functions as the primary Horde questing hub and outpost in the Hillsbrad Foothills.",al={"who owns tarren mill","is tarren mill horde or alliance","tarren mill faction"},it="in_charge"},{q="Why are Tarren Mill and Southshore fighting?",a="Tarren Mill represents the Forsaken and the Horde's southern reach in Lordaeron, while Southshore is the last major stronghold of the Alliance in the region. Their close proximity makes ongoing territorial warfare inevitable as both factions contest control of Hillsbrad's fertile land and strategic roads.",al={"southshore vs tarren mill","why fight southshore","hillsbrad war"},it="conflict"},{q="What was Tarren Mill like before the plague?",a="It was a peaceful human farming and milling settlement of the Kingdom of Lordaeron. During the Second War, Alliance soldiers famously freed captive high elven archers near the town, securing Quel'Thalas's military pact with the Alliance of Lordaeron.",al={"tarren mill history","who lived here before","tarren mill lore"},it="origin"},{q="What threats exist around Tarren Mill besides the Alliance?",a="Beyond Southshore's forces, Tarren Mill must contend with local bandits of the Syndicate, highland yetis and ogres descending from the Alterac peaks, and fierce mountain wildlife roaming the foothills.",al={"tarren mill enemies","local dangers hillsbrad"},it="threat"},{q="What is Tarren Mill?",a="Tarren Mill is a northern outpost and settlement in the Hillsbrad Foothills, situated just below the Alterac Mountains. Once a modest farming community of the Kingdom of Lordaeron, it now serves as the primary Forsaken bastion and Horde stronghold in the region, standing as a direct counterweight to the Alliance at Southshore.",al={"tarren mill overview","what is this town","about tarren mill"},it="place",add=true},{q="What happened at Tarren Mill in the past?",a="During the Second War, Horde forces ambushed Silvermoon elven archers near the town, prompting King Terenas to order Alliance troops here to rescue the captives and solidify the elves' alliance with Lordaeron. Long after the Third War ravaged the kingdom, the human survivors were attacked by the Scourge seeking the Sunwell's essence. Eventually, the surviving humans fell away, and the Forsaken claimed the weathered settlement as their own staging ground.",al={"tarren mill history","past of tarren mill","second war tarren mill"},it="history",add=true},{q="Why is Tarren Mill in such disrepair?",a="The town suffered through the devastation of the Third War, subsequent Scourge attacks, and the loss of its original human population. The Forsaken who occupy it now view Tarren Mill primarily as a strategic military staging ground rather than a comfortable home, leaving its old buildings, church, and withered orchards in a state of neglected decay.",al={"why is tarren mill ruined","why does tarren mill look broken","tarren mill run down"},it="ruin",add=true},{q="Is Tarren Mill dangerous?",a="Tarren Mill is exceptionally dangerous. Situated on the volatile front lines of Hillsbrad, it faces relentless skirmishes and counterattacks from Alliance soldiers and champions from Southshore. Beyond the Alliance, Syndicate outlaws lurk in nearby ruins, mountain yetis stalk the northern slopes, and savage Crushridge ogres constantly threaten the perimeter.",al={"is it safe in tarren mill","tarren mill danger","threat level tarren mill"},it="danger",add=true}},ang={["faction:Horde"]="Tarren Mill is your only major refuge in the Hillsbrad Foothills, offering a bat handler, supplies, and vital military support against encroaching Alliance forces from Southshore.",["race:Undead"]="Taking hold of Tarren Mill expands Queen Sylvanas's southern borders, turning a once-proud Lordaeron farming town into a strategic stronghold against the living."},kw={"alterac","forsaken","hillsbrad","hillsbrad foothills","lordaeron","southshore","syndicate","tarren mill"},rel={"zone:hillsbrad","subzone:southshore","topic:forsaken","topic:horde","topic:alliance-of-lordaeron","zone:alterac","topic:syndicate","subzone:dun-garok"},src={"Tarren Mill"}}
E["zone:hillsbrad"] = {t="zone",n="Hillsbrad Foothills",z="hillsbrad",s="Hillsbrad Foothills is a green, fertile region that represents the last pastoral bastion of the fallen kingdom of Lordaeron. Despite having largely escaped the Scourge's plague, the land is torn apart by brutal open war between the humans of Southshore and the Forsaken entrenched at Tarren Mill. It serves as a violent crossroads where the armies of the Alliance and the Horde clash without mercy.",h="Hillsbrad Foothills is a green, fertile region that represents the last pastoral bastion of the fallen...",sec={{t="A Garden Beside the Ruins",b="While northern Lordaeron rots under the blight of the Scourge, Hillsbrad remains strikingly green. Its rolling pastures, pine groves, and working farmsteads offer travelers a rare glimpse of what the kingdom looked like before the Third War. Yet that tranquil appearance is deceptive. The peaceful fields and rural roads are constantly swept by armed patrols, rogue mercenaries, and scavenger beasts. What should be Lordaeron's breadbasket has instead become its most contested borderland.",sp=0},{t="The War of Southshore and Tarren Mill",b="The political heart of Hillsbrad is defined by two entrenched strongholds. In the south along the coast lies Southshore, an Alliance haven populated by human refugees and soldiers fiercely loyal to the Alliance. To the north sits Tarren Mill, once a quiet human farming hamlet that was wiped out by the Scourge and later fortified as the Forsaken's southernmost garrison. The open ground between the two settlements is known throughout Azeroth as a relentless kill zone, where Alliance and Horde champions wage perpetual skirmishes for control of the region.",sp=0},{t="Old Scars and Hidden Threats",b="Hillsbrad's history of violence runs deep. During the Second War, its coast and hills witnessed the first massive clashes between the Grand Alliance and the Old Horde. Later, the fortress of Durnholde Keep served as the internment camp where Thrall was raised before leading the orcish rebellion. Today, Durnholde lies in ruins, seized by the Syndicate—displaced human nobles turned bandit cutthroats. Coastal murlocs, hostile gnolls, and the shadowed dead on Purgation Isle ensure that no corner of the hills is truly secure.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Why isn't Hillsbrad blighted like the rest of Lordaeron?",a="The Scourge marched primarily along the central corridors toward the capital and the northern kingdoms, leaving Hillsbrad largely bypassed by the plague cauldrons that ruined the north. As a result, the soil remains fertile and the vegetation healthy, making it the most pristine remnant of old Lordaeron.",al={"why is hillsbrad green","did hillsbrad get plagued","why no plague in hillsbrad"},it="ruin"},{q="Who controls Hillsbrad right now?",a="Neither faction holds full control. The Alliance maintains Southshore and nearby farms like the Hillsbrad Fields, while the Forsaken hold Tarren Mill to the north. Dwarven forces hold the fortress of Dun Garok in the east, and the criminal Syndicate occupies the ruins of Durnholde Keep.",al={"who owns hillsbrad","hillsbrad faction control","is hillsbrad alliance or horde"},it="in_charge"},{q="What is Durnholde Keep?",a="Durnholde was once the headquarters of the Alliance internment camp system after the Second War, governed by Aedelas Blackmoore, who raised Thrall there as a gladiator slave. Thrall escaped, rallied the orcs, and laid waste to the keep. In the aftermath of Lordaeron's fall, the ruins were occupied by the Syndicate.",al={"durnholde lore","what happened at durnholde","who runs durnholde"},it="place",nx={15,16}},{q="Why do the Forsaken and humans fight so fiercely here?",a="Tarren Mill represents the southern frontier of Sylvanas Windrunner's domain, while Southshore is the Alliance's primary staging ground and port into Lordaeron. The Forsaken view Southshore as an existential threat to their southern flank, while the humans view the undead as horrific usurpers who must be driven from their homeland.",al={"why the southshore war","southshore vs tarren mill lore","hillsbrad conflict reason"},it="conflict"},{q="What is Purgation Isle?",a="Purgation Isle is an isolated, rugged island off the southern coast of Hillsbrad. Unlike the mainland hills, the island is infested with powerful undead ghouls, skeletons, and vengeful spirits, making it an extremely dangerous offshore haven for dark magic and restless dead.",al={"purgation isle lore","island off southshore","why undead on purgation isle"},it="place"},{q="Who are the bandits occupying the camps and towers?",a="They belong to the Syndicate, an organized network of former nobility and foot soldiers from the fallen human kingdom of Alterac. Cast out for their kingdom's betrayal during the Second War, they now operate as ruthless bandits seeking to reclaim their lands through blackmail, theft, and slaughter.",al={"hillsbrad bandits","who is the syndicate","syndicate in hillsbrad"},it="threat"},{q="What is Hillsbrad Foothills?",a="Hillsbrad Foothills is a rolling, temperate coastal territory along the southern edge of fallen Lordaeron, bounded by Silverpine Forest to the west, the snow-draped Alterac Mountains to the north, and Thoradin's Wall leading into the Arathi Highlands to the east. Unlike the blighted lands to the north, Hillsbrad remains lush and pastoral, with green meadows, productive farms, and seaside cliffs. Beneath this idyllic veneer, it serves as a violent borderland contested between the surviving humans of the Alliance and the encroaching Forsaken.",al={"what is hillsbrad","hillsbrad foothills overview","tell me about hillsbrad"},it="place",add=true},{q="What happened at Hillsbrad Foothills?",a="Hillsbrad has long been one of the bloodiest battlegrounds in Lordaeron. During the Second War, it saw the very first clashes between the Alliance and the Old Horde, including fierce skirmishes with forest trolls and coastal raids that left towns like Hillsbrad and Southshore briefly in ruins. Later, orc internment camps were centered here at Durnholde Keep until Thrall's rebellion leveled the fortress. When the Third War broke out, Thrall stole ships from Southshore to reach Kalimdor, and the Scourge later swept the north, eventually prompting the Forsaken to seize Tarren Mill.",al={"hillsbrad history","battle of hillsbrad history","past of hillsbrad"},it="history",add=true},{q="Is Hillsbrad Foothills dangerous?",a="Extremely dangerous. Beyond native predators like mountain lions, snapping turtles, and prowling spiders, Hillsbrad is an active war zone. Southshore's human guards and Tarren Mill's undead Deathstalkers hunt opposing travelers along the roads. In addition, cutthroats of the Syndicate operate out of scattered towers and the ruins of Durnholde, hostile Daggerspine naga and Torn Fin murlocs infest the coast, Mudsnout gnolls roam the woods, and dwarf riflemen occupy Dun Garok in force.",al={"how dangerous is hillsbrad","is hillsbrad safe","dangers of hillsbrad"},it="danger",add=true},{q="What is Tarren Mill and why is the Horde here?",a="Tarren Mill is a dilapidated settlement in the northern foothills that serves as the Forsaken's southernmost stronghold in Lordaeron. Once a peaceful human farming village, it fell during the Scourge invasion and was later occupied by Sylvanas Windrunner's forces. From here, the Horde projects power southward, harboring Apothecaries working on virulent concoctions and stationing troops to mount repeated assaults against Southshore and the nearby human farmlands.",al={"what is tarren mill","why horde in tarren mill","tarren mill horde base"},it="place",add=true,nx={11}},{q="Was Tarren Mill a human town before?",a="Yes. Prior to the Third War, Tarren Mill was a thriving town under the Kingdom of Lordaeron. In the Second War, King Terenas sent troops here to liberate captured high elven archers held nearby by the Horde, an act that helped cement Quel'Thalas's alliance with humanity. Even after the kingdom fell, a contingent of humans briefly clung to the town before the Scourge and subsequent Forsaken occupation claimed it.",al={"did humans live in tarren mill","was tarren mill human","tarren mill past"},it="history",add=true},{q="Who's in charge in Tarren Mill?",a="High Executor Darthalia commands the Forsaken military garrison at Tarren Mill. She directs the war effort throughout the foothills, ordering surgical strikes against human farmers, the town of Southshore, and rival factions across the region. Alongside her, Royal Apothecary Society researchers like Apothecary Lydon oversee local operations and chemical experiments.",al={"who runs tarren mill","tarren mill leader","tarren mill commander"},it="in_charge",add=true},{q="What is the Battle of Hillsbrad actually about?",a="The ongoing battle is a territorial and existential clash for southern Lordaeron. The humans of Southshore and Hillsbrad Fields fight to defend the last remnants of their uncorrupted homeland and retain a vital coastal foothold. Conversely, the Forsaken seek to expand the borders of their fledgling kingdom outward from the Undercity, systematically destroying human agricultural supply lines and driving out the Alliance so they cannot mount a counter-invasion.",al={"why are they fighting in hillsbrad","battle of hillsbrad purpose","hillsbrad war reason"},it="purpose",add=true},{q="What is Southshore?",a="Southshore is a bustling Alliance port town positioned along the southern coastline. Originally a humble fishing hamlet, it served as the landing point for refugees from Stormwind during the First War before expanding into a heavily defended military harbor in the Second War. Today, led by Magistrate Henry Maleb and Marshal Redpath, it acts as the primary redoubt for human survivors, sailors, and Alliance adventurers in northern Lordaeron.",al={"what is southshore","southshore overview","alliance southshore"},it="place",add=true},{q="Was Durnholde Keep where orcs were kept prisoner?",a="Yes. Following the Alliance's victory in the Second War, Durnholde Keep served as the headquarters for the entire southern internment camp network, commanded by Lieutenant General Aedelas Blackmoore. Captured orcs were imprisoned and pacified here by Alliance guards. Most notably, Blackmoore raised the orphaned infant Thrall within its arena walls, who eventually broke free, mobilized his brethren, and smashed the keep to rubble with the aid of the earth spirits.",al={"was durnholde an internment camp","orcs imprisoned at durnholde","durnholde internment"},it="history",add=true},{q="Who holds Durnholde now?",a="The shattered stone courtyards and burnt-out lodges of Durnholde are now occupied by the Syndicate. These exiled nobles, disgraced retainers, and bandits from the fallen kingdom of Alterac have fortified the ruins, using them as a staging ground to raid supply lines, caravans, and travelers across eastern Hillsbrad.",al={"who is at durnholde keep","durnholde bandits","who controls durnholde"},it="residents",add=true},{q="What is Dun Garok and why are dwarves here?",a="Dun Garok is a sturdy dwarven fortress tucked into the rocky southeastern bluffs of Hillsbrad, garrisoned by the Stormpike clan and Ironforge Mountaineers under Captain Ironhill. These stalwart troops arrived to reinforce Alliance positions, secure nearby mining resources like the Azurelode Mine, and prevent Forsaken forces from pushing eastward through the mountains toward Thoradin's Wall.",al={"what is dun garok","why are there dwarves in hillsbrad","dun garok dwarves"},it="threat",add=true},{q="What are these murlocs and naga-looking things on the coast?",a="The shoreline is overrun by the Torn Fin tribe of murlocs and serpent-like naga known as the Daggerspine. The Torn Fin stalk the shallows, attacking fishermen and competing with miners along the coast. Meanwhile, the Daggerspine naga have crept ashore to establish coastal enclaves, viciously striking at anyone traveling near the waves or scavenging the shoreline.",al={"hillsbrad coast murlocs","naga in hillsbrad","hillsbrad coastal monsters"},it="threat",add=true},{q="How did I end up in Hillsbrad Foothills?",a="Your road here depends on your allegiance. If you march with the Horde, you likely journeyed south from the Sepulcher in Silverpine Forest, following the long winding road east along Lordaeron's southern border until you reached Tarren Mill. If you fight for the Alliance, you traveled far from the dwarven halls of Ironforge, marching north across Loch Modan and the sodden marshes of the Wetlands, traversing the Arathi Highlands, and passing through the ancient breach of Thoradin's Wall to reach the port of Southshore. Alternatively, daring sailors and swimmers sometimes brave the sea passage directly north from Menethil Harbor.",al={"how did i get to hillsbrad","how did i get here","why am i in hillsbrad foothills","how do i reach hillsbrad"},it="arrival",add=true},{q="What am I supposed to be doing in Hillsbrad Foothills?",a="You stand on one of the most volatile front lines in Azeroth. For the Alliance, your duty centers on Southshore and Hillsbrad Fields: defending human farmers from undead aggression, hunting the rogue bandits of the Syndicate, and curbing the savage creatures infesting the shores. For the Horde, High Executor Darthalia and the Royal Apothecary Society at Tarren Mill demand the systematic dismantling of human resistance, harvesting ingredients for a new plague, and pushing back against the Stormpike dwarves and Alliance soldiers. Across the fields between the two towns, survival demands eternal vigilance against enemy champions.",al={"what am i doing here","what should i do in hillsbrad","what is my purpose in hillsbrad","why am i here"},it="purpose",add=true}},ang={["race:Human"]="Southshore is one of your people's final refuges in Lordaeron; walking these pastures is a painful reminder of the great kingdom that was lost to betrayal and undeath.",["race:Undead"]="Tarren Mill anchors the southern frontier of the Forsaken realm, where Apothecary Lydon works tirelessly to develop the New Plague to secure your people's future.",["race:Orc"]="This soil holds monumental weight for your people: the ruined ramparts of Durnholde Keep are where Warchief Thrall broke his chains and reawakened the spirit of the Horde.",["race:Dwarf"]="The soldiers of Dun Garok represent Ironforge's resolute military commitment to defending their human allies and containing the undead threat north of the Wetlands.",["class:Rogue"]="Hidden high in the mountains above the foothills lies Ravenholdt Manor, the secretive gathering place and training ground for Azeroth's most elite guild of thieves and assassins."},kw={"azurelode","dun garok","durnholde","hillsbrad","hillsbrad fields","purgation isle","southshore","syndicate","tarren mill"},rel={"subzone:southshore","subzone:tarren-mill","subzone:durnholde-keep","subzone:hillsbrad-fields","subzone:dun-garok","subzone:purgation-isle","zone:alterac","zone:arathi"},m={levels="20-30"},src={"Hillsbrad Foothills (Classic)","Hillsbrad Foothills"}}
